(120101,'chemistry','The property of carbon to form bonds with other carbon atoms is called ___','Catenation','The element carbon has the unique property called catenation due to which it forms covalent bonds with other carbon atoms. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 334; Paragraph No.1)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> General introduction',NULL,'1','mcq','Carbonation','Catenation','Tetravalent','Covalent bond','NEW','11-334','11-256',NULL),
(120102,'chemistry','What type of bonds does carbon form with other carbon atoms due to its catenation property?','Covalent','The element carbon has the unique property called catenation due to which it forms covalent bonds with other carbon atoms. It also forms covalent bonds with atoms of other elements like hydrogen, oxygen, nitrogen, sulphur, phosphorus and halogens. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 334; Paragraph No.1)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> General introduction',NULL,'1','mcq','Ionic','Covalent','Coordinate','None of these','NEW','11-334','11-256',NULL),
(120103,'chemistry','Which among the following statements is correct ?\n \n a.Organic compounds are vital for sustaining life on earth.\n \n b.They include complex molecules like genetic information bearing deoxyribonucleic acid (DNA) and proteins.','Both','Organic compounds are vital for sustaining life on earth and include complex molecules like genetic information bearing deoxyribonucleic acid (DNA) and proteins that constitute essential compounds of our blood, muscles and skin. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 334; Paragraph No.2)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> General introduction',NULL,'2','mcq','Only a','Only b','Both','None of these','NEW','11-334','11-256',NULL),
(120104,'chemistry','Which among the following statements is correct ?\n a. Organic compounds constitute essential compounds of our blood, muscles and skin.\n b. Organic compounds appear in materials like clothing fuels, polymers, dyes and medicines.','Both','Organic compounds are vital for sustaining life on earth and include complex molecules like genetic information bearing deoxyribonucleic acid (DNA) and proteins that constitute essential compounds of our blood, muscles and skin. Organic compounds appear in materials like clothing, fuels, polymers, dyes and medicines. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 334; Paragraph No.2)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> General introduction',NULL,'2','mcq','Only a','Only b','Both','None of these','NEW','11-334','11-256',NULL),
(120105,'chemistry','Which scientist synthesised an organic compound, urea from an inorganic compound, ammonium cyanate ?','F. Wohler','F. Wohler synthesised an organic compound, urea from an inorganic compound, ammonium cyanate. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 334; Paragraph No.3)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> General introduction',NULL,'1','mcq','Berzilius','F. Wohler','Kolbe','None of these','NEW','11-334','11-256',NULL),
(120106,'chemistry','Who among the following synthesized acetic acid ?','Kolbe','The pioneering synthesis of acetic acid by Kolbe (1845) and that of methane by Berthelot (1856) showed conclusively that organic compounds could be synthesised from inorganic sources in a laboratory. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 334; Paragraph No.3)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> General introduction',NULL,'1','mcq','Berzilius','F. Wohler','Kolbe','None of these','NEW','11-334','11-256',NULL),
(120107,'chemistry','Who among the following gave vital force theory ?','Berzilius','Berzilius, a Swedish chemist proposed that a ‘vital force’ was responsible for the formation of organic compounds. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 334; Paragraph No.3)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> General introduction',NULL,'1','mcq','Berzilius','F. Wohler','Kolbe','None of these','NEW','11-334','11-256','/ncert/pyq/biology/mcq/120107q.png'),
(120108,'chemistry','What is A in the given diagram(1201)','Urea','The formula of Urea is NH2CONH2. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 334; Paragraph No.3)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> General introduction',NULL,'3','mcq','Urea','Ammonia','Cyanide','All of these','NEW','11-334','11-256',NULL),
(120109,'chemistry','Chemists distinguish between organic compounds obtained from plants and animals and inorganic compounds prepared from ________ sources.','Mineral','Around the year 1780, chemists began to distinguish between organic compounds obtained from plants and animals and inorganic compounds prepared from mineral sources. (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 334; Paragraph No.2)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> General introduction',NULL,'1','mcq','Mineral','Salt','Rocks','Fossils','NEW','11-334','11-256',NULL),
(120110,'chemistry','Which of them is true for organic compounds?','Organic compounds could be synthesised from inorganic sources in a laboratory.','The pioneering synthesis of acetic acid by Kolbe (1845) and that of methane by Berthelot (1856) showed conclusively that organic compounds could be synthesised from inorganic sources in a laboratory. (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 334; Paragraph No.3)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> General introduction',NULL,'2','mcq','Organic compounds cannot be synthesized in the laboratory.','Organic compounds are special compounds that can be only made by living things in living systems.','Organic compounds could be synthesised from inorganic sources in a laboratory.','None of these','NEW','11-334','11-256',NULL),
(120111,'biology','Identify the part marked C in the diagram (1202)','Nutrient solution','NCERTclass 11 Page No 195 Figure 12.2','Plant Physiology >> Mineral Nutrition >> Methods to study the mineral requirements',NULL,'2','mcq','Adequate solution','Mineral solution','Nutrient solution','Water solution','DELETED',NULL,NULL,'/ncert/pyq/biology/mcq/120111q.png'),
(120201,'chemistry','Which among the following statements is correct ?\n a. Hybridisation influences the bond length and bond enthalpy (strength) in compounds.\n b. The sp hybrid orbital contains less s character and hence it is farthest to its nucleus.','Only a','Hybridisation influences the bond length and bond enthalpy (strength) in compounds. The sp hybrid orbital contains more s character and hence it is closer to its nucleus. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 257; Paragraph No.2)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Tetravalence of carbon and shapes of compounds',NULL,'2','mcq','Only a','Only b','Both a and b','None of these','NEW','11-335','11-257',NULL),
(120202,'chemistry','Which among the following statements is correct ?\n a. The sp hybrid orbital forms shorter and stronger bonds than the sp³ hybrid orbital\n b. The sp² hybrid orbital is intermediate in s character between sp and sp³','Both','More is the s character, stronger and shorter are the bonds. s- character is higher in sp hybrid orbital. The sp² hybrid orbital is intermediate in s character between sp and sp³ and, hence, the length and enthalpy of the bonds it forms, are also intermediate between them. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 335; Paragraph No.2)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Tetravalence of carbon and shapes of compounds',NULL,'2','mcq','Only a','Only b','Both','None of these','NEW','11-335','11-257',NULL),
(120203,'chemistry','Which among the following statements is correct ?\n a. The bond length and enthalpy of the bonds of sp hybrid orbital are intermediate between sp² and sp³\n b. The change in hybridisation affects the electronegativity of carbon','Only b','The sp² hybrid orbital is intermediate in s character between sp and sp³ and, hence, the length and enthalpy of the bonds it forms, are also intermediate between them. \n \n The change in hybridisation affects the electronegativity of carbon. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 335; Paragraph No.2)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Tetravalence of carbon and shapes of compounds',NULL,'2','mcq','Only a','Only b','Both','None of these','NEW','11-335','11-257',NULL),
(120204,'chemistry','Which among the following statements is correct ?\n a.The greater the s character of the hybrid orbitals, the greater is the electronegativity.\n b. Relative electronegativity is reflected in several physical and chemical properties of the molecules.','Both','The greater the s character of the hybrid orbitals, the greater is the electronegativity. Relative electronegativity is reflected in several physical and chemical properties of the molecules. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 335; Paragraph No.2)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Tetravalence of carbon and shapes of compounds',NULL,'2','mcq','Only a','Only b','Both','None of these','NEW','11-335','11-257',NULL),
(120205,'chemistry','Which among the following statements is correct ?\n a. In a pi bond formation, parallel orientation of the two p orbitals on adjacent atoms is necessary for a proper sideways overlap.\n b. The electron charge cloud of the pi bond is located above and below the plane of bonding atoms.','Both','In a pi bond formation, parallel orientation of the two p orbitals on adjacent atoms is necessary for a proper sideways overlap. The electron charge cloud of the pi bond is located above and below the plane of bonding atoms. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 335; Paragraph No.3)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Tetravalence of carbon and shapes of compounds',NULL,'2','mcq','Only a','Only b','Both','None of these','NEW','11-335','11-257',NULL),
(120301,'chemistry','Which of the following formula is correct for the condensed form of ethane ?','CH₃CH₃','In condensed form, no single bond is shown. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 336; Paragraph No.1)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Structural representation of organic compounds',NULL,'1','mcq','CH₃-CH₃','H₂C-H-CH₃','CH₃CH₃','CH₂=CH₂','NEW','11-336','11-258',NULL),
(120302,'chemistry','Which of the following atom is not a heteroatom in a carbon structure?','Carbon','A non carbon atom in a carbon structure is called a heteroatom. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 336; Paragraph No.3)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Structural representation of organic compounds',NULL,'1','mcq','Carbon','Oxygen','Chlorine','Sulpher','NEW','11-336','11-258',NULL),
(120303,'chemistry','Which of the following is the condensed formula of CH₂CH₂CH₂CH₂CH₂CH₂CH₂CH₂CH₂CH₂CH₃?','(CH₂)₁₀CH₃','For determining the condensed formula, combine all the CH₂ terms together and assign the appropriate number to them, each time checking that carbon only forms four bonds with the other atoms. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 336; Paragraph No.3)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Structural representation of organic compounds',NULL,'2','mcq','(CH₂)₁₀CH₃','(CH₂)₃CH₂CHCH₂CH₂CH₂CH(CH₃)₂','(CH₂)₄CH(CH₂)₃CH (CH₂)CH₃','(CH₂)₃CH₂CH₂CH(CH₃)₂CH₃CHCH₂CH₃','NEW','11-336','11-258',NULL),
(120304,'chemistry','Write True or False?\n \n a. The 3-D structures of organic molecules can be represented on paper.\n \n b. In Solid and dashed wedge formula, dashed wedge is used to depict bond towards the observer.','T,F','The three-dimensional (3-D) structure of organic molecules can be represented on paper by using certain conventions.For example, by using solid and dashed wedge formula, the 3-D image of a molecule from a two-dimensional picture can be perceived. In these formulas the solid-wedge is used to indicate a bond projecting out of the plane of paper, towards the observer. The dashed-wedge is used to depict the bond projecting out of the plane of the paper and away from the observer. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 338; Paragraph No.1)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Structural representation of organic compounds',NULL,'3','mcq','T,T','T,F','F,T','F,F','NEW','11-338','11-260',NULL),
(120305,'chemistry','Which of the following is the correct skeletal structural formula for the compound X in the given diagram(1203)','C','Here ketonic group should be on the 3rd carbon and therefore option c is the correct answer. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 336; Paragraph No.3)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Structural representation of organic compounds',NULL,'3','mcq','A','B','C','D','NEW','11-336','11-258','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/120305q.png'),
(120306,'chemistry','Which of the following correctly matched the bond line and structural formula of the compounds in the given diagram(1204)','All of these','All of these have their valency satisfied and no violation of octet rule has been done in any, therefore all of them are correctly matched. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 336; Paragraph No.3)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Structural representation of organic compounds',NULL,'3','mcq','Only i','Only ii','Only iii','All of these','NEW','11-336','11-258','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/120306q.png'),
(120307,'chemistry','What does the solid wedge represent in a 2D image of a molecule ?','Out of plane and towards the observer','Solid-wedge is used to indicate a bond projecting out of the plane of paper, towards the observer. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 338; Paragraph No.1)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Structural representation of organic compounds',NULL,'1','mcq','Out of plane and away from the observer','Out of plane and towards the observer','In the plane','None of these','NEW','11-338','11-260',NULL),
(120308,'chemistry','What does the dashed wedge represent in a 2D image of a molecule ?','Out of plane and away from the observer','The dashed-wedge is used to depict the bond projecting out of the plane of the paper and away from the observer. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 338; Paragraph No.1)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Structural representation of organic compounds',NULL,'1','mcq','Out of plane and away from the observer','Out of plane and towards the observer','In the plane','None of these','NEW','11-338','11-260',NULL),
(120309,'chemistry','Which of the following is the condensed formula of CH₃CH₂CH₂CH₂CH₂CH₂CH₂CH₃?','CH₃(CH₂)6CH₃','For determining the condensed formula, combine all the CH₂ terms together and assign the appropriate number to them, each time checking that carbon only forms four bonds with the other atoms. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 336; Paragraph No.3)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Structural representation of organic compounds',NULL,'2','mcq','CH₃(CH₂)6CH₃','CH₃(CH₂)5C₂H6','CH₃(CH₂)5CH₃','CH₃(CH₂)6C₂H6','NEW','11-336','11-260',NULL),
(120310,'chemistry','In Dash structure, single dash represents','one bond','The lewis structures can be simplified by representing the two electron, covalent bond represented by dash. A single dash represents a single bond.\n Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 336; )','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Structural representation of organic compounds',NULL,'2','mcq','one bond','two bond','triple bond','None of these','NEW','11-336','11-258',NULL),
(120311,'chemistry','Which of them are not shown in bond line structure','C','In bond line strucutre carbon and hydrogen atoms are not shown and the lines representing Carbon Carbon bonds are drawn in a zig zag fashion.\n Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 336; )','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Structural representation of organic compounds',NULL,'2','mcq','N','C','O','Cl','NEW','11-336','11-258',NULL),
(120312,'chemistry','Which of them is not a molecular model?','Bond line model','Commonly three types of molecular model are used:\n 1. Framework model\n 2. Ball and stick model\n 3. Space filling model\n Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 338 )','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Structural representation of organic compounds',NULL,'2','mcq','Framework Model','Ball and Stick model','Bond line model','Space filling model','NEW','11-338','11-260',NULL),
(120313,'chemistry','The three-dimensional (3-D) structure of organic molecules can be represented on paper by using which conventions?','Both of these','The three-dimensional (3-D) structure of organic molecules can be represented on paper by using certain conventions.For example, by using solid and dashed wedge formula, the 3-D image of a molecule from a two-dimensional picture can be perceived. In these formulas the solid-wedge is used to indicate a bond projecting out of the plane of paper, towards the observer. The dashed-wedge is used to depict the bond projecting out of the plane of the paper and away from the observer. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 338; Paragraph No.1)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Structural representation of organic compounds',NULL,'1','mcq','Solid wedge','Dashed wedge','Both of these','None of these','NEW','11-338','11-260',NULL),
(120314,'chemistry','Which model emphasises the relative size of each atom based on its van der Waals radius?','Space-filling Model','The space-filling model emphasises the relative size of each atom based on its van der Waals radius. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 338; Paragraph No.1)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Structural representation of organic compounds',NULL,'1','mcq','Framework Model','Space-filling Model','Ball and stick Model','None of these','NEW','11-338','11-260',NULL),
(120315,'chemistry','Which model emphasizes the pattern of bonds of a molecule while ignoring the size of atoms?','Framework Model','In the framework model only the bonds connecting the atoms of a molecule and not the atoms themselves are shown. This model emphasizes the pattern of bonds of a molecule while ignoring the size of atoms. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 338; Paragraph No.1)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Structural representation of organic compounds',NULL,'1','mcq','Framework Model','Space-filling Model','Ball and stick Model','None of these','NEW','11-338','11-260',NULL),
(120316,'chemistry','In which model, both the atoms and the bonds are shown?','Ball and stick Model','In the ball-and-stick model, both the atoms and the bonds are shown. Balls represent atoms and the stick denotes a bond. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 338; Paragraph No.1)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Structural representation of organic compounds',NULL,'1','mcq','Framework Model','Space-filling Model','Ball and stick Model','None of these','NEW','11-338','11-260',NULL),
(120317,'chemistry','Which model shows only the bonds connecting the atoms of a molecule?','Framework Model','In the framework model only the bonds connecting the atoms of a molecule and not the atoms themselves are shown. This model emphasizes the pattern of bonds of a molecule while ignoring the size of atoms. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 338; Paragraph No.1)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Structural representation of organic compounds',NULL,'2','mcq','Framework Model','Space-filling Model','Ball and stick Model','None of these','NEW','11-338','11-260',NULL),
(120318,'biology','Which is activator of alcohol dehydrogenase','Zn⁺²','The enzyme alcohol dehydrogenase is activated by Zn⁺²','Plant Physiology >> Mineral Nutrition >> Criteria for essentiality',NULL,'1','mcq','Mg⁺²','Zn⁺²','C','H','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(120319,'biology','Which compound of the enzyme nitogenase helps in nitrogen fixation','Mo','Molybdenum(Mo) activates the nitrogenase enzyme which is involved in nitrogen fixation','Plant Physiology >> Mineral Nutrition >> Criteria for essentiality',NULL,'1','mcq','Mn','Mo','B','C','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(120320,'biology','_______ element plays a role in opening and closing of stomata','Potassium','Potassium ion is involved in the opening and closing of stomata','Plant Physiology >> Mineral Nutrition >> Criteria for essentiality',NULL,'1','fillup','Po,ta,ss,ium,phos',NULL,NULL,NULL,'DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(120321,'biology','Essential elements can also alter the ______ potential of the cell','Osmotic','Osmotic potential of the cell is also controlled by essential elements','Plant Physiology >> Mineral Nutrition >> Criteria for essentiality',NULL,'1','fillup','Os,mo,tic,act,ion',NULL,NULL,NULL,'DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(120401,'chemistry','Acyclic compounds are also called ____ compounds','Aliphatic','Acyclic compounds are also called aliphatic compounds. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 339; Paragraph No.2)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Classification of organic compounds',NULL,'1','mcq','Aliphatic','Heterocyclic','Aromatic','Homocyclic','NEW','11-339','11-261',NULL),
(120402,'chemistry','Acyclic compounds contain carbon atoms joined in the form of ____','Chain','Aliphatic compounds consist of straight or branched chain compounds. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 339; Paragraph No.2)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Classification of organic compounds',NULL,'1','mcq','Chain','Ring','Boat','Chair','NEW','11-339','11-261',NULL),
(120403,'chemistry','Alicyclic compounds contain carbon atoms joined in the form of ____','Ring','Alicyclic (aliphatic cyclic) compounds contain carbon atoms joined in the form of a ring. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 339; Paragraph No.3)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Classification of organic compounds',NULL,'1','mcq','Aromatic ring','Ring','Boat','Chair','NEW','11-339','11-261',NULL),
(120404,'chemistry','Which of the following is alicyclic compounds?','Cyclopropane','Alicyclic compounds - an organic compound that is both aliphatic & cyclic. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 339; Paragraph No.3)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Classification of organic compounds',NULL,'3','mcq','Cyclopropane','Benzene','Ethane','Hexane','NEW','11-339','11-261',NULL),
(120405,'chemistry','Which of the following is not an example of Acyclic compound?','Cyclopropane','Acyclic compounds are open chain compounds.. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 339; Paragraph No.3)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Classification of organic compounds',NULL,'2','mcq','Ethane','Acetaldehyde','Cyclopropane','Iso butane','NEW','11-339','11-261',NULL),
(120406,'chemistry','When atoms other than carbon are also present in the ring, the compound is called ____.','Heterocyclic','Sometimes atoms other than carbon are also present in the ring (heterocyclic). Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 339; Paragraph No.4)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Classification of organic compounds',NULL,'1','fillup','Het,ero,cyc,lic,ho,mo',NULL,NULL,NULL,'NEW','11-339','11-261',NULL),
(120407,'chemistry','Which one of the following is heterocyclic ?','Tetrahydrofuran','Sometimes atoms other than carbon are also present in the ring (heterocylic),Tetrahydrofuran is an example. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 339; Paragraph No.4)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Classification of organic compounds',NULL,'2','mcq','Cyclopropane','Tetrahydrofuran','Benzene','Cyclohexane','NEW','11-339','11-261',NULL),
(120408,'chemistry','Which one of the following is an aromatic compoud ?','Benzene','Benzenoid aromatic compounds. Benzene is one of those examples. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 339; Paragraph No.5)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Classification of organic compounds',NULL,'2','mcq','Cyclopropane','Tetrahydrofuran','Benzene','Cyclohexane','NEW','11-339','11-261',NULL),
(120409,'chemistry','Which one of the following is an aromatic compound ?','Aniline','Benzenoid aromatic compounds. Aniline is one of those examples.Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 339; Paragraph No.5)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Classification of organic compounds',NULL,'2','mcq','Cyclopropane','Tetrahydrofuran','Aniline','Acetaldehyde','NEW','11-339','11-261',NULL),
(120410,'chemistry','Which one of the following is an aromatic compound ?','Naphthalene','Benzenoid aromatic compounds. Naphthalene is one of those examples. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 339; Paragraph No.5)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Classification of organic compounds',NULL,'2','mcq','Acetaldehyde','Tetrahydrofuran','Naphthalene','Cyclopropane','NEW','11-339','11-261',NULL),
(120411,'chemistry','Which among the following statements is correct ?\n a. Aromatic compounds include benzene and other related ring compounds.\n b. Aromatic compounds can also be heterocyclic.','Both','Aromatic compounds include benzene and other related ring compounds (benzenoid). Like alicyclic compounds, aromatic compounds may also have hetero atom in the ring. Such compounds are called heterocyclic aromatic compounds. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 339; Paragraph No.5)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Classification of organic compounds',NULL,'2','mcq','only a','only b','Both','none of these','NEW','11-339','11-261',NULL),
(120412,'chemistry','Which one of the following is a non benzenoid ?','Tropone','Among the given examples of Benzenoid, Tropone is absent. As such, Tropone is non benzenoid. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 339; Paragraph No.5)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Classification of organic compounds',NULL,'1','mcq','Aniline','Benzene','Naphthalene','Tropone','NEW','11-339','11-261',NULL),
(120413,'chemistry','Which of the following represents the structure of benzene in the given diagram(1206)','A','Benzene structure has a six-carbon ring which is represented by a hexagon and it includes 3-double bonds. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 339; Paragraph No.5)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Classification of organic compounds',NULL,'3','mcq','A','B','C','D','NEW','11-339','11-261','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/120413q.png'),
(120414,'chemistry','Which of the following represents the structure of aniline in the given diagram(1207)','B','Aniline has 6 carbon (C) atoms, 7 hydrogen (H) atoms, and 1 nitrogen (N) atom in its chemical formula of C6H7N or C6H5NH2. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 339; Paragraph No.5)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Classification of organic compounds',NULL,'3','mcq','A','B','C','D','NEW','11-339','11-261','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/120414q.png'),
(120415,'chemistry','Which of the following represents the structure of naphthalene in the given diagram(1208)','C','Naphthalene\'s structure consists of a fused pair of benzene rings. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 339; Paragraph No.5)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Classification of organic compounds',NULL,'3','mcq','A','B','C','D','NEW','11-339','11-261','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/120415q.png'),
(120416,'chemistry','Which of the following represents the structure of tropone in the given diagram(1208)','D','The Tropone compound consists of a ring of seven carbon atoms with three conjugated alkene groups and a ketone group. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 339; Paragraph No.5)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Classification of organic compounds',NULL,'3','mcq','A','B','C','D','NEW','11-339','11-261','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/120416q.png'),
(120417,'chemistry','What type of compound is in the given diagram(1210)','Alicyclic and hetero','Tetrahydrofuran is an alicyclic and heterocyclic compound. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 339; Paragraph No.4)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Classification of organic compounds',NULL,'3','mcq','Alicyclic and homo','Alicyclic and hetero','Acyclic and hetero','Acyclic and homo','NEW','11-339','11-261','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/120417q.png'),
(120418,'chemistry','What type of compound is in the given diagram(1211)','Benzenoid and aromatic','Aniline is an aromatic compound, also a benzenoid. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 339; Paragraph No.5)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Classification of organic compounds',NULL,'3','mcq','Benzenoid and aromatic','non benzenoid and aromatic','Alicyclic','Acyclic','NEW','11-339','11-261','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/120418q.png'),
(120419,'chemistry','What type of compound is in the given diagram(1212)','Non benzenoid and aromatic','Tropone is non benzenoid and aromatic compound. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 339; Paragraph No.5)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Classification of organic compounds',NULL,'3','mcq','Benzenoid and aromatic','Non benzenoid and aromatic','Alicyclic','Acyclic','NEW','11-339','11-261','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/120419q.png'),
(120420,'chemistry','Which of the following represents the structure of Furan in the given diagram(1213)','A','Furan is a monocyclic heteroarene with a structure consisting of a 5-membered ring containing four carbons and one oxygen. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 340; Paragraph No.1)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Classification of organic compounds',NULL,'3','mcq','A','B','C','none of these','NEW','11-340','11-262','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/120420q.png'),
(120421,'chemistry','Which of the following represents the structure of Thiophene in the given diagram(1214)','B','Thiophene is a heterocyclic compound with the formula C4H4S. Consisting of a planar five-membered ring, it is aromatic as indicated by its extensive substitution reactions. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 340; Paragraph No.1)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Classification of organic compounds',NULL,'3','mcq','A','B','C','none of these','NEW','11-340','11-262','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/120421q.png'),
(120422,'chemistry','Which of the following represents the structure of Pyridine in the given diagram(1215)','C','Pyridine is a six-membered ring structure composed of five carbon atoms and one nitrogen atom. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 340; Paragraph No.1)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Classification of organic compounds',NULL,'3','mcq','A','B','C','none of these','NEW','11-340','11-262','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/120422q.png'),
(120423,'chemistry','Which of the following statements are correct ?\n a. Functional group is responsible for the characteristic chemical properties of the organic compounds.\n b. -OH, -CHO are examples of functional groups.','Both','The functional group is an atom or a group of atoms joined to the carbon chain which is responsible for the characteristic chemical properties of the organic compounds. The examples are hydroxyl group (–OH), aldehyde group (–CHO) and carboxylic acid group (–COOH) etc. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 340; Paragraph No.2)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Classification of organic compounds',NULL,'2','mcq','Only a','Only b','Both','none of these','NEW','11-340','11-262',NULL),
(120424,'chemistry','Which of the following statement/s are correct ?\n \n a. A group or a series of organic compounds each containing a characteristic functional group forms a homologous series and the members of the series are called homologues.\n \n b. The members of a homologous series can be represented by general molecular formula and the successive members differ from each other in molecular formula by a –CH unit.','Only a','A group or a series of organic compounds each containing a characteristic functional group forms a homologous series and the members of the series are called homologues. The members of a homologous series can be represented by general molecular formula and the successive members differ from each other in molecular formula by a –CH₂ unit. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 262; Paragraph No.3)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Classification of organic compounds',NULL,'2','mcq','Only a','Only b','a & b are incorrect','none of these','NEW','11-340','11-262',NULL),
(120425,'chemistry','Which of the following statements are correct ?\n a. Alkenes, alkynes, haloalkanes, alkanols, alkanals, alkanones, alkanoic acids, amines etc are different homologous series.\n b. It is also possible that a compound contains two or more identical or different functional groups. This gives rise to polyfunctional compounds.','Both','There are a number of homologous series of organic compounds. Some of these are alkanes, alkenes, alkynes, haloalkanes, alkanols, alkanals, alkanones, alkanoic acids, amines etc. It is also possible that a compound contains two or more identical or different functional groups. This gives rise to polyfunctional compounds.Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 340; Paragraph No.3)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Classification of organic compounds',NULL,'2','mcq','Only a','Only b','Both','none of these','NEW','11-340','11-262',NULL),
(120426,'chemistry','In homologous series, successive members differ by:','CH₂ unit','The members of a homologous series can be represented by general molecular formula and the successive members differ from each other in molecular formula by a –CH₂ unit. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 340; Paragraph No.3)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Classification of organic compounds',NULL,'1','mcq','C₂H₂ unit','CH unit','CH₂ unit','C₂H unit','NEW','11-340','11-262',NULL),
(120427,'biology','Magnesium is absorbed by the plants in the form of','Divalent Mg²⁺','Plants take up magnesium in the form of divalent Mg²⁺','Plant Physiology >> Mineral Nutrition >> Role of Macro- and Micro-nutrients 1',NULL,'1','mcq','Trivalent Mg²⁺','Divalent Mg²⁺','Mg²⁺','Monovalent Mg²⁺','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(120428,'biology','Which of the following functions does magnesium perform','All of them','Magnesium is involved in activation of respiratory enzymes, photosynthesis, synthesis of DNA and RNA','Plant Physiology >> Mineral Nutrition >> Role of Macro- and Micro-nutrients 1',NULL,'1','mcq','DNA and RNA synthesis','Activation of respiratory enzymes','Photosynthesis','All of them','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(120429,'biology','Magnesium helps to maintain ______ structure','Ribosome','Ribosome structure is maintained by magnesium','Plant Physiology >> Mineral Nutrition >> Role of Macro- and Micro-nutrients 1',NULL,'1','fillup','Rib,oso,me,Mit,och,ond,ria',NULL,NULL,NULL,'DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(120430,'biology','The ring structure of chlorophyll contains which essential element','Mg²⁺','Magnesium is the element found in the ring structure of chlorophyll','Plant Physiology >> Mineral Nutrition >> Role of Macro- and Micro-nutrients 1',NULL,'1','mcq','Ca²⁺','Mg²⁺','Zn²⁺','C','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(120431,'biology','Plants absorb sulphur in the form of','SO₄²⁻','The ionic form of sulphur taken up the plants is SO₄²⁻','Plant Physiology >> Mineral Nutrition >> Role of Macro- and Micro-nutrients 1',NULL,'1','mcq','SO₄²⁻','SO','SO₄','SO₂','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(120501,'chemistry','What is the system by which organic compounds are named called ?','International Union of Pure and Applied Chemistry','Systematic method of naming of organic compounds has been developed and is known as the IUPAC (International Union of Pure and Applied Chemistry) system of nomenclature. In this systematic nomenclature, the names are correlated with the structure such that the reader or listener can deduce the structure from the name. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 340; Paragraph No.4)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Nomenclature of organic compounds',NULL,'1','mcq','International Union of Applied Chemistry','International Union of Chemistry','International Union of Pure and Applied Chemistry','None of these','NEW','11-340','11-262',NULL),
(120502,'chemistry','Which of the following statement is incorrect ?\n a. Citric acid is named so because it is found in citrus fruits.\n b.The acid found in red ant is named formic acid.','Both a and b are correct','None of these is the correct answer beacuse the both given statements are correct. Citric acid is named so because it is found in citrus fruits. The acid found in red ant is named formic acid. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 340; Paragraph No.5)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Nomenclature of organic compounds',NULL,'2','mcq','Only a','Only b','Both a and b are correct','Both a and b are incorrect','NEW','11-340','11-262',NULL),
(120503,'chemistry','Before the _______ of nomenclature, however, organic compounds were assigned names based on their origin or certain properties.','IUPAC system','Before the IUPAC system of nomenclature, however, organic compounds were assigned names based on their origin or certain properties. Some common names are followed even today.Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 340; Paragraph No.5)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Nomenclature of organic compounds',NULL,'2','mcq','IUPAC system','Origin','Suffixes','Prefixes','NEW','11-340','11-262',NULL),
