(120518,'chemistry','Which of the following statements are correct ?\n a. Compounds containing carbon and hydrogen only are called hydrocarbons.\n b. A hydrocarbon is termed saturated if it contains only carbon-carbon single bonds.','Both a and b','Compounds containing carbon and hydrogen only are called hydrocarbons. A hydrocarbon is termed saturated if it contains only carbon-carbon single bonds. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 341; Paragraph No.1)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Nomenclature of organic compounds',NULL,'2','mcq','Only a','Only b','Both a and b','None of these','NEW','11-341','11-263',NULL),
(120519,'chemistry','Which of the following represents the structure of neohexane in the given diagram(1216)','C','It has 6 carbon atoms therefore a hexane and this structure also has neo part in it. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 341; Paragraph No.6)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Nomenclature of organic compounds',NULL,'3','mcq','A','B','C','D','NEW','11-341','11-263','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/120519q.png'),
(120520,'chemistry','What is the IUPAC name for the compound in the given diagram(1217)','3-Ethyl-4-methylhexane','Naming of alkyl groups in done in alphabetical order. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 342; Paragraph No.2)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Nomenclature of organic compounds',NULL,'3','mcq','4-Ethyl-3-methylhexane','3-Ethyl-4-methylhexane','3-Methyl-4-ethylhexane','None of these','NEW','11-342','11-264','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/120520q.png'),
(120521,'chemistry','What is the smallest alkane which can form a ring structure (cycloalkane)?','Cyclopropane','Cyclopropane is the only smallest alkane that can form a successful ring structure with C-C bond on removal of a hydrogen atom. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 343; Paragraph No.2)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Nomenclature of organic compounds',NULL,'2','mcq','Cyclopropane','Cyclobutane','Propane','Methane','NEW','11-342','11-264',NULL),
(120522,'chemistry','What is the substituent in the chain named by replacing the “ane” in the alkanes?','yl','An alkyl group is named by substituting ‘yl’ for ‘ane’ in the corresponding alkane. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 341; Paragraph No.3)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Nomenclature of organic compounds',NULL,'1','mcq','ylic','yl','yne','ene','NEW','11-342','11-264',NULL),
(120523,'chemistry','What is the IUPAC name for the compound in the given diagram(1218)','5-Ethyl-2,3,4-trimethyloctane','Longest carbon chain is selected, lowest numbering possible is given to substituents and alphabetical order is used. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 342; Paragraph No.1 and 2)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Nomenclature of organic compounds',NULL,'3','mcq','2,3,4-Trimethyl-5-ethyloctane','5-Ethyl-2,3,4-trimethyloctane','5-Propyl-2,3,4-trimethyloctane','3-Propyl-4,5,6-trimethyloctane','NEW','11-342','11-264','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/120523q.png'),
(120524,'chemistry','What is the IUPAC name for the compound in the given diagram(1219)','3,4-Dimethylhexane','Longest carbon chain is selected, lowest numbering possible is given to substituents and alphabetical order is used. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 342; Paragraph No.1 and 2)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Nomenclature of organic compounds',NULL,'3','mcq','3,4-Dimethylhexane','2-Ethyl-3-methylpentane','2,3-Dimethylbutane','1,2,Diethylhexane','NEW','11-342','11-264','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/120524q.png'),
(120525,'chemistry','What is the IUPAC name for the compound in the given diagram(1220)','None of these','Longest carbon chain is selected, lowest numbering possible is given to substituents and alphabetical order is used. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 342; Paragraph No.1 and 2)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Nomenclature of organic compounds',NULL,'3','mcq','2,5-Dimethylhexane','3,6-Dimethyl octane','2-Ethyl-5-methylheptane','None of these','NEW','11-342','11-264','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/120525q.png'),
(120526,'chemistry','What is the IUPAC name for the compound in the given diagram(1221)','4-Ethyl, 2,3 - dimethyloctane','Longest carbon chain is selected, lowest numbering possible is given to substituents and alphabetical order is used. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 342; Paragraph No.1,2 and 3)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Nomenclature of organic compounds',NULL,'3','mcq','4-Ethyl, 2,3 - dimethyloctane','3,6-dimethyl octane','2-Ethyl-5-methylheptane','5-Ethyl, 6,7 - dimethyl octane','NEW','11-342','11-264','/ncert/pyq/physics/mcq/120526q.png'),
(120527,'chemistry','What is the IUPAC name for the compound in the given diagram(1222)','3,4,Dimethylhexane','Longest carbon chain is selected, lowest numbering possible is given to substituents and alphabetical order is used. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 342; Paragraph No.1,2 and 3)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Nomenclature of organic compounds',NULL,'3','mcq','2,3,4-Trimethyl-5-ethyloctane','3,4,Dimethylhexane','2,3-Diethylbutane','3,4,Diethylhexane','NEW','11-342','11-264','/ncert/pyq/physics/mcq/120527q.png'),
