(120529,'chemistry','What is the IUPAC name for the compound in the given diagram(1224)','5-Ethyl-5,6,6-trimethyldecane','Longest carbon chain is selected, lowest numbering possible is given to substituents and alphabetical order is used. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 342; Paragraph No.1,2 and 3)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Nomenclature of organic compounds',NULL,'3','mcq','2,3,4-Trimethyl-thyl-5-ethyloctane','4-Ethyl-4,5,5-trimethyldecane','5-Propyl-2,3,4-trimethyloctane','5-Ethyl-5,6,6-trimethyldecane','NEW','11-342','11-264','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/120529q.png'),
(120530,'chemistry','What is the IUPAC name for the compound in the given diagram(1225)','3-ethyl-4,5-dipropyloctane','Longest carbon chain is selected, lowest numbering possible is given to substituents and alphabetical order is used. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 342; Paragraph No.1,2 and 3)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Nomenclature of organic compounds',NULL,'3','mcq','3-ethyl-4,5-dipropyloctane','4,5-Dipropyl-3-ethyloctane','5-Propyl-2,3,4-trimethyloctane','4,5,5-TriMethy-4-Ethyl Decane','NEW','11-342','11-264','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/120530q.png'),
(120601,'chemistry','A ________ is an atom or a group of atoms bonded together in a unique manner which is usually the site of chemical reactivity in an organic molecule.','Functional group','A functional group, as defined earlier, is an atom or a group of atoms bonded together in a unique manner which is usually the site of chemical reactivity in an organic molecule. Compounds having the same functional group undergo similar reactions. For example, CH3OH, CH3CH2OH, and (CH3)2CHOH — all having -OH functional group liberate hydrogen on reaction with sodium metal. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 344; Paragraph No. 1)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Nomenclature of organic compounds with functional group',NULL,'2','mcq','Substituent','Functional group','Replaced group','Specie','NEW','11-344','11-266',NULL),
(120602,'chemistry','What is the correct order of decreasing priority for functional group ?','COOH > SO₃H > COOR > COCl','The order of decreasing priority for some functional groups is: -COOH, –SO3H, -COOR (R=alkyl group), COCl, -CONH2, -CN,-HC=O, >C=O, -OH, -NH2, >C=C<, -C≡C- .Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 344; Paragraph No. 3)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Nomenclature of organic compounds with functional group',NULL,'3','order','1,COOH','2,SO₃H','3,COOR','4,COCl','NEW','11-344','11-266',NULL),
(120603,'chemistry','What is the IUPAC name for the compound in the given diagram(1237)','6-Methyloctan-3-ol','The -OH is on carbon atom 3. In addition, a methyl group is attached at 6th carbon. Hence, the systematic name of this compound is 6-Methyloctan-3-ol. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 344; Problem No. 12.8)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Nomenclature of organic compounds with functional group',NULL,'3','mcq','6-Methyloctan-3-ol','3-Methyloctan-6-ol','6-Ethylheptan-3-ol','2-Ethylheptan-6-ol','NEW','11-344','11-266','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/120603q.png'),
(120604,'chemistry','What is the IUPAC name for the compound in the given diagram(1238)','Hexan-2,4-dione','Presence of two keto groups is indicated by ‘di’, hence suffix becomes ‘dione’. The two keto groups are at carbons 2 and 4. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 344; Problem No. 12.8)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Nomenclature of organic compounds with functional group',NULL,'3','mcq','Hexan-2,4-dione','Hexan-2,4-diol','Hexan-2,4-dioic acid','None of these','NEW','11-344','11-266','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/120604q.png'),
(120605,'chemistry','What is the IUPAC name for the compound in the given diagram(1239)','5-Oxohexanoic acid','The principal functional group is the carboxylic acid group; hence the parent chain will be suffixed with ‘oic’ acid. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 345; Problem No. 12.8)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Nomenclature of organic compounds with functional group',NULL,'3','mcq','2-Oxohexanoic acid','5-Oxohexanoic acid','5-Carboxylichex-2-one','None of these','NEW','11-345','11-267','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/120605q.png'),
(120606,'chemistry','What is the IUPAC name for the compound in the given diagram(1240)','Hexa-1,3-dien-5-yne','The two C=C functional groups are present at carbon atoms 1 and 3, while the C≡C functional group is present at carbon 5. These groups are indicated by suffixes ‘diene’ and ‘yne’ respectively. The longest chain containing the functional groups has 6 carbon atoms; hence the parent hydrocarbon is hexane. The name of compound, therefore, is Hexa-1,3-dien-5-yne.Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 345; Problem No. 12.8)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Nomenclature of organic compounds with functional group',NULL,'3','mcq','Hexa-3,5-dien-1-yne','Hexa-1,3-dien-5-yne','Hexa-1,3,5-triene','None of these','NEW','11-345','11-267','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/120606q.png'),
(120607,'chemistry','What is the IUPAC name for the compound in the given diagram(1241)','But-1-ene','Here -ene is used as suffix. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 345; Table No. 12.4) diagram(e1204)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Nomenclature of organic compounds with functional group',NULL,'3','mcq','But-1-ene','But-3-ene','Butane','None of these','NEW','11-345','11-267','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/120607q.png'),
(120608,'chemistry','What is the IUPAC name for the compound in the given diagram(1242)','1-Bromobutane','Halogens are used as prefix. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 345; Table No. 12.4) diagram(e1204)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Nomenclature of organic compounds with functional group',NULL,'3','mcq','1-Bromobutane','4-Bromobutane','But-4-bromine','None of these','NEW','11-345','11-267','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/120608q.png'),
(120609,'chemistry','What is the IUPAC name for the compound in the given diagram(1243)','Butan-2-ol','ol is used as suffix for OH group and OH group is given the lowest number possible. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 345; Table No. 12.4) diagram(e1204)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Nomenclature of organic compounds with functional group',NULL,'3','mcq','Butan-3-ol','Butan-2-ol','Butan-4-ol','None of these','NEW','11-345','11-267','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/120609q.png'),
