(120703,'chemistry','Which of the following represents the structure of Aniline in the given diagram(1276)','C','Aminobenzene is commonly known as aniline. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 347; Paragraph No. 1)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Nomenclature of Substituted Benzene Compounds',NULL,'3','mcq','A','B','C','D','NEW','11-347','11-269','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/120703q.png'),
(120704,'chemistry','Which of the following represents the structure of Nitrobenzene in the given diagram(1277)','D','Nitrobenzene having a double bond between the nitrogen atom and the carbon atom and a single link between the nitrogen atom and the oxygen atom. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 347; Paragraph No. 1)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Nomenclature of Substituted Benzene Compounds',NULL,'3','mcq','A','B','C','D','NEW','11-347','11-269','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/120704q.png'),
(120705,'chemistry','What is the IUPAC name for the compound in the given diagram(1278)','1-Chloro-2,4-dinitrobenzene','Substituent of the base compound is assigned number1 and then the direction of numbering is chosen such that the next substituent gets the lowest number. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 347; Paragraph No. 4)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Nomenclature of Substituted Benzene Compounds',NULL,'3','mcq','1-Chloro-2,4-dinitrobenzene','1-Chloro-4,6-dinitrobenzene','4-chloro,1,3-dinitrobenzene','none of these','NEW','11-347','11-269','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/120705q.png'),
(120706,'chemistry','What is the IUPAC name for the compound in the given diagram(1279)','2-Chloro-1-methyl-4-nitrobenzene','Substituent of the base compound is assigned number1 and then the direction of numbering is chosen such that the next substituent gets the lowest number. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 347; Paragraph No. 4)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Nomenclature of Substituted Benzene Compounds',NULL,'3','mcq','1-Chloro-2-methyl-5-nitrobenzene','2-Chloro-1-methyl-4-nitrobenzene','3-Chloro-4-methyl-1-nitrobenzene','none of these','NEW','11-347','11-269','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/120706q.png'),
(120707,'chemistry','In the trivial system of nomenclature the terms ortho (o), meta (m) and para (p) are used as ______ to indicate the relative positions.','Prefixes','In the trivial system of nomenclature the terms ortho (o), meta (m) and para (p) are used as prefixes to indicate the relative positions.When a benzene ring is attached to an alkane with a functional group, it is considered as substituent, instead of a parent. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 347; Paragraph No. 2 and 5)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Nomenclature of Substituted Benzene Compounds',NULL,'2','mcq','Suffixes','Parent chain','Prefixes','Carbon root','NEW','11-347','11-269',NULL),
(120708,'chemistry','If benzene ring is disubstituted, the position of substituents is defined by numbering the carbon atoms of the ring such that the substituents are located at the ________ numbers possible.','Lowest','If benzene ring is disubstituted, the position of substituents is defined by numbering the carbon atoms of the ring such that the substituents are located at the lowest numbers possible. Substituent of the base compound is assigned number1 and then the direction of numbering is chosen such that the next substituent gets the lowest number. The substituents appear in the name in alphabetical order.Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 347; Paragraph No. 1 and 4)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Nomenclature of Substituted Benzene Compounds',NULL,'2','mcq','Lowest','Highest','Zero','Uncountable','NEW','11-347','11-269',NULL),
