(231534,'chemistry','On treatment of 100 mL of 0.1 M solution of\n CoCl₃.6H₂O with excess AgNO₃; 1.2 × 10²² ions\n are precipitated. The complex is [JEE (Main)-2017]','[Co(H₂O)₅Cl]Cl₂.H₂O','Millimoles of AgNO₃ = (1.2 × 10²²/6.023 × 10²³) × 1000 = 20\nMillimoles of CoCl₃·6H₂O = 0.1 × 100 = 10\nEach mole of CoCl₃·6H₂O gives two chloride ions.\n→  [Co(H₂O)₅Cl]Cl₂.H₂O','Inorganic chemistry >> Coordination Compounds >> JEE MAINS',NULL,'2','mcq','[Co(H₂O)₆]Cl₃','[Co(H₂O)₅Cl]Cl₂.H₂O','[Co(H₂O)₄Cl₂]Cl.2H₂O','[Co(H₂O)₃Cl₃].3H₂O','NEW','12-246','12-120',NULL),
