(231542,'chemistry','Among the ligands NH₃\n, en, CN⁻ and CO the\n correct order of their increasing field strength, is\n [AIEEE-2011]','NH₃ < en < CN⁻ < CO','NH₃ < en < CN⁻ < CO → Strong field ligands.','Inorganic chemistry >> Coordination Compounds >> JEE MAINS',NULL,'2','mcq','en < CH⁻ < NH₃ < CO','CO < NH₃ < en < CN⁻','NH₃ < en < CN⁻ < CO','CN⁻ < NH₃ < CO < en','NEW','12-248','12-122',NULL),
(231543,'chemistry','A solution containing 2.675 g of CoCl₃\n.6NH₃\n (molar\n mass = 267.5 g /mol) is passed through a cation\n exchanger. The chloride ions obtained in solution\n were treated with excess of AgNO₃\n to give 4.78 g\n of AgCl (molar mass = 143.5 g /mol). The formula\n of the complex is [AIEEE-2010]\n (At. mass of Ag = 108 u)','[Co(NH₃)\n₆]Cl₃','Moles of complex = 2.675/267.5 = 0.01\nMoles of AgCl precipitated = 4 - 78/143.5 = 0.033\nIt means 3Cl⁻ are released by one molecule of\n complex i.e. [Co(NH₃)\n₆]Cl₃','Inorganic chemistry >> Coordination Compounds >> JEE MAINS',NULL,'2','mcq','[CoCl(NH₃)\n₅]Cl₂','[Co(NH₃)\n₆]Cl₃','[CoCl₂(NH₃)\n₄]Cl','[CoCl₃(NH₃)\n₃]','NEW','12-246','12-120',NULL),
