(231629,'chemistry','Assertion : Toxic metal ions are removed by the chelating ligands.\nReason : Chelate complexes tend to be more stable.','Assertion and reason both are true, reason is correct explanation of\n assertion.','When a solution of chelating ligand is added to solution containing toxic metals ligands chelates the metal ions by formation of stable complex.','Inorganic chemistry >> Coordination Compounds >> NCERT Examplar',NULL,'1','mcq','Assertion and reason both are true, reason is correct explanation of\n assertion.','Assertion and reason both are true but reason is not the correct\n explanation of assertion.','Assertion is true, reason is false.','Assertion is false, reason is true.','NEW','12-248','12-122',NULL),
(2000044730,'physics','A  $100\\Omega $ resistance and a capacitor of  $100\\Omega $ reactance are connected in series across a 220$V$ source. When the capacitor is 50% charged, the peak value of the displacement current is','A','$Z = \\sqrt {{R^2} + X_C^2}  = \\sqrt {{{100}^2} + {{100}^2}}  = 100\\sqrt 2 $<br>${i_0} = \\frac{{{V_0}}}{Z} = \\frac{{{V_{rms}}\\sqrt 2 }}{Z} = \\frac{{220\\sqrt 2 }}{{100\\sqrt 2 }} = 2.2A$','Alternating Voltage Across Different Elements','Alternating Current','Medium',NULL,'$2.2\\,A$','$11A$','$4.4A$','$11\\sqrt 2 A$',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(231630,'chemistry','Assertion : [Cr(H₂O)₆]Cl₂ and [Fe(H₂O)₆]Cl₂ are reducing in nature.\nReason : Unpaired electrons are present in their d-orbitals.','Assertion and reason both are true but reason is not the correct\n explanation of assertion.','In the complexes, Co exists as Co²⁺ and Fe as Fe²⁺. Both of the complexes becomes stable by oxidation of metal ion to Co³⁺ and Fe³⁺.','Inorganic chemistry >> Coordination Compounds >> NCERT Examplar',NULL,'1','mcq','Assertion and reason both are true, reason is correct explanation of\n assertion.','Assertion and reason both are true but reason is not the correct\n explanation of assertion.','Assertion is true, reason is false.','Assertion is false, reason is true.','NEW','12-248','12-122',NULL),
(231631,'chemistry','Assertion : Linkage isomerism arises in coordination compounds\ncontaining ambidentate ligand.\nReason : Ambidentate ligand has two different donor atoms.','Assertion and reason both are true, reason is correct explanation of\n assertion.','Linkage isomerism arises due to two different donor atoms in ambidentate ligand.','Inorganic chemistry >> Coordination Compounds >> NCERT Examplar',NULL,'1','mcq','Assertion and reason both are true, reason is correct explanation of\n assertion.','Assertion and reason both are true but reason is not the correct\n explanation of assertion.','Assertion is true, reason is false.','Assertion is false, reason is true.','NEW','12-253','12-125',NULL),
(231632,'chemistry','Assertion : Complexes of MX₆ and MX₅L type (X and L are unidentate)\n do not show geometrical isomerism.\nReason : Geometrical isomerism is not shown by complexes of\n coordination number 6.','Assertion and reason both are true but reason is not the correct\n explanation of assertion.','For complexes of MX₆ and MX₅L  type, different geometric arrangements of the ligands is not possible.\nMA₄B₂, M(AA)₂B₂ and MA₃B₃ type of complexes are the complexes with coordination number 6 which show geometrical isomerism.','Inorganic chemistry >> Coordination Compounds >> NCERT Examplar',NULL,'1','mcq','Assertion and reason both are true, reason is correct explanation of\n assertion.','Assertion and reason both are true but reason is not the correct\n explanation of assertion.','Assertion is true, reason is false.','Assertion is false, reason is true.','NEW','12-252','12-124',NULL),
(231633,'chemistry','Assertion : [Fe(CN)₆]³⁻ ion shows magnetic moment corresponding to two\n unpaired electrons.\nReason : Because it has d²sp³ type hybridisation.','Assertion is false, reason is true.','[Fe(CN)₆]³⁻ ion shows magnetic moment corresponding to one unpaired electron.','Inorganic chemistry >> Coordination Compounds >> NCERT Examplar',NULL,'1','mcq','Assertion and reason both are true, reason is correct explanation of\n assertion.','Assertion and reason both are true but reason is not the correct\n explanation of assertion.','Assertion is true, reason is false.','Assertion is false, reason is true.','NEW','12-256','12-130',NULL),
(231701,'chemistry','A : The complex [Co(NH₃)\n₃Cl₃] gives white ppt. with AgNO₃ solution.\nR : Chlorine always gives white ppt with AgNO₃ solution.','Assertion & reason false are false.','[Co(NH₃)\n₃Cl₃] will not give while ppt. with AgNO₃ solution. Because there is no any Cl⁻ in the primary valency\n i.e. outside the co-ordination sphere.\nChlorine does not give white ppt. with AgNO₃ always.','Inorganic chemistry >> Coordination Compounds >> Assertion & Reason',NULL,'1','mcq','Assertion and reason both are true, reason is correct explanation of\n assertion.','Assertion and reason both are true but reason is not the correct\n explanation of assertion.','Assertion is true, reason is false.','Assertion & reason false are false.','NEW','12-246','12-120',NULL),
(231702,'chemistry','A : Glycinate ion is an unsymmetrical bidentate ligand.\nR : Glycinate ion is a conjugate base of glycine.','Assertion and reason both are true but reason is not the correct\n explanation of assertion.','Refer diagram(ne2333)','Inorganic chemistry >> Coordination Compounds >> Assertion & Reason',NULL,'2','mcq','Assertion and reason both are true, reason is correct explanation of\n assertion.','Assertion and reason both are true but reason is not the correct\n explanation of assertion.','Assertion is true, reason is false.','Assertion & reason false are false.','NEW','12-248','12-122',NULL),
(231703,'chemistry','A : K₄[Fe(CN)₆] is less stable than K₃[Fe(CN)₆].\nR : In K₄[Fe(CN)₆], the EAN of Fe is 36.','Assertion and reason both are true but reason is not the correct\n explanation of assertion.','K₄[Fe(CN)₆] =» Fe²⁺ =» 3d⁶\n=» CFSE = – 2.4 ∆₀\nK₃[Fe(CN)₆] is less stable than K₄[Fe(CN)₆]\nK₄[Fe(CN)₆] =» Fe²⁺ =» 24 electrons\nEAN = 24 + 2×6 = 36 =» But not the correct explanation.','Inorganic chemistry >> Coordination Compounds >> Assertion & Reason',NULL,'1','mcq','Assertion and reason both are true, reason is correct explanation of\n assertion.','Assertion and reason both are true but reason is not the correct\n explanation of assertion.','Assertion is true, reason is false.','Assertion & reason false are false.','NEW','12-246','12-120',NULL),
(231704,'chemistry','A : All square planar complexes can exhibit geometrical isomerism.\nR : In square planar complexes metal assumes sp³ hybridisation.','Assertion & reason false are false.','Square planar complexes of type [MA₄] and [MA₃B] can not exhibit geometrical isomerism.\nIn square planar complexes, metal is dsp² hybridized.','Inorganic chemistry >> Coordination Compounds >> Assertion & Reason',NULL,'2','mcq','Assertion and reason both are true, reason is correct explanation of\n assertion.','Assertion and reason both are true but reason is not the correct\n explanation of assertion.','Assertion is true, reason is false.','Assertion & reason false are false.','NEW','12-252','12-124',NULL),
(231705,'chemistry','A : K₄[Fe(CN₆)] and K₃[Fe(CN₆)] have different magnetic moment.\nR : Magnetic moment is decided by the number of unpaired electron and both have different number of unpaired\n electrons.','Assertion and reason both are true, reason is correct explanation of\n assertion.','K₄[Fe(CN₆)] and K₃[Fe(CN₆)] are coordination compounds of iron (III) ion and the cyanide ion. They differ in the number of potassium ions in their formulae, which affects their overall charge. K₄[Fe(CN₆)] is a neutral compound while K₃[Fe(CN₆)] has a negative charge due to the absence of one potassium ion.\n\nThe magnetic moment of a compound depends on the number of unpaired electrons present in the metal ion. In K₄[Fe(CN₆)], the iron (III) ion has five unpaired electrons, which results in a high magnetic moment. On the other hand, K₃[Fe(CN₆)] has only four unpaired electrons in its iron (III) ion, resulting in a lower magnetic moment.','Inorganic chemistry >> Coordination Compounds >> Assertion & Reason',NULL,'2','mcq','Assertion and reason both are true, reason is correct explanation of\n assertion.','Assertion and reason both are true but reason is not the correct\n explanation of assertion.','Assertion is true, reason is false.','Assertion & reason false are false.','NEW','12-256','12-130',NULL),
(231706,'chemistry','A : The degeneracy of d-orbitals is lost under strong field ligand.\nR : The degeneracy of d-orbitals does not get lost under chelated ligand field.','Assertion is true, reason is false.','In strong field, the d-orbital splits into t2g and eg orbitals. t2g and eg have different energies.\nChelated ligand fields are generally strong\n=» Statement (2) is false.','Inorganic chemistry >> Coordination Compounds >> Assertion & Reason',NULL,'1','mcq','Assertion and reason both are true, reason is correct explanation of\n assertion.','Assertion and reason both are true but reason is not the correct\n explanation of assertion.','Assertion is true, reason is false.','Assertion & reason false are false.','NEW','12-255','12-129',NULL),
(231707,'chemistry','A : Transition metal ion forming octahedral complex having d²sp³ or sp³d² hybridisation.\nR : Under the influence of strong field ligand inner d-orbitals take part in the hybridisation.','Assertion and reason both are true but reason is not the correct\n explanation of assertion.','Octahedral =» d²sp³ or sp³d²\nUnder strong field, electrons of d-orbital get paired and the orbital takes part in hybridization. But it is not the\n correct explanation for hybridization.','Inorganic chemistry >> Coordination Compounds >> Assertion & Reason',NULL,'1','mcq','Assertion and reason both are true, reason is correct explanation of\n assertion.','Assertion and reason both are true but reason is not the correct\n explanation of assertion.','Assertion is true, reason is false.','Assertion & reason false are false.','NEW','12-255','12-129',NULL),
(231708,'chemistry','A : Higher the charge density on the central ion, greater will be stability of the complex.\nR : Hard acid show a greater tendency for forming complexes with hard ligands such as F⁻.','Assertion and reason both are true but reason is not the correct\n explanation of assertion.','Both the statements are facts. But 2nd one is not giving the reason, why charge density on metal ion is\n responsible for stability.','Inorganic chemistry >> Coordination Compounds >> Assertion & Reason',NULL,'1','mcq','Assertion and reason both are true, reason is correct explanation of\n assertion.','Assertion and reason both are true but reason is not the correct\n explanation of assertion.','Assertion is true, reason is false.','Assertion & reason false are false.','NEW','12-255','12-129',NULL),
