(231715,'chemistry','A : [Fe(CN)₆]\n⁴⁻ follows EAN rule.\nR : Number of electrons in Fe in this complex ion is 36.','Assertion and reason both are true, reason is correct explanation of\n assertion.','[Fe(CN)₆]\n⁴⁻ =» Fe²⁺ =» 24 electrons\n6 CN⁻ ligands =» 6 × 2 = 12 electrons\n→ Total 24 + 12 = 36 electrons in the complex ion.','Inorganic chemistry >> Coordination Compounds >> Assertion & Reason',NULL,'1','mcq','Assertion and reason both are true, reason is correct explanation of\n assertion.','Assertion and reason both are true but reason is not the correct\n explanation of assertion.','Assertion is true, reason is false.','Assertion & reason false are false.','NEW','12-255','12-129',NULL),
