(80414,'chemistry','Which metal has highest first ionisation enthalpy?','Zn','Zn has highest first ionisation enthalpy and its  value is 906 kJ/mol.\n(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 220; Table 8.2)','Inorganic chemistry >> The d- and f-Block Elements >> Variation in Atomic and Ionic Sizes of Transition Metals',NULL,'1','mcq','Zn','Cu','Co','Ni','NEW','12-220','12-093',NULL),
