(111202,'chemistry','The valancy of all B-family can be more than 4 except','B','This is due to absence of d-subshell in boron,all other members of family\n can expand their octet by involving d or f subshell\n Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11;Page 320; Paragraph No.2)','Inorganic Chemistry >> The p-Block elements >> Group 13-elements-Important trends and anomalous properties of boron',NULL,'2','mcq','Al','Ga','In','B','NEW','11-320',NULL,NULL),
(111203,'chemistry','The trihalides of all members of B-family are','Covalent','Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11;Page 312; Paragraph No.2)','Inorganic Chemistry >> The p-Block elements >> Group 13-elements-Important trends and anomalous properties of boron',NULL,'1','mcq','Ionic','Metallic','Amphoteric','Covalent','NEW','11-312',NULL,NULL),
