(60852,'biology','Which of the following is not a character of collenchyma tissue ?','They are usually dead and without protoplast','NCERT XII : 85','Structural Organisation In Plants And Animals >> Anatomy of Flowering Plants >> Previous Year Questions 2',NULL,'3','mcq','They provide mechanical support to the growing part of the plant','They occur in layers below epidermis in dicotyledonous plants','They consist of cell with thick corner due to cellulose deposition','They are usually dead and without protoplast','NEW','11-085',NULL,NULL),
