(360326,'biology','Which two climatic factors are considered the most important in regulating decomposition by affecting the activities of soil microbes?','Temperature and soil moisture','Temperature and soil moisture are the most important climatic factors that regulate decomposition through their effects on the activities of soil microbes.','Ecology >> Ecosystem >> Decomposition',NULL,'1','mcq','Wind speed and humidity','Precipitation and sunlight','Temperature and soil moisture','Atmospheric pressure and cloud cover','NEW','12-244','12-208',NULL),
