(360504,'biology','Pyramid of numbers in grassland ecosystem is','Upright','Hence, the pyramid of numbers in the parasitic food chain is inverted. Since, now we know about the various food chains, therefore, the correct answer to this question is that the pyramid of numbers in the grassland ecosystem is always erect.','Ecology >> Ecosystem >> Ecological Pyramids',NULL,'2','mcq','Linear','Upright','Inverted','Negative.','NEW','12-249','12-213',NULL),
(360505,'biology','Top of an ecological pyramid is occupied by','Carnivores','An ecological pyramid also known as trophic pyramid is made up different levels shows the biomass an bio productivity at each increasing levels of the food chain. ... The top of the ecological pyramid is mainy occupied by the carnivores.','Ecology >> Ecosystem >> Ecological Pyramids',NULL,'1','mcq','Producers','Herbivores','Carnivores','None of the above','NEW',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(360506,'biology','In most food chains,','There are fewer individuals at the top predator level than at the second trophic level.','In most food chains,there are fewer individuals at the top predator level than at the second trophic level.','Ecology >> Ecosystem >> Ecological Pyramids',NULL,'3','mcq','There are fewer individuals at the top predator level than at the second trophic level.','There is less usable energy at the herbivore level than at the carnivore level.','There are few individuals at the decomposer level.','There is less usable energy at the auto-trophic level than at the carnivore level.','NEW',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(360507,'biology','Relationships in an ecosystem can be depicted through','All the above.','The relationship in an ecosystem can be depicted in pyramid of energy, pyramid of biomass, pyramid of numbers etc. When production is considered in terms of energy, the pyramid indicates the amount of energy flow at each level. This is called pyramid of energy.','Ecology >> Ecosystem >> Ecological Pyramids',NULL,'2','mcq','Pyramid of energy','Pyramid of biomass','Pyramid of numbers','All the above.','NEW','12-248','12-212',NULL),
(360508,'biology','What are the limitations of ecological pyramids?\nChoose the correct one.','All the above','There are certain limitations of ecological pyramids such as it does not take into account the same species belonging to two or more trophic levels. It assumes a simple food chain, something that almost never exists in nature; it does not accommodate a food web.','Ecology >> Ecosystem >> Ecological Pyramids',NULL,'2','mcq','It does not take into account the same species belonging to two or more trophic levels.','It assumes a simple food chain, something that almost never exists in nature.','It does not accommodate a food web.','All the above','NEW','12-250','12-214',NULL),
(360509,'biology','__________ are not given any place in ecological pyramids even though they play a vital role in the ecosystem','saprophytes','Saprophytes are not given any place in ecological pyramids even though they play a vital role in the ecosystem','Ecology >> Ecosystem >> Ecological Pyramids',NULL,'2','mcq','omnivores','saprophytes','detritus','none of the above','NEW','12-250','12-214',NULL),
(360510,'biology','In a pyramid of numbers, in a grassland ecosystem, the largest population is that of','Producers','In a pyramid of numbers, in a grassland ecosystem, the largest population is that of producers.','Ecology >> Ecosystem >> Ecological Pyramids',NULL,'2','mcq','Producers','Tertiary consumers','Secondary consumers','Primary consumers.','NEW','12-248','12-212',NULL),
(360511,'biology','The pyramid of biomass in sea is generally ______','inverted','The pyramid of biomass in sea is generally inverted because the biomass of fishes far exceeds that of phytoplankton.','Ecology >> Ecosystem >> Ecological Pyramids',NULL,'2','mcq','upright','inverted','linear','negative','NEW','12-249','12-213',NULL),
(360512,'biology','Each bar in the energy pyramid indicates the amount of _________  present at each trophic level in a given time or annually per unit area','energy','Each bar in the energy pyramid indicates the amount of energy present at each trophic level in a given time or annually per unit area','Ecology >> Ecosystem >> Ecological Pyramids',NULL,'2','mcq','biomass','number','energy','both a and c','NEW','12-249','12-213',NULL),
(360513,'biology','Which one of the following types of organisms occupy more than one trophic level in a pond ecosystem?','Fish','A single species may occupy more than one trophic level. In pond, fish occupy more than one trophic level. Small fishes act as secondary consumer. They feed on primary consumer.','Ecology >> Ecosystem >> Ecological Pyramids',NULL,'2','mcq','Fish','Zooplankton','Frog','Phytoplankton.','NEW',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(360514,'biology','A given organism may occupy more than one trophic level simultaneously in the same ecosystem at the same time, The given statement is true or false?','TRUE','A given organism may occupy more than one trophic level simultaneously in the same ecosystem at the same time','Ecology >> Ecosystem >> Ecological Pyramids',NULL,'2','mcq','TRUE','FALSE',NULL,NULL,'NEW','12-249','12-213',NULL),
