(360633,'biology','Choose the correct order of primary succession in water?','small phytoplanktons,rooted-submerged plants, rooted-floating angiosperms,free-floating plants,reed-swamp, marsh-meadow, scrub, trees,forest.','In primary succession in water, the pioneers are the small phytoplanktons,which are replaced with time by rooted-submerged plants, rooted-floating angiosperms followed by free-floating plants, then reed\\u0002swamp, marsh-meadow, scrub and finally the trees. The climax again would be a forest.','Ecology >> Ecosystem >> Ecological Succession',NULL,'1','mcq','small phytoplanktons,rooted-submerged plants, rooted-floating angiosperms,free-floating plants,marsh-meadow,reed-swamp, scrub, trees,forest.','small phytoplanktons,rooted-submerged plants,free-floating plants, rooted-floating angiosperms,reed-swamp, marsh-meadow, scrub, trees,forest.','small phytoplanktons,rooted-submerged plants, rooted-floating angiosperms,free-floating plants,reed-swamp, marsh-meadow, scrub, trees,forest.','rooted-submerged plants, rooted-floating angiosperms,small phytoplanktons,free-floating plants,reed-swamp, marsh-meadow, scrub, trees,forest.','OLD','12-250',NULL,NULL),
