(90313,'biology','When nitrogen base found attached to a sugar, they are called_______','Nucleosides','nitrogen bases –adenine, guanine, cytosine, uracil, and thymine. When found attached to a sugar, they are called nucleosides..(Reference  :NCERT Biology Class 11; page no:144, paragraph no:3)','Cell Structure And Functions >> Biomolecules >> Lipids and Nitrogen Bases',NULL,'2','fillup','Nu,cleo,sid,es',NULL,NULL,NULL,'NEW','11-144','11-106',NULL),
(90314,'biology','Nitrogen base and If a phosphate group is also found esterified to the sugar they are called______','Nucleotides','If a phosphate group is also found esterified to the sugar they are called nucleotides.(Reference  :NCERT Biology Class 11; page no:144, paragraph no:3)','Cell Structure And Functions >> Biomolecules >> Lipids and Nitrogen Bases',NULL,'2','fillup','Nu,cleo,tid,es',NULL,NULL,NULL,'NEW','11-144','11-106',NULL),
(90315,'biology','Nucleosides are: \n\ni. Thymidine, uridine and cytidine   \n\nii.Uridylic acid        \n\niii. Adenosine, guanosine','i and iii only','Adenosine, guanosine, thymidine, uridine and cytidine are nucleosides..(Reference  :NCERT Biology Class 11; page no:144, paragraph no:3)','Cell Structure And Functions >> Biomolecules >> Lipids and Nitrogen Bases',NULL,'2','mcq','i and ii only','i and iii only','ii only','ii and iii only','NEW','11-144','11-106',NULL),
(90316,'biology','Nucleotides are: \n\ni. Alanine  \n\nii.  Adenylic acid, thymidylic acid, guanylic acid   \n\niii. Cytidylic acid','ii and iii only','Adenylic acid, thymidylic acid, guanylic acid, uridylic acid and cytidylic acid are nucleotides. .(Reference  :NCERT Biology Class 11; page no:144, paragraph no:3)','Cell Structure And Functions >> Biomolecules >> Lipids and Nitrogen Bases',NULL,'3','mcq','i only','ii and iii only','ii only','i and iii only','NEW','11-144','11-106',NULL),
