(90401,'chemistry','Which one is not the isotope of hydrogen.','¹₂H','Hydrogen has three isotopes: protium, ¹₁H ;deuterium,²₁H or D and tritium,³₁H or T.\nReference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11;Page 285; paragraph no.4)','Inorganic Chemistry >> Hydrogen >> Isotopes of Hydrogen',NULL,'2','mcq','¹₁H','²₁H','¹₂H','³₁H','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(90402,'chemistry','The three isotopes of hydrogen differs in number of','Neutrons','Isotopes have same atomic no.but different atomic mass,mass no. is sum of protons and neutrons, protium has one proton and no neutron, deuterium has one proton and one neutron,Tritium has one proton and 2 neutrons. \nReference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11;Page 285; paragraph no.4)','Inorganic Chemistry >> Hydrogen >> Isotopes of Hydrogen',NULL,'2','mcq','Protons','Electrons','Neutrons','Neutrinos','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(90403,'chemistry','An american scientist ____________got nobel prize on separating deuterium.','Harold.C Urey','In the year 1934, an American scientist, Harold C. Urey, got Nobel Prize for separating hydrogen isotope of mass number 2 by physical methods.\nReference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11;Page 285; paragraph no.4)','Inorganic Chemistry >> Hydrogen >> Isotopes of Hydrogen',NULL,'1','fillup','Ha,rol,d.C, Ur,ey,be',NULL,NULL,NULL,'DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
