(90406,'chemistry','The concentration of Tritium is ________ of protium.','³₁H atom/ 10¹⁸ atoms of protium','The tritium concentration is about one atom per 10¹⁸ atoms of protium. \nReference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11;Page 285; paragraph no.5)','Inorganic Chemistry >> Hydrogen >> Isotopes of Hydrogen',NULL,'1','mcq','³₁H atom/ 10¹⁸ atoms of protium','³₁H atom/ 10¹⁸ atoms of Deutriam','³₁H atom/ 10¹⁶ atoms of protium','³₁H atom/  10¹⁷ atoms of  Protium','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(90407,'chemistry','Tritium radiates','𝞫-Particle','Tritium is radioactive and emits low energy β- particles (t1⁄2, 12.33 years).\nReference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11;Page 285; paragraph no.5)','Inorganic Chemistry >> Hydrogen >> Isotopes of Hydrogen',NULL,'1','mcq','𝞫-Particle','𝛼-Particle','ɣ-Particle','𝛅-Particle','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(90408,'chemistry','Match the following. diagram(n0902)','(i) - (d) ; (ii) - (c) ; (iii) - (b) ; (iv) - (a)','Since the isotopes have the same electronic configuration, they have almost the same chemical properties. The only difference is in their rates of reactions, mainly due to their different enthalpy of bond dissociation.\nReference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11;Page 286; paragraph no.1)\n\nTritium is radioactive and emits low energy β- particles (t1⁄2, 12.33 years)\nReference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11;Page 285; paragraph no.5)','Inorganic Chemistry >> Hydrogen >> Isotopes of Hydrogen',NULL,'3','mcq','(i) - (a) ; (ii) - (c) ; (iii) - (d) ; (iv) - (b)','(i) - (a) ; (ii) - (b) ; (iii) - (c) ; (iv) - (d)','(i) - (d) ; (ii) - (c) ; (iii) - (b) ; (iv) - (a)','(i) - (b) ; (ii) - (c) ; (iii) - (a) ; (iv) - (d)','DELETED',NULL,NULL,'/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/90408q.png'),
