(90631,'biology','Which of the following best describes the 3D view of Protein? i. Primary Structure ii. Secondary Structure iii. Tertiary Structure iv. Quaternary Structure','iii only','In addition, the long protein chain is also folded upon itself like a hollow woolen ball, giving rise to the tertiary structure (Figure 9.4 c). This gives us a 3-dimensional view of a protein.','Cell Structure And Functions >> Biomolecules >> Proteins and  Structure of Proteins',NULL,'2','mcq','iii only','i and iii ony','iii and iv only','ii and iii only','NEW','11-150','11-112',NULL),
