(90634,'biology','Which one of the following pattern of structure of protein describes the geometry of protein due to presence of more than one polypeptie chains?','Quaternary Structure only','Some proteins are an assembly of more than one polypeptide or subunits. The manner in which these individual folded polypeptides or subunitsare arranged with respect to each other (e.g. linear string of spheres, spheres arranged one upon each other in the form of a cube or plate etc.) is the architecture of a protein otherwise called the quaternary structure of a protein Ref NCERT11 Class Page 150','Cell Structure And Functions >> Biomolecules >> Proteins and  Structure of Proteins',NULL,'2','mcq','Primary and secondary structure','Tertiary Structure only','Secondary and tertiary structure only','Quaternary Structure only','NEW','11-150','11-112',NULL),
