(310303,'chemistry','Organic compound is fused with metallic sodium for testing nitrogen, sulphur and halogens because','To convert covalent compound in to ionic \n compound.','When organic compound is \n fused with sodium metal to \n convert these elements from \n covalent form in to ionic form','PRINCIPLES RELATED TO PRACTICAL \n CHEMISTRY>>QUANTITATIVE ANALYSIS>>CARIUS METHOD',NULL,'2','MCQ','To make the solution alkaline.','To convert in to elemental state of \n nitrogen, sulphur and halogens.','To convert covalent\n compound in to ionic\n compound.','To decrease fusion\n temperature.','NEW',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(310401,'chemistry','Estimation of oxygen in an organic compound can be made by.','Aluise method','Aluise′s method for the estimation of oxygen in an organic \n compound. This is known as Aluise\'s method. A known amount \n of organic compound is subjected to pyrolysis in a stream of \n nitrogen. The oxygen combines with carbon forming carbon\n monoxide.','PRINCIPLES RELATED TO PRACTICAL \n CHEMISTRY>>QUANTITATIVE ANALYSIS>>ESTIMATION OF \n CARBON AND HYDROGEN',NULL,'1','MCQ','Liebig’s Combustion Method','Aluise method','Kjeldahl Method','Carius Method','NEW',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(310402,'biology','When breeding is between animals of the same breed it is called_______','Inbreeding','When breeding is between animals of the same breed it is called inbreeding, while crosses between different breeds are called outbreeding.','Biology in Human Welfare >> Strategies for enhancement in food production >> Animal breeding',NULL,'1','mcq','Inbreeding','Outbreeding','Crossbreeding','Downbreeding','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(310403,'chemistry','The presence of carbon in an organic compound is detected by heating it with','CuO to convert it into carbon\ndioxide which turns lime \nwater milky','The given organic compound is mixed with dry copper oxide (CuO) and heated in a hard glass tube. The products of the reaction are passed over (white) anyhydrous copper sulphate and then bubbled through lime water. If copper sulphate turns blue due to the formation of CuSO4.5H2O (by waer vapor) then the compound contains hydrogen. If lime water is turned milky by CO2, then the compound contains carbon.','PRINCIPLES RELATED TO PRACTICAL \nCHEMISTRY>>QUANTITATIVE ANALYSIS>>ESTIMATION OF \nCARBON AND HYDROGEN',NULL,'1','MCQ','Sodium metal to convert it\ninto NaCN','CaO to convert it into CO which burns \nwith a blue flame','CuO to convert it into carbon\ndioxide which turns lime \nwater milky','Cu wire to give bluish green flame','NEW',NULL,NULL,NULL),
