(51058,'chemistry','What is the V of 2.8g CO at 27oC with 0.821 atm pressure?','30L','PV = nRT\n \n ​PV = (m/M) RT\n \n ​V = ​ (mM) (RT/P)\n \n Given values are:\n \n w = 2.8 g\n \n M = Molar mass of CO = 28 g mol-1\n \n T = 27°C = (273 + 27) = 300 K\n \n P = 0.821 atm\n \n R = 0.0821 L atm mol⁻¹ K⁻¹\n \n Putting the values in the formula we get :\n \n V = (2.8 g /28 g mol⁻¹) × (0.0821 L atm mol⁻¹K⁻¹) × (300 K)/(0.821 atm)\n \n = 3 L\n \n (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Exercises)','Physical chemistry >> States of matter >> Most Challenging Questions',NULL,'3','mcq','30L','3L','0.5L','1.5L','NEW',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(310406,'biology','In inbreeding, ___________________of the same breed are identified and mated in pairs.','Superior males and Superior females','In inbreeding, superior males and superior females of the same breed are identified and mated in pairs. The progeny obtained from such matings are evaluated and superior males and females among them are identified for further mating.','Biology in Human Welfare >> Strategies for enhancement in food production >> Animal breeding',NULL,'2','mcq','Superior males and Inferior females','Inferior males and Superior females','Inferior males and Inferior females','Superior males and Superior females','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
