(290328,'chemistry','Which condition is not favourable for low density polythene formation ?','6-7 atm pressure','Low density polythene: \n \n It is obtained by the polymerisation of ethene under high pressure of 1000 to 2000 atmospheres at a temperature of 350 K to 570 K in the presence of traces of dioxygen or a peroxide initiator (catalyst). \n \n The low density polythene (LDP) is obtained through the free radical addition and H-atom abstraction. It has highly branched structure.\n \n Reference : (NCERT Class-12 Page- 435 Paragraph-4)','Organic chemistry >> Polymers >> Types of polymerisation reactions',NULL,'1','mcq','High pressure','350K-570K','trace of dioxygen','6-7 atm pressure','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
