(290410,'chemistry','Which of them is true for Buna-S','It is copolymer formed by addition reaction.','The polymers made by addition polymerisation from two different monomers are termed as copolymers. \n \n Buna-S, which is formed by polymerisation of buta–1, 3–diene and styrene is an example of copolymer formed by addition polymerisation.\n \n Reference : (NCERT Class-12 Page- 440 Paragraph-1)','Organic chemistry >> Polymers >> Types of polymerisation reactions-2',NULL,'1','mcq','It is homopolymer formed by condensation reaction.','It is copolymer formed by condensation reaction.','It is copolymer formed by addition reaction.','It is homopolymer formed by addition reaction.','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
