(290412,'chemistry','Which of the following statement is not true for LDP?','Polymerisation occurs in presence of trace of nitrogen','Low density polythene: It is obtained by the polymerisation of ethene under high pressure of 1000 to 2000 atmospheres at a temperature of 350 K to 570 K in the presence of traces of dioxygen or a peroxide initiator (catalyst). \n \n The low density polythene (LDP) is obtained through the free radical addition and H-atom abstraction. \n \n It has highly branched structure.\n \n Reference : (NCERT Class-12 Page- 435 Paragraph-4)','Organic chemistry >> Polymers >> Types of polymerisation reactions-2',NULL,'2','mcq','Obtained by polymerisation of ethene','Polymerisation occurs in presence of trace of nitrogen','Pressure used in 1000 to 2000 atm','Temperature used is 350K to 570K','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(290413,'chemistry','Catalyst used in polymerisation reaction of LDP ?','either traces of dioxygen or a peroxide initiator','Low density polythene in the presence of traces of dioxygen or a peroxide initiator (catalyst). \n \n The low density polythene (LDP) is obtained through the free radical addition and H-atom abstraction. \n \n It has highly branched structure.\n \n Reference : (NCERT Class-12 Page- 435 Paragraph-4)','Organic chemistry >> Polymers >> Types of polymerisation reactions-2',NULL,'1','mcq','only traces of dioxygen','either traces of dioxygen or a peroxide initiator','only traces of dioxygen','either traces of ozone or a peroxide initiator','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(290414,'chemistry','Choose the correct statement: \n \n a) LDP is obtained through the free radical addition \n \n b)LDP is obtained through H-atom abstraction\n \n c) LDP is an unbranched structure','a,b','The low density polythene (LDP) is obtained through the free radical addition and H-atom abstraction.\n \n It has highly branched structure.\n \n Reference : (NCERT Class-12 Page- 435 Paragraph-4)','Organic chemistry >> Polymers >> Types of polymerisation reactions-2',NULL,'3','mcq','a','a,b','a,b,c','b,c','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(290415,'chemistry','Choose the correct statement:\n \n a)Low density polythene is chemically reactive \n \n b)Low density polythene is tough','only b','Low density polythene is chemically inert and tough but flexible and a poor conductor of electricity.\n \n Reference : (NCERT Class-12 Page- 435 Paragraph-5)','Organic chemistry >> Polymers >> Types of polymerisation reactions-2',NULL,'2','mcq','only a','only b','both a and b','none of these','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(290416,'chemistry','A) LDP is used to produce buckets,dustbins, bottles, pipes. \n \n B) HDP is used to produce squeeze bottles, toys and flexible pipes','Both A and B are incorrect','LDP is used in the insulation of electricity carrying wires and manufacture of squeeze bottles, toys and flexible pipes.\n \n Reference : (NCERT Class-12 Page- 436 Paragraph-1)','Organic chemistry >> Polymers >> Types of polymerisation reactions-2',NULL,'2','mcq','only A is correct','only B is correct','Both A and B are incorrect','Both A and B are correct','DELETED',NULL,NULL,'/ncert/pyq/biology/mcq/290416q.png'),
(290501,'chemistry','Polymer properties are closely related to all the following, except','mode of polymerisation','Polymer properties are closely related to their molecular mass, size and structure.\n \n Reference : (NCERT Class-12 Page- 442 Paragraph-1)','Organic chemistry >> Polymers >> Molecular Mass of Polymers',NULL,'1','mcq','molecular mass','size','structure','mode of polymerisation','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(290502,'chemistry','Choose the correct option for the following assertion and reason.\n \n Assertion (A) Molecular mass of polymer is expressed as an average.\n \n Reason (R) Polymer sample contains chains of varying lengths','Both A and R are correct; R is the correct explanation of A','The polymer sample contains chains of varying lengths and hence its molecular mass is always expressed as an average.\n \n Reference : (NCERT Class-12 Page- 442 Paragraph-1)','Organic chemistry >> Polymers >> Molecular Mass of Polymers',NULL,'3','mcq','Both A and R are correct; R is the correct explanation of A','Both A and R are correct; R is not the correct explanation of A.','A is correct; R is incorrect.','A is incorrect; R is correct','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(290503,'chemistry','The growth of the polymer chain during their synthesis depends on','availability of monomers','The growth of the polymer chain during their synthesis is dependent upon the availability of the monomers in the reaction mixture.\n \n Reference : (NCERT Class-12 Page- 442 Paragraph-1)','Organic chemistry >> Polymers >> Molecular Mass of Polymers',NULL,'2','mcq','availability of monomers','types of monomer','temperature of reaction mixture','None of the above','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(290504,'biology','_________that divide fast have the ability to multiply and become millions of individuals within hours.','Microbes','Microbes that divide fast have the ability to multiply and become millions of individuals within hours.','Genetics and Evolution >> Evolution >> Biological Evolution','Evolution','2','mcq','Buds','Microbes','Birds','Animals','NEW','12-134','12-117',NULL),
(290505,'biology','A change in the medium composition would bring out only that part of the population that can survive under ______ conditions.','New','A change in the medium composition would bring out only that part of the population (say B) that can survive under the new conditions.','Genetics and Evolution >> Evolution >> Biological Evolution','Evolution','1','mcq','New','Old','Hot','Temperate','NEW','12-134','12-117',NULL),
(290506,'biology','A new species can occur within ________.','Days','In due course of time this variant population outgrows the others and appears as new species. This would happen within days.','Genetics and Evolution >> Evolution >> Biological Evolution','Evolution','1','mcq','Hours','Days','Weeks','Months','NEW','12-134','12-117',NULL),
(290507,'biology','The evolution of fish or fowl can occurs in  ______.','Million years','The time required for evolution to happen in a fish or fowl would take millions of years as the life spans of these animals are in years. unlike bacteria with a short life span, it can occur in hours.','Genetics and Evolution >> Evolution >> Biological Evolution','Evolution','2','mcq','A year','Ten years','Hundred years','Million years','NEW','12-134','12-117',NULL),
(290508,'biology','Nature selects for ________.','Fitness','Nature selects for fitness. It refers to the theory of evolution proposed by Darwin.','Genetics and Evolution >> Evolution >> Biological Evolution','Evolution','3','mcq','Adaptability','Convergent Evolution','Fitness','Convergent Progression','NEW','12-134','12-117',NULL),
(290509,'biology','Fitness is based on characteristics which are __________.','Inherited','One must remember that so-called fitness is based on characteristics that are inherited.','Genetics and Evolution >> Evolution >> Biological Evolution','Evolution','1','mcq','Inherited','Progressive','Variable','Genomic','NEW','12-134','12-117',NULL),
(290510,'biology','Selection and evolution involve ________.','Genes','Hence, there must be a genetic basis for getting selected and evolving.','Genetics and Evolution >> Evolution >> Biological Evolution','Evolution','2','mcq','Genes','Cell Cytoskeleton','Cell membrane','Lysosomes','NEW','12-134','12-117',NULL),
