(290803,'chemistry','Regarding cross-linked or network polymers, which of the following statements is incorrect?','They contain strong covalent bonds in their polymer chains.','Cross-linked or network polymers are usually formed from bi-functional and tri-functional monomers and contains strong covalent bonds between various linear polymer chains like melamine, bakelite, etc.\n \n Reference : (NCERT Class-12 Page- 437 Paragraph-1)','Organic chemistry >> Polymers >> Previous year questions',NULL,'2','mcq','They contain covalent bonds between various linear polymer chains.','They are formed from bi- and tri-functional monomers.','Examples are bakelite and melamine.','They contain strong covalent bonds in their polymer chains.','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(290804,'chemistry','Which one of the following structures represents nylon 6, 6 polymer,refer diagram(n2934)','d','Nylon 6,6: \n \n It is prepared by the condensation polymerisation of hexamethylenediamine with adipic acid under high pressure and at high temperature.\n \n Reference : (NCERT Class-12 Page- 437 Paragraph-5)','Organic chemistry >> Polymers >> Previous year questions',NULL,'3','mcq','a','b','c','d','DELETED',NULL,NULL,'/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/290804q.png'),
(290805,'chemistry','Natural rubber has','all cis-configuration','cis-1, 4-polyisoprene is a natural rubber.\n \n Reference : (NCERT Class-12 Page- 440 Paragraph-4)','Organic chemistry >> Polymers >> Previous year questions',NULL,'2','mcq','alternate cis- and trans-configuration','random cis- and trans-configuration','all cis-configuration','all trans-configuration.','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(290806,'chemistry','Caprolactam is used in the manufacture of','nylon 6','Nylon 6: \n \n It is obtained by heating caprolactum with water at a high temperature.\n \n Reference : (NCERT Class-12 Page- 437 Paragraph-8)','Organic chemistry >> Polymers >> Previous year questions',NULL,'1','mcq','terylene','teflon','nylon 6, 6','nylon 6','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(290807,'chemistry','Which one of the following is an example of thermosetting polymer, refer diagram(n2935)','d','Novolac which further undergoes cross linking to produce bakelite (thermosetting polymer).\n \n Reference : (NCERT Class-12 Page- 438 Paragraph-3)','Organic chemistry >> Polymers >> Previous year questions',NULL,'3','mcq','a','b','c','d','DELETED',NULL,NULL,'/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/290807q.png'),
(290808,'chemistry','Which of the following organic compounds polymerizes to form the polyester dacron?','Terephthalic acid and ethylene glycol','Dacron is manufactured by heating a mixture of ethylene glycol and terephthalic acid at 420 to 460 K in the presence of zinc acetate-antimony trioxide catalyst.\n \n Reference : (NCERT Class-12 Page- 438 Paragraph-2)','Organic chemistry >> Polymers >> Previous year questions',NULL,'1','mcq','Propylene and para-hydroxy phenol','Benzoic acid and ethanol','Terephthalic acid and ethylene glycol','para-hydroxy phenol and Benzoic acid','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(290809,'chemistry','Nylon is an example of','polyamide','The polymers possessing amide linkages are important examples of synthetic fibres and are termed as nylons.\n \n Reference : (NCERT Class-12 Page- 437 Paragraph-4)','Organic chemistry >> Polymers >> Previous year questions',NULL,'1','mcq','polyamide','polyester','polythene','polysaccharide.','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(290810,'chemistry','Which is the monomer of neoprene in the following, refer diagram(n2936)','a','Neoprene or polychloroprene is formed by the free radical polymerisation of chloroprene.\n \n Reference : (NCERT Class-12 Page- 441 Paragraph-4)','Organic chemistry >> Polymers >> Previous year questions',NULL,'3','mcq','a','b','c','d','DELETED',NULL,NULL,'/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/290810q.png'),
