(290901,'chemistry','Select the correct option(s) from the following statements which explain about "Vulcanisation of Rubber", Choose the most appropriate answer from the options given below:\n\na. An appropriate additive is added with raw rubber and sulphur\n\nb. The temperature range is between 373K to 393K\n\nc. Sulphur forms multiple linear linkages at the reactive sites of double bonds and rubber is stiffened\n\nd. 5% of Sulphur is used in manufacture of tyre rubber','Only b and c','Vulcanisation of rubber: This process consists of heating a mixture of raw rubber with sulphur and an appropriate additive at a temperature range between 373K to 415K. During the process, sulphur forms cross links at the reactive sites of double bonds and rubber gets stiffened.\nIn the manufacture of tyre rubber, 5% of sulphur is used as a crosslinking agent.\n\nReference : (NCERT Class-12 Page- 441 Paragraph-1) diagram(ne2905)','Organic chemistry >> Polymers >> Exampler based Advanced Questions',NULL,'3','mcq','Only b and c','Only a and d','Only a,b and d','Only b,c and d','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(290902,'chemistry','Select the incorrect option(s) from the following statements which explain about "Biodegradable Polymer",Choose the most appropriate answer from the options given below:\n\na. Biodegradable Polymer contains structure similar to biopolymers\n\nb. PHBV is used in orthopaedic devices as well as sustained release tablets.\n\nc. Nylon 2-nylon 6 is a polyamide copolymer of glycine and caproic acid.\n\nd. PHBV undergoes bacterial degradation in the environment.','Only a,b and c','Poly β-hydroxybutyrate – co-β-hydroxy valerate (PHBV) It is obtained by the copolymerisation of 3-hydroxybutanoic acid and 3 - hydroxypentanoic acid. PHBV is used in speciality packaging, orthopaedic devices and in controlled release of drugs. PHBV undergoes bacterial degradation in the environment.Reference : (NCERT Class-12 Page- 442 Paragraph-4)\n\nNylon-2-nylon 6 is an alternating polyamide copolymer of glycine (H₂N–CH₂ – COOH) and amino caproic acid [H₂N (CH₂ )₅COOH] and is biodegradable.Reference : (NCERT Class-12 Page- 442 Paragraph-5)','Organic chemistry >> Polymers >> Exampler based Advanced Questions',NULL,'3','mcq','Only b and c','Only a and d','Only a,b and c','Only b,c and d','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(290903,'chemistry','Assertion (A):  Most of the synthetic polymers are not biodegradable.\n\nReason (R): Polymerisation process induces toxic character in organic molecules.\n\nIn the light of the above statements, choose the most appropriate answer from the options given\nbelow:','(A) is correct  (R) is incorrect.','A large number of polymers are quite resistant to the environmental degradation processes and are thus responsible for the accumulation of polymeric solid waste materials. \n\nThese solid wastes cause acute environmental problems and remain undegraded for quite a long time. \n\nReference : (NCERT Class-12 Page- 442 Paragraph-2)\n\nThe process of polymerisation does not induces any toxic character in organic molecules.\n\nAssertion is correct statement but reason is not a correct statement.','Organic chemistry >> Polymers >> Exampler based Advanced Questions',NULL,'3','mcq','Both (A) and (R) are correct and (R) is the correct explanation of (A).','Both (A) and (R) are correct but (R) is incorrect explanation of (A).','(A) is correct  (R) is incorrect.','(A) is incorrect but (R) is correct.','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(290904,'chemistry','Assertion (A):   Olefinic monomers undergo addition polymerization.\n\nReason (R): Polymerisation of vinyl chloride is initiated by peroxides/ persulphates.\n\nIn the light of the above statements, choose the most appropriate answer from the options given\nbelow:','Both (A) and (R) are correct but (R) is incorrect explanation of (A).','A variety of alkenes or dienes and their derivatives are polymerised in the presence of a free radical generating initiator (catalyst) like benzoyl peroxide, acetyl peroxide, tert-butyl peroxide, etc.\n\nThe polymerisation of olefin like ethene to polythene consists of heating or exposing to light a mixture of ethene with a small amount of benzoyl peroxide initiator.\n\nPolymerisation of vinyl chloride leads to production of PVC(Polyvinyl Chloride)\n\nOlefins are unsaturated compounds like ethene,butadiene etc\n\nReference : (NCERT Class-12 Page- 434 Paragraph-5, Page- 443 Paragraph-Table) diagram(ne2901)','Organic chemistry >> Polymers >> Exampler based Advanced Questions',NULL,'2','mcq','Both (A) and (R) are correct and (R) is the correct explanation of (A).','Both (A) and (R) are correct but (R) is incorrect explanation of (A).','(A) is correct  (R) is incorrect.','(A) is incorrect but (R) is  correct.','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(290905,'chemistry','Assertion (A): Polyamides are best used as fibres because of high tensile strength.\n\nReason (R): Strong intermolecular forces (like hydrogen bonding within polyamides) lead to close packing of chains and increase the crystalline character, provide high tensile strength to polymers.\n\nIn the light of the above statements, choose the most appropriate answer from the options given\nbelow:','Both (A) and (R) are correct and (R) is the correct explanation of (A).','Nylon 6,6 is fibre forming solid. \n\nIt possess high tensile strength due to strong intermolecular forces like H bonding.\n\nThese strong forces also lead to close packing of chains and thus impart crystalline nature.\n\nReference : (NCERT Class-12 Page- 437 Paragraph-6)','Organic chemistry >> Polymers >> Exampler based Advanced Questions',NULL,'2','mcq','Both (A) and (R) are correct and (R) is the correct explanation of (A).','Both (A) and (R) are correct but (R) is incorrect explanation of (A).','(A) is correct  (R) is incorrect.','(A) is incorrect but (R) is  correct.','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(290906,'chemistry','Assertion (A): For making rubber synthetically, isoprene molecules are polymerised.\n\nReason (R): Neoprene (a polymer of chloroprene) is a synthetic rubber.\n\nIn the light of the above statements, choose the most appropriate answer from the options given\nbelow:','(A) is incorrect but (R) is correct.','Natural rubber may be considered as a linear polymer of isoprene (2-methyl-1, 3-butadiene) and is also called as cis - 1, 4 - polyisoprene.\n\nReference : (NCERT Class-12 Page- 440 Paragraph-4) diagram(ne2921)','Organic chemistry >> Polymers >> Exampler based Advanced Questions',NULL,'3','mcq','Both (A) and (R) are correct and (R) is the correct explanation of (A).','Both (A) and (R) are correct but (R) is incorrect explanation of (A).','(A) is correct  (R) is incorrect.','(A) is incorrect but (R) is correct.','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(290907,'chemistry','Assertion (A): Network polymers are thermosetting.\n\nReason (R): Network polymers have high molecular mass.\n\nIn the light of the above statements, choose the most appropriate answer from the options given\nbelow:','Both (A) and (R) are correct but (R) is the incorrect explanation of (A).','Novolac on heating with formaldehyde undergoes cross linking to form an infusible solid mass called bakelite.\n\nBakelite is thermosetting polymer because it cannot be reused or remoulded.\n\nIt undergoes extensive cross linking in moulds and again become infusible thats ehy it becomes irreversible to mould and is thermosetting type\n\nReference : (NCERT Class-12 Page- 438 Paragraph-3)','Organic chemistry >> Polymers >> Exampler based Advanced Questions',NULL,'3','mcq','Both (A) and (R) are correct and (R) is the correct explanation of (A).','Both (A) and (R) are correct but (R) is the incorrect explanation of (A).','(A) is correct  (R) is incorrect.','(A) is incorrect but (R) is  correct.','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(290908,'chemistry','Assertion (A):  Polytetrafluoroethene is used in making non-stick cookware.\n\nReason (R): Fluorine has highest electronegativity.\n\nIn the light of the above statements, choose the most appropriate answer from the options given\nbelow:','Both (A) and (R) are correct but (R) is incorrect explanation of (A).','Polytetrafluoroethene (Teflon) \n\nTeflon is manufactured by heating tetrafluoroethene with a free radical or persulphate catalyst at high pressures\n\nIt is used in making oil seals and gaskets and also used for non-stick surface coated utensils.\n\nReference : (NCERT Class-12 Page- 436 Paragraph-3)','Organic chemistry >> Polymers >> Exampler based Advanced Questions',NULL,'2','mcq','Both (A) and (R) are correct and (R) is the correct explanation of (A).','Both (A) and (R) are correct but (R) is incorrect explanation of (A).','(A) is correct  (R) is incorrect.','(A) is incorrect but (R) is  correct.','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(290909,'chemistry','Assertion (A):  Polytetrafluoroethene is used in making non-stick cookware.\n\nReason (R): Fluorine has highest electronegativity.\n\nIn the light of the above statements, choose the most appropriate answer from the options given\nbelow:','Both (A) and (R) are correct but (R) is incorrect explanation of (A).','Polytetrafluoroethene (Teflon) \n\nTeflon is manufactured by heating tetrafluoroethene with a free radical or persulphate catalyst at high pressures.\n\nIt is used in making oil seals and gaskets and also used for non-stick surface coated utensils.\n\nReference : (NCERT Class-12 Page- 436 Paragraph-3)','Organic chemistry >> Polymers >> Exampler based Advanced Questions',NULL,'2','mcq','Both (A) and (R) are correct and (R) is the correct explanation of (A).','Both (A) and (R) are correct but (R) is incorrect explanation of (A).','(A) is correct  (R) is incorrect.','(A) is incorrect but (R) is  correct.','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(290910,'chemistry','Match the polymer given in Column I with their repeating units in Column II. diagram(n2944)','A⟶(4), B⟶(1), C⟶(2) ,D⟶(4), E⟶(3)','Polyacrylonitrile is used as a substitute for wool in making commercial fibres as orlon or acrilan.\n\nReference : (NCERT Class-12 Page- 436 Paragraph-5)\n\nThe polymers made by addition polymerisation from two different monomers are termed as copolymers. \n\nBuna-S, which is formed by polymerisation of buta–1, 3–diene and styrene is an example of copolymer formed by addition polymerisation.\n\nReference : (NCERT Class-12 Page- 440 Paragraph-1)\n\n"Novolac on heating with formaldehyde undergoes cross linking to form an infusible solid mass called bakelite.\n\nBakelite is thermosetting polymer because it cannot be reused or remoulded.\n\nIt undergoes extensive cross linking in moulds and again become infusible.\n\nReference : (NCERT Class-12 Page- 438 Paragraph-3)", diagram(ne2906)','Organic chemistry >> Polymers >> Exampler based Advanced Questions',NULL,'3','mcq','A⟶(2), B⟶(1), C⟶(4) ,D⟶(4), E⟶(3)','A⟶(4), B⟶(1), C⟶(2) ,D⟶(4), E⟶(3)','A⟶(4), B⟶(3), C⟶(2) ,D⟶(4), E⟶(1)','A⟶(4), B⟶(1), C⟶(2) ,D⟶(3), E⟶(4)','DELETED',NULL,NULL,'/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/290910q.png'),
(290911,'chemistry','Which of the following polymer is biodegradable? diagram(n2946)','C','Poly β-hydroxybutyrate – co-β-hydroxy valerate (PHBV) It is obtained by the copolymerisation of 3-hydroxybutanoic acid and 3 - hydroxypentanoic acid. PHBV is used in speciality packaging, orthopaedic devices and in controlled release of drugs. PHBV undergoes bacterial degradation in the environment.Reference : (NCERT Class-12 Page- 442 Paragraph-4)','Organic chemistry >> Polymers >> Exampler based Advanced Questions',NULL,'2','mcq','A','B','C','D','DELETED',NULL,NULL,'/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/290911q.png'),
(290912,'chemistry','In which of the following polymers ethylene glycol is one of the monomer units? diagram(n2947)','A','Terylene or Dacron is manufactured by heating a mixture of ethylene glycol and terephthalic acid at 420 to 460 K in the presence of zinc acetate-antimony trioxide catalyst.\n\nReference : (NCERT Class-12 Page- 438 Paragraph-2) diagram(ne2948)','Organic chemistry >> Polymers >> Exampler based Advanced Questions',NULL,'2','mcq','A','B','C','D','DELETED',NULL,NULL,'/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/290912q.png'),
(290913,'chemistry','Which of the following polymers, need atleast one diene monomer for their preparation?\n\na. Dacron\n\nb. Buna-S\n\nc. Neoprene\n\nd. Novolac','b,c','The polymers made by addition polymerisation from two different monomers are termed as copolymers. \n\nBuna-S, which is formed by polymerisation of buta–1, 3–diene and styrene is an example of copolymer formed by addition polymerisation.\n\nReference : (NCERT Class-12 Page- 435 Paragraph-2)\n\nNeoprene or polychloroprene is formed by the free radical polymerisation of chloroprene.\n\nReference : (NCERT Class-12 Page- 441 Paragraph-4)\ndiagram(ne2949)','Organic chemistry >> Polymers >> Exampler based Advanced Questions',NULL,'3','mcq','a,c','a,d','b,c','All except d','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(290914,'chemistry','Which of the following polymers have vinylic monomer units?\n\na. Acrilan\n\nb. Polystyrene\n\nc. Nylon\n\nd. Teflon','a,b,d','Acrilan, Polystyrene and teflon has vinylic monomeric units.diagram(ne2908)','Organic chemistry >> Polymers >> Exampler based Advanced Questions',NULL,'3','mcq','a,c','a,b,c','a,b,d','All of the above','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(290915,'chemistry','Identify the polymer given below diagram(n2951)','natural rubber','Natural rubber may be considered as a linear polymer of isoprene (2-methyl-1, 3-butadiene) and is also called as cis - 1, 4 - polyisoprene.\n\nReference : (NCERT Class-12 Page- 440 Paragraph-4) diagram(ne2907)','Organic chemistry >> Polymers >> Exampler based Advanced Questions',NULL,'2','mcq','neoprene','natural rubber','terylene','nylon 6,6','DELETED',NULL,NULL,'/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/290915q.png'),
(291001,'chemistry','Monomers are converted to polymer by','condensation reaction between monomers','In these reactions, the product of each step is again a bi-functional species and the sequence of condensation goes on. \n\nSince, each step produces a distinct functionalised species and is independent of each other, this process is also called as step growth polymerisation.\n\nReference : (NCERT Class-12 Page- 437 Paragraph-2)','Organic chemistry >> Polymers >> JEE Mains',NULL,'2','mcq','hydrolysis of monomer','condensation reaction between monomers','protonation of monomers','None of the above','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
