(291005,'chemistry','Bakelite is obtained from phenol by reacting with','HCHO','Bakelite is fomed by condesation polymerisation of phenol and formaldehyde. Bakelite is thermosetting polymer because it cannot be reused or remoulded.\n\nReference : (NCERT Class-12 Page- 438 Paragraph-3)','Organic chemistry >> Polymers >> JEE Mains',NULL,'1','mcq','(CH₂OH)₂','CH₃CHO','CH₃COCH₃','HCHO','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(291006,'chemistry','Buna-N synthetic rubber is a copolymer of : Refer diagram(n2959)','c','Buna –N is obtained by the copolymerisation of 1, 3 – buta–1, 3–diene and acrylonitrile in the presence of a peroxide catalyst.\n\nReference : (NCERT Class-12 Page- 441 Paragraph-5)','Organic chemistry >> Polymers >> JEE Mains',NULL,'2','mcq','a','b','c','d','DELETED',NULL,NULL,'/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/291006q.png'),
