(291261,'biology','The chronological order of human evolution from early to the recent is [NEET-II 2016]','Ramapithecus→Australopithecus→Homo habilis →homo erectus','The fossils of Ramapithecus were discovered by Edward Levis from the Pliocene rocks of Shivalik hills in India. They were present in the Pliocene era nearly 14-15 million years ago (mya). Australopithecus was the first ape-man found in African Pliocene era rocks present 5 mya. Homo habilis was believed to be present in East Africa 2 mya in the Pliocene era. Homo erectus appeared nearly 1.5 mya with a cranial capacity of 800-1300 cc.','Genetics and Evolution >> Evolution >> Previous Year Questions 3',NULL,'2','mcq','Australopithecus→Ramapithecus→Homo habilis→homo erectus','Ramapithecus→Australopithecus→Homo habilis →homo erectus','Ramapithecus→Homo habilis→australopithecus→homo erectus','Australopithecus→Homo habilis→ramapithecus →homo erectus','NEW',NULL,NULL,NULL),
