(21009,'biology','Lichens indicate so 2 pollution because they [AIPMT 1989]','Are sensitive to so 2','Lichens are found in Artic Tundra region grow in pollution free environment. They are often used as a indicator of pollution and also they are very sensitive to SO2. (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11; Page 22; Paragraph No. 5)','Diversity In Living World >> Biological Classification >> Previous Year Questions 2',NULL,'2','mcq','Show association between algae and fungi','Grow faster than others','Are sensitive to so 2','Flourish in so 2 rich environment','NEW','11-022','11-016',NULL),
(21010,'biology','Given below are two statements :\nStatement I : Mycoplasma can pass through less than 1 micron filter size.\n\nStatement II : Mycoplasma are bacteria with cell wall.\n\nIn the light of the above statements, choose the most appropriate answer from the options given below [NEET 2022]','Statement I is correct but Statement II is incorrect','Mycoplasma are the smallest cells and are only 0.3 μm in length. So it can pass through less than\n1 μm filter size.\nMycoplasma lack cell wall.','Diversity In Living World >> Biological Classification >> Previous Year Questions 3',NULL,'3','mcq','correct are Both Statement I and Statement II','Both Statement I and Statement II are incorrect','Statement I is correct but Statement II is incorrect','Statement I is incorrect but Statement II is correct','NEW','11-020','11-014',NULL),
(21011,'biology','Identify the asexual reproductive structure associated with Penicillium [NEET 2022]','Conidia','Conidia are the asexual reproductive structures produced in Penicillium.\nGemmules are produced in sponge\nBuds are produced in Hydra\nZoospores are produced in Chlamydomonas','Diversity In Living World >> Biological Classification >> Previous Year Questions 3',NULL,'2','mcq','Zoospores','Conidia','Gemmules','Buds','NEW','11-023','11-017',NULL),
(21012,'biology','Which of the following is a correct statement? [NEET 2022]','Cyanobacteria are a group of autotrophic organisms classified under kingdom Monera .','Slime moulds are classified under kingdom Protista.\nMycoplasma lack cell wall.\nBacteria can be autotrophic as well as heterotrophic.','Diversity In Living World >> Biological Classification >> Previous Year Questions 3',NULL,'3','mcq','Cyanobacteria are a group of autotrophic organisms classified under kingdom Monera .','Bacteria are exclusively heterotrophic organisms','Slime moulds are saprophytic organisms classified under Kingdom Monera','Mycoplasma have DNA, ribosome and cell wall.','NEW','11-020','11-014',NULL),
(21013,'biology','The symbiotic relationship of algae and fungus is found in [1997]','Lichen','Lichens are the symbiotic association between algae and fungi. Fungi provides the raw material and algae manufacture the food.(Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11; Page 22; Paragraph No. 5)','Diversity In Living World >> Biological Classification >> Previous Year Questions 3',NULL,'3','mcq','Lichen','Mycorrhiza','Pneumatophore','Bacteriophage','NEW','11-022','11-016',NULL),
(21014,'biology','Which of the following is a cyanobacterium?','Nostoc','Nostoc is a cyanobacterium. Cyanobacteria are gram (–) ve prokaryotes which perform oxygenic photosynthesis like plants Cyanobacteria can be unicellular (e.g. Spirulina), colonial. (e.g. Nostoc) or filamentous (e.g. Oscillatoria) (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11; Page 19; Paragraph No. 3)','Diversity In Living World >> Biological Classification >> Previous Year Questions 3',NULL,'3','mcq','Nostoc','Chara','E. coli','Polysiphonia','NEW','11-019','11-013',NULL),
(21015,'biology','Virus has [1998]','Either DNA or rna','Virus are obligate intracellular parasite which can reproduce only by invading and taking over other cells as they lack the cellular machinery for self reproduction. Virus has either DNA or RNA and never both.','Diversity In Living World >> Biological Classification >> Previous Year Questions 3',NULL,'3','mcq','Dna','Rna','Both a and b','Either DNA or rna','NEW','11-026','11-020',NULL),
(21016,'biology','Which is a unicellular fungus ? [1998]','Yeast','Yeast is the only member in kingdom fungi which is unicellular. Nostoc : Blue green algae E. coli : Bacterium Albugo : Parasitic fungi(Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11; Page 22; Paragraph No. 5)','Diversity In Living World >> Biological Classification >> Previous Year Questions 3',NULL,'3','mcq','Yeast','E.coli','Nostoc','Albugo','NEW','11-022','11-016',NULL),
(21017,'biology','Viroids have [2003]','Single stranded RNA not enclosed by protein coat.','Viroids are the smallest known agents of infectious diseases comprising of small single stranded molecule of RNA. Viroids lack capsid and have no proteins associated with them.(Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11; Page 27; Paragraph No. 1)','Diversity In Living World >> Biological Classification >> Previous Year Questions 3',NULL,'3','mcq','Single stranded RNA not enclosed by protein coat.','Single stranded DNA not enclosed by protein coat.','Double stranded DNA enclosed by protein coat.','Double stranded RNA enclosed by protein coat.','NEW','11-027','11-021',NULL),
(21018,'biology','Choose the correct names of the different bacteria according to their shapes. [2013] A - Spherical shape , B - Rod shape , C - Spiral shape , D - Comma shape','A – cocci, b – bacilli, c – spirilla, d – vibrio','(Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11; Page 18; Paragraph No. 3)','Diversity In Living World >> Biological Classification >> Previous Year Questions 3',NULL,'3','mcq','A – cocci, b – bacilli, c – spirilla, d – vibrio','A – bacilli, b – cocci, c – spirilla, d – vibrio','A – spirilla, b – bacilli, c – cocci, d – vibrio','A – spirilla, b – vibrio, c – cocci, d – bacilli','NEW','11-018','11-012',NULL),
(21019,'biology','Fungi are filamentous with the exception of "x" which is unicellular. identify x. [2017]','Yeast','Yeast being a unicellular fungus does not show filamentous nature. It is a microscopic fungus consisting of a single oval cell that reproduces by budding.(Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11; Page 22; Paragraph No. 5)','Diversity In Living World >> Biological Classification >> Previous Year Questions 3',NULL,'3','mcq','Yeast','Albugo','Mucor','Lichen','NEW','11-022','11-016',NULL),
(21020,'biology','In three domain system kingdom monera is divided into two divisions on the basis of sequencing of','16s rRNA','In 3 domain system kingdom monera is divided into 2 domains (Archea and Bacteria) on the basis of sequence of 16s rRNA','Diversity In Living World >> Biological Classification >> Previous Year Questions 3',NULL,'3','mcq','28s rRNA','23s rRNA','16s rRNA','5s rRNA','NEW',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(21021,'biology','Phylogenetic history of an organisms is known as','Phylogeny','Phylogeny is the study of the evolutionary history and relationships among different groups of organisms. It involves the analysis of genetic, morphological, and ecological data to reconstruct the evolutionary relationships among different species, genera, families, orders, and other taxonomic groups. The resulting phylogenetic tree shows the pattern of evolutionary relationships among the different groups of organisms, with the branches representing the evolutionary lineages and the nodes representing the points at which lineages diverged from one another.','Diversity In Living World >> Biological Classification >> Previous Year Questions 3',NULL,'3','mcq','Phylogeny','Ancestry','Ontogeny','Paleontology','NEW','11-017','11-011',NULL),
(21022,'biology','According to five Kingdom system, blue green algae belongs to','Monera','NCERT XI: 18-19','Diversity In Living World >> Biological Classification >> Previous Year Questions 3',NULL,'3','mcq','Metaphyta','Monera','Protista','Algae','NEW','11-019','11-013',NULL),
(21023,'biology','The thalloid body of a slime mould(Myxomycetes) is known as','Plasmodium','NCERT XI: 21','Diversity In Living World >> Biological Classification >> Previous Year Questions 3',NULL,'3','mcq','Protonema','Plasmodium','Fruiting body','Mycelium','NEW','11-021','11-015',NULL),
