(40724,'biology','Evidence for the reptilian origin of birds is the occurrence of','Scales','Birds have scales on their limbs. (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11; Page 58; Paragraph No. 3)','Diversity In Living World >> Animal Kingdom >> Class Tetrapoda','Animal Kingdom','3','mcq','Scales','Beak','Feathers','Hairs','NEW','11-058','11-049',NULL),
(40725,'biology','4 chambered heart is found in','All birds+ crocodile+ all mammals','Crocodile is a reptile having 4 chambered heart. (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11; Page 58; Paragraph No. 1)','Diversity In Living World >> Animal Kingdom >> Class Tetrapoda','Animal Kingdom','2','mcq','All reptiles','All birds+ crocodile+ all mammals','Only mammals','Frog','NEW','11-058','11-049',NULL),
(40726,'biology','Birds have bipedal locomotion as it','Spare fore limbs for flight','Hind limbs helps in bipedal locomotion while forelimbs helps in flight. (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11; Page 58; Paragraph No. 3)','Diversity In Living World >> Animal Kingdom >> Class Tetrapoda','Animal Kingdom','2','mcq','Increases rate of locomotion','Spare fore limbs for flight','Reduces weight','Has no fore limbs','NEW','11-058','11-049',NULL),
(40727,'biology','The hind limbs generally have scales and are modified for walking, swimming or clasping the tree branches.This is for class','Aves','In birds The hind limbs generally have scales and are modified for walking, swimming or clasping the tree branches. (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11; Page 58; Paragraph No. 3)','Diversity In Living World >> Animal Kingdom >> Class Tetrapoda','Animal Kingdom','2','mcq','Aves','Reptilia','Amphibians','mammals','NEW','11-058','11-049',NULL),
(40728,'biology','For aves which is/are incorrect among the following?','The forelimbs are unmodified','In Aves The forelimbs are modified into wings. The hind limbs generally have scales and are modified for walking, swimming or clasping the tree branches. (Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11; Page 58; Paragraph No. 3)','Diversity In Living World >> Animal Kingdom >> Class Tetrapoda','Animal Kingdom','2','mcq','The forelimbs are unmodified','Skin is dry without glands except the oil gland at the base of the tail','They are warm-blooded (homoiothermous) animals','The digestive tract of birds has additional chambers, the crop and gizzard','NEW','11-058','11-049',NULL),
(40729,'biology','Which of the following statement is/are true for aves? \n\ni)They necessarily not possess beak. \n\nii)Sexes are separate. Fertilisation is internal. They are oviparous and development is direct.\n\niii)Examples : Corvus (Crow), Columba (Pigeon), Psittacula (Parrot), Struthio (Ostrich), Pavo (Peacock), Aptenodytes (Penguin), Neophron (Vulture).','Only ii and iii','They possess beak. Sexes are separate. Fertilisation is internal. They are oviparous and development is direct.Examples : Corvus (Crow), Columba (Pigeon), Psittacula (Parrot), Struthio (Ostrich), Pavo (Peacock), Aptenodytes (Penguin), Neophron (Vulture).(Reference  : NCERT Biology Class 11; Page 58; Paragraph No. 3)','Diversity In Living World >> Animal Kingdom >> Class Tetrapoda','Animal Kingdom','2','mcq','Only i','Only i and ii','Only i and iii','Only ii and iii','NEW','11-058','11-049',NULL),
(40730,'biology','Identify the organism shown in diagram (0448)','Ornithorhynchus','(Reference   - NCERT Biology Class 11, Page No-59, Figure 4.24)','Diversity In Living World >> Animal Kingdom >> Class Tetrapoda','Animal Kingdom','3','mcq','Ornithorhynchus','Macropus','Pteropus','Balaenoptera','NEW','11-059','11-050','/ncert/pyq/biology/mcq/40730q.png'),
