(340315,'biology','In which year Eli Lilly produced human insulin?','1983','In\n1983, Eli Lilly an American company prepared two DNA sequences\ncorresponding to A and B, chains of human insulin and introduced them\nin plasmids of E. coli to produce insulin chains.','Biotechnology and Its Applications >> Biotechnology And Its Applications >> Genetically Engineered Insulin','Biotechnology and its applications','1','mcq','1983','1973','1982','1993','NEW','12-211','12-182',NULL),
(340316,'biology','Chain A and B were, A. Combined by creating disulfide bonds  B. produced separately  C. extracted.      Give the proper sequence.','B, C, A','Chains A and B were\nproduced separately, extracted and combined by creating disulfide bonds\nto form human insulin.','Biotechnology and Its Applications >> Biotechnology And Its Applications >> Genetically Engineered Insulin','Biotechnology and its applications','1','mcq','B, C, A','A, C, B','A, B, C','C, B, A','NEW','12-211','12-182',NULL),
(340317,'biology','Insulin from animal sources','caused allergic reaction in some patients','Insulin from an\nanimal source, though caused some patients to develop\nallergy or other types of reactions to the foreign\nprotein.','Biotechnology and Its Applications >> Biotechnology And Its Applications >> Genetically Engineered Insulin','Biotechnology and its applications','1','mcq','caused allergic reaction in some patients','worked like human insulin','has exact same structure like human insulin','all of the above','NEW','12-211','12-182',NULL),
(340401,'biology','If a person is born with a hereditary disease such as ADA deficiency which permanent corrective therapy be taken for such a disease?','Gene therapy','It can be cured by Gene Therapy . Genes carry the information that determines our traits,which are features or characteristics we inherit from our parents,Gene therapy involves using genes to fight or prevent disease . it might mean replacing a gene that isn\'t working properly,adding a good gene into a person who has a disease,or blocking a gene that is causing a problem.','Biotechnology and Its Applications >> Biotechnology And Its Applications >> Gene Therapy','Biotechnology and its applications','2','mcq','Gene therapy','rDNA technology','Embryo transfer','All of these','NEW','12-211','12-182',NULL),
(340402,'biology','The insertion of gene into a person\'s  cells and tissues to treat a disease.This method is called as','Gene Therapy','Gene therapy is a collection of methods that allows correction of a gene defect that has been diagnosed in a child/embryo. Here genes are inserted into a person’s cells and tissues to treat a disease.','Biotechnology and Its Applications >> Biotechnology And Its Applications >> Gene Therapy','Biotechnology and its applications','2','mcq','Genetic modification','Bio remediation','Genetic correction','Gene Therapy','NEW','12-211','12-182',NULL),
(340403,'biology','The first clinical gene therapy was given for treating','adenosine deaminase deficiency','The first clinical gene therapy was given in 1990 to a 4-year old girl with adenosine deaminase (ADA) deficiency. This enzyme is crucial for the immune system to function. The disorder is caused due to the deletion of the gene for adenosine deaminase.','Biotechnology and Its Applications >> Biotechnology And Its Applications >> Gene Therapy','Biotechnology and its applications','2','mcq','diabetes mellitus','chicken pox','rheumatoid arthritis','adenosine deaminase deficiency','NEW','12-211','12-182',NULL),
(340404,'biology','The first clinical gene therapy was given to whom and in which year?','4 year old girl, 1990','The first clinical gene therapy was given in 1990 to a 4-year old girl\nwith adenosine deaminase (ADA) deficiency.','Biotechnology and Its Applications >> Biotechnology And Its Applications >> Gene Therapy','Biotechnology and its applications','2','mcq','4 year old girl, 1990','4 year old boy, 1990','40 year old woman, 1990','40 year old woman, 1990','NEW','12-211','12-182',NULL),
(41409,'chemistry','The shape of the  CO₃²⁻  is:','Trigonal planar','It is AB₃ type molecule,three bond pairs remain as far apart as possible to minimize the repulsion between bond pairs and adopt the trigonal planar geometry.\n\nAs shown in diagram\n\nReference: (NCERT chemistry Class 11; page 114; Table 4.6) diagram(ne0410)','Inorganic chemistry >> Chemical bonding and molecular structure >> VSEPR theory',NULL,'3','mcq','Tetrahedral','Linear','Octahedral','Trigonal planar','NEW','11-113','11-113',NULL),
(340405,'biology','Which of the following has become a permanent cure for treatment of severe combined immunodeficiency (SCID)?','Gene therapy','Nearly every child with SCID is treated with a stem cell transplant, also known as a bone marrow transplant. This is the only available treatment option that has a chance of providing a permanent cure. The bone marrow cells or stem cells are administered through an IV, similar to a blood transfusion. Gene therapy could be a permanent cure for treatment of severe combined immunodeficiency (SCID).For Gene Therapy, the bone marrow is taken from the patient and doesn\'t require donor in general cases and enzyme replacement is a temporary solution, not compliant in the long run.','Biotechnology and Its Applications >> Biotechnology And Its Applications >> Gene Therapy','Biotechnology and its applications','2','mcq','Radio therapy','Gene therapy','Enzyme replacement therapy','Organ Transplant','NEW','12-211','12-182',NULL),
(340406,'biology','Correction of a genetic defect involves','delivery of a normal gene into the individual or embryo to take over the function of and compensate for the non-functional gene.','Gene therapy is a collection of methods that allows correction of a gene defect that has been diagnosed in a child/embryo. Here genes\nare inserted into a person’s cells and tissues to treat a disease.Correction of a genetic defect involves delivery of a normal gene into\nthe individual or embryo to take over the function of and compensate for the non-functional gene.','Biotechnology and Its Applications >> Biotechnology And Its Applications >> Gene Therapy','Biotechnology and its applications','3','mcq','delivery of a normal gene into the individual or embryo to take over the function of and compensate for the non-functional gene.','Polymerase chain reaction','ELISA','All of them','NEW','12-211','12-182',NULL),
(340407,'biology','When a patient with defective ADA was treated, what is the order of the following steps  performed for gene therapy? - \nI.Lymphocytes are transferred to culture dishes\n \n\nII.Lymphocytes were obtained from the patients\n\nIII. Lymphocytes were transfected with normal ADA genes\n\nIV. The transfected cells are returned to the patients.','ii,i,iii,iv','As a first step towards gene therapy, lymphocytes from the blood of the patient are grown in a culture outside the body. A functional ADA-cNDA  (using a retroviral vector) is then introduced into these lymphocytes, which are subsequently returned to the body of the patient. However, as these cells are not immortal, the patient requires periodic infusion of such genetically engineered lymphocytes. So, the correct answer is \'Patient does not require periodic infusion of genetically engineered lymphocytes\'.','Biotechnology and Its Applications >> Biotechnology And Its Applications >> Gene Therapy','Biotechnology and its applications','3','mcq','ii,iii,i,iv','i,ii,iii,iv','ii,i,iii,iv','i,iv,iii,ii','NEW','12-211','12-182',NULL),
(340408,'biology','Which are the techniques used to treat ADA deficiency in children.','both a and b','In some children ADA deficiency can be cured by bone marrow transplantation; in others it can be treated by enzyme replacement therapy, in which functional ADA is given to the patient by injection. But the problem with both of these approaches that they are not completely curative','Biotechnology and Its Applications >> Biotechnology And Its Applications >> Gene Therapy','Biotechnology and its applications','3','mcq','bone marrow transplantation','enzyme replacement therapy','both a and b','none of the above','NEW','12-211','12-182',NULL),
(340409,'biology','The gene isolate from marrow cells producing ADA is introduced into cells at early_________ stages, it could be a permanent cure.','embryonic','The gene isolate from marrow cells producing ADA is introduced into cells at early embryonic stages, it could be a permanent cure','Biotechnology and Its Applications >> Biotechnology And Its Applications >> Gene Therapy','Biotechnology and its applications','3','mcq','embryonic','Infant','fetus','zygote','NEW','12-211','12-182',NULL),
(340410,'biology','Which of the following is not true for ADA?','ADA stands for adinosine deoxy aminase','The first clinical gene therapy was given in 1990 to a 4-year old girl\nwith adenosine deaminase (ADA) deficiency. This enzyme is crucial for\nthe immune system to function.','Biotechnology and Its Applications >> Biotechnology And Its Applications >> Gene Therapy','Biotechnology and its applications','3','mcq','ADA is crucial for immune system to function','In the absence of this enzyme, purine metabolism is disturbed and T-cells fail to function','ADA deficiency is caused by deletion of the gene for ADA','ADA stands for adinosine deoxy aminase','NEW','12-211','12-182',NULL),
(340411,'biology','A functional ADA cDNA can be introduced into cells of the patients receiving gene therapy by a vector constituted by','Retrovirus','A functional ADA cDNA can be introduced into cells of the patients receiving gene therapy by a vector constituted by retrovirus.','Biotechnology and Its Applications >> Biotechnology And Its Applications >> Gene Therapy','Biotechnology and its applications','3','mcq','E. coli','Reovirus','Retrovirus','Agrobacterium','NEW','12-211','12-182',NULL),
(340412,'biology','What is gene therapy?','Both A and B','Gene therapy is a collection of methods that allows correction of a\ngene defect that has been diagnosed in a child/embryo.','Biotechnology and Its Applications >> Biotechnology And Its Applications >> Gene Therapy','Biotechnology and its applications','1','mcq','Collection of methods','correction of a genetic defect','Giving normal genes to cells by injection','Both A and B','NEW','12-211','12-182',NULL),
(340413,'biology','What causes ADA deficiency?','deletion of ADA gene','The first clinical gene therapy was given in 1990 to a 4-year old girl\nwith adenosine deaminase (ADA) deficiency. This enzyme is crucial for\nthe immune system to function. The disorder is caused due to the deletion\nof the gene for adenosine deaminase.','Biotechnology and Its Applications >> Biotechnology And Its Applications >> Gene Therapy','Biotechnology and its applications','2','mcq','deletion of ADA gene','suppression of ADA gene','presence of both Recessive ADA gene','Fault in ADA protein formation','NEW','12-211','12-182',NULL),
(340414,'biology','Which type of DNA is used to introduce ADA gene into the lymphocytes in gene therapy?','cDNA','A functional ADA cDNA (using a retroviral vector) is then\nintroduced into these lymphocytes, which are subsequently returned to\nthe patient.','Biotechnology and Its Applications >> Biotechnology And Its Applications >> Gene Therapy','Biotechnology and its applications','1','mcq','rDNA','bDNA','cDNA','zDNA','NEW','12-211','12-182',NULL),
(340415,'biology','Which of the following is correct with reference to genetically modified Lymphocytes for ADA deficiency?','Both B and C','However, as these cells are not immortal, the patient requires\nperiodic infusion of such genetically engineered lymphocytes. However, if\nthe gene isolate from marrow cells producing ADA is introduced into cells\nat early embryonic stages, it could be a permanent cure.','Biotechnology and Its Applications >> Biotechnology And Its Applications >> Gene Therapy','Biotechnology and its applications','2','mcq','cDNA containing lymphocytes become immortal','cDNA containing lymphocytes are not immortal','patient requires periodic infusion of such cells','Both B and C','NEW','12-211','12-182',NULL),
(41410,'chemistry','The molecular geometry of PCl₅','Trigonal bipyramidal','The molecular geometry of PCl₅ is Trigonal bipyramidal. \n\nAs shown in diagram \n\nReference: (NCERT chemistry Class 11; page 114; Table 4.6) diagram(ne0410)','Inorganic chemistry >> Chemical bonding and molecular structure >> VSEPR theory',NULL,'3','mcq','Tetrahedral','Trigonal bipyramidal','Octahedral','Trigonal planar','NEW','11-113','11-113',NULL),
(340501,'biology','Which of the following techniques serve the purpose of early diagnosis?\n 1)Recombinant DNA technology\n\n2) PCR (Polymerase Chain Reaction\n\n3) Enzyme-Linked Immunosorbent Assay (ELISA)\n\n4) Blood and Urine analysis','1,2 and 3','R-DNA technology: Recombinant DNA technology, joining together of DNA molecules from two different species that are inserted into a host organism to produce new genetic combinations. It can provide precise diagnostic information about genetic diseases. PCR (Polymerase Chain Reaction) involves amplification of the nucleic acid in the pathogen allowing us to detect the pathogen at very low concentration. PCR used to detect HIV in suspected AIDS patients and to detect gene mutations in suspected cancer patients. Using the conventional method of diagnosis(serum, urine analysis, etc.) early detection of disease is not possible as the markers for most diseases appear late. Enzyme-Linked Immunosorbent Assay (ELISA): The basic principle of ELISA is antigen-antibody reactions. ELISA can diagnose infections by detecting the presence of antigens (proteins of the pathogen) in the patient serum or by detecting the antibodies produced against the pathogen. So, the correct option is \'(i), (ii) and (iii)\'. Blood and Urine analysis are useful in diagnosis of a disease after the disease has progressed and presents with visible symptoms.','Biotechnology and Its Applications >> Biotechnology And Its Applications >> Molecular Diagnosis','Biotechnology and its applications','3','mcq','1,2 and 3','1,2 and 4','3 and 4','1 and 2','NEW','12-212','12-183',NULL),
(340502,'biology','For effective treatment of a disease','Early diagnosis and understanding its pathophysiology is required.','For effective treatment of a disease, early diagnosis and understanding its pathophysiology is very important.','Biotechnology and Its Applications >> Biotechnology And Its Applications >> Molecular Diagnosis','Biotechnology and its applications','3','mcq','Early diagnosis is not required but understanding its pathophysiology is very important.','Early diagnosis is required but understanding its pathophysiology is not required.','Early diagnosis and understanding its pathophysiology is required.','Neither early diagnosis nor understanding its pathophysiology is required.','NEW','12-212','12-183',NULL),
(340503,'biology','Presence of a pathogen (bacteria, viruses, etc.) is normally suspected only when','When the pathogen has produced disease symptoms','Presence of a pathogen (bacteria, viruses, etc.) is normally suspected only when the pathogen has produced a disease symptom','Biotechnology and Its Applications >> Biotechnology And Its Applications >> Molecular Diagnosis','Biotechnology and its applications','3','mcq','Soon after the pathogen enter into the host','When the concentration of pathogen is low in the host system','When the pathogen has produced disease symptoms','All of them','NEW','12-212','12-183',NULL),
(340504,'biology','How very low concentration of a bacteria or virus can be detected','amplification of their nucleic acid by PCR.','By this time the concentration of pathogen is already very high in the body. However, very low concentration of a bacteria or virus (at a time when the symptoms of the disease are not yet visible) can be detected by amplification of their nucleic acid by PCR.','Biotechnology and Its Applications >> Biotechnology And Its Applications >> Molecular Diagnosis','Biotechnology and its applications','3','mcq','amplification of their nucleic acid by ELISA','amplification of their nucleic acid by PCR.','amplification of their nucleic acid by Recombinant DNA.','all the above','NEW','12-212','12-183',NULL),
(340505,'biology','PCR is now routinely used to detect what disorders?','genetic disorders.','PCR is now routinely used to detect HIV in suspected AIDS patients. It is being used to detect mutations in genes in suspected cancer patients too. It is a powerful techqnique to identify many other genetic disorders.','Biotechnology and Its Applications >> Biotechnology And Its Applications >> Molecular Diagnosis','Biotechnology and its applications','3','mcq','genetic disorders.','Inflammation','Vitamin Deficiency','Communicable diseases like fever and cold','NEW','12-212','12-183',NULL),
(340506,'biology','It is a single stranded DNA or RNA, tagged with a radioactive molecule called ______ and is used to detect mutated genes.','Probe','A single stranded DNA or RNA, tagged with a radioactive molecule (probe) is allowed to hybridise to its complementary DNA in a clone of cells followed by detection using autoradiography. The clone having the mutated gene will hence not appear on the photographic film, because the probe will not have complementarity with the mutated gene.','Biotechnology and Its Applications >> Biotechnology And Its Applications >> Molecular Diagnosis','Biotechnology and its applications','3','mcq','RNAi','Probe','Plasmid','Primer','NEW','12-212','12-183',NULL),
(340507,'biology','A single stranded DNA or RNA, tagged with a radioactive molecule (probe) is allowed to hybridise to its complementary DNA in a clone of cells followed by detection using ?','Autoradiography','A single stranded DNA or RNA, tagged with a radioactive molecule (probe) is allowed to hybridise to its complementary DNA in a clone of cells followed by detection using autoradiography.','Biotechnology and Its Applications >> Biotechnology And Its Applications >> Molecular Diagnosis','Biotechnology and its applications','3','mcq','Photographic film','Autoradiography','Nitrocellulose paper','Replica plating','NEW','12-212','12-183',NULL),
(340508,'biology','The clone having the mutated gene will not appear on the photographic film. Why?','Because\nthe probe will not have complementarity with the mutated gene','The clone having the mutated gene will hence not appear on the photographic film, because the probe will not have complementarity with the mutated gene','Biotechnology and Its Applications >> Biotechnology And Its Applications >> Molecular Diagnosis','Biotechnology and its applications','3','mcq','Because\nthe probe will not have complementarity with the mutated gene','Because the DNA is not tagged with the probe','Because the DNA is single stranded','Because DNA is not mutated','NEW','12-212','12-183',NULL),
(340509,'biology','True about clone having the mutated gene in photographic film is\nA.Will not appear on the photographic film\n\nB.Will appear on the photographic film\n\nC.The probe will not have complementarity with the mutated gene\n\nD.The probe will  have complementarity with the mutated gene','A , C','A single stranded DNA or RNA, tagged with a radioactive molecule (probe) is allowed to hybridise to its complementary DNA in a clone of cells followed by detection using autoradiography. The clone having the mutated gene will hence not appear on the photographic film, because the probe will not have complementarity with the mutated gene','Biotechnology and Its Applications >> Biotechnology And Its Applications >> Molecular Diagnosis','Biotechnology and its applications','3','mcq','A only','A , C','B, D','B, C','NEW','12-212','12-183',NULL),
(340510,'biology','Which of the following is based upon the principle of antigen-antibody interaction?','ELISA','ELISA technique is based on the principles on the antigen-antibody interaction, used for diagnosis of AIDS.','Biotechnology and Its Applications >> Biotechnology And Its Applications >> Molecular Diagnosis','Biotechnology and its applications','3','mcq','PCR','ELISA','R DNA technology','RNA','NEW','12-212','12-183',NULL),
