(340601,'biology','Animals that have had their DNA manipulated to possess and express an extra (foreign) gene are known as which animals?','Transgenic animals','Animals that have had their DNA manipulated to possess and express an extra (foreign) gene are known as transgenic animals.','Biotechnology and Its Applications >> Biotechnology And Its Applications >> Transgenic Animals','Biotechnology and its applications','3','mcq','Transgenic animals','Mutated animals','Somatic hybrids','Super animals','NEW','12-212','12-183',NULL),
(340602,'biology','Maximum number(95%) of existing transgenic animals is of','Mice','Cover 95% of all existing trangenic animals are mice. Animals that have their DNA manipulated to possess and express an extra (foreign) gene are known as transgenic animals, e.g. rats, rabbits, pig, sheep, cows, fish, etc.','Biotechnology and Its Applications >> Biotechnology And Its Applications >> Transgenic Animals','Biotechnology and its applications','3','mcq','Pig','Fish','Mice','Cow','NEW','12-212','12-183',NULL),
(340603,'biology','Give some of the reasons why are transgenic animals are being produced?\n 1)To Study Normal physiology and development \n\n2)Study of disease \n\n3)For Biological products \n\n4)Testing Vaccine safety \n\n5)Chemical safety testing','1,2,3,4 and 5','Transgenic animals are being produced due to following reasons. 1)Normal physiology and development 2)Study of disease 3)Biological products 4)Vaccine safety 5)Chemical safety testing','Biotechnology and Its Applications >> Biotechnology And Its Applications >> Transgenic Animals','Biotechnology and its applications','3','mcq','1,2 and 3','1,3 and 5','2,3 and 5','1,2,3,4 and 5','NEW','12-212','12-183',NULL),
(340604,'biology','Transgenic animals can be specifically designed to allow the study of?','all the above','Transgenic animals can be specifically designed to allow the study of how genes are regulated, and how they affect the normal functions of the body and its development','Biotechnology and Its Applications >> Biotechnology And Its Applications >> Transgenic Animals','Biotechnology and its applications','3','mcq','how genes are regulated','how they affect the normal functions of the body','development of functions of the body.','all the above','NEW','12-212','12-183',NULL),
(340605,'biology','Which of the following statements are correct :\n 1) Many transgenic animals are designed to increase our understanding of how genes contribute to the development of  disease.\n\n2)  The milk produced by rosie cow contained the human alpha-lactalbumin and was nutritionally a less balanced product for human babies than natural cow-milk. \n\n3) Transgenic animals are made that carry genes which make them more sensitive to toxic substances than non-transgenic animals in chemical safety testing.','1,3 only','Many transgenic animals are designed to increase our understanding of how genes contribute to the development of disease. The milk contained the human alpha-lactalbumin and was nutritionally a more balanced product for human babies than natural cow-milk.Transgenic animals are made that carry genes which make them more sensitive to toxic substances than non-transgenic animals in chemical safety testing.','Biotechnology and Its Applications >> Biotechnology And Its Applications >> Transgenic Animals','Biotechnology and its applications','3','mcq','1 only','2 only','1,3 only','1,2 and 3','NEW','12-213','12-184',NULL),
(340606,'biology','What are the human diseases for which transgenic models does not exist ?','Rhinitis','Today transgenic models exist for many human diseases such as cancer, cystic fibrosis, rheumatoid arthritis and Alzheimer’s.','Biotechnology and Its Applications >> Biotechnology And Its Applications >> Transgenic Animals','Biotechnology and its applications','3','mcq','rheumatoid arthritis','cystic fibrosis','cancer','Rhinitis','NEW','12-213','12-184',NULL),
(340607,'biology','The biological product created by the introduction of portions of DNA which codes for α-1 antitrypsin, is used to treat?','Emphysema','Transgenic animals that produce useful biological products can be created by the introduction of the portion of DNA (or genes) which codes for a particular product such as human protein (α-1-antitrypsin) used to treat emphysema.','Biotechnology and Its Applications >> Biotechnology And Its Applications >> Transgenic Animals','Biotechnology and its applications','3','mcq','Emphysema','Cystic fibrosis','Asthma','Bronchitis','NEW','12-213','12-184',NULL),
(340608,'biology','When biological products are made using transgenic animals they are?','They are usually expensive','Medicines required to treat certain human diseases can contain biological products, but such products are often expensive to make.','Biotechnology and Its Applications >> Biotechnology And Its Applications >> Transgenic Animals','Biotechnology and its applications','3','mcq','They are usually expensive','They are less effective','They are cheap usually','All the above','NEW','12-213','12-184',NULL),
