(460170,'chemistry','Force of viscosity in a liquid is given by\n\nf=μA(dv/d3)\n\nWhere \nf=viscosity force, \nμ=coefficent of viscosity, \nA=Area of constant, \ndv/d3=velocity gradient',NULL,NULL,'Physical Chemistry Formulae >> States of Matter >> Viscosity',NULL,'1','flashcard',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
