(470122,'chemistry','The Enthalpy Change of a system can be given by\n\nΔH=ΔU+PΔV\nΔH=ΔU+Δn₉RT\n\nWhere \nΔH=Enthalpy Change, \nΔU=Internal energy change, \nΔn₉=n₉ₚ-n₉ᵣ= no. of gaseous moles in (product-r), \nT=Temperature, R=Universal gas constant, \nP=Pressure, \nΔV=Change in volume',NULL,NULL,'Physical Chemistry Formulae >> Thermodynamics >> Enthalpy Change',NULL,'1','flashcard',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'NEW',NULL,NULL,NULL),
