(470155,'chemistry','The general expression to calculate entropy change is given by\n\nΔS=nCᵥ in T₂/T₁+nR in V₂/V₁\n\nWhere \nn=no. of moles, \nCᵥ=Heat capacity of constant volume, \nV₂ & V₁ are volumes at temperature T₂ & T₁, \nR=Universal gas constant',NULL,NULL,'Physical Chemistry Formulae >> Thermodynamics >> Entropy Calculation',NULL,'1','flashcard',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'NEW',NULL,NULL,'/ncert/pyq/physics/mcq/470155q.png'),
