(490101,'chemistry','For the ionisation of H₂O, its constant is given by\n\nH₂O(i) + H₂O(i)⇌H₃O⁺(aq) +OH(aq)\n\n\nK=[H₃O⁺][OH⁻]/H₂O\nKw=[H⁺][OH⁻]=10⁻¹⁴ M² at 298K\n\nWhere \nK=Dissociation constant, \nKw=Ionic product of water',NULL,NULL,'Physical Chemistry Formulae >> Ionic Equilibrium >> Ionisation Constant & Ionic Product of Water',NULL,'1','flashcard',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'NEW',NULL,NULL,NULL),
