(490110,'chemistry','The ionisation constant of a weak acid dissociating as HA ⇌H⁺+H⁻ is given by \n\nKₐ=[H⁺][A⁻]/[HA] = C∝²/1-∝\nFor a weak acid, ∝<<1 1-∝=1\nKₐ=C∝²\n∝=√Kₐ/C\n\nWhere \nC=Concentration, \n∝=Degree of dissociation, \nKₐ=Dissociation constant',NULL,NULL,'Physical Chemistry Formulae >> Ionic Equilibrium >> Ionisation Constant of Weak Acid',NULL,'1','flashcard',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'NEW',NULL,NULL,NULL),
