(500107,'chemistry','The normality of a solution is given by\n\nN=n/V(ml) x 1000 =W/ExV(ml) x1000\n\nWhere \nn=No. of equivalents, \nV=Vol of solution in ml, \nW=wt of solute, \nE=Equivalent wt of solute',NULL,NULL,'Physical Chemistry Formulae >> Redox Reaction >> Normality',NULL,'1','flashcard',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'NEW',NULL,NULL,NULL),
