(510113,'chemistry','The mole fraction of a component in a solution is given by\n\nXₐ=nₐ/nₐ+n₆+... = nₐ/nₜ\n\nWhere \nnₐ=No.of moles of A, \nnₜ=Total no.of  moles of all components, \nXₐ=Mole fraction of A  \nFor a binary solution Xₐ+X₆=1',NULL,NULL,'Physical Chemistry Formulae >> Solutions >> Mole Fraction',NULL,'1','flashcard',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'NEW',NULL,NULL,NULL),
