(520116,'chemistry','The emf of an electrode concentration cell with following reaction is given by\nPt,H₂(P₁atm)/H⁺(1M)/H₂(P₂atm)/Pt\n\nE=0.059/2 log (P₁/P₂)\n\nWhere \nP₁=Partial pressure of H₂ in anode half, \nP₂=Partial pressure of H₂ in cathode half, \nE=emf',NULL,NULL,'Physical Chemistry Formulae >> Electrochemistry >> Electrode Concentration Cell',NULL,'1','flashcard',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'NEW',NULL,NULL,'/ncert/pyq/physics/mcq/520116q.png'),
