(520131,'chemistry','The Molar Conductivity of a solution is given by\n\nλm=K/C \n\nWhere \nK=Conductivity in S m⁻¹, \nC=Conc. in mol m⁻³, \nλm=Molar conductivity in Sm² mol⁻¹\n\nλm(Scm² mol⁻¹)=K(S cm⁻¹) / 1000 Lm⁻³ x molarity(mol L⁻¹)\nλm(Scm² mol⁻¹)=K(S cm⁻¹) x 1000(cm³/L) /Molarity (mol L⁻¹)',NULL,NULL,'Physical Chemistry Formulae >> Electrochemistry >> Molar Conductivity',NULL,'1','flashcard',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'NEW',NULL,NULL,NULL),
