(530150,'chemistry','The temperature dependence of rate constant as described by arrhenius equation is given by\n\nk=Ae⁻ᴱᵃ/ᴿᵀ \nin k=in A -Eₐ/RT\nlog k=log A - Eₐ/2.303RT\n\nWhere  \ne⁻ᴱᵃ/ᴿᵀ=Fraction of moleculer with KE>Eₐ, \nEₐ=Activation energy, \nT=Temperature, \nK=Rate constant, \nA=Arrhenius constant',NULL,NULL,'Physical Chemistry Formulae >> Chemical Kinetics >> Arrhenius Equation',NULL,'1','flashcard',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'NEW','12-113','12-079',NULL),
