(100530,'chemistry','Which of the following is not deliquescent?','KCl','Except KCl all the other compounds absorb moisture when kept open to air.\n\n(Reference- NCERT Chemistry Class 11 (Part 2); Page 305; Paragraph 10.4 and Page 304 and Paragraph 10.3.1)','Inorganic chemistry >> The s Block Elements >> Group 1 elements - Important Compounds of Sodium',NULL,'1','mcq','LiCl','CaCl₂','NaOH','KCl','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(260233,'chemistry','Write the correct IUPAC NAME of the given compound in diagram?(n26004)','2-hydroxycyclopentane carbaldehyde','The substituents are prefixed in alphabetical order along with numerals indicating their positions in the carbon chain. \n\nThe same applies to cyclic ketones, where the carbonyl carbon is numbered one. \n\nWhen the aldehyde group is attached to a ring, the suffix carbaldehydeis added after the full name of the cycloalkane.\n\nReference : (NCERT - Class 12 Page-359 Paragraph -1)','Organic Chemistry >> Aldehydes,ketones & carboxylic acids >> Nomenclature and Structure of Carbonyl Group',NULL,'3','mcq','2-hydroxycyclopentanal','1-hydroxycyclopentane carbaldehyde','2-hydroxycyclopentane carbaldehyde','cyclopentane-2-ol carbaldehyde','NEW','12-359','12-229','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/260233q.png'),
(100531,'chemistry','Mark the false statement.','Solvay Process can be extended to manufacture of potassium carbonate.','It may be mentioned here that Solvay process cannot be extended to the manufacture of potassium carbonate because potassium hydrogencarbonate is too soluble to be precipitated by the addition of ammonium hydrogencarbonate to a saturated solution of potassium chloride. \n\nSodium hydroxide is a white, translucent solid. It melts at 591 K. It is readily soluble in water to give a strong alkaline solution. \n\nCrystals of sodium hydroxide are deliquescent. \n\nThe sodium hydroxide solution at the surface reacts with the CO₂ in the atmosphere to form Na₂CO₃. \n\n(Reference- NCERT Chemistry Class 11 (Part 2); Page 305; Paragraph 10.4)','Inorganic chemistry >> The s Block Elements >> Group 1 elements - Important Compounds of Sodium',NULL,'2','mcq','It is readily soluble in water to give a strong alkaline solution.','Crystals of sodium hydroxide are deliquescent.','Solvay Process can be extended to manufacture of potassium carbonate.','The sodium hydroxide solution at the surface reacts with the CO₂ in the atmosphere to form Na₂CO₃.','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(100532,'chemistry','What is formed on saturating a solution of sodium carbonate with carbon dioxide?','Baking soda','Sodium hydrogen carbonate is made by saturating a solution of sodium carbonate with carbon dioxide.\n \n(Reference- NCERT Chemistry Class 11 (Part 2); Page 306; Paragraph 10.4)','Inorganic chemistry >> The s Block Elements >> Group 1 elements - Important Compounds of Sodium',NULL,'1','mcq','Baking soda','NaOH','NaH','H₂CO₃','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(100533,'chemistry','How many of following statements are correct?\n\n1. Sodium hydrogencarbonate is made by saturating a solution of sodium carbonate with carbon dioxide.\n\n2. The white crystalline powder of sodium hydrogen carbonate, being less soluble, gets separated out. \n\n3. Sodium hydrogen carbonate is known as baking soda because it decomposes on heating to generate bubbles of carbon dioxide.\n\n4. CO₂ bubbles leave holes in cakes or pastries and making them light and fluffy.','4','Sodium hydrogencarbonate is known as baking soda because it decomposes on heating to generate bubbles of carbon dioxide (leaving holes in cakes or pastries and making them light and fluffy). \n\nSodium hydrogencarbonate is made by saturating a solution of sodium carbonate with carbon dioxide. \n\nThe white crystalline powder of sodium hydrogencarbonate, being less soluble, gets separated out. \n\n(Reference- NCERT Chemistry Class 11 (Part 2); Page 306; Paragraph 10.4)','Inorganic chemistry >> The s Block Elements >> Group 1 elements - Important Compounds of Sodium',NULL,'2','mcq','1','2','3','4','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
