(100547,'chemistry','Which of the following is not the use of NaOH?','Manufacture of glass, soap, borax and Caustic soda.','Sodium carbonate is used in the manufacture of glass, soap, borax and Caustic soda. All the others are uses of NaOH.\n\n(Reference- NCERT Chemistry Class 11 (Part 2); Page 306; Paragraph 10.4(uses))','Inorganic chemistry >> The s Block Elements >> Group 1 elements - Important Compounds of Sodium',NULL,'2','mcq','The manufacture of soap, paper, artificial silk and a number of chemicals.','In the textile industries for mercerising cotton fabrics.','As a laboratory reagent.','Manufacture of glass, soap, borax and Caustic soda.','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
