(100736,'chemistry','KCl exists as W. what is W?','Anhydrous','NaCl and KCl do not form hydrates. \n\nHence they are anhydrous.\n \n(Reference- NCERT Chemistry Class 11 (Part 2); Page 307; Paragraph 10.6.4)','Inorganic chemistry >> The s Block Elements >> Group 2 Elements- Properties and Uses',NULL,'1','mcq','Dihydrate','Trihydrate','Pentahydrate','Anhydrous','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL);
