(100737,'chemistry','Beryllium and magnesium appear to be somewhat _______.','greyish','Beryllium and magnesium appear to be somewhat greyish \n\n(Reference- NCERT Chemistry Class 11 (Part 2); Page 307; Paragraph 10.6.5)','Inorganic chemistry >> The s Block Elements >> Group 2 Elements- Properties and Uses',NULL,'1','mcq','blackish','whitish','bluish','greyish','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(100738,'chemistry','The melting and boiling points of alkaline earth metals are _______ than the corresponding alkali metals due to smaller sizes.','higher','The melting and boiling points of alkaline earth metals are higher than the corresponding alkali metals due to smaller sizes. \n\n(Reference- NCERT Chemistry Class 11 (Part 2); Page 307; Paragraph 10.6.5)','Inorganic chemistry >> The s Block Elements >> Group 2 Elements- Properties and Uses',NULL,'1','mcq','lower','higher','equal','none of these','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(100739,'chemistry','Why are the melting and boiling points of alkaline earth metals higher than the corresponding alkali metals?','Because of their smaller sizes','The melting and boiling points of these metals are higher than the corresponding alkali metals due to smaller sizes. \n\n(Reference- NCERT Chemistry Class 11 (Part 2); Page 307; Paragraph 10.6.5)','Inorganic chemistry >> The s Block Elements >> Group 2 Elements- Properties and Uses',NULL,'1','mcq','Because of their smaller sizes','Because of their smaller first ionisation enthalpies','Because of their large sizes','Because of their higher second ionisation enthalpies','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(100740,'chemistry','Why are group 2 elements strongly electropositive in nature?','Because of the low ionisation enthalpies,','Because of the low ionisation enthalpies, they are strongly electropositive in nature.\n \n(Reference- NCERT Chemistry Class 11 (Part 2); Page 307; Paragraph 10.6.5)','Inorganic chemistry >> The s Block Elements >> Group 2 Elements- Properties and Uses',NULL,'1','mcq','Because of the high ionisation enthalpies,','Because of their smaller sizes','Because of the low ionisation enthalpies,','Because of their smaller sizes','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(100741,'chemistry','Because of the smaller ionisation enthalpies, group 2 elements are strongly __________ in nature.','electropositive','Because of the low ionisation enthalpies, they are strongly electropositive in nature.\n \n(Reference- NCERT Chemistry Class 11 (Part 2); Page 307; Paragraph 10.6.5)','Inorganic chemistry >> The s Block Elements >> Group 2 Elements- Properties and Uses',NULL,'1','mcq','magnetic','attractive','electropositive','excitable','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(100742,'chemistry','Arrange the following elements wrt electropositive nature','Be < Mg < Ca < Sr','The electropositive character increases down the group from Be to Ba.\n\n(Reference- NCERT Chemistry Class 11 (Part 2); Page 307; Paragraph 10.6.5)','Inorganic chemistry >> The s Block Elements >> Group 2 Elements- Properties and Uses',NULL,'3','mcq','Sr < Mg < Ca < Be','Be < Mg < Ca < Sr','Sr < Ca < Mg < Be','Sr < Mg < Ca < Be','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(100743,'chemistry','Which colour does Calcium imparts to flame?','Brick red','Calcium, Strontium and Barium impart characteristic brick red, crimson and apple green colours respectively to the flame.\n\n(Reference- NCERT Chemistry Class 11 (Part 2); Page 307,308; Paragraph 10.6.5)','Inorganic chemistry >> The s Block Elements >> Group 2 Elements- Properties and Uses',NULL,'1','mcq','Crimson','Brick red','Apple green','Violet','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(100744,'chemistry','Which colour does Strontium imparts to flame?','Crimson','Calcium, Strontium and Barium impart characteristic brick red, crimson and apple green colours respectively to the flame.\n\n(Reference- NCERT Chemistry Class 11 (Part 2); Page 307,308; Paragraph 10.6.5)','Inorganic chemistry >> The s Block Elements >> Group 2 Elements- Properties and Uses',NULL,'1','mcq','Apple green','Violet','Crimson','Brick red','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(100745,'chemistry','Which colour does Barium imparts to flame?','Apple green','Calcium, Strontium and Barium impart characteristic brick red, crimson and apple green colours respectively to the flame. \n\n(Reference- NCERT Chemistry Class 11 (Part 2); Page 307,308; Paragraph 10.6.5)','Inorganic chemistry >> The s Block Elements >> Group 2 Elements- Properties and Uses',NULL,'1','mcq','Crimson','Brick red','Apple green','Violet','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(100746,'chemistry','What is the colour of alkaline earth metals?','Silvery white','The alkaline earth metals, in general, are silvery white.\n\n(Reference- NCERT Chemistry Class 11 (Part 2); Page 307; Paragraph 10.6.5)','Inorganic chemistry >> The s Block Elements >> Group 2 Elements- Properties and Uses',NULL,'1','mcq','Greyish white','Silvery white','Blackish blue','Golden yellow','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(100747,'chemistry','How do alkaline earth metals appear?','Lustrous','The alkaline earth metals, in general, are silvery white and lustrous.\n\n(Reference- NCERT Chemistry Class 11 (Part 2); Page 307; Paragraph 10.6.5)','Inorganic chemistry >> The s Block Elements >> Group 2 Elements- Properties and Uses',NULL,'1','mcq','Dull','Dim','Lustrous','Bright','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(100748,'chemistry','How do alkaline earth metals appear when touched?','Soft','The alkaline earth metals, in general, are silvery white, lustrous and relatively soft.\n \n(Reference- NCERT Chemistry Class 11 (Part 2); Page 307; Paragraph 10.6.5)','Inorganic chemistry >> The s Block Elements >> Group 2 Elements- Properties and Uses',NULL,'1','mcq','Heavy','Brittle','Rough','Soft','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(100749,'chemistry','The alkaline earth metals are ______ than the alkali metals.','Harder','The alkaline earth metals, in general, are silvery white, lustrous and relatively soft but harder than the alkali metals \n\n(Reference- NCERT Chemistry Class 11 (Part 2); Page 307; Paragraph 10.6.5)','Inorganic chemistry >> The s Block Elements >> Group 2 Elements- Properties and Uses',NULL,'1','mcq','Brittle','Harder','Brighter','Darker','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(100750,'chemistry','In flame the electrons are transferred to ______ energy levels','higher','In flame the electrons are excited to higher energy levels \n\n(Reference- NCERT Chemistry Class 11 (Part 2); Page 308; Paragraph 10.6.5)','Inorganic chemistry >> The s Block Elements >> Group 2 Elements- Properties and Uses',NULL,'1','mcq','lower','higher','second','third','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(100751,'chemistry','In flame, when electrons drop back to the ground state, energy is emitted in which form?','Visible light','In flame the electrons are excited to higher energy levels \n\n(Reference- NCERT Chemistry Class 11 (Part 2); Page 308; Paragraph 10.6.5)','Inorganic chemistry >> The s Block Elements >> Group 2 Elements- Properties and Uses',NULL,'1','mcq','Infrared energy','Visible light','Ultraviolet energy','Heat energy','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(100752,'chemistry','Which element among the following doesn\'t give flame test?','Mg','The electrons in Mg are too strongly bound to get excited by flame. \n\nHence, these elements do not impart any colour to the flame. \n\n(Reference- NCERT Chemistry Class 11 (Part 2); Page 308; Paragraph 10.6.5)','Inorganic chemistry >> The s Block Elements >> Group 2 Elements- Properties and Uses',NULL,'1','mcq','Mg','Ca','Sr','Ba','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(100753,'chemistry','Which element among the following doesn\'t give flame test?','Be','The electrons in Be are too strongly bound to get excited by flame. \n\nHence, these elements do not impart any colour to the flame. \n\n(Reference- NCERT Chemistry Class 11 (Part 2); Page 308; Paragraph 10.6.5)','Inorganic chemistry >> The s Block Elements >> Group 2 Elements- Properties and Uses',NULL,'1','mcq','Ca','Sr','Be','Ba','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(100754,'chemistry','The flame test for Ca, Sr and Ba is helpful in their detection in qualitative analysis and estimation by ______.','flame photometry','The flame test for Ca, Sr and Ba is helpful in their detection in qualitative analysis and estimation by flame photometry \n\n(Reference- NCERT Chemistry Class 11 (Part 2); Page 308; Paragraph 10.6.5)','Inorganic chemistry >> The s Block Elements >> Group 2 Elements- Properties and Uses',NULL,'1','mcq','excitation energy','ionisation energies','flame photometry','none of these','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(100755,'chemistry','Which of the following are typical characteristics of metals?','High melting points and boiling points','The alkaline earth metals like those of alkali metals have high electrical and thermal conductivities which are typical characteristics of metals \n\n(Reference- NCERT Chemistry Class 11 (Part 2); Page 308; Paragraph 10.6.5)','Inorganic chemistry >> The s Block Elements >> Group 2 Elements- Properties and Uses',NULL,'1','mcq','Low melting points and boiling points','High Iionisation energies','High melting points and boiling points','Low Iionisation energies','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(100756,'chemistry','What is the comparison between reactivity of alkaline earth metals and alkali metals?','Alkaline earth metals are less reactive','The alkaline earth metals are less reactive than the alkali metals.\n \n(Reference- NCERT Chemistry Class 11 (Part 2); Page 308; Paragraph 10.6.6)','Inorganic chemistry >> The s Block Elements >> Group 2 Elements- Properties and Uses',NULL,'1','mcq','Alkali metals are less reactive','Alkaline earth metals are less reactive','Alkaline earth metals are more reactive','Reactivity of both the groups is nearly same','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(100757,'chemistry','What is trend of reactivity of alkaline earth metals down the group?','Reactivity increases down the group','The reactivity of Group 2 elements increases on going down the group. \n\n(Reference- NCERT Chemistry Class 11 (Part 2); Page 308; Paragraph 10.6.6)','Inorganic chemistry >> The s Block Elements >> Group 2 Elements- Properties and Uses',NULL,'1','mcq','Reactivity decreases down the group','Reactivity increases down the group','Reactivity is almost same through the group','None of these','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(100758,'chemistry','Beryllium and Magnesium are kinetically ______ to Oxygen and water.','inert','Beryllium and Magnesium are kinetically inert to Oxygen and water.\n\n(Reference- NCERT Chemistry Class 11 (Part 2); Page 308; Paragraph 10.6.6)','Inorganic chemistry >> The s Block Elements >> Group 2 Elements- Properties and Uses',NULL,'1','mcq','active','inert','energetic','potent','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(100759,'chemistry','Why are Beryllium and Magnesium are kinetically inert to oxygen and water?','Because of the formation of an oxide film on their surface.','Beryllium and Magnesium are kinetically inert to oxygen and water because of the formation of an oxide film on their surface. \n\n(Reference- NCERT Chemistry Class 11 (Part 2); Page 308; Paragraph 10.6.6)','Inorganic chemistry >> The s Block Elements >> Group 2 Elements- Properties and Uses',NULL,'1','mcq','Because of its high reactivity towards nitrogen than oxygen','Because of the formation of an oxide film on their surface.','Because of the its low reactivity towards oxygen','Because of diatomicity of oxygen','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
