(100761,'chemistry','What does Magnesium gives on burning with air?','MgO Mg₃N₂','Magnesium is more electropositive and burns with dazzling brilliance in air to give MgO and Mg₃N₂. \n\n(Reference- NCERT Chemistry Class 11 (Part 2); Page 308; Paragraph 10.6.6)','Inorganic chemistry >> The s Block Elements >> Group 2 Elements- Properties and Uses',NULL,'2','mcq','MgO MgCl₂','Mg₃N₂ MgCl₂','MgCl₂ MgBr₂','MgO Mg₃N₂','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
