(100770,'chemistry','Which gas is liberated when alkaline earth metals react with acids?','Hydrogen','The alkaline earth metals readily react with acids liberating dihydrogen\n \n(Reference- NCERT Chemistry Class 11 (Part 2); Page 308; Paragraph 10.6.6)','Inorganic chemistry >> The s Block Elements >> Group 2 Elements- Properties and Uses',NULL,'1','mcq','Hydrogen','Chlorine','Oxygen','Nitrogen','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(100771,'chemistry','Which of the following is true?','Like alkali metals, the alkaline earth metals are strong reducing agents.','Like alkali metals, the alkaline earth metals are strong reducing agents. \n\n(Reference- NCERT Chemistry Class 11 (Part 2); Page 308; Paragraph 10.6.6)','Inorganic chemistry >> The s Block Elements >> Group 2 Elements- Properties and Uses',NULL,'2','mcq','Like alkali metals, the alkaline earth metals are strong reducing agents.','Unike alkali metals, the alkaline earth metals are strong reducing agents.','Like alkali metals, the alkaline earth metals are strong oxidising agents.','Unike alkali metals, the alkaline earth metals are strong oxidising agents.','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(100772,'chemistry','Reducing power of Group 2 metals is _____ to those of their corresponding alkali metals','lesser','Reducing power is less than those of their corresponding alkali metals \n\n(Reference- NCERT Chemistry Class 11 (Part 2); Page 308; Paragraph 10.6.6)','Inorganic chemistry >> The s Block Elements >> Group 2 Elements- Properties and Uses',NULL,'1','mcq','lesser','more','equal','similar','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(100773,'chemistry','Assertion : Beryllium has reducing nature \n\nReason : It has large hydration energy associated with the small size of Be⁺² ion and relatively large value of the atomization enthalpy.\n\nChoose the correct option.','Both the Assertion and the Reason are correct and the Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion','Beryllium has less negative value compared to other alkaline earth metals. \n\nHowever, its reducing nature is due to large hydration energy associated with the small size of Be2+ ion and relatively large value of the atomization enthalpy of the metal \n\n(Reference- NCERT Chemistry Class 11 (Part 2); Page 308; Paragraph 10.6.6)','Inorganic chemistry >> The s Block Elements >> Group 2 Elements- Properties and Uses',NULL,'3','mcq','Both the Assertion and the Reason are correct and the Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion','The Assertion and the Reason are correct but the Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion','The statement of the Assertion is false but the Reason is true','Both the statements are false','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
