(100841,'chemistry','2M(NO₃)₂  →  2MO + 4NO₂ + O₂ . Here M cannot be -','K','2M(NO₃)₂   →  2MO + 4NO₂ + O₂ (M = Be, Mg, Ca, Sr, Ba) \n\n(Reference- NCERT Chemistry Class 11 (Part 2); Page 309; Paragraph 10.7)','Inorganic chemistry >> The s Block Elements >> Group 2 Elements - General Characteristics',NULL,'1','mcq','Ca','Sr','Ba','K','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(100842,'chemistry','Assertion : The solubility of alkaline earth metal hydroxides in water increase down the group. \n\nReason : Since lattice enthalpy increases much more than the hydration enthalpy with increasing ionic size, the solubility increases as we go down the group.\n\nChoose the correct option.','The statement of the Reason is false but the Assertion is true.','Among alkaline earth metal hydroxides, the anion being common the cationic radius will influence the lattice enthalpy. \n\nSince lattice enthalpy decreases much more than the hydration enthalpy with increasing ionic size, the solubility increases as we go down the group. \n\nThus, the statement of the Reason is false but the Assertion is true.\n\n(Reference- NCERT Chemistry Class 11 (Part 2); Page 310; Problem 10.4)','Inorganic chemistry >> The s Block Elements >> Group 2 Elements - General Characteristics',NULL,'3','mcq','Both the Assertion and the Reason are correct and the Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.','The Assertion and the Reason are correct but the Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.','The statement of the Reason is false but the Assertion is true.','Both the statements are false.','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(100843,'chemistry','Assertion : The solubility of alkaline earth metal carbonates in water decreases down the group. \n\nReason : The hydration enthalpies decrease down the group, solubility will decrease as found for alkaline earth metal carbonates.\n\nChoose the correct option.','Both the Assertion and the Reason are correct and the Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.','The size of anions being much larger compared to cations, the lattice enthalpy will remain almost constant within a particular group. \n\nSince the hydration enthalpies decrease down the group, solubility will decrease as found for alkaline earth metal carbonates and sulphates. \n\nThus, both the Assertion and the Reason are correct and the Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion\n\n(Reference- NCERT Chemistry Class 11 (Part 2); Page 310; Problem 10.5)','Inorganic chemistry >> The s Block Elements >> Group 2 Elements - General Characteristics',NULL,'3','mcq','Both the Assertion and the Reason are correct and the Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.','The Assertion and the Reason are correct but the Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.','The statement of the Reason is false but the Assertion is true.','Both the statements are false.','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(100844,'chemistry','Assertion : The solubility of alkaline earth metal sulphates in water decreases down the group. \n\nReason : The hydration enthalpies decrease down the group, solubility will decrease as found for alkaline earth metal sulphates.\n\nChoose the correct option.','Both the Assertion and the Reason are correct and the Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion','The size of anions being much larger compared to cations, the lattice enthalpy will remain almost constant within a particular group. \n\nSince the hydration enthalpies decrease down the group, solubility will decrease as found for alkaline earth metal carbonates and sulphates. \n\nThus, both the Assertion and the Reason are correct and the Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion\n\n(Reference- NCERT Chemistry Class 11 (Part 2); Page 310; Problem 10.5)','Inorganic chemistry >> The s Block Elements >> Group 2 Elements - General Characteristics',NULL,'3','mcq','Both the Assertion and the Reason are correct and the Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion','The Assertion and the Reason are correct but the Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion','The statement of the Reason is false but the Assertion is true','Both the statements are false','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(100913,'chemistry','Beryllium and aluminium ions have _______ tendency to form complexes, BeF₄²⁻, AlF₆ ³⁻','strong','Beryllium and aluminium ions have strong tendency to form complexes, BeF₄²⁻, AlF₆ ³⁻\n \n(Reference- NCERT Chemistry Class 11 (Part 2); Page 310; Paragraph 10.8.1)','Inorganic chemistry >> The s Block Elements >> Group 2 Elements - Anomalous Behaviour of Be and Diagonal relationship',NULL,'1','mcq','strong','weak','extremely weak','slightly weak','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(101308,'chemistry','How many statements are not incorrect? \n\n1) LiCl is insoluble in acetone.\n\n2) Li is the only alkali metal to form nitride directly.\n\n3) Solution of Na₂CO₃ is acidic.\n\n4) Na is more useful than K.','2','1) LiCl is soluble in acetone.\n\n2) Li is the only alkali metal to form nitride directly.\n\n3) Solution of Na₂CO₃ is alkaline. \n\n4) Na is more useful than K.\n\n(Reference- NCERT Chemistry Class 11 (Part 2); Page 313-314; Back Exercise )','Inorganic chemistry >> The s Block Elements >> Back Exercise',NULL,'3','mcq','1','2','3','4','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(101309,'chemistry','How many statements are not correct? \n\n1) LiCl is insoluble in acetone.\n\n2) Li is the only alkali metal to form nitride directly.\n\n3) Solution of Na₂CO₃ is acidic.\n\n4) Na is more useful than K.','2','1) LiCl is soluble in acetone.\n\n2) Li is the only alkali metal to form nitride directly.\n\n3) Solution of Na₂CO₃ is alkaline. \n\n4) Na is more useful than K.\n\n(Reference- NCERT Chemistry Class 11 (Part 2); Page 313-314; Back Exercise )','Inorganic chemistry >> The s Block Elements >> Back Exercise',NULL,'3','mcq','1','2','3','4','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(101310,'chemistry','How many statements are correct? \n\n1) Alkali Metals are prepared by elecrolysis of their fused chlorides.\n\n2) K is more useful than Na.\n\n3) Solution of Na₂CO₃ is alkaline.\n\n4) BeO is soluble in water.','2','1) Alkali Metals are prepared by elecrolysis of their fused chlorides \n\n2) Na is more useful than K \n\n3) Solution of Na₂CO₃ is alkaline \n\n4) BeO is almost insoluble in water \n\n(Reference- NCERT Chemistry Class 11 (Part 2); Page 313-314; Back Exercise )','Inorganic chemistry >> The s Block Elements >> Back Exercise',NULL,'3','mcq','1','2','3','4','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(101311,'chemistry','How many statements are incorrect?\n \n1) Alkali Metals are prepared by elecrolysis of their fused chlorides.\n\n2) K is more useful than Na.\n\n3) Solution of Na₂CO₃ is alkaline.\n\n4) BeO is soluble in water.','2','1) Alkali Metals are prepared by elecrolysis of their fused chlorides \n\n2) Na is more useful than K \n\n3) Solution of Na₂CO₃ is alkaline \n\n4) BeO is almost insoluble in water \n\n(Reference- NCERT Chemistry Class 11 (Part 2); Page 313-314; Back Exercise )','Inorganic chemistry >> The s Block Elements >> Back Exercise',NULL,'3','mcq','1','2','3','4','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(101312,'chemistry','How many statements are incorrect?\n \n1) BeSO₄ is soluble in water.\n\n2) BeO is soluble in water.\n\n3) BaO is soluble in water.\n\n4) BaSO₄ is soluble in water.','2','1) BeSO₄ is soluble in water \n\n2) BeO is insoluble in water \n\n3) BaO is soluble in water \n\n4) BaSO₄ is insoluble in water \n\n(Reference- NCERT Chemistry Class 11 (Part 2); Page 313-314; Back Exercise )','Inorganic chemistry >> The s Block Elements >> Back Exercise',NULL,'3','mcq','1','2','3','4','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(101313,'chemistry','How many statements are correct?\n \n1) BeSO₄ is soluble in water.\n\n2) BeO is soluble in water.\n\n3) BaO is soluble in water.\n\n4) BaSO₄ is soluble in water.','2','1) BeSO₄ is soluble in water\n \n2) BeO is insoluble in water \n\n3) BaO is soluble in water \n\n4) BaSO₄ is insoluble in water \n\n(Reference- NCERT Chemistry Class 11 (Part 2); Page 313-314; Back Exercise )','Inorganic chemistry >> The s Block Elements >> Back Exercise',NULL,'3','mcq','1','2','3','4','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(101314,'chemistry','How many statements are incorrect? \n\n1) KI is more soluble than LiI in ethanol.\n\n2) Li is used in photoelectric cells.\n\n3) Alkali metals are obtained by chemical reduction methods.\n\n4) K₂CO₃ is prepared by Solvay process.','4','1) LiI is more soluble than KI in ethanol \n\n2) Li is not used in photoelectric cells \n\n3) Alkali metals are not obtained by chemical reduction methods \n\n4) K₂CO₃ is not prepared by Solvay process \n\n(Reference- NCERT Chemistry Class 11 (Part 2); Page 313-314; Back Exercise )','Inorganic chemistry >> The s Block Elements >> Back Exercise',NULL,'3','mcq','1','2','3','4','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(101315,'chemistry','How many statements are correct?\n \n1) KI is more soluble than LiI in ethanol.\n\n2) Li is used in photoelectric cells.\n\n3) Alkali metals are obtained by chemical reduction methods.\n\n4) K₂CO₃ is prepared by Solvay process.','0','1) LiI is more soluble than KI in ethanol \n\n2) Li is not used in photoelectric cells \n\n3) Alkali metals are not obtained by chemical reduction methods \n\n4) K₂CO₃ is not prepared by Solvay process \n\n(Reference- NCERT Chemistry Class 11 (Part 2); Page 313-314; Back Exercise )','Inorganic chemistry >> The s Block Elements >> Back Exercise',NULL,'3','mcq','0','1','2','3','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(101316,'chemistry','Arrange the following ions with respect to the mobilities of the alkali metal ions in aqueous solution.','Li⁺ < Na⁺ < K⁺ < Rb⁺','The mobilities of the alkali metal ions in aqueous solution are Li⁺<Na⁺<K⁺<Rb⁺<Cs⁺\n \n(Reference- NCERT Chemistry Class 11 (Part 2); Page 313-314; Back Exercise )','Inorganic chemistry >> The s Block Elements >> Back Exercise',NULL,'3','mcq','Rb⁺ < K⁺ < Na⁺ < Li⁺','Li⁺ < Na⁺ < K⁺ < Rb⁺','Li⁺ < K⁺ < Na⁺ < Rb⁺','Li⁺ < Na⁺ < Rb⁺ < K⁺','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
