(101642,'chemistry','Complete the following reactions\nO₂⁻ + H₂O ------→','OH⁻ +H₂O₂+O₂','2O₂⁻ + 2H₂O ------→2OH⁻ +H₂O₂+O₂','Inorganic chemistry >> The s Block Elements >> NCERT Exemplar Questions',NULL,'2','mcq','OH⁻ +H₂O₂+O₂','H₂O +O₂','O₂+ OH⁻','OH⁻ +H₂O₂','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(101701,'chemistry','The major component of portland cement is','𝐶𝑎𝑂','𝐶𝑎𝑂 present in 50 − 60% oxide. Remaining composition includes: Silica (20-25%), MgO(2-3%) etc .Reference Class 11 Chapter 10 The s-block elements Page No.312','Inorganic chemistry >> The s Block Elements >> Previous Year JEE Questions',NULL,'1','mcq','𝑀𝑔𝑂','𝐶𝑎𝑂','𝑆𝑖𝑂₂','𝐴𝑙₂𝑂₃','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(101702,'chemistry','Statement−1: Lithium forms hydrated salt.\nStatement−2 ∶ Lithium has more polarizing power than other alkali metals.','Both Statement− 1 & Statement−2 are true','Lithium Ions have smaller sizes as compared to other Ions of the group. Hence, it has a greater value of charge to radius\nratio and polarising power. Hence, it can form hydrated salts easily .Reference Class 11 Chapter 10 The s-block elements Page No.304','Inorganic chemistry >> The s Block Elements >> Previous Year JEE Questions',NULL,'2','mcq','Statement− 1 is true & Statement−2 is false','Statement− 1 is false & Statement−2 is true','Both Statement− 1 & Statement−2 are true','Both Statement−1 & Statement−2 are false','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(101703,'chemistry','Number of water of crystallization in gypsum, plaster of paris (POP) and dead burnt plaster are\nrespectively:','2,0.5,0','𝐺𝑦𝑝𝑠𝑢𝑚 = 𝐶𝑎𝑆𝑂4 ⋅ 2𝐻2𝑂\nPlaster of paris (𝑃𝑂𝑃) = 𝐶𝑎𝑆𝑂4 ⋅ 1/2 𝐻2𝑂\nDead burnt of plaster = 𝐶𝑎𝑆𝑂4','Inorganic chemistry >> The s Block Elements >> Previous Year JEE Questions',NULL,'1','mcq','2,0.5,0','0,0.5,2','2,0,0.5','0.2,2,0','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(101704,'chemistry','A s-block element (M) reacts with oxygen to form an oxide of the formula MO2. The oxide is pale yellow in colour and paramagnetic. The element','K','On combustion in excess of air,Potassium,rubidium and caesium form the superoxides,MO2 . .Reference Class 11 Chapter 10 The s-block elements Page No.303','Inorganic chemistry >> The s Block Elements >> Previous Year JEE Questions',NULL,'1','mcq','Mg','Na','Ca','K','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
