(250531,'chemistry','Write the name of missing compound in the following reaction?\ndiagram(n2507)','Cumene','Phenol is manufactured from the hydrocarbon, cumene. Cumene (isopropylbenzene) is oxidised in the presence of air to cumene hydroperoxide. It is converted to phenol and acetone by treating it with dilute acid.\n(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 332; Paragraph No. 4)','Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> Alcohols and Phenols',NULL,'3','mcq','Cumene','Aniline','Benzene','Chlorobenzene','NEW','12-332','12-202','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/250531q.png'),
