(250540,'chemistry','Arrange the following compounds in order of their increasing\nboiling points:\nPentan-1-ol, butan-1-ol, butan-2-ol, ethanol, propan-1-ol, methanol.','methanol, ethanol, propan-1-ol, butan-2-ol, butan-1-ol, pentan-1-ol','The high boiling points of alcohols are mainly due to the presence of intermolecular hydrogen bonding in them.\n(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 334; Example; 11.3)','Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> Alcohols and Phenols',NULL,'3','mcq','methanol, ethanol, propan-1-ol, butan-2-ol, butan-1-ol, pentan-1-ol','methanol, ethanol, pentan-1-ol, butan-2-ol, butan-1-ol, propan-1-ol','pentan-1-ol, butan-1-ol, butan-2-ol, propan-1-ol, ethanol, methanol','methanol, ethanol, butan-2-ol, propan-1-ol, butan-1-ol, pentan-1-ol','NEW','12-334','12-204',NULL),
