(250645,'chemistry','In case of phenol, the polarisation of bromine molecule takes place even in the absence of Lewis acid\nWhich of the above statement(s) is/are correct pertaining to the mentioned molecular reaction?','The highly activating effect of –OH group attached to the benzene ring.','In case of phenol, the polarisation of bromine molecule takes place even in the absence of Lewis acid. It is due to the highly activating effect of –OH group attached to the benzene ring.\n(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 342; Paragraph No. 2)','Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> Alcohols and Phenols 2',NULL,'2','mcq','The highly activating effect of –OH group attached to the benzene ring.','The presence of benzene ring.','The high electronegativity of bromine.','All of the above','NEW','12-342','12-212',NULL),
(250646,'chemistry','When phenol is treated with bromine water, which compound is formed?','2,4,6-tribromophenol','When phenol is treated with bromine water, 2,4,6-tribromophenol is formed.\n(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 342; Paragraph No. 3)','Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> Alcohols and Phenols 2',NULL,'1','mcq','2,6-diibromophenol','2,4,6-tribromophenol','2,3,6-tribromophenol','3,4,6-tribromophenol','NEW','12-342','12-212',NULL),
