(250648,'chemistry','On treating phenol with chloroform in the presence of sodium hydroxide, a –CHO group is introduced at ortho position of benzene ring. This reaction is known as?','Reimer - Tiemann Reaction','On treating phenol with chloroform in the presence of sodium hydroxide, a –CHO group is introduced at ortho position of benzene ring. This reaction is known as Reimer - Tiemann reaction.\n(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 343; Paragraph No. 1)','Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> Alcohols and Phenols 2',NULL,'1','mcq','Kolbe\'s Reaction','Oxidation','Williamson Synthesis','Reimer - Tiemann Reaction','NEW','12-343','12-213',NULL),
