(250950,'chemistry','The major products C and D formed in the following reactions respectively are:\ndiagram(n2546)','H₃C−CH₂−CH₂−I and I−C(CH₃)₃','Ethers react with HI to form alkyl halide and alcohol. if there is excess HI then alcohol formed will react further to give alhyl iodide.\nOdisha NEET 2019','Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> Previous Year Question',NULL,'2','mcq','H₃C−CH₂−CH₂−I and I−C(CH₃)₃','H₃C−CH₂−CH₂−OH and I−C(CH₃)₃','H₃C−CH₂−CH₂−I and HO−C(CH₃)₃','H₃C−CH₂−CH₂−OH and HO−C(CH₃)₃','NEW','12-347','12-217','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/250950q.png'),
(250951,'chemistry','The heating of phenyl methyl ether with HI produces:','phenol','In the first step HI will attack phenyl methyl ether to give oxonium ion and iodide ion. in the second step iodide ion attack on methyl group of oxonium ion and produce phenol and methyl iodide as final product.\nNEET 2017\ndiagram(ne2547)','Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> Previous Year Question',NULL,'2','mcq','iodobenzene','phenol','benzene','ethyl chloride','NEW','12-347','12-217',NULL),
(250952,'chemistry','The reaction, can be classified as:\ndiagram(n2548)','Williamson ether synthesis reaction','As the final product is an ether so it is ether formation reaction. This is not dehydration reaction as dehydration involves the removal of water molecule.\nNEET-I 2016','Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> Previous Year Question',NULL,'1','mcq','dehydration reaction','Williamson alcohol synthesis reaction','Williamson ether synthesis reaction','alcohol formation reaction.','NEW','12-345','12-215','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/250952q.png'),
(250953,'chemistry','The reaction, is Called:\ndiagram(n2549)','Williamson synthesis','williamson synthesis an important laboratory method for the preparation of symmetrical and unsymmetrical ethers. In this method, an alkyl halide is allowed to react with sodium alkoxide.\nNEET 2015','Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> Previous Year Question',NULL,'1','mcq','Etard reaction','Gattermann-Koch reaction','Williamson synthesis','Williamson continuous etherification process.','NEW','12-345','12-215','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/250953q.png'),
