(250955,'chemistry','Identify Z in the sequence of reactions:\ndiagram(n2550)','CH₃—(CH₂)₃ — O — CH₂CH₃','First alkene will convert into 1-Bromobutane which will further react with C₂H₅ONa to give CH₃—(CH₂)₃ — O — CH₂CH₃ as a final product.\nNEET 2014','Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> Previous Year Question',NULL,'2','mcq','CH₃—(CH₂)₃ — O — CH₂CH₃','(CH₃)₂CH — O — CH₂CH₃','CH₃(CH₂)₄ — O — CH₃','CH₃CH₂— CH(CH₃) — O— CH₂CH₃','NEW','12-345','12-215','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/250955q.png'),
(250956,'chemistry','Among the following ethers, which one will produce methyl alcohol on treatment with hot concentrated HI?\ndiagram(n2551)','a','This is an example of Nucleophilic substituion reaction of ether. Primary and secondary ethers react with HX through Sɴ2 mechanism and produce alcohol with most substituted carbon atom. but tertiary ethers react with HX through Sɴ1 and produce alcohol with less substituted carbon.\nNEET 2013','Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> Previous Year Question',NULL,'2','mcq','a','b','c','d','NEW','12-345','12-215','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/250956q.png'),
(250957,'chemistry','In the reaction, which of the following compounds will be formed?\ndiagram(n2552)','c','This is an example of Nucleophilic substituion reaction of ether. Primary and secondary ethers react with HX through Sɴ2 mechanism and produce alcohol with most substituted carbon atom. but tertiary ethers react with HX through Sɴ1 and produce alcohol with less substituted carbon.\nNEET 2007','Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> Previous Year Question',NULL,'2','mcq','a','b','c','d','NEW','12-345','12-215','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/250957q.png'),
