(250959,'chemistry','Ethyl chloride is converted into diethyl ether by:','Williamson’s synthesis','It is an important laboratory method for the preparation of symmetrical and unsymmetrical ethers. In this method, an alkyl halide is allowed to react with sodium alkoxide.\nNEET 1999','Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> Previous Year Question',NULL,'1','mcq','Perkins reaction','Grignard reaction','Wurtz synthesis','Williamson’s synthesis','NEW',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(250960,'chemistry','Which one of the following compounds is resistant to nucleophilic attack by hydroxyl ions?','Diethyl ether','Nucleophile attack on those atoms which bear partial positive charge while in diethyl ether no carbon atom posses partial positive charge that,s why OH⁻ will not attack . but on other compound carbon has partial poitive charge due to unsaturation so OH⁻ will attack those compounds.\nNEET 1998','Organic Chemistry >> Alcohols, Phenols and Ether >> Previous Year Question',NULL,'1','mcq','Diethyl ether','Acetonitrile','Acetamide','Methyl acetate','NEW','12-345','12-215',NULL),
