(290351,'chemistry','What is -|-CH₂— CH(C₆H₅ )n?','homopolymer','It is a homopolymer and the monomer from which it is obtained is styrene.\n \n Reference : (NCERT Class-12 Page- 436 Paragraph-Example)','Organic chemistry >> Polymers >> Types of polymerisation reactions',NULL,'2','mcq','homopolymer','copolymer','Both a and b','Neither a or b','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(290352,'chemistry','Repetitive condensation reaction between two bi-functional or trifunctional mono-meric units forms :','nylon 6','Condensation type of polymerisation generally involves a repetitive condensation reaction between two bi-functional or trifunctional mono-meric units.\n \n Reference : (NCERT Class-12 Page- 437 Paragraph-1)','Organic chemistry >> Polymers >> Types of polymerisation reactions',NULL,'1','mcq','polythene','teflon','nylon 6','polyacrylonitrile','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(290353,'chemistry','When polymerisation involves a repetitive condensation reaction between two bi-functional monomers. Some small molecules like water, alcohol etc, are lost. This polymerisation is known as','step-growth polymerisation','In these reactions, the product of each step is again a bi-functional species and the sequence of condensation goes on. \n \n Since, each step produces a distinct functionalised species and is independent of each other, this process is also called as step growth polymerisation.\n \n Reference : (NCERT Class-12 Page- 437 Paragraph-2)','Organic chemistry >> Polymers >> Types of polymerisation reactions',NULL,'2','mcq','addition polymerisation','step-growth polymerisation','Both (a) or (b)','Neither (a) nor (b)','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(290354,'chemistry','Condensation polymer is not formed by loss of','ammonia','These polycondensation reactions may result in the loss of some simple molecules as water, alcohol, hydrogen chloride, etc., and lead to the formation of high molecular mass condensation polymers.\n \n Reference : (NCERT Class-12 Page- 437 Paragraph-1)','Organic chemistry >> Polymers >> Types of polymerisation reactions',NULL,'1','mcq','water','hydrogen chloride','alcohol','ammonia','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(290355,'chemistry','Which of them is not true for condensation polymers?\n \n a. The polycondensation reactions leads to formation of high molecular mass condensation polymers\n \n b. The product of each step is also a bifunctional species\n \n c. Each step produce distinct functionalised species and is dependent of each other\n \n d. Also called as step growth polymerisation','c','These polycondensation reactions may result in the loss of some simple molecules as water, alcohol, hydrogen chloride, etc., and lead to the formation of high molecular mass condensation polymers.\n \n In these reactions, product of each step is again a bifunctional species and the sequence of condensation goes on. \n \n Since each step produces a distinct functionalised species and is independent of each other, this process is also called step growth polymerisation.\n \n Reference : (NCERT Class-12 Page- 437 Paragraph-1, Paragraph-2)','Organic chemistry >> Polymers >> Types of polymerisation reactions',NULL,'2','mcq','a','b','c','d','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(290356,'chemistry','Monomer used for formation of Dacron is ?','Ethylene glycol,Terepthalic acid','The formation of terylene or dacron by the interaction of ethylene glycol and terephthalic acid is an example of this type of polymerisation.\n \n Reference : (NCERT Class-12 Page- 437 Paragraph-3)','Organic chemistry >> Polymers >> Types of polymerisation reactions',NULL,'1','mcq','Caprolactum','Adipic acid, Hexamethylenediamine','Ethylene glycol,Terepthalic acid','Phenol, Formaldehyde','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(290357,'chemistry','Identify the product in the given diagram(n2912)','terylene','The formation of terylene or dacron by the interaction of ethylene glycol and terephthalic acid is an example of this type of polymerisation.\n \n Reference : (NCERT Class-12 Page- 437 Paragraph-3)','Organic chemistry >> Polymers >> Types of polymerisation reactions',NULL,'3','mcq','teflon','HDP','terylene','orlon','DELETED',NULL,NULL,'/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/290357q.png'),
(290358,'chemistry','Nylons are the polymers possessing','amide linkage','These polymers possessing amide linkages are important examples of synthetic fibres and are termed as nylons.\n \n Reference : (NCERT Class-12 Page- 437 Paragraph-4)','Organic chemistry >> Polymers >> Types of polymerisation reactions',NULL,'1','mcq','dicarboxylic acids and diols','amino groups','amide linkage','All of the above','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(290359,'chemistry','Nylon 6, 6 can be prepare by all, except','monoamines with dicarboxylic acids','The general method of preparation consists of the condensation polymerisation of diamines with dicarboxylic acids or condensation of amino acids or their lactams.\n \n Reference : (NCERT Class-12 Page- 437 Paragraph-4)','Organic chemistry >> Polymers >> Types of polymerisation reactions',NULL,'2','mcq','diamines with dicarboxylic acids','condensation of amino acids','condensation of their lactams','monoamines with dicarboxylic acids','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(290360,'chemistry','The product of the given reaction in diagram(n2913)','nylon-6,6','Nylon 6,6: It is prepared by the condensation polymerisation of hexamethylenediamine with adipic acid under high pressure and at high temperature.\n \n Reference : (NCERT Class-12 Page- 437 Paragraph-5)','Organic chemistry >> Polymers >> Types of polymerisation reactions',NULL,'3','mcq','nylon-6','nylon-6,6','teflon','bakelite','DELETED',NULL,NULL,'/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/290360q.png'),
(290361,'chemistry','The high tensile strength of nylon-6,6 is attributed to','H-bond','It possess high tensile strength. This characteristic can be attributed to the strong intermolecular forces like hydrogen bonding.\n \n Reference : (NCERT Class-12 Page- 437 Paragraph-6)','Organic chemistry >> Polymers >> Types of polymerisation reactions',NULL,'1','mcq','H-bond','amide bond','networking','branching','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(290362,'chemistry','The close packing of chains of nylon-6,6 impart its','crystalline nature','These strong forces also lead to close packing of chains and thus impart crystalline nature.\n \n Reference : (NCERT Class-12 Page- 437 Paragraph-6)','Organic chemistry >> Polymers >> Types of polymerisation reactions',NULL,'1','mcq','tensile strength','crystalline nature','crease resistance','amorphous nature','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(290363,'chemistry','Nylon-6,6 is used in all, except','ropes','Nylon 6, 6 is used in making sheets, bristles for brushes and in textile industry.\n \n Reference : (NCERT Class-12 Page- 437 Paragraph-7)','Organic chemistry >> Polymers >> Types of polymerisation reactions',NULL,'1','mcq','sheets','bristles','textiles','ropes','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(290364,'chemistry','Identify the reactant of the given polymerisation reaction in diagram(n2914)','caprolactum','Nylon 6: It is obtained by heating caprolactum with water at a high temperature.\n \n Reference : (NCERT Class-12 Page- 437 Paragraph-8)','Organic chemistry >> Polymers >> Types of polymerisation reactions',NULL,'3','mcq','caprolactum','hexamethylenediamine','adipic acid','terephthalic acid','DELETED',NULL,NULL,'/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/290364q.png'),
(290365,'chemistry','Nylon 6 is used in all , except','sheets','Nylon 6 is used for the manufacture of tyre cords, fabrics and ropes. Nylon 6,6 is used in making sheets, bristles for brushes and in textile industry\n \n Reference : (NCERT Class-12 Page- 438 Paragraph-1, Page-437 Paragraph 7)','Organic chemistry >> Polymers >> Types of polymerisation reactions',NULL,'1','mcq','tyre cords','fabrics','sheets','ropes','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(290366,'chemistry','Condensation products of dicarboxylic acids and diols is','Terylene','Polyesters \n \n These are the polycondensation products of dicarboxylic acids and diols. \n \n Dacron or terylene is the best known example of polyesters.\n \n Reference : (NCERT Class-12 Page- 438 Paragraph-2)','Organic chemistry >> Polymers >> Types of polymerisation reactions',NULL,'1','mcq','Polyamides','Bakelite','Terylene','All of the above','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(290367,'chemistry','Best known example of polyesters?','dacron','Polyesters \n \n These are the polycondensation products of dicarboxylic acids and diols. \n \n Dacron or terylene is the best known example of polyesters.\n \n Reference : (NCERT Class-12 Page- 438 Paragraph-2)','Organic chemistry >> Polymers >> Types of polymerisation reactions',NULL,'1','mcq','teflon','dacron','orlon','nylon-6,6','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(290368,'chemistry','Dacron is made by heating a mixture of ethylene glycol and terephthalic acid at what temperature?','420 to 460 K','It is manufactured by heating a mixture of ethylene glycol and terephthalic acid at 420 to 460 K in the presence of zinc acetate-antimony trioxide catalyst.\n \n Reference : (NCERT Class-12 Page- 438 Paragraph-2)','Organic chemistry >> Polymers >> Types of polymerisation reactions',NULL,'1','mcq','320 to 360 K','520 to 560 K','420 to 460 K','533 to 640 K','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(290369,'chemistry','Dacron is made by heating a mixture of ethylene glycol and terephthalic acid in the presence of catalyst?','zinc acetate-antimony trioxide','It is manufactured by heating a mixture of ethylene glycol and terephthalic acid at 420 to 460 K in the presence of zinc acetate-antimony trioxide catalyst.\n \n Reference : (NCERT Class-12 Page- 438 Paragraph-2)','Organic chemistry >> Polymers >> Types of polymerisation reactions',NULL,'1','mcq','Ziegler-Natta','Titanium tetrachloride and triphenylaluminium','zinc acetate-antimony trioxide','antimony oxide','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(290370,'chemistry','Polymer used in making safety helmets','terylene','Dacron fibre (terylene) is crease resistant and is used in blending with cotton and wool fibres and also as glass reinforcing materials in safety helmets, etc.\n \n Reference : (NCERT Class-12 Page- 438 Paragraph-2)','Organic chemistry >> Polymers >> Types of polymerisation reactions',NULL,'1','mcq','caprolactum','acrilan','orlon','terylene','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(290371,'chemistry','Which of them is not the oldest synthetic polymer','melamine','Phenol – formaldehyde polymers are the oldest synthetic polymers. \n \n These are obtained by the condensation reaction of phenol with formaldehyde in the presence of either an acid or a base catalyst.\n \n Reference : (NCERT Class-12 Page- 438 Paragraph-3)','Organic chemistry >> Polymers >> Types of polymerisation reactions',NULL,'1','mcq','bakelite','novolac','melamine','PHBV','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(290372,'chemistry','When the reaction initiates between the phenol and formaldehyde to give bakelite. This initial reaction is an example of','aromatic electrophilic substitution','The reaction starts with the initial formation of o-and/or p-hydroxymethylphenol derivatives, which further react with phenol to form compounds having rings joined to each other through–CH2 groups. \n \n The initial product could be a linear product – Novolac used in paints.\n \n Reference : (NCERT Class-12 Page- 438 Paragraph-3)','Organic chemistry >> Polymers >> Types of polymerisation reactions',NULL,'2','mcq','aromatic nucleophilic substitution','aldol condensation','aromatic electrophilic substitution','free radical reaction','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(290373,'chemistry','Novolac on heating with formaldehyde undergoes cross linking to form :','Bakelite','Novolac on heating with formaldehyde undergoes cross linking to form an infusible solid mass called bakelite.\n \n Bakelite is thermosetting polymer because it cannot be reused or remoulded.\n \n Reference : (NCERT Class-12 Page- 438 Paragraph-3)','Organic chemistry >> Polymers >> Types of polymerisation reactions',NULL,'1','mcq','Natural rubber','Paints','Bakelite','PHBV','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(290374,'chemistry','Which among the following is not a thermosetting polymer','dacron','Bakelite is thermosetting polymer which cannot be reused or remoulded.\n \n Reference : (NCERT Class-12 Page- 438 Paragraph-3)','Organic chemistry >> Polymers >> Types of polymerisation reactions',NULL,'1','mcq','novolac','bakelite','melamine','dacron','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
