(281239,'chemistry','Which of the following statements about enzymes is true?','Enzymes are highly specific both in binding chiral substrates and in catalysing their reactions.','Enzymes are highly specific both in binding chiral substrates and in catalysing their reactions.\n (1995)','Organic chemistry >> Biomolecules >> Previous year question',NULL,'2','mcq','Enzymes catalyse chemical reactions by increasing the activation energy.','Enzymes are highly specific both in binding chiral substrates and in catalysing their reactions.','Enzymes lack in nucleophilic groups.','Pepsin is proteolytic enzyme.','NEW','12-425','12-295',NULL),
(281240,'chemistry','Enzymes take part in a reaction and?','Increase the rate of a chemical reaction.','Enzymes being biocatalyst increases the rate of a chemical reaction by providing alternative lower activation energy pathways.\n (1993)','Organic chemistry >> Biomolecules >> Previous year question',NULL,'2','mcq','Decrease the rate of a chemical reaction.','Increase the rate of a chemical reaction.','Both (a) and (b)','None of these','NEW','12-425','12-295',NULL),
(281241,'chemistry','Deficiency of vitamin B1 causes the disease?','Beri-beri','Deficiency of vitamin B₁ causes Beri-beri.\n Deficiency of vitamin B₆ causes convulsions.\n Deficiency of vitamin B₂ causes Cheilosis.\n Deficiency of vitamin E causes Sterility.\n (2012)','Organic chemistry >> Biomolecules >> Previous year question',NULL,'1','mcq','Convulsions','Beri-beri','Cheilosis','Sterility','NEW','12-426','12-296',NULL),
