(281248,'chemistry','In DNA, the complementary bases are?','Adenine and Thymine; Guanine and Cytosine','DNA contains two types of nitrogenous bases;\n Purine → Adenine (A) and Guanine (G)\n Pyrimidine → Cytosine (C) and Thymine (T)\n The purine and pyrimidine bases pair only in certain combination. Adenine pairs with thymine (A : T) by two hydrogen bonds and guanine with cytosine (G : C) by three hydrogen bonds.\n (2008, 1998)','Organic chemistry >> Biomolecules >> Previous year question',NULL,'3','mcq','Adenine and Guanine; Thymine and Cytosine','Uracil and Adenine; Cytosine and Guanine','Adenine and Thymine; Guanine and Cytosine','Adenine and Thymine; Guanine and Uracil.','NEW','12-428','12-298',NULL),
(281249,'chemistry','RNA and DNA are chiral molecules, their chirality is due to?','D-sugar component','The constituents of nucleic acids are nitrogenous bases, sugar and phosphoric acid. The sugar present in DNA is D(–)-2-deoxyribose and the sugar present in RNA is D(–)-ribose. Due to these D(–)-sugar components, DNA and RNA molecules are chiral molecules.\n (2007)','Organic chemistry >> Biomolecules >> Previous year question',NULL,'3','mcq','Chiral bases','Chiral phosphate ester units','D-sugar component','L-sugar component','NEW','12-428','12-298',NULL),
(281250,'chemistry','A sequence of how many nucleotides in messenger RNA makes a codon for an amino acid?','Three','The four bases in mRNA : adenine, cytosine, guanine and uracil have been shown to act in the form of triplets; each triplet behaving as a code for the synthesis of a particular amino acid.\n (2004)','Organic chemistry >> Biomolecules >> Previous year question',NULL,'2','mcq','Three','Four','One','Two','NEW',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(281251,'chemistry','Chargaff\'s rule states that in an organism?','Amount of adenine (A) is equal to that of thymine (T) and the amount of guanine (G) is equal to that of cytosine (C).','Chargaff\'s rule states that in an organism amount of A = T and that of G = C.\n (2003)','Organic chemistry >> Biomolecules >> Previous year question',NULL,'3','mcq','Amount of adenine (A) is equal to that of thymine (T) and the amount of guanine (G) is equal to that of cytosine (C).','Amount of adenine (A) is equal to that of guanine (G) and the amount of thymine (T) is equal to that of cytosine (C).','Amount of adenine (A) is equal to that of cytosine (C) and the amount of thymine (T) is equal to that of guanine (G).','Amounts of all bases are equal.','NEW',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(281252,'chemistry','Which of the following is correct about H-bonding in nucleotide?','A – T, G – C','The structure of DNA molecule is a double helix made up of polynucleotide chains which are held together by H-bonds. \n In these helices the adenine (A) base is linked with thymine (T) by H-bonds and guanine (G) is linked with cytosine (C) by H-bonds as A≡T, and G≡C.\n (2001)','Organic chemistry >> Biomolecules >> Previous year question',NULL,'1','mcq','A – T, G – C','A – G , T – C','G – T, A – C','A – A, T – T','NEW','12-429','12-299',NULL),
(281253,'chemistry','An example of biopolymer is?','DNA','DNA is an example of biopolymer.\n (1994)','Organic chemistry >> Biomolecules >> Previous year question',NULL,'1','mcq','Teflon','Neoprene','Nylon-6, 6','DNA','NEW','12-427','12-297',NULL),
(281254,'chemistry','The couplings between base units of DNA is through?','Hydrogen bonding','The structure of DNA molecule is a double helix structure. \n In this structure double helix are made up of polynucleotide chains which are held together by Hydrogen bonds.\n (1992)','Organic chemistry >> Biomolecules >> Previous year question',NULL,'2','mcq','Hydrogen bonding','Electrostatic bonding','Covalent bonding','Van der Waals’ forces.','NEW','12-429','12-299',NULL),
(281255,'chemistry','Which of the following hormones is produced under the conditions of stress which stimulate glycogenolysis in the liver of human beings?','Adrenaline','Adrenaline hormone helps to release fatty acids from fat and glucose from liver glycogen under the condition of stress. \n Hence, it is also called ‘flight or fight hormone’\n (2014)','Organic chemistry >> Biomolecules >> Previous year question',NULL,'1','mcq','Thyroxin','Insulin','Adrenaline','Estradiol','NEW',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(281256,'chemistry','Which of the following hormones contains iodine?','Thyroxine','Thyroid hormones produces two hormones that are released by the thyroid gland namely triiodothyronine (T3) and thyroxine(T4). \n These are tyrosine-based hormones that are responsible for the regulation of metabolism. \n These two hormones are partially composed of iodine.\n (2009)','Organic chemistry >> Biomolecules >> Previous year question',NULL,'2','mcq','Testosterone','Adrenaline','Thyroxine','Insulin','NEW','12-431','12-301',NULL),
