(110817,'chemistry','Greater the reduction potential greater will be the','all of these','greater the reduction potential greater will be ability to oxidize itself, and \n get more oxidation no. and more electropositive.\n Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11;Page 319; Problem 11.1))','Inorganic Chemistry >> The p-Block elements >> Group 13-Chemical properties',NULL,'2','mcq','Reducing power','Electropositivity','oxidation no.','all of these','NEW','11-319',NULL,NULL),
(111204,'chemistry','Boron triflouride reacts with lewis bases by making','Co-ordinate Covalent bond','Lewis base donate electrons to empty p orbital of boron by making co-\n ordinate Covalent bond, Donar lewis base and acceptor Boron ,\n Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11;Page 320; Paragraph No.2)','Inorganic Chemistry >> The p-Block elements >> Group 13-elements-Important trends and anomalous properties of boron',NULL,'2','mcq','Metallic bond','Hydrogen bond','Co-ordinate Covalent bond','Ionic Bond','NEW','11-320',NULL,NULL),
