(111803,'chemistry','Covalent radius significantly increase from C to Si but from Si to Pb , a small increase in radius occurs , this is due to,','Completely filled d or f subshell','As along group shell no.change , from third to onwards periods, no.of\n subshell incraeses, heavier members have completely filled d or f sub-\n shells,these subshells produce very low screening effect, so size remain\n almost same from Ge to pb.\n Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11;Page 323; Paragraph No.4)','Inorganic Chemistry >> The p-Block elements >> Group 14-elements-Electronic Configuration',NULL,'2','mcq','involvement of d subshell','Completely filled d or f subshell','screening effect','inert pair effect','NEW','11-323',NULL,NULL),
(112001,'chemistry','Ionization Energy of C family is ________ than B family','higher','The size of Carbon family is smaller as compared to B family, smaller\n the size difficult will be the removal of electron, large amount of Energy\n required , that\'s why C family have higher ionization enthalpies.\n Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11;Page 323; Paragraph No.5)','Inorganic Chemistry >> The p-Block elements >> Group 14-elements-Ionization Energy',NULL,'2','fillup','hi,gh,er,lo,wer,',NULL,NULL,NULL,'NEW','11-323',NULL,NULL),
(112002,'chemistry','Ionization Energy of C family decrease as we move','Top to bottom','Down the group size inrease,so easy to remove electron due to less \n hold of nucleus on outermost electrons, so ionization energy decrease\n Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11;Page 323; Paragraph No.5)','Inorganic Chemistry >> The p-Block elements >> Group 14-elements-Ionization Energy',NULL,'1','mcq','Left to right','Right to left','Top to bottom','bottom to top','NEW','11-323',NULL,NULL),
(112003,'chemistry','There is slight increase in Ionization enthalpy from Sn to Pb due to','poor screening effect','From Sn to Pb ,there are completely filled d or f- subshell, which are diff-\n used in nature , cause poor screening effect ,that\'s why ionization E \n instead of decrease starts incraesing.\n Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11;Page 323; Paragraph No.5)','Inorganic Chemistry >> The p-Block elements >> Group 14-elements-Ionization Energy',NULL,'2','mcq','high screening effect','inert pair effect','poor screening effect','increase in size','NEW','11-323',NULL,NULL),
(112004,'chemistry','The elements of C family are more Electronegative than B-family due to','small size','Small size,high ionization energy,high electron affinity, high abilty to \n attract electrons itself,so high will be the electronegativity\n Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11;Page 323; Paragraph No.6)','Inorganic Chemistry >> The p-Block elements >> Group 14-elements-Ionization Energy',NULL,'2','mcq','large size','small size','Low Ionization E','Low Electron Affinity','NEW','11-323',NULL,NULL),
