(112403,'chemistry','Oxides in higher oxidation state are generally','acidic','Higher the oxidation state,higher will be the electronegativity, moreover\n High negative charge on oxygen increase its polarization,more power to\n to attract electrons thus more acidic.\n Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11;Page 324; Paragraph No.3)','Inorganic Chemistry >> The p-Block elements >> Group 14-elements-Reactivity towards Oxygen',NULL,'2','mcq','Basic','acidic','Neutral','amphoteric','NEW','11-324',NULL,NULL),
