(112602,'chemistry','Which halide of group 14 is more Covalent (X=Br,Cl,I)','MX₄','MX₄ is more Covalent as it have Central Atom in its maximum positive\n oxidation state(4+), more oxidation state, more will be polarization,\n more will be the covalentb character\n Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11;Page 324; Paragraph No.6)','Inorganic Chemistry >> The p-Block elements >> Group 14-elements-Reactivity towards Halogens',NULL,'2','mcq','MX₅','MX₃','MX₄','MX₂','NEW','11-324',NULL,NULL),
