(112604,'chemistry','Stability of MX₂ of Carbon family increase as we move','top to bottom','Down the group due to involvement of d or f subshell,inert pair effect\n operate which only allow np electrons to participate in bonding,\n Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11;Page 324; Paragraph No.6)','Inorganic Chemistry >> The p-Block elements >> Group 14-elements-Reactivity towards Halogens',NULL,'2','mcq','top to bottom','bottom to top','left to right','right to left','NEW','11-324',NULL,NULL),
(112605,'chemistry','which tetra halide is not hydrolysed by water','CCl₄','CCl₄ is not hydrolysed by water as it don\'t have d subshell to accomo-\n date the electrons from oxygen of water,while all other memebrs have d-\n subshell and easily hydrolysed by water\n Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11;Page 325; Paragraph No.1)','Inorganic Chemistry >> The p-Block elements >> Group 14-elements-Reactivity towards Halogens',NULL,'2','mcq','SnCl₄','CCl₄','SiCl₄','GeCl₄','NEW','11-325',NULL,NULL),
(112606,'chemistry','SiCl₄ undergo hydrolysis by accepting lone pairs from water in d-subshell and form','Si(OH)₄','SiCl₄ is hydrolysed by water as it have d subshell to accomo-\n date the electrons from oxygen of water,similarly all other memebrs have \n d-subshell and easily hydrolysed by water\n Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11;Page 325; Paragraph No.1)','Inorganic Chemistry >> The p-Block elements >> Group 14-elements-Reactivity towards Halogens',NULL,'2','mcq','Si(OH)₂Cl₂','Si(OH)Cl₃','Si(OH)₄','Si(OH)₃Cl','NEW','11-325',NULL,NULL),
(112607,'chemistry','[SiF₆]²⁻ is known whereas [SiCl₆]²⁻, is not known due to','both a and b','Six large chloride ions cannot be accomodated around Si⁴⁺ due to limita-\n tion of its size,moreover due to size difference,interactions between Si⁴⁺\n and Cl is not very strong \n Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11;Page 325; Problem no.11.6 )','Inorganic Chemistry >> The p-Block elements >> Group 14-elements-Reactivity towards Halogens',NULL,'2','mcq','Large size of Chlorine','small size of Si','both a and b','less electronegativity of Cl','NEW','11-325',NULL,NULL),
(112608,'chemistry','The central atom in MX₄ have hybridization','sp³','Since central atom is making four bonds ,so four hybrid orbitals required\n to make four sigma bond, sp³ have four hybrid orbitals(one s and 3 p)\n Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11;Page 325; Paragraph No.2)','Inorganic Chemistry >> The p-Block elements >> Group 14-elements-Reactivity towards Halogens',NULL,'2','mcq','sp','sp³d²','sp³','sp²','NEW','11-325',NULL,NULL),
