(112610,'chemistry','SnF₄,PbF₄, are','Ionic','SnF₄,PbF₄ are ionic due to presence of highly electronegative flourine\n greater the electronegative difference greater will be the ionic character\n Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11;Page 325; Paragraph No.2)','Inorganic Chemistry >> The p-Block elements >> Group 14-elements-Reactivity towards Halogens',NULL,'2','mcq','Covalent','Ionic','Metallic','Reactive','NEW','11-325',NULL,NULL),
(112611,'chemistry','PbI₄ is not formed due to','not release enough E to excite 6s electrons','when Pb-I bond form initially, it do not release enough amount of E to\n excite the 6s electron to 6p empty orbital, that,s why it only have two un-\n paired electrons for bonding can\'t make PbI₄,\n Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11;Page 325; Paragraph No.2)','Inorganic Chemistry >> The p-Block elements >> Group 14-elements-Reactivity towards Halogens',NULL,'2','mcq','not release enough E to excite 6s electrons','Iodine is highly inert','iodine is less electronegative','iodine have complete subshell','NEW','11-325',NULL,NULL),
