(112707,'chemistry','C=S bond have ______ bonding','pㄫ-dㄫ','since sulfur have d-subshell which it can use to make multiple bonds,\n while Carbon have only p to make multiple bond that\'s why the type of\n bonding between C=S is pㄫ-dㄫ,\n Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11;Page 325; Paragraph no. 5)','Inorganic Chemistry >> The p-Block elements >> Group 14-elements-Important trends and anomalous behaviour of carbon',NULL,'2','mcq','dㄫ-dㄫ','pㄫ-dㄫ','pㄫ-pㄫ','fㄫ-pㄫ','NEW','11-325',NULL,NULL),
(112708,'chemistry','Heavier atoms of group 14 can\'t make _______','pㄫ-pㄫ','Heavier members have diffused d or f subshell, these atomic orbitals\n are too large to allow effective overlaping,that\'s why pㄫ-pㄫ is not shown\n by them.\n Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11;Page 325; Paragraph no. 5)','Inorganic Chemistry >> The p-Block elements >> Group 14-elements-Important trends and anomalous behaviour of carbon',NULL,'2','fillup','pㄫ-,pㄫ,dㄫ-,dㄫ.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'NEW','11-325',NULL,NULL),
(112709,'chemistry','The Tendency to show catenation decrease along ______','Top to bottom','As we move down size increase ,electronegativity decrease,bond length\n increase bond strength decrease, C-C bond is stronger bond which allow\n C to make chains ,while all other members make weak bond ,which pre-\n vents them to be self linked,that\'s why this property decrease along \n group\n Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11;Page 325; Paragraph no. 5)','Inorganic Chemistry >> The p-Block elements >> Group 14-elements-Important trends and anomalous behaviour of carbon',NULL,'2','mcq','Bottom to top','Top to bottom','Left to right','Right to left','NEW','11-325',NULL,NULL),
(112710,'chemistry','The order of Catenation is _____','C>>Si>Ge=Sn','As we move down size increase ,electronegativity decrease,bond length\n increase bond strength decrease, C-C bond is stronger bond which allow\n C to make chains ,while all other members make weak bond ,which pre-\n vents them to be self linked,that\'s why this property decrease along \n group\n Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11;Page 325; Paragraph no. 5)','Inorganic Chemistry >> The p-Block elements >> Group 14-elements-Important trends and anomalous behaviour of carbon',NULL,'2','mcq','C>>Si>Ge=Sn','Si>>C>Ge=Sn','C>>Si>Sn=Ge','C>>Si>Pb=Sn','NEW','11-325',NULL,NULL),
(112711,'chemistry','Bond enthalpies of group 14 are in order','C-C>Si-Si>Ge-Ge>Sn-Sn','As we move down the group size increase,which leads to increase in \n bond length,bond length and bond stregth are inversly linked,more \n bond length,smaller strength,less energy required to break the bond,\n Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11;Page 325; Table)','Inorganic Chemistry >> The p-Block elements >> Group 14-elements-Important trends and anomalous behaviour of carbon',NULL,'2','mcq','C-C>Si-Si>Ge-Ge>Sn-Sn','C-C<Si-Si<Ge-Ge<Sn-Sn','C-C>Ge-Ge>Si-Si>Sn-Sn','Sn-Sn>Si-Si>Ge-Ge>C-C','NEW','11-325',NULL,NULL),
