(120216,'chemistry','Choose the correct option regarding the following assertion(A) and reason(R)\n Assertion: Hybridisation influences bond length and bond enthalpy in organic compounds.\n Reason: More the s character of hybrid orbital, shorter and stronger will be the bond.','Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is the correct explanation of Assertion','Hybridisation influences bond length and bond enthalpy in organic compounds. More the s character of hybrid orbital, shorter and stronger will be the bond. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 335; Paragraph No.2)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Tetravalence of carbon and shapes of compounds',NULL,'3','mcq','Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is the correct explanation of Assertion','Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion','Assertion is true but Reason is false.','Assertion is false but Reason is true.','NEW','11-335','11-257',NULL),
(120217,'chemistry','Choose the correct option regarding the following assertion(A) and reason(R)\n \n Assertion: sp³ hybrid carbon is more electronegative than sp hybrid carbon atom.\n \n Reason: sp hybrid orbitals are more closer to the nucleus than sp³','Assertion is false but Reason is true.','sp hybrid carbon is more electronegative than sp³. sp hybrid orbitals are more closer to the nucleus. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 335; Paragraph No.2)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Tetravalence of carbon and shapes of compounds',NULL,'3','mcq','Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is the correct explanation of Assertion','Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion','Assertion is true but Reason is false.','Assertion is false but Reason is true.','NEW','11-335','11-257',NULL),
(120218,'chemistry','Choose the correct option regarding the following assertion(A) and reason(R)\n Assertion: Rotation about (C=C) is restricted.\n Reason: Electron charge cloud of the sigma and pi bond is located above and below the plane of bonding atoms.','Assertion is true but Reason is false.','Rotation about (C=C) is restricted. Electron charge cloud of the pi bond is located above and below the plane of bonding atoms. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 335; Paragraph No.3)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Tetravalence of carbon and shapes of compounds',NULL,'3','mcq','Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is the correct explanation of Assertion','Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion','Assertion is true but Reason is false.','Assertion is false but Reason is true.','NEW','11-335','11-257',NULL),
(120219,'chemistry','π bonds provide the _________ centres in the molecules containing multiple bonds.','Most Reactive','In general,π bonds provide the most reactive centres in the molecules containing multiple bonds. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 335; Paragraph No.3)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Tetravalence of carbon and shapes of compounds',NULL,'1','mcq','Chiral','Most Reactive','Least Reactive','None of these','NEW','11-335','11-257',NULL),
(120220,'chemistry','In which of the following molecule, all atoms lie in a same plane?','CH₂=CH₂','In CH₂=CH₂ molecule all the atoms must be in the same plane. The p orbitals are mutually parallel and both the p orbitals are perpendicular to the plane of the molecule. Rotation of one CH2 fragment with respect to other interferes with maximum overlap of p orbitals and, therefore, such rotation about carbon-carbon double bond (C=C) is restricted. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 335; Paragraph No.3)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Tetravalence of carbon and shapes of compounds',NULL,'2','mcq','CH₃CH₃','CH₂=CH₂','H₂C-H-CH₃','CH₃-CH₃','NEW','11-335','11-257',NULL),
(120221,'chemistry','Why is sp hybrid orbital is more electronegative than sp2 and sp3 hybridised orbitals?','Greater s character','The greater the s character of the hybrid orbitals, the greater is the electronegativity. Thus, a carbon atom having an sp hybrid orbital with 50% s character is more electronegative than that possessing sp2 or sp3 hybridised orbitals.','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Tetravalence of carbon and shapes of compounds',NULL,'2','mcq','Greater s character','Simpler Molecule','Less p character','Complex Molecule','NEW','11-335','11-257',NULL),
(120531,'chemistry','What is the IUPAC name for the compound in the given diagram(1226)','1,3-dimethylcyclopentane','Longest carbon chain is selected, lowest numbering possible is given to substituents and alphabetical order is used.For ring alkanes, cyclo word is used. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 342; Paragraph No.1,2 and 3)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Nomenclature of organic compounds',NULL,'3','mcq','1,4-dimethylcyclopentane','1,3-dimethylcyclopentane','1,5-dimethylcyclopentane','2,5-dimethylcyclopentane','NEW','11-342','11-264','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/120531q.png'),
(120532,'chemistry','What is the IUPAC name for the compound in the given diagram(1227)','Methylcyclopropane','Longest carbon chain is selected, lowest numbering possible is given to substituents and alphabetical order is used.For ring alkanes, cyclo word is used. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 342; Paragraph No.1,2 and 3)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Nomenclature of organic compounds',NULL,'3','mcq','4,5,5-Trimethy-4-Ethyl Decane','Methylcyclopropane','Cyclobutane','Butane','NEW','11-342','11-264','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/120532q.png'),
(120533,'chemistry','What is the IUPAC name for the compound in the given diagram(1228)','5-sec-butyl-2,7-dimethylnonane','Longest carbon chain is selected, lowest numbering possible is given to substituents and alphabetical order is used. In alphabetical order, the prefixes iso- and neo- are considered to be the part of the fundamental name of alkyl group. The prefixes sec- and tert- are not considered to be the part of the fundamental name. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 343; Paragraph No. 1)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Nomenclature of organic compounds',NULL,'3','mcq','5-sec-butyl-2,7-dimethylnonane','2,7-dimethyl-5-sec-butylnonane','5-sec-butyl-3,8-dimethylnonane','2,9-dimethyl-5-sec-butylnonane','NEW','11-342','11-264','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/120533q.png'),
(120534,'chemistry','What is the IUPAC name for the compound in the given diagram(1229)','1-(1-methylethyl)-cyclohexane','Longest carbon chain is selected, lowest numbering possible is given to substituents and alphabetical order is used.For ring alkanes, cyclo word is used. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 342; Paragraph No.1,2 and 3)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Nomenclature of organic compounds',NULL,'3','mcq','1-Propyl-cyclohexane','1-(1-methylethyl)-cyclohexane','2-cyclohexylpropane','1-Cyclohexyl-1,1-dimethylmethane','NEW','11-342','11-264','/ncert/pyq/physics/mcq/120534q.png'),
(120535,'chemistry','What is the IUPAC name for the compound in the given diagram(1230)','1,1-Dimethylcyclobutane','Longest carbon chain is selected, lowest numbering possible is given to substituents and alphabetical order is used.For ring alkanes, cyclo word is used. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 342; Paragraph No.1,2 and 3)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Nomenclature of organic compounds',NULL,'3','mcq','1,1-Dimethylcyclobutane','1,4-Dimethylcyclobutane','1-cyclobutane-1-methylmethane','1-(1-methylethyl)-cyclohexane','NEW','11-342','11-264','/ncert/pyq/physics/mcq/120535q.png'),
(120536,'chemistry','What is the IUPAC name for the compound in the given diagram(1231)','Cyclobutylcyclopentane','Longest carbon chain is selected, lowest numbering possible is given to substituents and alphabetical order is used.For ring alkanes, cyclo word is used. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 342; Paragraph No.1,2 and 3)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Nomenclature of organic compounds',NULL,'3','mcq','Cyclobutylcyclopentane','cyclopentylcyclobutane','Bicyclononane','Dimethylcyclobutane','NEW','11-342','11-264','/ncert/pyq/physics/mcq/120536q.png'),
(120537,'chemistry','What is the IUPAC name for the compound in the given diagram(1232)','1-Ethyl-2,3-dimethylpropane','Longest carbon chain is selected, lowest numbering possible is given to substituents and alphabetical order is used.For ring alkanes, cyclo word is used. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 342; Paragraph No.1,2 and 3)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Nomenclature of organic compounds',NULL,'3','mcq','1-Ethyl-2,3-dimethylpropane','2,3-Dimethyl-1-Ethylpropane','3-Ethyl-1,2-dimethylpropane','None of these','NEW','11-342','11-264','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/120537q.png'),
(120538,'chemistry','What is the IUPAC name for the compound in the given diagram(1233)','1-Methyl-1-propylcyclopropane','Longest carbon chain is selected, lowest numbering possible is given to substituents and alphabetical order is used.For ring alkanes, cyclo word is used.When ring and side chain have same carbons then ring is considered as parent chain. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 342; Paragraph No.1,2 and 3)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Nomenclature of organic compounds',NULL,'3','mcq','1-Methyl-1-propylcyclopropane','1Propyl-1-methylcyclopropane','1-Cyclopropyl-1-methylpropane','1-Methyl1-cyclopropylpropane','NEW','11-342','11-264','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/120538q.png'),
(120539,'chemistry','What is the IUPAC name for the compound in the given diagram(1234)','Cyclopropylbutane','Longest carbon chain is selected, lowest numbering possible is given to substituents and alphabetical order is used.For ring alkanes, cyclo word is used. More number carbon having is chosen as parent chain and ring as substituent. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 342; Paragraph No.1,2 and 3)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Nomenclature of organic compounds',NULL,'3','mcq','Cyclopropylbutane','Butycyclopropane','Heptane','4-cyclopropyl','NEW','11-342','11-264','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/120539q.png'),
(120540,'chemistry','What is the IUPAC name for the compound in the given diagram(1235)','2,5,6- Trimethyloctane','Lowest locant number, 2,5,6 is lower than 3,5,7, Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 343; Problem No. 12.7)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Nomenclature of organic compounds',NULL,'3','mcq','2,5,6- Trimethyloctane','3,4,7-Trimethyloctane','2-Butyl-5-methylhexane','2-Ethyl-3,6-dimethylheptane','NEW','11-343','11-265','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/120540q.png'),
(120541,'chemistry','What is the IUPAC name for the compound in the given diagram(1236)','3-Ethyl-5-methylheptane','substituents are in equivalent position; lower number is given to the one that comes first in the name according to alphabetical order. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 343; Problem No. 12.7)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Nomenclature of organic compounds',NULL,'3','mcq','3-Ethyl-5-methylheptane','5-Ethyl-3-methylheptane','3,5-Diethylhexane','None of these','NEW','11-343','11-265','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/120541q.png'),
(120542,'chemistry','Choose the correct option regarding the following assertion(A) and reason(R)\n Assertion: Organic chemistry deals with millions of compounds. In order to clearly identify them, a systematic method of naming has been developed and is known as the IUPAC (International Union of Pure and Applied Chemistry) system of nomenclature.\n Reason: In this systematic nomenclature, the names are correlated with the structure such that the reader or listener can deduce the structure from the name.','Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is the correct explanation of Assertion','Organic chemistry deals with millions of compounds. In order to clearly identify them, a systematic method of naming has been developed and is known as the IUPAC (International Union of Pure and Applied Chemistry) system of nomenclature. In this systematic nomenclature, the names are correlated with the structure such that the reader or listener can deduce the structure from the name. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 340; Paragraph No.4)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Nomenclature of organic compounds',NULL,'3','mcq','Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is the correct explanation of Assertion','Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion','Assertion is true but Reason is false.','Assertion is false but Reason is true.','NEW','11-340','11-262',NULL),
(120543,'chemistry','IUPAC is','International Union of Pure and Applied Chemistry','Organic chemistry deals with millions of compounds. In order to clearly identify them, a systematic method of naming has been developed and is known as the IUPAC (International Union of Pure and Applied Chemistry) system of nomenclature. In this systematic nomenclature, the names are correlated with the structure such that the reader or listener can deduce the structure from the name. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 340; Paragraph No.4)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Nomenclature of organic compounds',NULL,'3','mcq','International Union of Applied Chemistry','International Union of Pure Applied Commission','International Union of Pure and Applied Chemistry','None of these','NEW','11-340','11-262',NULL),
(120544,'chemistry','At least one carbon-carbon double or triple bond in hydrocarbons referred to as:','Unsaturated hydrocarbons','Unsaturated hydrocarbons are those, which contain at least one carbon-carbon double or triple bond. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 341; Paragraph No.2 )','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Nomenclature of organic compounds',NULL,'1','mcq','Saturated hydrocarbons','Unsaturated hydrocarbons','Supersaturated hydrocarbons','None of these','NEW','11-341','11-263',NULL),
(120545,'chemistry','Choose the correct option regarding the following assertion(A) and reason(R)\n Assertion: Straight chain hydrocarbon compounds are based on their chain structure, and end with suffix ‘-ane’ and carry a prefix indicating the number of carbon atoms present in the chain.\n Reason: The aforementioned assertion is exceptional from CH4 to C4H10, where the prefixes are derived from trivial names.','Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is the correct explanation of Assertion','Straight chain hydrocarbons: The names of such compounds are based on their chain structure, and end with suffix ‘-ane’ and carry a prefix indicating the number of carbon atoms present in the chain (except from CH4 to C4H10, where the prefixes are derived from trivial names). Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 341; Paragraph No.2 )','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Nomenclature of organic compounds',NULL,'2','mcq','Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is the correct explanation of Assertion','Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion','Assertion is true but Reason is false.','Assertion is false but Reason is true.','NEW','11-341','11-263',NULL),
(120546,'chemistry','In which compounds, small chains of carbon atoms are attached at one or more carbon atoms of the parent chain?','Branched chain','In a branched chain compound small chains of carbon atoms are attached at one or more carbon atoms of the parent chain. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 341; Paragraph No.3 )','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Nomenclature of organic compounds',NULL,'1','mcq','Straight chain','Branched chain','Cyclic','Heterocyclic','NEW','11-341','11-263',NULL),
(120547,'chemistry','Justify the statement regarding hydrocarbons: "An alkyl group is derived from a hydrocarbon by removing a hydrogen atom from carbon"','Saturated hydrocarbons','In a branched chain compounds, an alkyl group is derived from a saturated hydrocarbon by removing a hydrogen atom from carbon. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 341; Paragraph No.3 )','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Nomenclature of organic compounds',NULL,'2','mcq','Saturated hydrocarbons','Unsaturated hydrocarbons','Supersaturated hydrocarbons','None of these','NEW','11-341','11-263',NULL),
(120548,'chemistry','Match the following Alkane with their Molecular formula:','C2H6-Ethane, C3H8-Propane, C4H10-Butane, C10H22-Decane','Abbreviations are used for some alkyl groups. For example, methyl is abbreviated as Me, ethyl as Et, propyl as Pr and butyl as Bu. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 341; Table No.12.3)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Nomenclature of organic compounds',NULL,'3','match','C2H6, Ethane','C3H8, Propane','C4H10, Butane','C10H22, Decane','NEW','11-341','11-263',NULL),
(120549,'chemistry','Identify the correct group for the given structure: –CH2C(CH3)3','Neopentyl group','Common branched groups have specific trivial names. For example, the propyl groups can either be n-propyl group or isopropyl group. The branched butyl groups are called secbutyl, isobutyl and tert-butyl group. We also encounter the structural unit, –CH2C(CH3)3, which is called neopentyl group. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 341; Paragraph No.6 )','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Nomenclature of organic compounds',NULL,'2','mcq','Isobutyl group','Neopentyl group','Tert-butyl group','n-propyl group','NEW','11-341','11-263',NULL),
(120550,'chemistry','How many rules are followed for the nomenclature of branched chain alkanes?','Six','There are six rules followed for the nomenclature of branched chain alkanes. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 341; Paragraph No.6 )','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Nomenclature of organic compounds',NULL,'1','mcq','Three','Four','Five','Six','NEW','11-341','11-263',NULL),
(120551,'chemistry','Choose the correct option regarding the following assertion(A) and reason(R)\n Assertion: The carbon atoms of the parent chain are numbered to identify the parent alkane and to locate the positions of the carbon atoms.\n Reason: At which branching takes place due to the substitution of alkyl group in place of hydrogen atoms.','Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is the correct explanation of Assertion','The carbon atoms of the parent chain are numbered to identify the parent alkane and to locate the positions of the carbon atoms at which branching takes place due to the substitution of alkyl group in place of hydrogen atoms. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 342; Paragraph No.2 )','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Nomenclature of organic compounds',NULL,'2','mcq','Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is the correct explanation of Assertion','Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion','Assertion is true but Reason is false.','Assertion is false but Reason is true.','NEW','11-342','11-264',NULL),
(120552,'chemistry','Which of the following is not a branched butyl group?','neobutyl','Common branched groups have specific trivial names. For example, the propyl groups can either be n-propyl group or isopropyl group. The branched butyl groups are called secbutyl, isobutyl and tert-butyl group. We also encounter the structural unit, –CH2C(CH3)3, which is called neopentyl group. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 341; Paragraph No.6 )','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Nomenclature of organic compounds',NULL,'2','mcq','sec butyl','isobutyl','tert-butyl','neobutyl','NEW','11-341','11-263',NULL),
(120553,'chemistry','The numbers are separated from the groups by ________ and there is no break between methyl and nonane.','Hyphens','The numbers are separated from the groups by hyphens and there is no break between methyl and nonane. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 342; Paragraph No.3 )','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Nomenclature of organic compounds',NULL,'1','mcq','Hyphens','Commas','Dashes','Brackets','NEW','11-342','11-264',NULL),
(120554,'chemistry','If two or more identical substituent groups are present then the numbers are separated by :','Commas','If two or more identical substituent groups are present then the numbers are separated by commas. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 342; Paragraph No.4 )','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Nomenclature of organic compounds',NULL,'1','mcq','Hyphens','Commas','Dashes','Brackets','NEW','11-342','11-264',NULL),
(120555,'chemistry','Choose the correct option regarding the following assertion(A) and reason(R)\n \n Assertion: The names of identical substituents are not repeated, instead prefixes such as di (for 2), tri (for 3), tetra (for 4), penta (for 5), hexa (for 6) etc. are used.\n \n Reason: While writing the name of the substituents in alphabetical order, these prefixes are considered.','Assertion is true but Reason is false.','The names of identical substituents are not repeated, instead prefixes such as di (for 2), tri (for 3), tetra (for 4), penta (for 5), hexa (for 6) etc. are used. While writing the name of the substituents in alphabetical order, these prefixes, however, are not considered. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 342; Paragraph No.4 )','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Nomenclature of organic compounds',NULL,'2','mcq','Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is the correct explanation of Assertion','Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion','Assertion is true but Reason is false.','Assertion is false but Reason is true.','NEW','11-342','11-264',NULL),
(120556,'chemistry','Naming the given compound according to IUPAC nomenclature: diagram(12136)','3-ethyl-6-methyloctane','The following compound is 3-ethyl-6-methyloctane and not 6-ethyl-3-methyloctane. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 342; Paragraph No.5 )','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Nomenclature of organic compounds',NULL,'3','mcq','6-methyl-3-ethyloctane','3-methyl-6-ethyloctane','3-ethyl-6-methyloctane','6-ethyl-3-methyloctane','NEW','11-342','11-264','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/120556q.png'),
(120557,'chemistry','Justify the statement regarding IUPAC nomenclature: "The lower number is given to the one coming first in the alphabetical listing".','If the two substituents are found in equivalent positions','If the two substituents are found in equivalent positions, the lower number is given to the one coming first in the alphabetical listing. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 342; Paragraph No.5 )','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Nomenclature of organic compounds',NULL,'2','mcq','If more than two substituents are found in any positions','If the no substituent is found in any positions','If the two substituents are found in different positions','If the two substituents are found in equivalent positions','NEW','11-342','11-264',NULL),
(120558,'chemistry','Which prefixes are not considered to be the part of the fundamental name?','Sec- and tert-','The prefixes sec- and tert- are not considered to be the part of the fundamental name. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 343; Paragraph No.1 )','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Nomenclature of organic compounds',NULL,'2','mcq','Iso- and neo-','Sec- and tert-','But- and pent-','None of these','NEW','11-343','11-265',NULL),
(120559,'chemistry','Choose the correct option regarding the following assertion(A) and reason(R)\n \n Assertion: Saturated monocyclic compound is named by prefixing ‘cyclo’ to the corresponding straight chain alkane.\n \n Reason: Compounds having the same functional group undergo similar reactions.','Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion','A saturated monocyclic compound is named by prefixing ‘cyclo’ to the corresponding straight chain alkane.If side chains are present, then the rules given above are applied. \n Compounds having the same functional group undergo similar reactions. For example, CH3OH, CH3CH2OH, and (CH3)2CHOH — all having -OH functional group liberate hydrogen on reaction with sodium meta\n Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 343; Paragraph No.2 )','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Nomenclature of organic compounds',NULL,'2','mcq','Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is the correct explanation of Assertion','Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion','Assertion is true but Reason is false.','Assertion is false but Reason is true.','NEW','11-343','11-265',NULL),
(213106,'chemistry','Halogens have very _____.','high electronegatativity','Halogens have very high electronegativity. \n(Reference\' (NCERT Chemistry Class 12 Page No. 199 Paragraph No. 1)','Inorganic chemistry >> The p-Block Elements >> Group 17 Elements - Physical Properties',NULL,'2','mcq','high electronegatativity','maximum positive electron gain enthalpy','lowest electron affinity','lowest ionisation energy','NEW','12-199',NULL,NULL),
(120627,'chemistry','What is the IUPAC name for the compound in the given diagram(1261)','2-Chlorohexane','Functional group should get the lowest number with longest carbon chain possible. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 344; Paragraph No. 2)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Nomenclature of organic compounds with functional group',NULL,'3','mcq','5-Chlorohexane','2-Chlorohexane','1-Chloro-1-methylpentane','None of these','NEW','11-344','11-266','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/120627q.png'),
(120628,'chemistry','What is the IUPAC name for the compound in the given diagram(1262)','Nitroethane','Functional group should get the lowest number with longest carbon chain possible. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 344; Paragraph No. 2)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Nomenclature of organic compounds with functional group',NULL,'3','mcq','2-Nitroethane','Nitroethane','Ethanamine','Ethanamide','NEW','11-344','11-266','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/120628q.png'),
(120629,'chemistry','What is the IUPAC name for the compound in the given diagram(1263)','2-Methylbutanamide','Functional group should get the lowest number with longest carbon chain possible hers suffix amide is used and it\'s carbon is the given the first priority. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 344; Paragraph No. 2)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Nomenclature of organic compounds with functional group',NULL,'3','mcq','2-Ethylbutanamide','2-Methylbutanamide','1-Amino-2-methylpropane','None of these','NEW','11-344','11-266','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/120629q.png'),
(120630,'chemistry','What is the IUPAC name for the compound in the given diagram(1264)','3-Methylpent-3-en-2-ol','Functional group should get the lowest number with longest carbon chain possible, here OH is given priority over double bond. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 344; Paragraph No. 2)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Nomenclature of organic compounds with functional group',NULL,'3','mcq','2,3-Dimethylpent-3en-2-ol','3-Methylpent-3-en-2-ol','3-Methylpent-2-en-3-ol','none of these','NEW','11-344','11-266','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/120630q.png'),
(120631,'chemistry','What is the IUPAC name for the compound in the given diagram(1265)','3-Chloro-2-iodo-4-oxopentanoic acid','Functional group should get the lowest number with longest carbon chain possible, alphabetical order is used. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 344; Paragraph No. 2)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Nomenclature of organic compounds with functional group',NULL,'3','mcq','2-iodo-3-Chloro-4-oxopentanoic acid','3-Chloro-2-iodo-4-oxopentanoic acid','4-oxo-3-Chloro-2-iodopentanoic acid','none of these','NEW','11-344','11-266','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/120631q.png'),
(120632,'chemistry','What is the IUPAC name for the compound in the given diagram(1266)','4-Butylpent-2,4-dien-1-al','Functional group should get the lowest number, choose the chain which has the maximum number of pi bonds. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 344; Paragraph No. 2)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Nomenclature of organic compounds with functional group',NULL,'3','mcq','5-vinyloct-3-en-1-al','4-Butylpent-2,4-dien-1-al','5-vinyloct-5-en-1-al','none of these','NEW','11-344','11-266','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/120632q.png'),
(120633,'chemistry','What is the IUPAC name for the compound in the given diagram(1267)','4-Methylcyclobut-2-en-1-ol','Here OH is given priority over double bond and double bond is given lowest number possible. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 344; Paragraph No. 2)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Nomenclature of organic compounds with functional group',NULL,'3','mcq','4-Methylcyclobut-1-en-3-ol','4-Methylcyclobut-2-en-1-ol','2-Methylcyclobut-3-en-1-ol','none of these','NEW','11-344','11-266','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/120633q.png'),
(120634,'chemistry','What is the IUPAC name for the compound in the given diagram(1268)','2-Chloromethyl-4-methylhaxanal','Functional group should get the lowest number with longest carbon chain possible, alphabetical order is used. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 344; Paragraph No. 2)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Nomenclature of organic compounds with functional group',NULL,'3','mcq','2-Chloromethyl-4-methylhaxanal','2,4-Dimethlhaxanal','1-Chloro-4-ethylpentanal','none of these','NEW','11-344','11-266','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/120634q.png'),
(120635,'chemistry','What is the IUPAC name for the compound in the given diagram(1269)','2-Methylpent-1-en-4-yne','Double bond gets priority over triple bond. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 344; Paragraph No. 2)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Nomenclature of organic compounds with functional group',NULL,'3','mcq','4-Methylpent-4-en-1-yne','2-Methylpent-1-en-4-yne','2-Methylpent-2-en-4-yne','none of these','NEW','11-344','11-266','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/120635q.png'),
(120636,'chemistry','What is the IUPAC name for the compound in the given diagram(1270)','But-1-en-1-ol','OH when present as priority group, ol is used as suffix. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 344; Paragraph No. 2)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Nomenclature of organic compounds with functional group',NULL,'3','mcq','But-2-en-1-ol','But-1-en-1-ol','1-Hydroxybut-1-ene','none of these','NEW','11-344','11-266','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/120636q.png'),
(120637,'chemistry','What is the IUPAC name for the compound in the given diagram(1271)','3-chloro-1,2-epoxypropane','The numbering will start from left side. Chlorine will get number 3. Hence, the IUPAC name is 3-Chloro-1,2-epoxypropane. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 344; Paragraph No. 2)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Nomenclature of organic compounds with functional group',NULL,'3','mcq','1chloro-2,3-epoxypropane','3-chloro-1,2-epoxypropane','3-chloro-1,1-epoxypropane','none of these','NEW','11-344','11-266','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/120637q.png'),
(120638,'chemistry','What is the IUPAC name for the compound in the given diagram(1272)','Pent-2-en-2,3-diol','Lowest locant rule is applied to give lowest number to functional group. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 344; Paragraph No. 2)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Nomenclature of organic compounds with functional group',NULL,'3','mcq','Pent-3-en-3,4-diol','Pent-2-en-2,3-diol','2-Methylbut-2-en-2,3-diol','none of these','NEW','11-344','11-266','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/120638q.png'),
(120639,'chemistry','What is the IUPAC name for the compound in the given diagram(1273)','N-Bromoethanamide','N is used to indiacte the group or substituent attached with nitrogen and amide is used as suffix for amides. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 344; Table No. 12.4)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Nomenclature of organic compounds with functional group',NULL,'3','mcq','1-Bromoacetamide','N-Bromoethanamide','Ethanoyl Bromide','none of these','NEW','11-345','11-267','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/120639q.png'),
(213107,'chemistry','All Halogens are ______.','coloured','All Halogens are coloured.\n(Reference\' (NCERT Chemistry Class 12 Page No. 199 Paragraph No. 2)','Inorganic chemistry >> The p-Block Elements >> Group 17 Elements - Physical Properties',NULL,'2','mcq','colourless','coloured','gaseous','solid','NEW','12-199',NULL,NULL),
(120640,'chemistry','What is the IUPAC name of Cl₂CHCH₂OH?','2,2-Dichloroethan-1-ol','Lowest locant rule is applied to give lowest number to functional group. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 344; Paragraph No. 2)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Nomenclature of organic compounds with functional group',NULL,'1','mcq','2,2-Dichloroethan-1-ol','2,2-Dual Chlorine ethanol','1, 1-dichloro-2-ethanol','none of these','NEW','11-344','11-266',NULL),
(120641,'chemistry','What is the IUPAC name for the compound in the given diagram(12108)','3-Methylpentanenitrile','Lowest locant rule is applied to give lowest number to functional group and maximum carbon chain length is chosen. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 344; Paragraph No. 2)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Nomenclature of organic compounds with functional group',NULL,'3','mcq','3-Methylpentane-5nitrile','3-Methylpentanenitrile','3-Ethylbutanenitrile','none of these','NEW','11-344','11-266','/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/120641q.png'),
(120642,'chemistry','Choose the correct option regarding the following assertion(A) and reason(R)\n Assertion: In case of polyfunctional compounds,the choice of pricipal functional group is made on the basis of order of preference.\n Reason: The decreasing priority for some functional groups is -COOH, –SO₃H, -COOR (R=alkyl group), COCl, -CONH₂, -CN,-HC=O, >C=O, -OH, -NH₂, >C=C<, -C≡C- .','Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion','In the case of polyfunctional compounds, one of the functional groups is chosen as the principal functional group and the compound is then named on that basis. The remaining functional groups, which are subordinate functional groups, are named as substituents using the appropriate prefixes. The choice of principal functional group is made on the basis of order of preference. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 344; Paragraph No. 3)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Nomenclature of organic compounds with functional group',NULL,'3','mcq','Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is the correct explanation of Assertion','Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion','Assertion is true but Reason is false.','Assertion is false but Reason is true.','NEW','11-344','11-266',NULL),
(120643,'chemistry','Compounds having -OH functional group liberate hydrogen on reaction with__________.','Sodium metal','Compounds having the same functional group undergo similar reactions. For example, CH3OH, CH3CH2OH, and (CH3)2CHOH — all having -OH functional group liberate hydrogen on reaction with sodium metal. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 344; Paragraph No. 1)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Nomenclature of organic compounds with functional group',NULL,'2','mcq','Sodium metal','Calcium carbonate','Carboxalic acid','Hydronium ion','NEW','11-344','11-266',NULL),
(120644,'chemistry','The presence of _________ enables systematisation of organic compounds into different classes.','Functional groups','The presence of functional groups enables systematisation of organic compounds into different classes. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 344; Paragraph No. 1)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Nomenclature of organic compounds with functional group',NULL,'1','mcq','Substituent','Functional groups','Nitrogen','Specie','NEW','11-344','11-266',NULL),
(120645,'chemistry','Match the following representation with their respective functional groups:','H-R, Alkoxy-OR, Halogens-F Cl I, Nitro-NO2','The –R, C6H5-, halogens (F, Cl, Br, I), –NO2, alkoxy (–OR) etc. are always prefix substituents. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 344; Paragraph No. 3)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Nomenclature of organic compounds with functional group',NULL,'3','match','H, R','Alkoxy, OR','Halogens, F Cl I','Nitro, NO2','NEW','11-344','11-266',NULL),
(120646,'chemistry','Choose the correct option regarding the following assertion(A) and reason(R)\n Assertion: In the case of polyfunctional compounds, one of the functional groups is chosen as the principal functional group and the compound is then named on that basis.\n Reason: The choice of principal functional group is made on the basis of order of preference.','Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is the correct explanation of Assertion','In the case of polyfunctional compounds, one of the functional groups is chosen as the principal functional group and the compound is then named on that basis. The remaining functional groups, which are subordinate functional groups, are named as substituents using the appropriate prefixes. The choice of principal functional group is made on the basis of order of preference. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 344; Paragraph No. 2)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Nomenclature of organic compounds with functional group',NULL,'2','mcq','Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is the correct explanation of Assertion','Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion','Assertion is true but Reason is false.','Assertion is false but Reason is true.','NEW','11-344','11-266',NULL),
(120647,'chemistry','What do you called the compound containing both an alcohol and a keto group?','Hydroxyalkanone','A compound containing both an alcohol and a keto group is named as hydroxyalkanone since the keto group is preferred to the hydroxyl group.Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 344; Paragraph No. 2)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Nomenclature of organic compounds with functional group',NULL,'1','mcq','Hydroxyketone','Hydroxyalkanone','Ketohydroxy','Alkanonehydroxy','NEW','11-344','11-266',NULL),
(120648,'chemistry','Choose the correct option regarding the following assertion(A) and reason(R)\n Assertion: If more than one functional group of the same type are present, their number is indicated by adding di, tri, etc. before the class suffix. \n Reason: In such cases the full name of the parent alkane is written before the class suffix.','Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is the correct explanation of Assertion','If more than one functional group of the same type are present, their number is indicated by adding di, tri, etc. before the class suffix. In such cases the full name of the parent alkane is written before the class suffix.Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 344; Paragraph No. 6)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Nomenclature of organic compounds with functional group',NULL,'2','mcq','Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is the correct explanation of Assertion','Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion','Assertion is true but Reason is false.','Assertion is false but Reason is true.','NEW','11-344','11-266',NULL),
(120649,'chemistry','The functional group present in the molecule is identified which determines the choice of appropriate ______','Suffix','The functional group present in the molecule is identified which determines the choice of appropriate suffix. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 344; Paragraph No. 2)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Nomenclature of organic compounds with functional group',NULL,'1','mcq','Suffix','Prefix','Parenthesis','Carbon atom','NEW','11-344','11-266',NULL),
(120650,'chemistry','Choose the correct option regarding the following assertion(A) and reason(R)\n \n Assertion: The longest chain of carbon atoms containing the functional group is numbered in such a way that the functional group is attached at the carbon atom possessing lowest possible number in the chain.\n \n Reason: The functional group present in the molecule is identified which determines the choice of appropriate prefix.','Assertion is true but Reason is false.','The functional group present in the molecule is identified which determines the choice of appropriate suffix. The longest chain of carbon atoms containing the functional group is numbered in such a way that the functional group is attached at the carbon atom possessing lowest possible number in the chain. Reference: (NCERT Chemistry Class 11; Page No. 344; Paragraph No. 2)','Organic chemistry >> Organic chemistry - some basic principles and techniques >> Nomenclature of organic compounds with functional group',NULL,'2','mcq','Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is the correct explanation of Assertion','Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion','Assertion is true but Reason is false.','Assertion is false but Reason is true.','NEW','11-344','11-266',NULL),
