(130344,'chemistry','Dihydrogen gas adds to alkenes and alkynes in the presence of finely divided catalysts like platinum, palladium or nickel to form alkanes. This process is called','hydrogenation','Dihydrogen gas adds to alkenes and alkynes in the presence of finely divided catalysts like platinum, palladium or nickel to form alkanes. \n\nThis process is called hydrogenation.\n\nReference: (NCERT Chemistry Class-11, Page-378, Paragraph - 5)','Organic chemistry >> Hydrocarbon >> Alkanes',NULL,'1','fillup','hy,dr,og,en,at,ion,ol,ui,th',NULL,NULL,NULL,'NEW','11-378','11-300',NULL),
