(220833,'chemistry','Identify the incorrect statement from the following','The oxidation number of K in KO2 is +4','NEET 2022','Inorganic chemistry >> Redox Reactions >> Previous Year Questions',NULL,'2','mcq','Li is the strongest reducing agent among the alkali metals','Alkali metal react with water to form their hydroxides','The oxidation number of K in KO2 is +4','Ionisation enthalpy of alkali metal decreases from top to bottom in the group.','NEW','11-268','11-240',NULL),
(220834,'chemistry','Standard reduction of the half reactions are given below\n1- F2 + 2e- ---> 2F ; E=+2.85V\n2- Cl2 + 2e- ----> 2Cl- ; E= +1.36V\n3- Br2 + 2e- ----> 2Br- ; E= +1.06V\n4- I2 + e- ----> 2I- ; E= 0.53V','F2 and I-','AIPMT 2012','Inorganic chemistry >> Redox Reactions >> Previous Year Questions',NULL,'2','mcq','Br2 and Cl-','Cl2 and Br-','Cl2 and I2','F2 and I-','NEW','11-275','11-247',NULL),
(220835,'chemistry','A set of species capable of showing disproportionation reaction is','Cl2, ClO-2, ClO3-, S8','NEET 2022','Inorganic chemistry >> Redox Reactions >> Previous Year Questions',NULL,'2','mcq','ClO-2, ClO-3, ClO-4, Cl2','Cl2, ClO-2, ClO3-, S8','ClO-4, ClO-, ClO-2, F2','ClO-3, ClO-4, H2O2, ClO-','NEW','11-272','11-244',NULL),
(220836,'chemistry','The Change in the oxidation number of chlorine when chlorine gas reaqcts with hot and concentrated Sodium Hydroxide Solution is','0 to -1 and 0 to +5','AIPMT 2012','Inorganic chemistry >> Redox Reactions >> Previous Year Questions',NULL,'1','mcq','0 to +1 and 0 to -5','0 to -1 and 0 to +5','0 to -1 and 0 to +3','0 to +1 and 0 to -3','NEW','11-268','11-240',NULL),
