(220839,'chemistry','A solution contains Fe2+, Fe3+ and I- ions. This solution was treated with iodine at 35 C. E for Fe3+/Fe2+= 0.77V and E for I2/2I- = 0.536 V.\nThe favourable redox reaction is','I- will be oxidized to I2','AIPMT2011','Inorganic chemistry >> Redox Reactions >> Previous Year Questions',NULL,'2','mcq','Fe2+ will be oxidized to Fe3+','I2 will be reduced to I-','There will be no redox reaction','I- will be oxidized to I2','NEW','11-278','11-250',NULL),
