(220841,'chemistry','Standard electrode potentials are\nFe2+/ Fe ; E= -0.44\nFe3+/Fe2+ ; E= 0.77\nIf Fe2+ , Fe3+ and Fe blocks are kept together than','Fe3+ decreases','AIPMT2001','Inorganic chemistry >> Redox Reactions >> Previous Year Questions',NULL,'1','mcq','Fe3+ increases','Fe3+ decreases','Fe2+/Fe3+ remain unchanged','Fe2+ decreases','NEW','11-278','11-250',NULL),
