(150318,'chemistry','Which of the following are possible variations in the tetragonal crystal system?\n \n a. Primitive\n \n b. Body-centred \n \n c. End-centred \n \n d. Face-centred','a and b','In tetragonal crystal system, only primitive and body centred unit cells are possible. \n(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 10 Table 1.3)','Physical chemistry >> Solid state >> Close Packed Structures',NULL,'2','mcq','a and c','a and b','a, b and d','b and c','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(150319,'chemistry','In which of the following crystal system, α=ß=Γ=90° and a=b≠c ?','Tetragonal','In tetragonal crystal system a=b≠c and α=ß=Γ=90° \n(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 10 Table 1.3)','Physical chemistry >> Solid state >> Close Packed Structures',NULL,'1','mcq','Tetragonal','Trigonal','Orthorhombic','Cubic','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(150320,'chemistry','In which of the following crystal system, α=ß=Γ=90° and a≠b≠c ?','Orthorhombic','In orthorhombic crystal system, all of angles are equal to 90° and all dimension are different. \n(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 10 Table 1.3)','Physical chemistry >> Solid state >> Close Packed Structures',NULL,'1','mcq','Tetragonal','Trigonal','Orthorhombic','Cubic','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(150321,'chemistry','Which type of crystal system is found in rhombic sulphur?','Orthorhombic','Rhombic Sulphur is an example of orthorhombic Crystal system. \n(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 10 Table 1.3)','Physical chemistry >> Solid state >> Close Packed Structures',NULL,'2','mcq','Tetragonal','Trigonal','Orthorhombic','Cubic','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
