(150324,'chemistry','Which crystal system has the following dimensional relation α=ß=Γ≠90° a=b=c ?','Trigonal','In trigonal or rhombohedral crystal system, all dimensions are equal and angles are also equal but not equal to 90°. \n(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 10 Table 1.3)','Physical chemistry >> Solid state >> Close Packed Structures',NULL,'1','mcq','Tetragonal','Trigonal','Orthorhombic','Cubic','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(150325,'chemistry','Which of the following statements are correct?\n \n a. Calcite has trigonal crystal system.\n \n b. Cinnebor has rhombohedral crystal syste.','Both statements are correct','Examples of trigonal or rhombohedral crystal sytem are calcite and cinnabor. \n(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 10 Table 1.3)','Physical chemistry >> Solid state >> Close Packed Structures',NULL,'2','mcq','Both statements are correct','a is correct but b is incorrect','a is incorrect but b is correct','Both statements are incorrect','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(150326,'chemistry','Which of the following crystal system has following dimensional relation? α=Γ=90°ß≠90° a≠b≠c ?','Monoclinic','Monoclinic crystal, all sides are unequal α=Γ=90°ß≠90° a≠b≠c. \n(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 10 Table 1.3)','Physical chemistry >> Solid state >> Close Packed Structures',NULL,'1','mcq','Monoclinic','Trigonal','Hexagonal','Triclinc','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(150327,'chemistry','Which of the following are possible variations in the monoclinic crystal system?\n \n a. Primitive\n \n b. Body-centred \n \n c. End-centred \n \n d. Face-centred','a and c','In monoclinic crystal system, primitive and end centric unit cells are only possible. \n(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 10 Table 1.3)','Physical chemistry >> Solid state >> Close Packed Structures',NULL,'2','mcq','a and c','a and b','a, b and d','b and c','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
