(300336,'chemistry','The real active compound of Protonsil is','Sulphanilamide','In 1932, he succeeded in preparing the first effective antibacterial agent, prontosil, which resembles in structure to the compound, salvarsan. Soon it was discovered that in the body prontosil H.W. Florey and Alexander Fleming shared the Nobel prize for Medicine in 1945 for their independent contributions to the development of penicillin. is converted to a compound called sulphanilamide, which is the real active compound. Thus the sulpha drugs were discovered.(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 455 Para 2 )','Organic Chemistry >> Chemistry in everydaylife >> Therapeutic action of different classes of Drugs 2',NULL,'1','mcq','Azodye','Salvarsan','Sulphanilamide','None of these','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
