(300343,'chemistry','Which of the following is correct about penicillin?\n1. Penicillin G is narrow spectrum antibiotic.\n\n2. It is bacteriostatic.\n\n3. Ampicillin and amoxicillin are synthetic modification of penicillin.\n\n4. It is extracted from antibacterial fungus penicillin.','1 and 3','Bactericidal:  Penicillin Aminoglycosides Ofloxacin   Bacteriostatic: Erythromycin Tetracycline Chloramphenicol   and Penicillin extracted from Fungus Penicilium. (Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 455 Para 2 )','Organic Chemistry >> Chemistry in everydaylife >> Therapeutic action of different classes of Drugs 2',NULL,'2','mcq','1 and 4','1 and 3','1 and 2','1,3 and 4','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(300344,'chemistry','______________Isolated in 1947, is a broad spectrum antibiotic. It is rapidly absorbed from the gastrointestinal tract and hence can be given orally in case of typhoid, dysentery, acute fever.','Chloramphenicol','Chloramphenicol,  isolated in 1947, is a broad spectrum antibiotic. It is rapidly absorbed from the gastrointestinal tract and hence can be given orally in case of typhoid, dysentery, acute fever, certain form of urinary infections, meningitis and pneumonia. (Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 455 Para 2 )','Organic Chemistry >> Chemistry in everydaylife >> Therapeutic action of different classes of Drugs 2',NULL,'1','mcq','Dysidazrine','Chloramphenicol','Vancomycin','Penicillin','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
