(300347,'chemistry','Which of the following is true :','Ampicillin : Bacteriocidal, Chloramphenicol : Bacteriostatic','Bactericidal:  Penicillin Aminoglycosides Ofloxacin   Bacteriostatic: Erythromycin Tetracycline Chloramphenicol','Organic Chemistry >> Chemistry in everydaylife >> Therapeutic action of different classes of Drugs 2',NULL,'2','mcq','Ampicillin : Bacteriocidal, Chloramphenicol : Bacteriocidal','Only Penicillin is Bacteriocidal','Ampicillin : Bacteriocidal, Chloramphenicol : Bacteriostatic','Ampicillin : Bacteriostatic, Chloramphenicol :  Bacteriocidal','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(300348,'chemistry','Consider the following:\n1. Antibiotics which kill or inhibit a wide range of Gram-positive and Gram-negative bacteria are said to be broad spectrum antibiotics. \n2. Effective mainly against Gram-positive and Gram-negative bacteria are narrow spectrum antibiotics.\n3. Antibiotics effective against a single organism or disease, they are referred to as limited spectrum antibiotics.\n4. Penicillin G is Narrow spectrum antibiotic.\nQ. How many of above are Correct?.','1,3 and 4','Antibiotics which kill or inhibit a wide range of Gram-positive and Gram-negative bacteria are said to be broad spectrum antibiotics. Those effective mainly against Gram-positive or Gram-negative bacteria are narrow spectrum antibiotics. If effective against a single organism or disease, they are referred to as limited spectrum antibiotics. Penicillin G has a narrow spectrum. (Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 455 Para 2 )','Organic Chemistry >> Chemistry in everydaylife >> Therapeutic action of different classes of Drugs 2',NULL,'3','mcq','3 and 4 only','1,2 and 3','1,2 and 4','1,3 and 4','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
