(300422,'chemistry','_________  are applied to inanimate objects such as floors, drainage system, instruments, etc.','Disinfectants','Disinfectants  are applied to inanimate objects such as floors, drainage system, instruments, etc. (Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 456 Para 1 )','Organic Chemistry >> Chemistry in everydaylife >> Therapeutic action of different classes of Drugs 3',NULL,'1','mcq','Antipyretic','Antiseptics','Disinfectants','All of these','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(300423,'chemistry','Which of the following is true ?\n1. Disinfectants  are applied to inanimate objects such as floors, drainage system, instruments, etc.\n2. Same substances can act as an antiseptic as well as disinfectant by varying the concentration.\n3.  0.2 per cent  solution of phenol is an antiseptic while its one percent solution is disinfectant.\n4. Antiseptic and disinfectants cannot be same because Tincture of Iodine is Antiseptic and Chlorine is Disinfectant.','1,2 and 3','Disinfectants  are applied to inanimate objects such as floors, drainage system, instruments, etc. Same substances can act as an antiseptic as well as disinfectant by varying the concentration. For example, 0.2 per cent  solution of phenol is an antiseptic while its one percent solution is disinfectant.(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 456 Para 1 )','Organic Chemistry >> Chemistry in everydaylife >> Therapeutic action of different classes of Drugs 3',NULL,'3','mcq','2 and 3','1 and 3','1,2 and 3','all of these','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(300424,'chemistry','Assertion: Same substances can act as an antiseptic as well as disinfectant.\nReason: High Concentration act as Antiseptic and low Concentration act as disinfectants.','Assertion is True  but the Reason is false','Disinfectants  are applied to inanimate objects such as floors, drainage system, instruments, etc. Same substances can act as an antiseptic as well as disinfectant by varying the concentration. For example, 0.2 per cent  solution of phenol is an antiseptic while its one percent solution is disinfectant.(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 456 Para 1 )','Organic Chemistry >> Chemistry in everydaylife >> Therapeutic action of different classes of Drugs 3',NULL,'3','mcq','Both the Assertion and the Reason are correct and the Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion','The Assertion and the Reason are correct but the Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion','Assertion is True  but the Reason is false','Both the Assertion and Reason are false.','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
