(300707,'chemistry','Chloroamphenicol is an-','antibiotic-broad spectrum.','In NCERT only Narrow spectrum Antibiotic is PENICILLIN G. And other examples are Broad Spectrum antibiotics .(Reference NCERT class 12 page 447 paragraph3 Main 2012)','Organic Chemistry >> Chemistry in everydaylife >> Previous Year question',NULL,'1','mcq','antifertility drug','antihistamine','antiseptic and disinfectant','antibiotic-broad spectrum.','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(300708,'chemistry','The artificial sweetner stable at cooking temperature \nand does not provide calories is','sucralose','Sucralose is trichloro derivative of sucrose. Its\nappearance and taste is like sugar. It is stable at cooking\ntemperature and it does not provide calories.(Reference NCERT class 12 page 449 paragraph last NEET 2019)','Organic Chemistry >> Chemistry in everydaylife >> Previous Year question',NULL,'1','mcq','saccharin','aspartame','sucralose','alitame','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(300709,'chemistry','Artificial sweetner which is stable under cold \nconditions only is','aspartame','Aspartame is stable under cold conditions and\nunstable at cooking temperature.\n(Reference NCERT class 12 page 450 paragraph 1NEET 2014)','Organic Chemistry >> Chemistry in everydaylife >> Previous Year question',NULL,'1','mcq','saccharin','sucralose','aspartame','alitame','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(300710,'chemistry','Which of the following is a cationic detergent?','Cetyltrimethyl ammonium bromide','Cetyltrimethyl ammonium bromide is a\ncationic detergent.\n(Reference NCERT class 12 page 452 paragraph 3 NEET 2004)','Organic Chemistry >> Chemistry in everydaylife >> Previous Year question',NULL,'2','mcq','Sodium lauryl sulphate','Sodium stearate','Cetyltrimethyl ammonium bromide','Sodium dodecylbenzene sulphonate','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
