(213413,'chemistry','The reaction shown below is disproportionation reaction because\n3Cl₂  +  6NaOH 🠖 5NaCl + NaClO₃ +  3H₂O','Cl changes from zero oxidation state to -1 and +5 oxidation state','The following reaction is disproportionation reaction because Cl changes from zero oxidation state to -1 and +5 oxidation state.\n3Cl₂  +  6NaOH 🠖 5NaCl + NaClO₃ +  3H₂O  \nOxidation state of Chlorine in Cl₂ is 0\nOxidation state of Chlorine in NaCl is -1\nOxidation state of Chlorine in NaClO₃ is +5\n(Reference\' (NCERT Chemistry Class 12 Page No. 204 Problem 7.17)','Inorganic chemistry >> The p-Block Elements >> Chlorine',NULL,'3','mcq','Cl changes from zero oxidation state to -1 and +5 oxidation state','Cl changes from zero oxidation state to -5 and +1 oxidation state','Cl changes from zero oxidation state to -1 and +3 oxidation state','Cl changes from zero oxidation state to +1 and -3 oxidation state','NEW','12-204',NULL,NULL),
(213414,'chemistry','What does HCl on reaction with finely divides Fe form?','Ferrous chloride','HCl on reaction with finely divides Fe forms Ferrous chloride.\nIts reaction with iron produces H₂\nFe + 2HCl → FeCl₂ + H₂\nLiberation of hydrogen prevents the formation of ferric chloride.\n(Reference\' (NCERT Chemistry Class 12 Page No. 204 Problem 7.18)','Inorganic chemistry >> The p-Block Elements >> Chlorine',NULL,'1','mcq','Ferric chloride','Ferrous chloride','Ferrous hydride','Ferric hydride','NEW','12-204',NULL,NULL),
(213415,'chemistry','Phosgene is a________ gas.','poisonous','Phosgene is a poisonous gas. \n(Reference\' (NCERT Chemistry Class 12 Page No. 204 Paragraph No. 1)','Inorganic chemistry >> The p-Block Elements >> Chlorine',NULL,'1','mcq','non-toxic','poisonous','greenish yellow','pale blue','NEW','12-204',NULL,NULL),
