(213505,'chemistry','When _____ parts of concentrated HCl and ____ part of concentrated HNO₃ are mixed, aqua regia is formed.','three, one','When three parts of concentrated HCl and one part of concentrated HNO₃ are mixed, aqua regia is formed which is used for dissolving noble metals, e.g., gold, platinum.\n(Reference\' (NCERT Chemistry Class 12 Page No. 204 Paragraph No. 6)','Inorganic chemistry >> The p-Block Elements >> Hydrogen Chloride',NULL,'1','mcq','one, three','three, one','two, one','one, two','NEW','12-204',NULL,NULL),
