(213701,'chemistry','When two different halogens react with each other, ___________________ are formed.','interhalogen compounds','When two different halogens react with each other, interhalogen compounds are formed.\n(Reference\' (NCERT Chemistry Class 12 Page No. 206 Paragraph No. 1)','Inorganic chemistry >> The p-Block Elements >> Interhalogen Compounds - Properties',NULL,'1','mcq','oxoacids of halogen','interhalogen compounds','hydrogen halides','intrahalogen compounds','NEW','12-206',NULL,NULL),
(213702,'chemistry','Interhalogen compounds are all _______ molecules and are __________ in nature.','covalent and diamagnetic','Interhalogen compounds are covalent molecules and are diamagnetic in nature. They are volatile solids or liquids at 298 K except ClF.\n(Reference\' (NCERT Chemistry Class 12 Page No. 207 Paragraph No. 1)','Inorganic chemistry >> The p-Block Elements >> Interhalogen Compounds - Properties',NULL,'3','mcq','ionic and diamagnetic','ionic and paramagnetic','covalent and diamagnetic','covalent and paramagnetic','NEW','12-207',NULL,NULL),
(213703,'chemistry','X–X′ bond in interhalogens is _______ than X–X bond in halogens.','weaker','Chemical reactions of interhalogen compounds can be compared with individual halogens. In general, interhalogen compounds are more reactive than halogens(except fluorine). This is because X-X\' bond in interhalogens is weaker than X-X bond in halogens except F-F bond. \n(Reference\' (NCERT Chemistry Class 12 Page No. 207 Paragraph No. 1)','Inorganic chemistry >> The p-Block Elements >> Interhalogen Compounds - Properties',NULL,'2','mcq','stronger','smaller','weaker','longer','NEW','12-207',NULL,NULL),
(213704,'chemistry','X–X′ bond in interhalogens is weaker than X–X bond in halogens except _______ bond.','F–F','Chemical reactions of interhalogen compounds can be compared with individual halogens. In general, interhalogen compounds are more reactive than halogens(except fluorine). This is because X-X\' bond in interhalogens is weaker than X-X bond in halogens except F-F bond. \n(Reference\' (NCERT Chemistry Class 12 Page No. 207 Paragraph No. 1)','Inorganic chemistry >> The p-Block Elements >> Interhalogen Compounds - Properties',NULL,'3','mcq','F–F','Br-Br','Cl-Cl','I-I','NEW','12-207',NULL,NULL),
(213705,'chemistry','The molecular structure of interhalogens can be explained on the basis of;','VSEPR theory','The molecular structures of interhalogen compounds are in accordance to VSEPR theory.\n\\(Reference\' (NCERT Chemistry Class 12 Page No. 207 Paragraph No. 3)','Inorganic chemistry >> The p-Block Elements >> Interhalogen Compounds - Properties',NULL,'2','mcq','VESPR theory','VSEPR theory','VSERP theory','SEVPR theory','NEW','12-207',NULL,NULL),
(213706,'chemistry','The molecular shape shown in diagram(n2109)','Bent T-shaped','The central atom Br has seven electrons in the valence shell. Three of these will form electron pair bonds with three fluorine atoms leaving behind four electrons. Thus, there are three bond pairs and two lone pairs. According to VSEPR theory, these will occupy the corners of a trigonal bipyramid. The two lone pairs will occupy the equatorial positions to minimise lone pair-lone pair and the bond pair lone pair repulsions which are greater than the bond pair-bond pair repulsions. In addition, the axial fluorine atoms will be bent towards the equatorial fluorine in order to minimise the lone-pair-lone pair repulsions. The shape would be that of a slightly bent ‘T’.\n(Reference\' (NCERT Chemistry Class 12 Page No. 207 Paragraph No. 4)','Inorganic chemistry >> The p-Block Elements >> Interhalogen Compounds - Properties',NULL,'2','mcq','Trigonal bipyramidal','Octahedral','Tetrahedral','Bent T-shaped','NEW','12-207',NULL,'/ncert/pyq/chemistry/mcq/213706q.png'),
(213801,'chemistry','Inter halogen compounds can be used as _________ solvents.','non-aqueous','Interhalogen compounds can be used as non-aqueous solvents. \n(Reference\' (NCERT Chemistry Class 12 Page No. 207 Paragraph No. 4)','Inorganic chemistry >> The p-Block Elements >> Interhalogen Compounds - Uses',NULL,'2','mcq','aqueous','non-aqueous','gaseous','liquid','NEW','12-207',NULL,NULL),
(213802,'chemistry','ClF₃ and BrF₃ are used for the production of _______ in the enrichment of ²³⁵U.','UF₆','ClF₃ and BrF₃ are used for the production of UF₆ in the enrichment of ²³⁵U. \n(Reference\' (NCERT Chemistry Class 12 Page No. 207 Paragraph No. 4)','Inorganic chemistry >> The p-Block Elements >> Interhalogen Compounds - Uses',NULL,'2','mcq','UF₆','UF₂','UF₃','None of these','NEW','12-207',NULL,NULL),
(213901,'chemistry','All group 18 elements are chemically  __________.','unreactive','All group-18 elements are chemically unreactive.\n(Reference\' (NCERT Chemistry Class 12 Page No. 208 Paragraph No. 1)','Inorganic chemistry >> The p-Block Elements >> Group 18 Elements - Occurance',NULL,'1','mcq','reactive','unreactive','unstable','coloured','NEW','12-208',NULL,NULL),
