(214349,'chemistry','Match the following interhalogen compounds with their correct physical state and colour','IBr-Black solid, ICl₃-Orange solid, BrF₃-Yellow green liquid, IF₃-Yellow powder','The correct match is IBr-Black solid, ICl3-Orange solid, BrF3-Yellow green liquid, IF3-Yellow powder\n(Reference\' (NCERT Chemistry Class 12 Page no. 206 Table 7.11)','Inorganic chemistry >> The p-Block Elements >> Most challenging questions',NULL,'2','match','IBr,Black solid','ICl₃,Orange solid','BrF₃,Yellow green liquid','IF₃,Yellow powder','NEW','12-206',NULL,NULL),
(214350,'chemistry','Interhalogen compounds undergo hydrolysis to give hydrogen halide and an oxoacid. Match interhalogen compounds with the correct oxoacid they obtain.','XX\'-Hypohaite, XX\'₃-Halite, XX\'₅-Halate, XX\'₇- Perhalate','The correct match is XX\'-Hypohaite, XX\'3-Halite, XX\'5-Halate, XX\'7-Perhalate\n(Reference\' (NCERT Chemistry Class 12 Page no. 207 Paragraph 2)','Inorganic chemistry >> The p-Block Elements >> Most challenging questions',NULL,'2','match','XX\',Hypohaite','XX\'₃,Halite','XX\'₅,Halate','XX\'₇,Perhalate','NEW','12-207',NULL,NULL),
