(71733,'chemistry','The pH of 0.005 M codeine (C₁₈H₂₁NO₃) solution is 9.95. Calculate its ionization constant and pKb.','1.59 × 10⁻⁶','[H⁺] = antilog(-9.95) = 1.12 × 10⁻¹⁰\n[OH⁻] = 10⁻¹⁴/1.12 × 10⁻¹⁰ = 8.92 × 10⁻⁵ M\n\nBut , Kb = [M⁺][OH⁻]/[MOH] = (8.92 × 10⁻⁵ )²/0.05 = 1.59 × 10⁻⁶.','Physical Chemistry >> Equilibrium >> NCERT Exercise',NULL,'2','mcq','1.59 × 10⁻⁶','2 × 10⁻⁷','2 × 10⁻⁸','2','NEW','11-221','11-197',NULL),
(71734,'chemistry','The pH of 0.005 M codeine (C₁₈H₂₁NO₃) solution is 9.95. Calculate its pKb. [Ionization constant = 1.59 × 10⁻⁶]','5.8','[H⁺] = antilog(-9.95) = 1.12 × 10⁻¹⁰\n[OH⁻] = 10⁻¹⁴/1.12 × 10⁻¹⁰ = 8.92 × 10⁻⁵ M\n\nBut , Kb = [M⁺][OH⁻]/[MOH] = (8.92 × 10⁻⁵ )²/0.05 = 1.59 × 10⁻⁶.\n\npKb = -logKb = -log(1.59 × 10⁻⁶) = 5.80','Physical Chemistry >> Equilibrium >> NCERT Exercise',NULL,'2','mcq','5.8','6.8','7.2','9.2','NEW','11-221','11-197',NULL),
