(42023,'chemistry','Which of the following species have same shape \na.CO₂         \nb.CCl₄         \nc.O₃         \nd.NO₂⁻','c,d','The shape of following species are a.CO₂-linear                                       b.CCl₄-tetrahedral                                  c.O₃-bent                                      d.NO₂⁻-bent','Inorganic chemistry >> Chemical bonding and molecular structure >> Exemplar Questions',NULL,'2','mcq','a,d','a,c','a,b','c,d','NEW','11-114','11-114',NULL),
(42024,'chemistry','Which of the following statement are correct?              \n\nA. hybridisation of central atom, sp \nB. Its resonant structure has 1C –O single bond and two C=O double bonds.                          \nC. The average formal charge on each oxygen  is 0.67 units.    \nD.all C—O bond length are equal','c,d','Hybridisation of central atom sp² ,hence a is wrong .due to resonance C—O bond length are equal ,formal charge on each atom is -2/3 =-0.67 units','Inorganic chemistry >> Chemical bonding and molecular structure >> Exemplar Questions',NULL,'3','mcq','a,d','a,c','a,b','c,d','NEW','11-109','11-109',NULL),
(42101,'chemistry','In which of the following species the interatomic "bond angle is 109° 28""?"','NH₃ ,BF₄⁻¹','In NH₃ ,BF₄⁻¹ the hybridisation is sp³ and the bond angle is 109 ° 28\'','Inorganic chemistry >> Chemical bonding and molecular structure >> JEE Mains',NULL,'3','mcq','NH₃ ,BF₄⁻¹','NH₄⁺,BF₃','NH₃ ,BF₄','NH₂⁻¹ ,BF₃','NEW','11-116','11-116',NULL),
(42102,'chemistry','Which of the following are arranged in aa increasing order of their bond strengths? [2002|','O₂²⁻ <O₂⁻ <O₂ <O₂⁺','The electronic configuration of O₂ is           Y O₂ = (σ1s)²(σ*1s)²(σ2s)²(σ*2s)²(σ2p𝓏)²(𝛑2pᵧ²=𝛑2pₓ² (𝛑*2pᵧ¹=𝛑*2pₓ¹). So after addition of electrons there will be no unpaired electrons','Inorganic chemistry >> Chemical bonding and molecular structure >> JEE Mains',NULL,'2','mcq','O₂⁻ <O₂ <O₂⁺ <O₂²⁻','O₂²⁻ <O₂⁻ <O₂ <O₂⁺','O₂⁻<O₂²⁻ <O₂ < O₂⁺','O₂²⁻ >O₂⁻ <O₂ <O₂⁺','NEW','11-129','11-129',NULL),
(42103,'chemistry','Hybridisation of the central atom changes in:','AlH₃ changes to AlH₄⁻','Hybridisation =1/2[(no of e⁻ in valence shell of atom) + (no of monovalent atoms around it) -(charge on cation) +(charge on anion )]  for AlH₃ hybridisation =1/2[3+3-0+0] =3 =sp².        For AlH₄⁻ Hybridisation =1/2[3+4-0+1] = 4 =sp³','Inorganic chemistry >> Chemical bonding and molecular structure >> JEE Mains',NULL,'1','mcq','AlH₃ changes to AlH₄⁻','H₂O changes to H₃O⁺','NH₃ changes to NH₄⁺','In all cases','NEW',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(42104,'chemistry','An ether is more volatile than an alcohol having        \nthe same molecular formula. This is due to','inter-molecular hydrogen bonding in alcohol','In ether there is no H-Bonding while alcohol have intermolecular H-Bonding','Inorganic chemistry >> Chemical bonding and molecular structure >> JEE Mains',NULL,'1','mcq','alcohols having resonance structures','inter-molecular hydrogen bonding in ethers','inter-molecular hydrogen bonding in alcohol','dipolar character ofethers','NEW','11-131','11-131',NULL),
(42105,'chemistry','Which one of the following pairs of molecules will have permanent dipole moments for both','NO₂ and O₃','Both NO₂ and O₃ have angular shape, and hence will have net dipole moment','Inorganic chemistry >> Chemical bonding and molecular structure >> JEE Mains',NULL,'1','mcq','NO₂ and CO₂','NO₂ and O₃','SiF₄ and CO₂','SiF₄ and NO₂','NEW','11-111','11-111',NULL),
(42106,'chemistry','Which one of the following compounds has the smallest bond angle in its molecule?','H₂S','In H₂S due to low electronegativity of sulphur the lp —lp repulsion is more than bp—bp repulsion and hence bond angle is minimum .','Inorganic chemistry >> Chemical bonding and molecular structure >> JEE Mains',NULL,'2','mcq','OH₂','H₂S','NH₃','SO₂','NEW','11-108','11-108',NULL),
(42107,'chemistry','The bond order in NO is 2.5 while that in NO⁺ is 3. Which of the following statements is true for these two species ?','Bond length in NO is greater than in NO+','Now since bond order of NO⁺ given (3) is higher than that of NO (2.5) .Thus bond length of NO⁺ will be shorter.','Inorganic chemistry >> Chemical bonding and molecular structure >> JEE Mains',NULL,'1','mcq','Bond length in NO+ is equal to that in NO','Bond length in NO is greater than in NO+','Bond length in NO⁺ is greater than in NO','Bond length is unpredictable','NEW','11-107','11-107',NULL),
(42108,'chemistry','The states of hybridization of boron and oxygen atoms in boric acid (H₃BO₃)  are respectively','sp², sp³','The states of hybridization of boron and oxygen atoms in boric acid (H₃BO₃)  are respectively\nsp², sp³ it is because of the trigonal polar structure of the molecule','Inorganic chemistry >> Chemical bonding and molecular structure >> JEE Mains',NULL,'2','mcq','sp³,sp²','sp², sp³','sp² ,sp²',NULL,'NEW','11-120','11-120',NULL),
(42109,'chemistry','Which one of the following has the regular tetrahedral structure?','BF₄⁻','BF₄⁻=sp³ tetrahedral.         SF₄         =sp³d see saw shaped.              XeF₄=sp³ d² square planar.                        [Ni(CN)₄]²⁻ =dsp² square planar','Inorganic chemistry >> Chemical bonding and molecular structure >> JEE Mains',NULL,'1','mcq','BF₄⁻','SF₄','XeF₄','[Ni(CN)₄]²⁻','NEW','11-114','11-114',NULL),
(42110,'chemistry','The maximum number of 90° angles between bond pair-bond pair of electrons is observed in','sp³d²','In sp³d² the number of 90 ° angle bond is 12','Inorganic chemistry >> Chemical bonding and molecular structure >> JEE Mains',NULL,'2','mcq','dsp²','sp³d','dsp³','sp³d²','NEW','11-115','11-115',NULL),
(42111,'chemistry','Lattice energy of an ionic compound depends upon','charge of ion and size of ion','The value of lattice energy depends on the charge present on the two ions and the distance between them','Inorganic chemistry >> Chemical bonding and molecular structure >> JEE Mains',NULL,'1','mcq','charge of ion and size of ion','packing of ions only','size of ion only','Charge on the ion only','NEW','11-107','11-107',NULL),
(42112,'chemistry','Which of the following molecules/ions does not contain unpaired electrons?','O₂²⁻','According to distribution of electrons in molecular orbital theory only O₂²⁻ does not contain any unpaired electrons','Inorganic chemistry >> Chemical bonding and molecular structure >> JEE Mains',NULL,'1','mcq','N₂⁺','O₂','O₂²⁻','B₂','NEW','11-126','11-126',NULL),
(42113,'chemistry','In which of the following molecules/ions are all the bonds not equal?','SF₄','SF the hybridisation is sp³d   and the shape of molecule is see-saw','Inorganic chemistry >> Chemical bonding and molecular structure >> JEE Mains',NULL,'2','mcq','XeF₄','BF₄⁻','SF₄','SiF₄','NEW','11-114','11-114',NULL),
(42114,'chemistry','Which of the following species exhibits the diamagnetic behaviour?','decreasing electronegativity','Diamagnetic species has no unpair electrons, whereas paramagnetic species has one or more unpaired electrons','Inorganic chemistry >> Chemical bonding and molecular structure >> JEE Mains',NULL,'1','mcq','decreasing Ip-bp repulsion','decreasing electronegativity','increasing bp-bp repulsion','increasing p-orbital character in sp3','NEW','11-129','11-129',NULL),
(42115,'chemistry','The charge/size ratio of a cation determines its polarizing power. Which one of the following sequences represents the increasing order ofthe polarizing power of the cationic species, K⁺,Ca²⁺,Mg²⁺,Be²⁺','K⁺<Ca²⁺<Mg²⁺<Be²⁺','Smaller, the size and higher the charge more will be the polarising power of cation since the order of size of cation is K⁺>Ca²⁺>Mg²⁺>Be²⁺,so the correct order of polarising power is K⁺<Ca²⁺<Mg²⁺<Be²⁺','Inorganic chemistry >> Chemical bonding and molecular structure >> JEE Mains',NULL,'3','mcq','Ca²⁺ <Mg²⁺ <Be²⁺ <K⁺','Mg²⁺ <Be²⁺ <K⁺<Ca²⁺','Be²⁺ <K⁺<Ca²⁺<Mg²⁺','K⁺<Ca²⁺<Mg²⁺<Be²⁺','NEW','11-112','11-112',NULL),
(42116,'chemistry','In which of the following ionization processes, the bond order has increased and the magnetic behaviour has changed?','NO → NO⁺','NO= bond order 2.5 ,paramagnetic.             NO⁺ = bond order 3 ,diamagnetic','Inorganic chemistry >> Chemical bonding and molecular structure >> JEE Mains',NULL,'2','mcq','N₂ → N₂⁺','C₂ → C₂⁺','NO → NO⁺','O₂ → O₂⁺','NEW','11-109','11-109',NULL),
(42117,'chemistry','Which of the following hydrogen bonds is the strongest','F—H - - - F','Greater the difference between electronegativity of bonded atoms, stronger will be the bond  since F  is most electronegative F—H is strong bond','Inorganic chemistry >> Chemical bonding and molecular structure >> JEE Mains',NULL,'2','mcq','O—H - - - F','O—H - - - H','F—H - - - F','O—H - - - O','NEW','11-132','11-132',NULL),
(42118,'chemistry','The species in which the N atom is in state of sp hybridisation','NO₂⁺','Hybridisation =1/2[(no of e⁻ in valence shell of atom) + (no of monovalent atoms around it) -(charge on cation) +(charge on anion )]  for NO₂⁺ it is so hybridised','Inorganic chemistry >> Chemical bonding and molecular structure >> JEE Mains',NULL,'1','mcq','NO₃⁻','NO₂','NO₂⁺','NO₂⁻','NEW','11-113','11-113',NULL),
(42119,'chemistry','Which of the following species is not paramagnetic','NO₂⁺','NO₂⁺ is not paramagnetic because it doesn\'t contain unpaired electrons','Inorganic chemistry >> Chemical bonding and molecular structure >> JEE Mains',NULL,'1','mcq','NO','CO','O₂','NO₂⁺','NEW','11-129','11-129',NULL),
(42120,'chemistry','The bond dissociation energy of B- F in BF is 646 kJ mol-\' whereas that of C- Fin CF₄  is 515kJ mol!. The correct reason for higher B - F        bond dissociation energy as compared to that of C- F  is','significant P π  - p π interaction between B and F in BF₃  whereas there is no possibility	of such interaction between C and Fin CF₄','The delocalised P π —P π  bonding between filled P orbital of B leads to shortening of B—F Bond,which results in higher bond dissociation energy','Inorganic chemistry >> Chemical bonding and molecular structure >> JEE Mains',NULL,'2','mcq','stronger σ bond between B and F in BF₃ as compared to that between C and F in CF₄','significant P π  - p π interaction between B and F in BF₃  whereas there is no possibility	of such interaction between C and Fin CF₄','lower degree of p π- p π interaction between B and F in BF₃ ; than that between C and F in CF₄','smaller size of B- atom as compared to that','NEW','11-109','11-109',NULL),
(42121,'chemistry','Using MO theory, predict which of the following  species has the shortest bond length?','O₂²⁺','Bond order = (no of bonding electrons- no of antibonding electrons)/2  bond order in O₂⁺ =(10-5)/2 = 2.5.     O₂=(10-7)/2 =1.5        O₂²⁻.  (10-8)/2 =1          O₂²⁺ =(10-4)/2 = 3 bond order is indirectly proportional to bond length,therefore bond length is shortest in O₂²⁺','Inorganic chemistry >> Chemical bonding and molecular structure >> JEE Mains',NULL,'1','mcq','O₂⁺','O₂⁻','O₂²⁻','O₂²⁺','NEW','11-126','11-126',NULL),
(42122,'chemistry','The number of types of bonds between two carbon atoms in calcium carbide is','1 σ , 2 π','Calcium carbide exist as Ca²⁺ and C₂²⁻ according to the MO configuration it contains 1 σ and 2 π bond','Inorganic chemistry >> Chemical bonding and molecular structure >> JEE Mains',NULL,'2','mcq','1 σ , 1 π','2 σ , 1 π','2 σ , 2 π','1 σ , 2 π','NEW','11-126','11-126',NULL),
(42123,'chemistry','Ortho-Nitrophenol is less soluble in water than p- and m- Nitrophenols because :','o-Nitrophenol shows intramolecular H-bonding','Compounds involved in Chelation become non-polar. Consequently some compounds are soluble in nonpolar solvents like ether benzene etc and or only sparingly soluble in water where is meta and para isomers are more soluble in water and less soluble in non polar solvents','Inorganic chemistry >> Chemical bonding and molecular structure >> JEE Mains',NULL,'1','mcq','o-Nitrophenol is more volatile steam than those of m- and p-isomers.','o-Nitrophenol shows intramolecular H-bonding','o-Nitrophenol shows intermolecular H-bonding','Melting point of o-Nitrophenol is lower than those of m- and p-isomers.','NEW',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(42124,'chemistry','In which of the following pairs the two species are not isostructural ?','PF₅ and BrF₅','PF₅ = trigonal bipyramidal.                BrF₅ = square pyramidal','Inorganic chemistry >> Chemical bonding and molecular structure >> JEE Mains',NULL,'2','mcq','CO₃²⁻ and NO₃,-','PCl₄⁺ and SiCl₄','PF₅ and BrF₅','AlF₆³⁻ and SF₆','NEW','11-114','11-114',NULL),
