(42201,'chemistry','Select the correct statement','The attractive force which holds various constituents ( atoms,ions) together in different chemical species is called a chemical bond','Obviously there must be some force which holds the constituent atom together in the molecules. The attractive force which holds various constituents ( atoms,ions) together in different chemical species is called a chemical bond (Reference: NCERT class 11 part 1 Padre 96 paragraph 1)','Inorganic chemistry >> Chemical bonding and molecular structure >> Advanced Questions',NULL,'3','mcq','The repulsive force which holds various constituents ( atoms,ions) together in different chemical species is called a chemical bond','The attractive force which holds various constituents ( atoms,ions) together in different chemical species is called a chemical bond','The attractive force which repels various constituents ( atoms,ions) together in different chemical species is called a chemical bond','None of the above','NEW','11-100','11-100',NULL),
