(42203,'chemistry','Select the correct statements.          .\n\n1. Lewis pictured the atom in terms of a positively charged \'kernel\'.                                  \n\n2.He, further assumed that these eight electrons occupy the corners of a cube.which surround the \'Kernel\'.\n\n3.Lewis postulated that atoms achieve the stable octet when they are linked by chemical bonds.','1 , 2 , 3','Thus the single outer shell electron of sodium would occupy one corner of the cube, while in the case of a noble gas all the eight corners would be occupied. This octet of electrons, represents\na particularly stable electronic arrangement.(Reference: NCERT class 11 part 1 Padre 97 paragraph 1)','Inorganic chemistry >> Chemical bonding and molecular structure >> Advanced Questions',NULL,'3','mcq','1,2 only','1 , 2 , 3','2,3 only','1,3 only','NEW','11-100','11-100',NULL),
