(42240,'chemistry','AB is an ionic compound then','A should have low I.E. and B should have high E.A.','AB  form ionic compound when electronegativity difference is too large and hence A should have low ionisation energy and B should have high electron affinity (Reference : NCERT Class 11 part 1 page 102 Paragraph 2 in topic 4.2)','Inorganic chemistry >> Chemical bonding and molecular structure >> Advanced Questions',NULL,'1','mcq','A should have low I.E. and B should have high E.A.','B should have low E.A. and A should have high I.E.','A should have high I.E. and B should have high E.A.','B should have low E.A. and A should have low I. E.','NEW','11-106','11-106',NULL),
