(42246,'chemistry','Among LiCI, BeCl ₂ , BCl₃ and CCl₄, the covalent bond character varies as','LiCI < BeCl ₂  < BCl₃ < CCl₄','More the charge density of cation  more is the covalent character .order of charge density and thus the covalent character is LiCI < BeCl ₂  < BCl₃ < CCl₄ (Reference : NCERT Class 11 part 1 page 107 topic 4.2 Paragraph 3)','Inorganic chemistry >> Chemical bonding and molecular structure >> Advanced Questions',NULL,'3','mcq','LiCI < BeCl ₂ > BCl₃ > CCl₄','BCl₃ > BeCl ₂ > CCl₄ > LiCI','LiCI < BeCl ₂  < BCl₃ < CCl₄','LiCI > BeCl ₂ > BCl₃ > CCl₄','NEW','11-106','11-106',NULL),
(42247,'chemistry','The dipole moment of o, p and m-dichlorobenzene will be in the order','o > m > p','The dipole moment of to dipole is inclined at angle theta is given by the equation, μ = √ X² +Y² +2XYcosθ as the angle increases from 90° to 180°. The value of cos θ becomes more and more negative. Hence, resultant decreases thus dipole moment is maximum when θ is equal to 90°.(Reference : NCERT Class 11 part 1 page 109 Paragraph 2)','Inorganic chemistry >> Chemical bonding and molecular structure >> Advanced Questions',NULL,'2','mcq','0 > p > m','p > 0 > m','m > o> p','o > m > p','NEW','11-111','11-111',NULL),
