(161307,'chemistry','Henry’s law constant for the molality of methane in benzene at 298 K is 4.27 x 10⁵ mm Hg. Calculate the solubility of methane in benzene at 298 K under 760 mm Hg.','178 × 10⁻⁵','Here, p = 760 mm Hg, KH = 4.27 × 10⁵ mm Hg (at 298 K)\nAccording to Henry’s law, p = KHχ\nχ = p/Kh = 760 mmHg / 4.27 × 10⁵ mm Hg\n= 178 × 10⁻⁵','Physical chemistry >> Solutions >> NCERT Exercise',NULL,'2','mcq','178 × 10⁻³','178 × 10⁻⁵','178 × 10⁻⁴','178 × 10⁵','NEW','12-041','12-007',NULL),
