(161315,'chemistry','Calculate the mass percentage of aspirin (C₉H₈O₄ in acetonitrile (CH₃CN) when 6.5g of CHO is dissolved in 450 g of CH₃CN.','1.424 %','Mass of aspirin = 6.5 g\nMass of acetonitrile = 450 g\nThen, total mass of the solution = (6.5 + 450) g = 456.5 g\nTherefore, mass percentage of C₉H₈O₄ = (6.5/456.5) × 100% = 1.424 %','Physical chemistry >> Solutions >> NCERT Exercise',NULL,'2','mcq','1.424 %','14.24 %','0.1424 %','24%','NEW','12-036','12-002',NULL),
