(190326,'chemistry','Foam Rubber is an example of _____.','Solid Sol','Foam rubber is an example of solid sol colloidal system of gas dispersed in solid.\nReference : (NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 136; Table 5.4)','Physical chemistry >> Surface chemistry >> Colloids',NULL,'1','mcq','Solid Sol','Emulsions','Foam','Gels','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
