(190328,'chemistry','Whipped Cream is an example of _____.','Foam','Whipped cream is an example of foam colloidal system of gas dispersed in liquid.\nReference : (NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 136; Table 5.4)','Physical chemistry >> Surface chemistry >> Colloids',NULL,'1','mcq','Aerosols','Emulsions','Foam','Gels','DELETED',NULL,NULL,NULL),
