(230221,'chemistry','Which ions would not be present when carnallite is dissolved in distilled water?','Ca⁺²','Both double salts as well as complexes are formed by combination of two or more stable compounds in stoichiometric ratio\n\nMixed salts and Complex compounds differ in the fact that double salts such as carnallite, KCl.MgCl2.6H2O,\nMohr’s salt, FeSO4.(NH4)2SO4.6H2O, potash alum, KAl(SO4)2.12H2O, etc.\ndissociate into simple ions completely when dissolved in water.However, complex ions such as [Fe(CN)6]4– of K4 [Fe(CN)6] do not dissociate into\nFe2+ and CN– ions.(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 246; Paragraph 1)','Inorganic chemistry >> Coordination Compounds >> Werner\'s Theory of Coordination Compounds',NULL,'2','mcq','K⁺','Mg⁺²','Ca⁺²','All of these','NEW','12-246','12-120',NULL),
(230222,'chemistry','Which ions would be present when K₄[Fe(CN)₆] is dissolved in distilled water?','K⁺','Mixed salts and Complex compounds differ in the fact that double salts such as carnallite, KCl.MgCl2.6H2O,\nMohr’s salt, FeSO4.(NH4)2SO4.6H2O, potash alum, KAl(SO4)2.12H2O, etc.\ndissociate into simple ions completely when dissolved in water.However, complex ions such as [Fe(CN)6]4– of K4 [Fe(CN)6] do not dissociate into\nFe2+ and CN– ions.(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 246; Paragraph 1)','Inorganic chemistry >> Coordination Compounds >> Werner\'s Theory of Coordination Compounds',NULL,'2','mcq','K⁺','Fe⁺²','Fe⁺³','CN⁻','NEW','12-246','12-120',NULL),
(230223,'chemistry','Werner explained the difference in properties of certain nitrogen containing organic substances on the basis of ____.','isomerism','(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 246; Paragraph 2)','Inorganic chemistry >> Coordination Compounds >> Werner\'s Theory of Coordination Compounds',NULL,'1','fillup','is,om,eri,sm',NULL,NULL,NULL,'NEW','12-246','12-120',NULL),
(230224,'chemistry','Werner extended vant Hoff\'s theory of tetrahedral carbon and modified it for which element?','Nitrogen','Werner extended vant Hoff’s theory of tetrahedral carbon atom and modified\nit for nitrogen.(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 246; Paragraph 2)','Inorganic chemistry >> Coordination Compounds >> Werner\'s Theory of Coordination Compounds',NULL,'1','mcq','Phosphorous','Fluorine','Nitrogen','Chlorine','NEW','12-246','12-120',NULL),
