(230324,'chemistry','Choose the odd one with respect to common geometrical shapes in coordination compounds of transition metals.','Trigonal bipyramidal','The most common coordination polyhedra are octahedral, square planar and\ntetrahedral.(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 248; Paragraph 3)','Inorganic chemistry >> Coordination Compounds >> Definition of terms pertaining to Coordination Compounds',NULL,'2','mcq','Trigonal bipyramidal','Tetrahedral','Octahedral','Square planar','NEW','12-248','12-122',NULL),
