(231002,'chemistry','What will be colour of complex if green colour is absorbed by it?','Red','The complementary colour is the colour\ngenerated from the wavelength left over; if green light is absorbed by\nthe complex, it appears red.(Reference: NCERT Chemistry Class 12; Page 259; Paragraph 2)','Inorganic chemistry >> Coordination Compounds >> Colour in Coordination Compounds',NULL,'2','mcq','Red','Green','Blue','White','NEW','12-259','12-133',NULL),
