('fa618a6e-f879-4315-b8bb-cc3b7b160253',NULL,2020,'Biology','Biotechnology and Its Applications','Microbes in Biotechnology',NULL,'12','Medium','Match the organism with its use in biotechnology.\n\n\n\n![diagram](/api/public/diagram/daf7a6dc-ab7d-497a-880c-40333efb522a)\n\n','[{"key": "A", "text": "(a) (ii) (b) (iv) (c) (iii) (d) (i)"}, {"key": "B", "text": "(a) (iv) (b) (iii) (c) (i) (d) (ii)"}, {"key": "C", "text": "(a) (iii) (b) (ii) (c) (iv) (d) (i)"}, {"key": "D", "text": "(a) (iii) (b) (iv) (c) (i) (d) (ii)"}]','["B"]','Bacillus thuringiensis produces Cry proteins, Thermus aquaticus provides Taq DNA polymerase, Agrobacterium tumefaciens acts as a cloning vector, and Salmonella typhimurium was used in construction of the first recombinant DNA molecule.','2026-08-06 07:53:04.739897','85e39b88-bbd6-454b-96fe-b707a7bf8ddf','pyq_2020_E1',27,'2020:E1:832'),
('850ed0e6-80a1-40e0-ada7-86234009fdc7',NULL,2020,'Biology','Plant Physiology','Mineral Nutrition',NULL,'11','Medium','Match the following concerning essential elements and their functions in plants:\nSelect the correct option\n\n\n\n![diagram](/api/public/diagram/8cb1a9f7-bc51-4ac1-9c14-25e505acdbf8)\n\n','[{"key": "A", "text": "(a) (ii) (b) (i) (c) (iv) (d) (iii)"}, {"key": "B", "text": "(a) (iv) (b) (iii) (c) (ii) (d) (i)"}, {"key": "C", "text": "(a) (iii) (b) (iv) (c) (ii) (d) (i)"}, {"key": "D", "text": "(a) (iv) (b) (i) (c) (ii) (d) (iii)"}]','["C"]','Iron is required for chlorophyll biosynthesis, zinc is needed for IAA biosynthesis, boron helps in pollen germination, and manganese is involved in photolysis of water during photosynthesis.','2026-08-06 07:53:04.739897','85e39b88-bbd6-454b-96fe-b707a7bf8ddf','pyq_2020_E1',28,'2020:E1:854'),
('fe042607-8411-4d2f-9c52-fed9fc0c14a4',NULL,2020,'Biology','Biomolecules','Proteins and Secondary Metabolites',NULL,'11','Medium','Match the following:\n\nChoose the correct option from the following.\n\n\n\n![diagram](/api/public/diagram/16adb0c7-9626-4750-81e7-aa07bf05783f)\n\n','[{"key": "A", "text": "(a) (ii) (b) (iv) (c) (iii) (d) (i)"}, {"key": "B", "text": "(a) (iii) (b) (i) (c) (iv) (d) (ii)"}, {"key": "C", "text": "(a) (iii) (b) (iv) (c) (i) (d) (ii)"}, {"key": "D", "text": "(a) (ii) (b) (iii) (c) (i) (d) (iv)"}]','["A"]','Malonate inhibits catalytic activity, collagen possesses peptide bonds, chitin forms fungal cell walls, and ricin is a secondary metabolite.','2026-08-06 07:53:04.739897','85e39b88-bbd6-454b-96fe-b707a7bf8ddf','pyq_2020_E1',30,'2020:E1:856'),
('56b21e51-0faf-49dd-841d-a2cdbe67187b',NULL,2020,'Biology','Structural Organisation in Animals and Plants','Animal Classification',NULL,'11','Medium','Match the following columns and select the correct option.\n\n\n\n![diagram](/api/public/diagram/d8d83985-93e8-42c3-a2ff-5d39d4866a63)\n\n','[{"key": "A", "text": "(a)-(ii), (b)-(iii), (c)-(iv), (d)-(i)"}, {"key": "B", "text": "(a)-(iii), (b)-(iv), (c)-(i), (d)-(ii)"}, {"key": "C", "text": "(a)-(iv), (b)-(ii), (c)-(iii), (d)-(i)"}, {"key": "D", "text": "(a)-(i), (b)-(iv), (c)-(iii), (d)-(ii)"}]','["A"]','Cyclostomes possess 6-15 pairs of gill slits, Chondrichthyes have heterocercal tails, Osteichthyes possess air bladder, and Trygon has poison sting.','2026-08-06 07:53:04.739897','85e39b88-bbd6-454b-96fe-b707a7bf8ddf','pyq_2020_E1',37,'2020:E1:869'),
('74146a9a-eedf-458f-a4ce-5a9c1de7989a',NULL,2020,'Biology','Biology and Human Welfare','Microbes in Human Welfare',NULL,'12','Medium','Match the following columns and select the correct option.\n\n\n\n![diagram](/api/public/diagram/549a5376-3c39-4346-8e9e-cc8bad585735)\n\n','[{"key": "A", "text": "(a)-(iii), (b)-(iv), (c)-(ii), (d)-(i)"}, {"key": "B", "text": "(a)-(ii), (b)-(i), (c)-(iv), (d)-(iii)"}, {"key": "C", "text": "(a)-(i), (b)-(ii), (c)-(iv), (d)-(iii)"}, {"key": "D", "text": "(a)-(iv), (b)-(iii), (c)-(ii), (d)-(i)"}]','["B"]','Clostridium butylicum produces butyric acid, Trichoderma polysporum produces Cyclosporin-A, Monascus purpureus produces blood cholesterol lowering agents, and Aspergillus niger produces citric acid.','2026-08-06 07:53:04.739897','85e39b88-bbd6-454b-96fe-b707a7bf8ddf','pyq_2020_E1',48,'2020:E1:885'),
('a1d87bf8-562b-436f-8cd3-ff12ca67ffbe',NULL,2020,'Biology','Cell Structure and Function','Cell Division',NULL,'11','Medium','Match the following with respect to meiosis:\n\nSelect the correct option from the following.\n\n\n\n![diagram](/api/public/diagram/56fc3f94-fd23-4680-8568-f1f5deb66498)\n\n','[{"key": "A", "text": "(a)-(iii), (b)-(iv), (c)-(i), (d)-(ii)"}, {"key": "B", "text": "(a)-(iv), (b)-(iii), (c)-(ii), (d)-(i)"}, {"key": "C", "text": "(a)-(i), (b)-(ii), (c)-(iv), (d)-(iii)"}, {"key": "D", "text": "(a)-(ii), (b)-(iv), (c)-(iii), (d)-(i)"}]','["B"]','Synapsis occurs during zygotene, crossing over during pachytene, chiasmata become visible during diplotene, and terminalization occurs during diakinesis.','2026-08-06 07:53:04.739897','85e39b88-bbd6-454b-96fe-b707a7bf8ddf','pyq_2020_E1',52,'2020:E1:889'),
