('c41e9741-4e3e-487d-a083-20c561e3cacb',NULL,2020,'Biology','Ecology and Environment','Ecosystem',NULL,'12','Medium','Match the trophic levels with their correct species examples in grassland ecosystem.\n\nSelect the correct option.\n\n\n\n![diagram](/api/public/diagram/904dfd0d-2955-44cf-b69b-934cc371acc7)\n\n','[{"key": "A", "text": "(a)-(ii), (b)-(iii), (c)-(iv), (d)-(i)"}, {"key": "B", "text": "(a)-(iii), (b)-(ii), (c)-(i), (d)-(iv)"}, {"key": "C", "text": "(a)-(iv), (b)-(iii), (c)-(ii), (d)-(i)"}, {"key": "D", "text": "(a)-(i), (b)-(ii), (c)-(iii), (d)-(iv)"}]','["A"]','Grass is the producer and occupies the first trophic level. Rabbit is a primary consumer at the second trophic level. Crow acts as a secondary consumer at the third trophic level. Vulture occupies the fourth trophic level.','2026-08-06 07:53:04.739897','85e39b88-bbd6-454b-96fe-b707a7bf8ddf','pyq_2020_E1',60,'2020:E1:914'),
