(120,'biology',100,553,1107,'','[{"text": "A - Secondary spermatocyte,<br>B - Primary spermatocyte,<br>C - Spermatids<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - Primary spermatocyte,<br>B - Secondary spermatocyte,<br>C - Spermatids<br>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A - Primary spermatocyte,<br>B - Spaermatids,<br>C - Spermatocyte<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - Secondary spermatocyte,<br>B - Spermatids,<br>C - Primary spermatocyte.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'NCERT figure 3.8',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/100_120_question_1.png'),
(121,'biology',103,964,2246,'From the given statements, select the incorrect statement.<br>I. Health, for a long time, was considered as a state of body and mind where there was a balance of certain \'humors\'.<br>II. This is what early Greeks like Hippocrates as well as Indian Ayurveda system of medicine asserted.<br>III. It was thought that persons with \'Brown bile\' belonged to hot personality and would have fevers.','[{"text": "I only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III only", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "All of them", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'It was thought that the person with \'black bile\' belonged to hot personality and would have fevers',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(123,'biology',105,1276,3093,'The correct sequence of levels of biological organisation is','[{"text": "Communities $\\\\rightarrow$ Cells $\\\\rightarrow$ Tissues $\\\\rightarrow$<br>Organs $\\\\rightarrow$ Individual organism $\\\\rightarrow$<br>Biomes $\\\\rightarrow$ Ecological $\\\\rightarrow$ Population $\\\\rightarrow$ Macromolecules", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Macromolecules $\\\\rightarrow$ Tissues $\\\\rightarrow$ Cells $\\\\rightarrow$ Organs $\\\\rightarrow$ Population $\\\\rightarrow$ Ecosystem $\\\\rightarrow$ Commiunities $\\\\rightarrow$ Biomes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Micromolecules $\\\\rightarrow$ Cells $\\\\rightarrow$ Tissues $\\\\rightarrow$ Organs $\\\\rightarrow$ Individual organism $\\\\rightarrow$ Communities $\\\\rightarrow$ Population $\\\\rightarrow$ Biomes $\\\\rightarrow$ Ecosystem", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Macromolecules $\\\\rightarrow$ Cells $\\\\rightarrow$ Tissues $\\\\rightarrow$ Organs $\\\\rightarrow$ Individual organism $\\\\rightarrow$ Population $\\\\rightarrow$ Communities $\\\\rightarrow$ Ecosystem $\\\\rightarrow$ Biomes", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Macromolecules $\\rightarrow$ Cells $\\rightarrow$ Tissues $\\rightarrow$ Organs $\\rightarrow$ Individual organism $\\rightarrow$ Population $\\rightarrow$ Communities $\\rightarrow$ Ecosystem $\\rightarrow$ Biomes.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(124,'biology',100,553,1107,'Which of the following is a set of haploid cells in male and female<br>','[{"text": "Primary Spermatocyte, Spermatid, Ootid<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Polar body, Ovum, Spermatozoan, Spermatid<br>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Secondary Spermatocyte, Spermatogonium, Ovum<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ovum, Spermatozoan, Spermatogonium, Oogonium", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'In male secondary spermatocyte spermatid and spermatozoan are haploid cells. In female secondary oocyte, polar bodies, ootid are haploid.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(125,'biology',103,964,2246,'\'Good humour\' hypothesis was disproved by','[{"text": "Edward Jenner", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Edward Wilson", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "William Harvey", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "William Wilson", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Humor hypothesis states that there is a link between humor and health. According to them, the health was considered as a state of mind where there exists a balance between certain humors.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(126,'biology',105,1276,3093,'The study of interactions among organisms and between the organism and its abiotic environment is','[{"text": "Economics", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Environmental study", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ecology", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Ecotomy", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The study of interactions among organisms and between the organism and its abiotic environment is Ecology.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(128,'biology',100,553,1107,'During________, in the primary spermatocyte, the homologous chromosomes undergo crossing over and this results in genetic variations in the chromosomes<br>','[{"text": "Pachytene phase of Prophase-II<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pachytene phase of Prophase-I<br>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Zygotene phase of Prophase-I<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Zygotene phase of Prophase-II", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Pachytene phase of Prophase-I',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(129,'biology',103,964,2246,'The discovery of blood circulation by William Harvey using experimental method and the demonstration of ____ with black bile using thermometer disproved the \'good humor\' hypothesis of health.','[{"text": "High body temperature in persons", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Low body temperature in persons", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Normal body temperature in persons", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "None of them", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The discovery of blood circulation by William Harvey using experimental method and the demonstration of normal body temperature in persons with black bile using thermometer disproved the \'good humor\' hypothesis of health.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(130,'biology',105,1276,3093,'Study of inter relationship between living organisms and their environment is called','[{"text": "Phytosociology", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Phytogeography", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ecology", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Ecosystem", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Phytosociology- study of plants & their composition, and development and the relationship between species with in them.<br>Phytogeography- the branch of botany that deals with the geographical distribution of plants.<br>Ecosystem- a biological community of interacting organisms and their physical environment.  Ecology is the study of organisms and how they interact with the environment around them.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(131,'biology',100,553,1107,'Spermatogonium undergoes  ____.','[{"text": "Reduction division", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mitosis", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Meiosis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of these", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The spermatogonia (sing. spermatogonium) present on the inside wall of seminiferous tubules multiply by mitotic division and increase in numbers.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(132,'biology',103,964,2246,'Which of the following adversely affect human health?','[{"text": "Change in lifestyle", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Genetic disorders", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Infections", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Health is affected by -<BR>(i) genetic disorders - deficiencies with which a child is born and deficiencies/defects which the child inherits from parents from birth<BR>(ii) infections and<BR>(iii) life style including food and water we take, rest and exercise we give to our bodies, habits that we have or lack etc.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(134,'biology',105,1276,3093,'Plants and animals living in a given area constitute','[{"text": "Population", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Ecosystem", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Community", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Plankton", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Plants and animals living in a given area constitute population.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(135,'biology',100,553,1107,'Primary spermatocyte differs from spermatogonium in<br>','[{"text": "DNA content<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Number of chromosomes<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Size and volume<br>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Size and chromosomes", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The spermatogonia during the growth phase grow in size and volume and form primary spermatocytes.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(136,'biology',103,964,2246,'Health is a combination of','[{"text": "Physical well being", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mental and social well-being", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Absence of disease", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of them", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Health does not simply mean \'absence of disease\' or \'physical fitness\'. It could be defined as a state of complete physical, mental and social well-being.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(138,'biology',105,1276,3093,'Identify the basic levels of ecology','[{"text": "Organisms", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Populations", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Communities & Biomes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Basic level of Ecology-Organisms, populations, communities & Biomes.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(139,'biology',100,553,1107,'Which type of cells contain 23 chromosomes?','[{"text": "Spermatogonia", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Primary spermatocyte", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Secondary spermatocyte", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "None of the above", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Spermatogonia and primary spermatocyte are diploid whereas, the secondary spermatocyte after first meiotic division becomes haploid.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(140,'biology',103,964,2246,'Necessary steps for achieving good health are','[{"text": "Awareness about diseases", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Improper disposal of wastes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Vaccination", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both 1 and 3", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Awareness about diseases and their effect on different bodily functions, vaccination (immunisation) against infectious diseases, proper disposal of wastes, control of vectors and maintenance of hygiene in food and water resources are necessary for achieving good health.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
