(146,'biology',100,553,1107,'The cell which undergo meiosis-II is known as<br>','[{"text": "Sperm", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Spermatid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Secondary spermatocyte", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Primary Spermatocyte", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The secondary spermatocytes undergo the second meiotic division to produce four equal, haploid spermatids.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(147,'biology',103,964,2246,'Select the correct option with respect to maintaining good health.<br>i. Balanced diet, personal hygiene and regular exercise<br>ii. Yoga to achieve mental health only.<br>iii. Awareness about diseases and their effect on different bodily functions<br>iv. Vaccination (immunisation) against infectious diseases<br>v. Proper disposal of wastes, control of vectors<br>vi. Maintenance of hygienic food and water resources','[{"text": "i, ii, iii", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ii, iii, iv, v", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "i, iii, iv, v, vi", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "i, iii, v", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Statement (ii) is incorrect: yoga has been practised since time immemorial to achieve physical and mental health.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(149,'biology',105,1276,3093,'Amongst the following the highest level of ecological hierarchy is','[{"text": "Individual", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ecosystem", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Communities and Biome", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "All of them", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The highest level of ecological hierarchy is Communities and Biome.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(150,'biology',100,553,1107,'During spermatogenesis, which cells are the first to contain haploid number of chromosomes?<br>','[{"text": "Primary spermatocyte", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Spermatogonium", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Secondary spermatocyte", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Spermatid", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'A primary spermatocyte completes the first meiotic division (reduction division) leading to formation of two equal, haploid cells called secondary spermatocytes, which have only 23 chromosomes each.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
