(160,'biology',105,1276,3093,'Ecology is basically concerned with ____ levels of biological organisation','[{"text": "Four", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Three", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Two", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Five", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Ecology is basically concerned with four levels of biological organisation.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(161,'biology',100,553,1107,'The difference between primary and secondary spermatocyte lies in _____<br>','[{"text": "Primary gamete/secondary gamete in males<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Number of chromosomes<br>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Being hormone producing/non-hormone producing<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Presence/absence of a tail", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Primary and Secondary spermatocytes have different number of chromosomes.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(162,'biology',103,964,2246,'Which of the following pair contains infectious disease?','[{"text": "Typhoid and Obesity", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "AIDS and Cancer", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pneumonia and malaria", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Cancer and malaria", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Malaria is a vector-borne disease that spreads by the biting of the female Anopheles mosquito; pneumonia is transmitted through droplets coming out of the mouth and air. These pathogenic disorders do not require vector as a medium in the process of transmission.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(163,'biology',105,1276,3093,'Ecology in organismic level is essentially','[{"text": "Physiological ecology", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Morphological ecology", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Behavioural ecology", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Anatomical ecology", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Physiological ecology is the study of adjustments of organisms to survive and reproduce successfully in their changing environment',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(165,'biology',100,553,1107,'Spermiogenesis is<br>','[{"text": "Transformation of sperm into spermatids.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Transfermation of spermatogonia into primary spermatocyte.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Transformation of secondary spermatocyte into spermatids.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Transformation of spermatid into spermatozoa.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Transformation of spermatid into spermatozoa is called Spermatogenesis.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(166,'biology',103,965,2247,'Agents that cause infectious diseases are called','[{"text": "Carcinogens", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mutations", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pathogens", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Micro-organisms", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'A wide range of organisms belonging to bacteria, viruses, fungi, protozoans, helminths, etc., could cause diseases in man. Such disease causing organisms are called pathogens. Most parasites are therefore pathogens as they cause harm to the host by living in (or on) them. The pathogens can enter our body by various means, multiply and interfere with normal vital activities, resulting in morphological and functional damage.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(167,'biology',105,1276,3093,'The \'term\' biosphere is used for a zone containing living beings in','[{"text": "Lithosphere, hydrosphere and atmosphere", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Lithosphere and hydrosphere", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Hydrosphere", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Lithosphere", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The \'term\' biosphere is used for a zone containing living beings in Lithosphere, hydrosphere and atmosphere.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(168,'biology',100,553,1107,'The expulsion of sperms from seminiferous tubules is known as ______','[{"text": "Ejaculation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Spermatogenesis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Spermiation", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "None of these", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'After spermiogenesis, sperm heads become embedded in the Sertoli cells, and are finally released from the seminiferous tubules by the process called spermiation.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(170,'biology',103,965,2247,'Pathogens could belong to','[{"text": "Bacteria, viruses", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Fungi", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Protozoans, helminths", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of them", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'A wide range of organisms belonging to bacteria, viruses, fungi, protozoans, helminths, etc., could cause diseases in man. Such disease causing organisms are called pathogens. Most parasites are therefore pathogens as they cause harm to the host by living in (or on) them. The pathogens can enter our body by various means, multiply and interfere with normal vital activities, resulting in morphological and functional damage.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(171,'biology',105,1276,3093,'Major biomes such as desert, rainfall and tundra are formed due to','[{"text": "Annual variation in the intensity of temperature", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Annual variation in the duration of temperature", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Annual variation in the precipitation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All the above", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Biomes vary in their characteristics due to variation in the intensity of temperature, duration of temperature and rainfall pattern.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(172,'biology',100,553,1107,'Select the correct option.<br>','[{"text": "A - Primary spermatocyte,<br>\\nB - Sertoli cells,<br>\\nC - Spermatogonium<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - Sertoli cells,<br>\\nB - Spermatozoa,<br>\\nC - Spermatogonium<br>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A - Sertoli cells,<br>\\nB - Primary spermatocyte,<br>\\nC - Spermatozoa<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - Sertoli cells,<br>\\nB - Spermatozoa,<br>\\nC - Primary spermatocyte", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'A - Sertoli cells, B - Spermatozoa,<br>C - Spermatogonium',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/100_172_question_1.png'),
(174,'biology',103,965,2247,'What do the pathogens do in the host body?','[{"text": "Multiply themselves", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Interfere with normal vital activities", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Resulting in morphological and functional damage.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of them", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The pathogens can enter our body by various means, multiply and interfere with normal vital activities, resulting in morphological and functional damage. Pathogens have to adapt to life within the environment of the host.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(175,'biology',105,1276,3093,'Major biomes of India include','[{"text": "Tropical rainforest, Deciduous<br>forest, Desert and polar region", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Tropical rain forest, Deciduous forest, Desert, Sea coast", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Alpine region, Deciduous forest, Desert, Himalayan region", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Tropical rainforest, Alpine region, Polar region, Desert", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Major biomes of India include Tropical rain forest; Deciduous Forest; Desert; Sea coast.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(177,'biology',103,965,2247,'One of the biggest challenge for the parasites in the host gut is','[{"text": "Surviving in the stomach at high $\\\\mathrm{pH}$ and resisting the various digestive enzymes.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Surviving in the stomach at low $\\\\mathrm{pH}$ and resisting the various digestive enzymes.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Resisting the heat of the body", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of them", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Pathogens have to adapt to life within the environment of the host. For example, the pathogens that enter the gut must know a way of surviving in the stomach at low $\\mathrm{pH}$ and resisting the various digestive enzymes.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(178,'biology',105,1276,3093,'Pneumatophores are found in vegetation of which ecosystem','[{"text": "Desert", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Tropical rain forest", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sunderbans", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "All of the above", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Sunderbans region comprising Bangladesh and part of West Bengal, is a common large halophytic area',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(179,'biology',100,553,1107,'Spermiation takes place from ____ and the stages released are____ (respectively)<br>','[{"text": "Germinal epithelium & Spermatogonia<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sertoli cells & Mature spermatids<br>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Primordial germ cells & Spermatozoa<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sertoli cells & Spermatids", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Spermiation is the process of releasing spermatozoa from sertoli cells. The stages released are mature spermatids (spermatozoa)',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(181,'biology',103,965,2247,'Causative agent of typhoid fever is','[{"text": "<i>Entamoeba histolytica</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Mycobacterium</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Salmonella typhi</i>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "<i>Treponema pallidum</i>", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Typhoid is an acute infection of intestine. It is transmitted by faeco-oral route, also called enteric fever.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(182,'biology',100,553,1107,'If &nbsp;centriole of mature sperm is destroyed, which of the following is going to be affected?','[{"text": "Spermatogenesis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Fertilization", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cleavage", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "None of these", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Sperms carry centriole and the ovum is devoid of it, which means the zygote will not have centriole required for spindle formation during cleavage.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(183,'biology',105,1276,3093,'The part of the earth and atmosphere supporting life is','[{"text": "Biota", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Biome", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ecotone", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Biosphere", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Biota - the animal and plant life of a particular region, habitat, or geological period.<br>Biome -a large geographical area characterised by the presence of distinct group of vegetation and animals<br>Ecotone - a region of transition between two biological communities',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(185,'biology',103,965,2247,'<i>Salmonella typhi</i> affects ____ to cause typhoid','[{"text": "Heart", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Lungs", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Intestine", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Liver to cause typhoid", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Salmonella typhi ia an enteric pathogen hence affects intestine',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(186,'biology',105,1276,3093,'$0^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$ to $25^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$ annual variations in the intensity and duration of temperature and 30 to $80 \\mathrm{~cm}$ annual variation in precipitation, account for the formation of a major biome as','[{"text": "Temperate forest", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Coniferous forest", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Tropical forest", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Grassland", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Grassland',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(187,'biology',100,553,1107,'Another role of sperm besides activating egg is to carry','[{"text": "DNA", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "RNA", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ribosomes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mitochondria", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The sperm carries the DNA or genetic information within the male pronucleus present inside the nucleus.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(188,'biology',103,965,2247,'Which test is carried out if disease is caused by <i>Salmonella typhi</i>?','[{"text": "Widal test", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Lisman test", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Blood test", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Barium test", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The widal test, developed in 1896 and named after Georges-Fernand Widal, who introduced it, is a presumptive serological test for enteric fever or undulant fever where by bacteria causing typhoid fever are mixed with a serum containing specific antibodies obtained from an infected individual.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(3612,'biology',75,717,1513,'When the veinlets form a network, the venation is termed as','[{"text": "Reticulate", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Parallel", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both 1 and 2", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of them", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'When the veinlets form a network, the venation is termed as reticulate',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(190,'biology',105,1276,3093,'Which of the following lead to the formation of a wide variety of habitats within each biome','[{"text": "Regional variation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Local variation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Abiotic components", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both 1 and 2", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Regional and local variations in a particular place leads to the changes in the habitats in a biome',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(191,'biology',100,553,1107,'Hyaluronidase is present in','[{"text": "Blood", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ovary", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sperm", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Ovum", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'When the sperm reaches the ovum, it is able to penetrate the egg membrane with the assistance of hyaluronidase enzymes present on the surface of the sperm.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(192,'biology',103,965,2247,'Which test is an antigen-antibody depended for the confirmation of typhoid fever?','[{"text": "ECG", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mantoux test", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Widal test", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Urine test", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'It mostly occurs due to the contaminated food and water. Based on the antigen antibody reaction, the confirmatory test for typhoid is done by widal test. The causative agent for typhoid fever is salmonella typhi.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(193,'biology',105,1276,3093,'Formation of wide variety of habitats takes place by','[{"text": "Types of species inhabiting that area", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Regional variation alone", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Regional and local variation of environment conditions", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "All of the above", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Formation of wide variety of habitats takes place by Regional and local variation of environment conditions',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(194,'biology',100,553,1107,'Which part of the sperm provides energy to fertilize the egg?','[{"text": "Sperm head", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Acrosome", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sperm tail", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Middle piece", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Structure of sperm is head, middle piece and tail. Head consists of single set of chromosomes. It is haploid. Middle piece contains mitochondria. Mitochondria produce energy for movement of tail. The tail of sperm is with contractile proteins. The energy for contraction is released from mitochondria',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
