(215,'biology',103,965,2247,'A classic case in medicine, that of Mary Mallon nicknamed','[{"text": "Typhoid Mary", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Cholera Mary", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cancer Mary", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Tuberculosis Mary", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'A classic case in medicine, that of Mary Mallon nicknamed Typhoid Mary, is worth mentioning here. She was a cook by profession and was a typhoid carrier who continued to spread typhoid for several years through the food she prepared.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(216,'biology',100,553,1107,'What differentiates a sperm from egg?<br>','[{"text": "Mitochondria forms a sheath in egg and is diffused in sperm<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Presence of centriole in sperm contributes for cleavage after fertilization.<br>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Nucleus is clear in sperm and very compact in egg<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cytoplasm is more abundant in sperm than in egg", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The sperm contains proximal centriole which contributes to egg cell. Egg cell is devoid of centriole and centriole is a must for cell division.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(217,'biology',105,1276,3093,'Match the columns I and II with respect to the temperatures of the following regions.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Temperate forest<br>B. Arctic and Alpine Tundra<br>C. Grassland</div><div class="column-right">P. ${\\rm{ - 11^\\circ C}}$ to ${\\rm{0^\\circ C}}$<br>Q. 10 to ${\\rm{20^\\circ C}}$<br>R. 0 to ${\\rm{25^\\circ C}}$</div></div>','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{Q}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{P}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{Q}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{R}$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'$\\mathrm{A}-\\mathrm{Q}, \\mathrm{B}-\\mathrm{P}, \\mathrm{C}-\\mathrm{R}$',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(218,'biology',103,965,2247,'Identify the correct statement about typhoid<br>A. Mary Mallon was a cook by profession and was a typhoid carrier who continued to spread typhoid for several years through the food she prepared.<br>B. <em>Salmonella typhi</em> is a pathogenic moneran which causes typhoid fever in human beings.','[{"text": "Only A", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only B", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both are correct", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Statement A. that of Mary Mallon nicknamed Typhoid Mary, is worth mentioning here. She was a cook by profession and was a typhoid carrier who continued to spread typhoid for several years through the food she prepared.<br>Statement B. <em>Salmonella typhi</em> is a pathogenic bacterium (bacteria belongs to kingdom monera) which causes typhoid fever in human beings.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(220,'biology',100,553,1107,'The head of mature mammalian sperm is made of<br>','[{"text": "An acrosome<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Elongated nucleus covered by acrosome<br>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Two centrioles and an axial filament.<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Nucleus, acrosome, cytoplasm and mitochondrial sheath.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Acrosome-In mammals the acrosome contains digestive enzymes (including hyaluronidase and acrosin). These enzymes break down the outer membrane of the ovum, called the zona pellucida, allowing the haploid nucleus in the sperm cell to join with the haploid nucleus in the ovum',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
