(227,'biology',100,553,1107,'In the absence of acrosome the sperm<br>','[{"text": "Cannot penetrate the egg<br>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Cannot get energy", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cannot take food", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cannot swim fast", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The acrosome releases lytic enzymes necessary to dissolve the zona pellucida. In its absence, the sperm is unable to penetrate the egg.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(228,'biology',103,965,2247,'Which of the following statements regarding the disease typhoid is/are correct? <br>I. <em>Salmonella typhi </em>are the pathogenic virus which enter human intestine through contaminated food and water and migrate to other organs through blood.<br>II. Sustained high fever $\\left(39^{\\circ} \\mathrm{F}\\right.$ to $\\left.40^{\\circ} \\mathrm{F}\\right)$, weakness, stomach pain, constipation, headache and loss of appetite are some common symptoms of typhoid.<br>III. Widal test is used for diagnosis of typhoid fever.<br>IV. A classic case in medicine, of Mary Mallon nicknamed, Typhoid Mary who was a carrier','[{"text": "I and II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III and IV", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "II and IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I and IV", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Statements that are incorrect:-I. <em>Salmonella typhi</em> are the pathogenic bacteria which enter human intestine through contaminated food and water and migrate to other organs through blood.<br>II.sustained high fever $\\left(39^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}\\right.$ to $40^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$ ), weakness, stomach pain, constipation, headache and loss of appetite are some of the common symptoms of typhoid.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(230,'biology',105,1276,3093,'Habitat includes','[{"text": "Biotic components", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Abiotic components", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pathogens, predators, parasites and competitors", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All the above", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Habitat is the place where the organisms reside. It includes all the components of that place.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(231,'biology',100,553,1107,'Which is true about viability of mammalian sperm<br>','[{"text": "Sperm viability is determined by its motility<br>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Sperms must be concentrated in thin suspension<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sperm is more active in acidic medium<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sperm remains viable only for 24 hours", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The motility of sperm along is an indication of a viable sperm also. It can survive in alkaline medium. The estimated life span of a normal mammalian sperm is 5-6 days.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
