(295,'biology',103,965,2247,'Which of the following pathogens causes whooping cough?','[{"text": "<i>Corynebacterium</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Bordetella pertussis</i>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "<i>Vibrio cholerae</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Clostridium tetani</i>", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Pertussis, a respiratory illness commonly known as whooping cough, is a very contagious disease caused by a type of bacteria called Bordetella pertussis. These bacteria attach to the cilia (tiny, hair-like extensions) that line part of the upper respiratory system. The bacteria release toxins (poisons), which damage the cilia and cause airways to swell.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
