(336,'biology',103,965,2247,'Name the disease that spreads through contaminated water.','[{"text": "Amoebiasis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Typhoid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cholera", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All the above", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'1) Houseflies act as mechanical carriers and serve to transmit the amoebiasis parasite from faeces of infected person to food and food products, thereby contaminating them. Drinking water and food contaminated by the faecal matter are the main source of infection.<br>2) Typhoid pathogens generally enter the small intestine through food and water contaminated with them and migrate to other organs through blood.<br>3) Cholera is caused by Virio cholerae. These may get into healthy person with contaminated food and water',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(337,'biology',100,553,1108,'In human females at the time of birth there are two million ova, how many of them normally reach maturity incourse of normal reproductive life (approximately)','[{"text": "500", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "1,000", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "2,000", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "5,000", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The eggs are stored within follicles in the ovary. Within a woman\'s life span, large numbers of follicles and oocytes will be recruited to begin the growth and maturation process. The large majority, will not reach full maturity.Most will die off in a process called atresia. Thus, only about 300-500 of these eggs will mature over a women\'s life span.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(339,'biology',105,1277,3094,'The study of soil and organism living in it is known as','[{"text": "Pedology", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Zoology", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Dendrology", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Exobiology", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Zoology- study of animals, Dendrology-the scientific study of trees, Exobiology- the branch of science that deals with the possibility and likely nature of life on other planets or in space. <i>Pedology</i> is study of soil and organisms in it.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
