(441,'biology',103,965,2247,'Where will you look for the sporozoites of the malarial parasite?','[{"text": "RBCs of human suffering from malaria", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Spleen of infected person", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Salivary glands of freshly moulted female <i>Anopheles</i> mosquito", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Saliva of infected female <i>Anopheles</i> mosquito", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'When a female Anopheles mosquito bites an infected person, these parasites enter the mosquito\'s body and undergo further development. The parasites multiply within them to form sporozoites that are stored in their salivary glands.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
