(461,'biology',103,965,2247,'The malarial parasite requires two hosts ____ to complete its life cycle','[{"text": "Primary host - human and intermediate mosquitoes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Primary host- mosquitoes and intermediate human", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Primary host- human male and intermediate human female", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Primary host - Female mosquito and intermediate male mosquitoes", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Technically the primary host of a parasite bean sexual cycle of the parasite and secondary host bears asexual cycle of the parasite. So, sexual cycle of Plasmodium is taken place in mosquito (i.e., primary host) and asexual cycle is completed in man (i.e. secondary host).',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(463,'biology',100,554,1109,'In human females, ovulation occurs during menstrual cycle<br>','[{"text": "In the beginning of proliferative phase<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Just before the end of secretory phase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "In the middle of secretory phase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "At the end of proliferative phase", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'During the proliferative phase, there is a rapid increase in the levels of LH and FSH in the middle of cycle. LH secretion reaches to its maximum level in the mid-cycle which is also known as LH surge. Due to this, the Graafian follicle rises to the surface, ruptures and releases the ovum. This process is called as ovulation. This occurs at the end of the proliferative phase.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
