(465,'biology',103,965,2247,'Sporogony of malarial parasite occurs in','[{"text": "Liver of man", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Stomach wall of mosquito", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "RBCs of man", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Salivary glands of mosquito", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Sporogony of malarial parasites occur in stomach wall of mosquito. It is an asexual multiplication phase. The nucleus of the oocyst divides and followed by cytoplasmic division, several sporozoites are formed.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(467,'biology',105,1278,3095,'Animals like snail and fish go into____to avoid summer related problems and animal like bear go into ____ to avoid winter related stress.','[{"text": "Hibernation, aestivation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Migration, hibernation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Aestivation, hibernation", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Aestivation, migration", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Aestivation, hibernation',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(468,'biology',100,554,1109,'Diagram represent.<br>','[{"text": "A - Ovary $\\\\mathrm{B}$ - progesterone", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - Ovary B - Oestrogen", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - Anterior lobe of pituitary gland, B-FSH", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A - Posterior lobe of pitutary gland, B-FSH", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'A- Anterior lobe of pituitary gland, B-FSH',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/100_468_question_1.png'),
(469,'biology',103,965,2247,'Malaria is a disease which is affected when the sickle-shaped sporozoite is injected into the blood of a healthy human being by the bite of infected Anopheles mosquito. It damages the','[{"text": "Lungs", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Heart", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "liver", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Kidney", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'During the infective stage of Malaria, the sporozoites are injected into the blood of a healthy human being by the bite of infected Anopheles female mosquito, leads to damage of liver cells and destroy the red blood corpuscles and release yellowish pigment, the Schuffner\'s granules.Deposition of this pigment in blood produces yellowish colour of eyes and skin',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(471,'biology',100,554,1109,'Uterine endometrium, epithelial glands and connective tissue are broken down in menstrual cycle. This is due to<br>','[{"text": "Lack of estrogen<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Lack of progesterone<br>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Over secretion of FSH<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Over production of progesterone", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'When there is a drop in the level of progesterone, the uterine endometrium begins to shed due to contractions along with connective tissue and other cells. This is known as the menstrual flow in the menstrual cycle.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(472,'biology',105,1278,3095,'Diapause is a','[{"text": "Stage of development", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Stage of suspended development", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Stage of delayed development", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Rapid developmental stage", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Diapause is a stage of suspended development',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(473,'biology',103,965,2247,'From which kind of hosts, life cycle of <em>Plasmodium</em> passes?','[{"text": "Male of human and of&nbsp;<em>Anopheles</em>&nbsp;mosquito", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Male of human and male of <em>Anopheles</em> mosquito", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Human and female <em>Anopheles</em> mosquito", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Human and Male <em>Anopheles</em> mosquito", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'It is interesting to note that the malarial parasite requires two hosts - human and mosquitoes - to complete its life cycle; the female <em>Anopheles</em> mosquito is the vector (transmitting agent) too.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(474,'biology',105,1278,3095,'Diapause, is shown by','[{"text": "Migratory birds", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Bears", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Snails and fish", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Zooplanktons", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Diapause, is shown by zooplanktons.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(475,'biology',100,554,1109,'Withdrawal of which of the following hormones is the immediate cause of menstruation?','[{"text": "FSH-RH", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Estrogen", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Progesterone", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{FSH}$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'In the absence of fertilization, the corpus luteum begins to degenerate. This causes a decline in the levels of progesterone and estrogen. Corpus luteum changes into corpus albicans.Due to these uterine contractions, there by causing the disintegration of the endometrial lining finally leading to menstruation.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(476,'biology',103,965,2247,'Which of the following is incorrect about malaria?','[{"text": "It is caused through the bite of infected male anopheles.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "The rupture of RBCs is associated with release of a toxic substance haemozoin.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Malignant malaria is caused by <em>Plasmodium falciparum</em>.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Plasmodium enters the human body as sporozoites.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'<em>Plasmodium</em>, a tiny protozoan is responsible for this disease. <em>Plasmodium </em>enters the human body as sporozoites (infectious form) through the bite of infected female <em>Anopheles </em>mosquito.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(478,'biology',105,1279,3096,'Attribute of the organisms that enable organisms to survive and reproduce in its habitat are called','[{"text": "Mutation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Adaptations", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Mimicry", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Surviving abilities", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Attribute of the organisms that enable organisms to survive and reproduce in its habitat are called Adaptations.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(479,'biology',100,554,1109,'At menopause there is rise in urinary excretion of','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{MSH}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{FSH}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{LH}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{STH}$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Menopause marks the end of the menstrual cycle and is therefore, characterized by high FSH levels. Even a high level of FSH during menopause fails to stimulate the growth of the ovarian follicles, induce ovulation, and increase the level of estrogen.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(480,'biology',103,965,2247,'Give the correct sequence for pre erythrocytic cycle?','[{"text": "Saliva-sprozoites-blood-liver- asexual reproduction- gametocytes", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Merozoites-saliva-blood-liverasexual reproduction-gametocytes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Saliva-asexual reproduction-blood-liver- sporozoites gametocytes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Saliva-sporozoites-liver-blood- asexual reproduction-gametocytes", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Each sporozoite grows in the liver cell to form a large and round schizont, which divides to form about 1,000 small spindleshaped merozoites. This multiple fission is called schizogamy. The schizont ruptures and merozoites are liberated into liver venous passage. This phase of reproduction is termed as pre-erythrocytic phase.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(482,'biology',100,554,1109,'Hormone having no role in menstruation is','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{LH}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{FSH}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{GH}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "None of these", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Hormones responsible for menstrual flow are FSH, LH, Estrogen and progesterone. GH is growth hormone.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(483,'biology',105,1279,3096,'Adaptations are meant for','[{"text": "Change", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Improvement", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Survival", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Extinction", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Adaptations are meant for survival.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(486,'biology',105,1279,3096,'Adaptation is any attribute of the organism that enables the organism to survive and reproduce in its habitat. These attributes are','[{"text": "Morphological only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Physiological only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Morphological, physiological, behavioural", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Behavioural only", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Morphological, physiological, behavioural.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(488,'biology',103,965,2247,'The fertilisation of gametocytes of <i>Plasmodium</i> takes place inside','[{"text": "Human RBC", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Human Liver", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mosquito gut", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Mosquito salivary gland", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The merozoites give rise to the male and female gametocytes. When a female Anopheles mosquito bites this individual, it takes up the gametocytes with the blood. In the stomach of the mosquito, the fertilization of these gametes occurs.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(489,'biology',100,554,1109,'Egg is ovulated from ovary in<br>','[{"text": "Primary oocyte stage<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Secondary oocyte stage", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Menstrual phase<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mature ovum stage", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Egg is ovulated from ovary in Secondary oocyte stage.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(490,'biology',103,965,2247,'<i>Plasmodium</i> belongs to which kingdom?','[{"text": "Kingdom Monera", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Kingdom Protista", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Kingdom Fungi", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "KIngdom Animalia", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Plasmodium is a protozoan and protozoa belongs to kingdom protista.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(491,'biology',105,1279,3096,'Adaptations that have evolved over a long evolutionary time and are ____ fixed.','[{"text": "Genetically", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Phenotypically", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mutationally", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Randomly", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Adaptations that have evolved over a long evolutionary time and are genetically fixed',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(493,'biology',100,554,1109,'Oocyte is liberated from ovary under the influence of $\\mathrm{LH}$, in which of the following phase<br>','[{"text": "End of Meiosis II<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "End of Meiosis I<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Arrested at anaphase II.<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Arrested at metaphase II.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Oocyte released during ovulation is arrested at metaphase II.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(494,'biology',103,965,2247,'In the life cycle of <i>Plasmodium</i> in humans, which organs are involved?','[{"text": "Stomach", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{RBC}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Liver", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both 2 and 3", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Plasmodium enters the human body as sporozoites (infectious form) through the bite of infected female Anopheles mosquito. The parasites initially multiply within the liver cells and then attack the red blood cells (RBCs) resulting in their rupture. Therefore, liver and RBC are involved in the life cycle of Plasmodium.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(495,'biology',105,1279,3096,'A terrestrial mammal who seldom drinks water','[{"text": "Kangaroo mouse", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Rhinoceros", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Kangaroo rat", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Camel", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'A terrestrial mammal who seldom drinks water is kangaroo rat.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
