(498,'biology',105,1279,3096,'Kangaroo rat is capable of meeting all its water requirements through internal fat oxidation. This animal is found in','[{"text": "North American deserts", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Australian deserts", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Rajasthan", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Scotland", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Kangaroo rat is capable of meeting all its water requirements through internal fat oxidation. This animal is found in North American deserts',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(510,'biology',103,965,2247,'Identify the stage in which sporozite enters human','[{"text": "B", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{C}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "D", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Plasmodium enters the human body as sporozoites (infectious form) through the bite of infected female Anopheles mosquito.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/103_510_question_1.png'),
(499,'biology',103,965,2247,'Which of the following statements is not correct regarding malarial infection?','[{"text": "<em>Plasmodium </em>enters the human body as sporozoites throught the bite of freshly moulted female anopheles mosquito.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "High fever recurring every three to four days.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sporozoites initially multiply within the liver cells and then attack the RBC\'s resulting in their rupture.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "When a female <em>Anopheles </em>mosquito bites an infected person, these parasites enter the mosquito\'s body and undergo further development.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Malaria which is caused by <em>Plasmodium </em>is a vector-borne disease transmitted by infected female Anopheles mosquito. The credit of the working out complicated life cycle of the malarial parasite goes to Sir Ronald Ross. Hence the name Ross cycle.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(500,'biology',100,554,1109,'Which of the following does not occur between 5-28 days of menstrual cycle?','[{"text": "Premenstrual phase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Luteal phase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Secretory phase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Menstrual phase", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The cycle starts with the menstrual phase, when menstrual flow occurs and it lasts for 3-5 days.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(502,'biology',105,1279,3096,'In the absence of an external source of water, kangaroo rat in North American desert is capable of meeting all its water requirements through','[{"text": "Internal fat oxidation", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Taking liquid food", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Reducing his activities", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Hibernation", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'In the absence of an external source of water, Kangaroo rat in North American desert is capable of meeting all its water requirements through internal fat oxidation.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(503,'biology',103,965,2247,'Which is the right sequence for life cycle of Anopheles mosquito?','[{"text": "Fertilisation in mosquito $\\\\rightarrow$ sporozoites $\\\\rightarrow$ Gametocyte from infected mosquito $\\\\rightarrow$ sporozoites", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Fertilisation in mosquito $\\\\rightarrow$ sporozoites $\\\\rightarrow$ oocyst $\\\\rightarrow$ gametocyte $\\\\rightarrow$ Gametocyte from infected mosquito", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Gametocyte from infected mosquito $\\\\rightarrow$ fertilisation in mosquito $\\\\rightarrow$ sporozoites $\\\\rightarrow$ Non infected person", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Fertilisation in mosquito $\\\\rightarrow$ sporozoites $\\\\rightarrow$ oocyst $\\\\rightarrow$ Gametocyte from infected mosquito", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The malaria parasite life cycle involves two hosts. During a blood meal, a malaria-infected female Anopheles mosquito inoculates sporozoites into the human host<br>1) Sporozoites infect liver cells<br>2) and mature into schizonts<BR>3) which rupture and release merozoites<BR>4) (Of note, in $P$. vivax and $P$. ovale a dormant stage [hypnozoites] can persist in the liver and cause relapses by invading the bloodstream weeks, or even years later.) After this initial replication in the liver (exo-erythrocytic schizogony), the parasites undergo asexual multiplication in the erythrocytes (erythrocytic schizogony). Merozoites infect red blood cells. The ring stage trophozoites mature into schizonts, which rupture releasing merozoites. Some parasites differentiate into sexual erythrocytic stages (gametocytes)<BR>5) Blood stage parasites are responsible for the clinical manifestations of the disease.The gametocytes, male (microgametocytes) and female (macrogametocytes), are ingested by an Anopheles mosquito during a blood meal<BR>6) The parasites\' multiplication in the mosquito is known as the sporogonic cycle. While in the mosquito\'s stomach, the microgametes penetrate the macrogametes generating zygotes<BR>7) The zygotes in turn become motile and elongated (ookinetes)<BR>8) which invade the midgut wall of the mosquito where they develop into oocysts<BR>9) The oocysts grow, rupture, and release sporozoites<BR>10) Which make their way to the mosquito\'s salivary glands. Inoculation of the sporozoites into a new human host perpetuates the malaria life cycle.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(504,'biology',100,554,1109,'Correct sequence of hormone secretion from beginning of menstruation is<br>','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{FSH}$, progesterone, estrogen<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Estrogen, FSH, progesterone<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Estrogen, progesterone, FSH<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{FSH}$, estrogen, progesterone", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Correct sequence of hormone secretion is FSH, oestrogen, Progesterone',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(505,'biology',105,1279,3096,'The kangaroo rats of North American deserts do not need to drink water because','[{"text": "They meet their water requirement through internal fat oxidation in which the water is a byproduct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Their nephrons lack loops of Henle", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "They have numerous sweat glands", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of the above", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The Kangaroo rats of North American deserts do not need to drink water because they meet their water requirements through internal oxidation fats in which water is a by-product. They have long loops of Henle and are able to concentrate their urine thereby minimizing the loss of water from their body and also they do not have sweat glands so no perspiration occurs in the animals.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(507,'biology',103,965,2247,'Identify the following.','[{"text": "Sporozoite in RBC", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sporozoite in salivary gland", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Merozoite in salivary gland", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Gametocyte in RBC", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The parasites multiply within mosquito to form sporozoites that are stored in their salivary glands.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/103_507_question_1.png'),
(508,'biology',100,554,1109,'If mammalian ovum fails to get fertilized, which of the following is unlikely?','[{"text": "Corpus luteum will disintegrate", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Development of zygote", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Progesterone secretion rapidly increases", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Estrogen secretion further decreases", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'In the absence of fertilisation, the corpus luteum degenerates.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(509,'biology',105,1279,3096,'Which of the following organs helps in physiological adaptation in desert rodents','[{"text": "Spleen", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Liver", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Kidney", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Lungs", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Kidney helps in physiological adaptation in desert rodents',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(512,'biology',100,554,1109,'In a 32-day menstrual cycle, ovulation occurs on','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{1}}{{\\\\rm{4}}^{th}}$ day", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{1}}{{\\\\rm{8}}^{th}}$ day", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{1}}{{\\\\rm{6}}^{th}}$ day", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{2}}{{\\\\rm{0}}^{th}}$ day", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'In duration, luteal phase is the most constant part of the female reproductive cycle (14 days). In a 28-day menstrual cycle, ovulation occurs on ${\\rm{1}}{{\\rm{4}}^{{\\rm{th}}}}$ day (28-14=14). In a 32 day menstrual cycle, ovulation occurs on 18th day $(32-14=18)$.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(513,'biology',105,1279,3096,'Which is the characteristic of desert adaptation?','[{"text": "Thick cuticle on their leaf surface", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Stomata arranged in deep pits", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Stomata remain closed during day (CAM)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of the above", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'<br>(1) Thick cuticle on their leaf surface<br>(2) Stomata arranged in deep pits<br>(3) Stomata remain closed during day (CAM)',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(514,'biology',103,965,2247,'Causative organism of amoebiasis is','[{"text": "<i>Plasmodium vivax</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Entamoeba histolytica</i>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "<i>Streptococcus pneumoniae</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Salmonella sp.</i>", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'<i>Entamoeba histolytica</i> is a protozoan parasite in the large intestine of human which causes amoebiasis (amoebic dysentery).',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(515,'biology',100,554,1109,'Luteal phase is other name of<br>','[{"text": "Menstrual flow phase<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Follicular phase<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Proliferative phase<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Secretory phase", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Luteal phase is also known as secretory phase.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(517,'biology',105,1279,3096,'An adaptation of <i>Opuntia</i> is that, it performs photosynthesis by','[{"text": "Flower", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Stem", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Roots", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Shoot", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'An adaptation of Opuntia is that, it performs photosynthesis by stem.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(518,'biology',103,965,2247,'Causative organism of dysentery caused by a protista is','[{"text": "<i>Plasmodium vivax</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Entamoeba histolytica</i>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "<i>Streptococcus pneumoniae</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Salmonella sp.</i>", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'<i>Entamoeba histolytica</i> is a protozoan parasite in the large intestine of human which causes amoebiasis (amoebic dysentery).',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(519,'biology',100,554,1109,'Which is correctly matched in a normal menstrual cycle?<br><div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "Endometrium secretes nutrients for Implantation-11 to 18 days<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Rise in progesterone level- 1 to 15 days<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Release of egg- $5^{\\\\text {th }}$ day<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Endometrium regenerates- 5 to 10 days", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'After menstrual phase proliferative phase occurs during which the endometrium undergoes repair. This period lasts for 5-10 days.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
