(567,'biology',100,555,1110,'After insemination the correct pathway of sperm movement is','[{"text": "Vagina $\\\\rightarrow$ Cervix $\\\\rightarrow$ Uterus $\\\\rightarrow$ Ampulla $\\\\rightarrow$ Isthmus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Vagina $\\\\rightarrow$ Uterus $\\\\rightarrow$ Cervix $\\\\rightarrow$ Isthmus $\\\\rightarrow$ Ampulla", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Vagina $\\\\rightarrow$ Cervix $\\\\rightarrow$ Ampulla $\\\\rightarrow$ Uterus $\\\\rightarrow$ Isthmus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Vagina $\\\\rightarrow$ Cervix $\\\\rightarrow$ Uterus $\\\\rightarrow$ Isthmus $\\\\rightarrow$ Ampulla", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The sperm has to reach ampulla of fallopian tube, for fertilising the Ovum. It has to pass through<br>Vagina $\\rightarrow$ Cervix $\\rightarrow$ Uterus $\\rightarrow$ Isthmus $\\rightarrow$ Ampulla',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(569,'biology',105,1279,3096,'Desert lizards lack the ____A_____ ability that mammals have to deal with the ____B____ temperatures of their habitat, but manage to keep their body temperature fairly constant by ____C____ means.','[{"text": "A - morphological, B - High, $\\\\mathrm{C}$ - behavioural", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - physiological, B - high, C - behavioural", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A - behavioural, B - high, C - physiological", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - physiological, B - high, C - morphological", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'A - physiological, B - high, C - behavioural',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(570,'biology',103,965,2247,'Which one is not a symptom of disease caused in Amoebiasis?','[{"text": "Congestion in chest", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Constipation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Abdominal pain and cramps", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Stools with excess mucus and blood clots", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Symptoms of amoebiasis disease include constipation, abdominal pain and cramps, stools with excess mucous and blood clots. Chest congestion is caused when the body\'s mucus production kicks into overdrive, which can be caused by respiratory infections like cold or flu, allergic reactions, airborne irritants, or even indulging in a spicy meal.3 This excess mucus finds its way into the lungs - or is generated there - and causes an uncomfortable fullness.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(571,'biology',100,555,1110,'Onset of pregnancy<br>','[{"text": "Stimulates testosterone secretion.<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Leads to degeneration of ovary.<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Inhibit further ovulation.<br>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Inhibits fusion of egg and sperm nuclei.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Pregnancy is the state when the menstrual cycle temporarily stops and the fertilized egg develops to form a young one of the organism.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(572,'biology',105,1279,3096,'Mark the incorrect statement.','[{"text": "Many fishes thrive in Antarctic water where temperature is always below zero.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Some microbes can survive in hot springs where temperature exceeds $100^{\\\\circ} \\\\mathrm{C}$.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Deep sea fishes can survive even at a depth where pressure exceeds $100 \\\\mathrm{~atm}$.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Desert lizards have marvelous physiological ability to survive scorching heat of desert.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Desert lizards lack the physiological ability that mammals love to deal with the high temperature of their habitat but manage to keep their body temperature fairly constant by behavioural means. They bask in the sun and absorb heat when their body temperature drops below the comfort zone, but move into shade when the ambient temperature starts increasing.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
