(595,'biology',105,1279,3096,'Whales, the world\'s largest living mammals, live in the ocean, but why there are not very small aquatic mammals?','[{"text": "They cannot regulate body temperature effectively in water", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "They get eaten by large animals", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Their kidneys cannot handle life in the marine environment", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "They lose too much heat from evaporation.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'They cannot regulate body temperature effectively in water',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(596,'biology',103,965,2247,'Infection of <em>Ascaris</em> usually occurs by','[{"text": "Eating imperfectly cooked pork containing&nbsp;<em>Ascaris</em>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Tse-Tse fly", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mosquiote bite", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Drinking water containing eggs of <em>Ascaris</em>", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The eggs of the parasite are excreted along with the faeces of infected persons which contaminate soil, water, plants, etc. A healthy person acquires this infection through contaminated water, vegetables, fruits, etc.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(597,'biology',100,555,1111,'Female produce only','[{"text": "Either X or Y type of gamete", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "One type of gamete X", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "One type of gamete Y", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "No gametes", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Female produce only one type of gamete X',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(598,'biology',105,1279,3096,'Which of the following statement is false w.r.t adaptation?','[{"text": "All adaptations are generally fixed in all organisms.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Many xerophytic plants have thick cuticle on leaf epidermis, sunken stomata", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Some xerophytic plants have special photosynthetic pathway (CAM) that enables their stomata to close during day", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Opuntia has spines (modified leaves), photosynthetic phylloclade (stem)", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'All adaptations are generally fixed in all organisms.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(600,'biology',103,965,2247,'The causative agent of Filariasis is','[{"text": "<i>Wuchereria bancrofti</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Wuchereria malayi</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Wuchereria lumbricoides</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both 1 and 2", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Wuchereria (W. bancrofti and W. malayi), the filarial worms cause a slowly developing chronic inflammation of the organs in which they live for many years, usually the lymphatic vessels of the lower limbs and the disease is called elephantiasis or filariasis',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(601,'biology',100,555,1112,'During cleavage all divisions are','[{"text": "Mitotic", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Determinate", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Equal", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Reductive", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The cleavage is a progressive division of the zygote with increased number of cells with decreasing size. All the cells divide mitotically.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(602,'biology',105,1280,3097,'Population is best described by organisms that&nbsp;','[{"text": "Potentially interbreed", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Share or compete for similar resources", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Live in groups in a well defined geographical area", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of them", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Population is best described by stated by<br>(1) Potentially interbreed<br>(2) Share or compete for similar resources<br>(3) Live in groups in a well defined geographical area.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL);
