(620,'biology',103,965,2247,'Which one is responsible for the disease from the given figure','[{"text": "Ringworm", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Filarial worm", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Amoebiasis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Plasmodium", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The filarial worms are amongst the most important nematode parasite which cause filariasis. The worm responsible for this disease is <i>Wuchereria bancrofti.</i> It is an important filarial parasite of man in Africa and Asia.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/103_620_question_1.png'),
(621,'biology',105,1280,3097,'Which of the following is a population attribute?','[{"text": "Majority of them live in groups in a well-defined geographical location", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Never share or compete for similar resources", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Potentially never interbreed", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Single individuals of any species cannot live in isolation", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Majority of them live in groups in a well- defined geographical location',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(622,'biology',100,555,1112,'Mixing up of the chromosomes of a sperm and an ovum is known as','[{"text": "Karyogamy or amphimixis.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Karyogamy or apomixis.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Apogamy or amphimixis.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Apogamy or apomixis.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Mixing up of the chromosomes of a sperm and an ovum is known as karyogamy or amphimixis.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(623,'biology',103,965,2247,'<i>Wuchereria</i> are transmitted to a healthy person through the ____','[{"text": "Bite by the female <i>Culex</i> vectors.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Bite by the female <i>Anopheles</i> vectors.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Bite by the female <i>Aedes</i> vectors.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Bite by the female house fly.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Wuchereria bancrofti is the organism which causes filariasis in humans. The parasite completes its life cycle in two hosts. The humans serve as their definitive host. The culex mosquitoes are the intermediate host. The organism transmits the disease with the help of culex mosquitoes.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(624,'biology',105,1280,3097,'Demography is the study of','[{"text": "Population growth", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Birth rates", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Family pedigrees", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Death rates", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Demography is the study of population growth.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(626,'biology',100,555,1112,'Which of the following will be lost only during implantation of the embryo in the wall of the uterus?','[{"text": "Zona pellucida", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Corona radiata", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Trophoblast", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Discus proligerus", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'At the time of fertilisation, the spermlysis dissolve corona radiata but zona pellucida is lost only at the time of implantation.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(627,'biology',103,965,2247,'Select the appropriate option<br>I. Malaria is an arthropod - mosquito protozoal disease.<br>II. Filaria is an arthropod - mosquito helminthic disease.','[{"text": "Only I is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only II is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both are correct", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "None are correct", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Statement I :Malaria is caused by a protozoan parasite, Plasmodium and its vector is an arthropod, female Anopheles mosquito.<br>Statement II : Filaria is caused by an aschelminth, Wuchereria and its vector is an arthropod, female Culex mosquito.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(628,'biology',105,1280,3097,'Members of biological species are potentially able to:','[{"text": "Undergo changes in all the individuals at the same time", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mutate", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Interbreed", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Express all the same genes", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Members of biological species are potentially able to: interbreed.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(630,'biology',100,555,1112,'Cell division that occurs in zygote is called','[{"text": "Cleavage", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Meiosis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mitosis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Differentiation", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'After fertilization the ovum turns into a zygote which undergoes subsequent divisions thereby increasing in cell number with decreased cell size in a process called cleavage.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(631,'biology',103,965,2247,'Identify the name of two aschelminths, which cause ascariasis and filariasis, respetively.','[{"text": "<i>Ancyclostoma</i> and <i>Wuchereria</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Wucheraria</i> and <i>Ascaris</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Ascaris</i> and <i>Wuchereria</i>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "<i>Ancyclostoma</i> and <i>Wuchereria</i>", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The disease, Ascariasis is caused by an intestinal parasite called Ascaris also known as roundworm. Filariasis is a parasitic disease caused by an infection of roundworms of the filarial species, Wuchereria bancrofti.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(632,'biology',105,1280,3097,'Which out of the following is considered a population for the purpose of ecological studies?','[{"text": "Individuals resulting from asexual reproduction only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Individuals resulting from sexual reproduction only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Individuals resulting from asexual and sexual reproduction", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "None of them", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Individuals resulting from asexual and sexual reproduction',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(633,'biology',100,555,1111,'The human male has which of the following sex chromosome pattern?','[{"text": "XYY", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "X X", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "X Y", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "YY", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Sex chromosome of the human male is: $X Y$',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(634,'biology',103,965,2247,'Many fungi belonging to genera are responsible for skin infections','[{"text": "<i>Microsporum</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Trichophyton</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Epidermophyton</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of them", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Many fungi belonging to the genera Microsporum, Trichophyton and<br>Epidermophyton are responsible for ringworms which is one of the most common infectious diseases in man.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(635,'biology',105,1280,3097,'Which out of the following represents a population?<br>A. The cormorants in a wetland<br>B. Rats in an abandoned dwelling<br>C. Teakwood trees in a forest tract<br>D. Bacteria in a culture plate<br>E. Lotus plants in a pond','[{"text": "Only A and B", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only A, B and C", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only A, B, C and D", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of them", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'A. The cormorants in a wetland<br>B. Rats in an abandoned dwelling<br>C. Teakwood trees in a forest tract<br>D. Bacteria in a culture plate<br>E. Lotus plants in a pond, are some examples of a population.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(637,'biology',100,555,1112,'Which alphabet represents 2-celled embryo?<br>','[{"text": "C", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "F", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "G", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "E", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'NCERT figure 3.11',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/100_637_question_1.png'),
(638,'biology',103,965,2247,'Many fungi are responsible for skin lesions called :','[{"text": "Filariasis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ascariasis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ringworms", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Amoebiasis", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Many fungi belonging to the genera Microsporum, Trichophyton and<br>Epidermophyton are responsible for ringworms which is one of the most common infectious diseases in man. Appearance of dry, scaly lesions on various parts of the body such as skin, nails and scalp are the main symptoms of the disease. These lesions are accompanied by intense itching.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(639,'biology',105,1280,3097,'An individual may have births and ____, but a population has ____ and death rates.','[{"text": "Death rate, birth rates", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Deaths, birth", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Deaths, birth rates", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Death rate, birth", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Deaths, birth rates',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(640,'biology',100,555,1112,'Cleavage is the rapid mitotic division occuring on the way through isthmus to oviduct. It occurs in','[{"text": "Ovum", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Zygote", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Sperm", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Fully formed foetus", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The mitotic division starts as the zygote moves through the Isthmus of the oviduct called cleavage towards the uterus.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(641,'biology',103,965,2247,'The pathogens of genera, <i>Microsporum, Trichophyton</i> and <i>Epidermophyton</i> are generally acquired','[{"text": "From soil or by using towels,", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Clothes or even the comb of infected individuals", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Bite of mosquito", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both 1 and 2", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Ringworms are generally acquired from soil or by using towels, clothes or even the comb of infected individuals.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(643,'biology',105,1280,3097,'If in a pond, there are 20 lotus plants of last year and through reproduction 8 new plants are added. Then, the birth rate is','[{"text": "0.8 offspring lotus per year", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "0.4 offspring lotus per year", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "0.2 offspring lotus per year", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "0.6 offspring lotus per year", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Rate $=$ Change in population/Orignal population $=28-20 / 40=8 / 20=0.4=820=0.4$ offspring lotus per year.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(644,'biology',100,555,1112,'Cleavage forms 2-4-8-16 cells, These cells are called','[{"text": "Blastocysts", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Blastomeres", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Morula", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Zygote", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Cleavage form $2,4,8,16$ daughter cells called blastomeres.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(645,'biology',103,965,2247,'What are the main symptoms of ringworm?','[{"text": "Appearance of dry, scaly lesions on various parts of the body", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Lesions are accompanied by intense itching.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Oozing of pus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both 1 and 2", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Appearance of dry, scaly lesions on various parts of the body such as skin, nails and scalp are the main symptoms of the disease. These lesions are accompanied by intense itching. Heat and moisture help these fungi to grow, which makes them thrive in skin folds such as those in the groin or between the toes.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(646,'biology',105,1280,3097,'Sex ratio is the','[{"text": "Ratio of females to males", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Ratio of males to females", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ratio of married females to married males", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ratio of infant girl to infant boy", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Sex ratio is defined as the number of females per 1000 males. This information is a valuable source for finding the population of women. According to 2011 Census, sex ratio is 940, which means 940 females per 1000 males in India. Although it is an upward trend as compared to 2001 census where sex ratio was 933. But is is still a matter of concern as female foeticide is still very prevalent. Although there are some states like Kerala and Union Territory like Puducherry in India have sex ratio in which females are more than males. Kerala houses a number of 1084 females to that of 1000 males',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(647,'biology',100,555,1112,'Embryo at 8-16 cells stage is called','[{"text": "Blastula", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Morula", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Trophoblast", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The embryo with 8 to 16 blastomeres is called a morula.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(648,'biology',103,965,2247,'What body parts are affected in ringworm?','[{"text": "Skin, nails and scalp", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Lungs", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Digestive system", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Lymphatic system", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Areas of the body that can be affected by ringworm include:<br>• Feet (tinea pedis, commonly called "athlete\'s foot")<br>• Groin, inner thighs, or buttocks (tinea cruris, commonly called "jock itch")<br>• Scalp (tinea capitis)<br>• Beard (tinea barbae)<br>• Hands (tinea manuum)<br>• Toenails or fingernails (tinea unguium, also called "onychomycosis")',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(649,'biology',105,1280,3097,'If birth rate is 100 , death rate is 10 and number of individuals in population group is 1000 , then what will be the percentage of natural growth rate?','[{"text": "$0.09 \\\\%$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$9.0 \\\\%$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$0.9 \\\\%$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$90 \\\\%$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'If birth rate is 100 , death rate is 10 and number of individuals in population group is 1000 , then $9.0 \\%$ will be the percentage of natural growth rate.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(650,'biology',100,555,1112,'Trophoblast of blastocyst attaches to the','[{"text": "Endometrium", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Myometrium", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Perimetrium", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mesoderm", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The trophoblast layer gets attached to the endometrium.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(651,'biology',103,965,2247,'What helps the fungi to grow in the skin folds?','[{"text": "Moisture alone", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Dryness alone", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Heat and moisture", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Closed areas", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Heat and moisture help these fungi to grow, which makes them thrive in skin folds such as those in the groin or between the toes.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
