\mathrm{P}$ is correct.',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(672,'biology',103,965,2247,'Measures for public hygiene include','[{"text": "Proper disposal of waste and excreta", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Periodic cleaning and disinfection of water reservoirs, pools, cesspools and tanks", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Observing standard practices of hygiene in public catering", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of them", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Public hygiene includes proper disposal of waste and excreta; periodic cleaning and disinfection of water reservoirs, pools, cesspools and tanks and observing standard practices of hygiene in public catering.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(673,'biology',105,1280,3097,'Bell-shaped age pyramid indicates that','[{"text": "Number of pre-reproductive and reproductive individual is almost equal", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Post-reproductive individuals are comparatively fewer", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both 1 and 2", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "None of the above", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Bell-shaped age pyramid indicates that<br>(1) Number of pre-reproductive and<br>reproductive individual is almost equal<br>(2) Post-reproductive individuals are comparitively fewer.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(674,'biology',103,965,2247,'Name the diseases transmitted through food and water?','[{"text": "Amoebiasis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Typhoid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ascariasis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of them", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Amoebiasis is an infection caused by the microorganism Entamoeba hystolytica, that is transmitted through contaminated food or water. Amoebiasis is also known as amoebic dysentery.<br>Typhoid fever is caused by Salmonella typhi bacteria. Contaminated food and water or close contact with an infected person cause typhoid fever.<br>It is caused by a parasite called Ascaris lumbricoides that is found in the soil. The organism is transmitted from one person to another by ingesting contaminated food and water.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(675,'biology',105,1280,3097,'Triangular -shaped age pyramid indicates that','[{"text": "Number of pre-reproductive is very less", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Post-reproductive individuals are comparatively fewer", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both 1 and 2", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of the above", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Triangular-shaped age pyramid indicates that Post-reproductive individuals are comparitively fewer.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(676,'biology',100,556,1114,'At the time of implantation in uterus.<br>','[{"text": "Embryo is at morula stage.<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Three germinal layers are made in embryo<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Embryo is at blastocyst stage<br>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Inner cell mass differentiates in trophoblast cells.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Embryo at the stage of blastocyst becomes embedded in the endometrium of the uterus. This is called implantation and it leads to pregnancy.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(689,'biology',103,965,2247,'<i>Gambusia,</i> an ____ is used to control an ____','[{"text": "Ostheichthyes, annelida", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ostheichthyes, arthropod", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Chondrichthyes, arthropod", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Chondrichthyes, annelida", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Mosquitofish (Gambusia affinis) are small fish (Osteichthyes) in the guppy family that are natural predators of mosquito (arthropod) larvae and pupae, making them an environmentally friendly alternative to mosquito control without the use of chemical insecticides.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(677,'biology',103,965,2247,'What measures have to be taken to prevent the spread of mosquitoes?<br>i. Avoiding stagnation of water in and around residential areas<br>ii. Regular cleaning of household coolers,<br>iii. Use of mosquito nets<br>iv. Introducing fishes like <em>Gambusia </em>in ponds that feed on mosquito larvae<br>v. Spraying of perfumes in ditches, drainage areas and swamps<br>vi. Doors and windows should be always kept open','[{"text": "Only i, ii and iii", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only ii, iii and iv", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only i, ii, iii and iv", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "All of them", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'For diseases such as malaria and filariasis that are transmitted through insect vectors, the most important measure is to control or eliminate the vectors and their breeding places. This can be achieved by avoiding stagnation of water in and around residential areas, regular cleaning of household coolers, use of mosquito nets, introducing fishes like <em>Gambusia </em>in ponds that feed on mosquito larvae, spraying of insecticides in ditches, drainage areas and swamps, etc. In addition, doors and windows should be provided with wire mesh to prevent the entry of mosquitoes.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(678,'biology',100,557,1115,'During pregnancy, which part of uterus helps in expansion and then in contraction during child birth','[{"text": "Perimetrium", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Myometrium", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Endometrium", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of these", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Deep to the perimetrium layer, the myometrium forms the middle muscular layer of the uterus. During pregnancy the myometrium allows the uterus to expand and then contracts the uterus during childbirth.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(679,'biology',105,1280,3097,'Match the columns I and II.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Growing<br>B. Stable<br>C. Declining</div><div class="column-right">P. Triangular<br>Q. Urn<br>R. Bell</div></div>','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{Q}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{P}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{Q}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{R}$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'${\\rm{A - P, B - R, C - Q}}$',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(680,'biology',103,965,2247,'Which of the following disease is not transmitted by <i>Aedes aegypti</i>?','[{"text": "Chikungunya", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Dengue", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Chicken - pox", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both (1) and (2)", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Chickenpox infection is caused by the varicella-zoster virus. It can spread through direct contact with the rash. It can also spread when a person with the chickenpox coughs or sneezes and you inhale the air droplets.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(681,'biology',105,1280,3097,'The age structure of a population represents','[{"text": "Relative number of individuals at each age", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Number of newborns each year", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Number of individuals getting married", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Relative number of individuals of each sex only", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The age structure of a population represents Relative number of individuals at each age.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(682,'biology',100,556,1113,'Which of the following hormones prevents regression of corpus luteum, if fertilization takes place?','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{LH}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "hCG", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{FSH}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Progesterone", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'hCG(human chorionic gonadotrophin) prevents regression of corpus luteum, if fertilisation takes place.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(683,'biology',103,965,2247,'Which of the following fish is introduced in pond to control or eliminate the vector mosquito?','[{"text": "<i>Rohu</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Gambusia</i>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "<i>Catla</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Betta</i>", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Mosquitofish (Gambusia affinis) are small fish in the guppy family that are natural predators of mosquito larvae and pupae, making them an environmentally friendly alternative to mosquito control without the use of chemical insecticides. This method is referred to as biological control and is part of our integrated pest management program (IPM). Gambusia are easily maintained and have a broad tolerance to a wide range of environmental conditions such as poor food supply and temperature changes.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(684,'biology',100,556,1113,'The placenta is connected to embryo through____ cord.','[{"text": "Chlorionic", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Umbilical", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Amniocentic", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Uterine", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The placenta is connected to the embryo through an umbilical cord which helps in the transport of substances to and from the embryo.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(685,'biology',105,1280,3097,'The representation of age pyramid for human population given here, shows','[{"text": "Declining population", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Stable population", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Increasing population", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Fluctuating population", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'As the base of the pyramid is denoted by pre reproductive individuals the number of pre reproductive individuals is same hence not undergoing any changes it is a stable pyramid.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/105_685_question_1.png'),
(686,'biology',103,965,2247,'Recently chikungunya and dengue cases were reported from various parts of the country. Choose the correct vector responsible for these diseases','[{"text": "<em>Anopheles </em>mosquito", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "House fly", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<em>Culex </em>mosquito", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<em>Aedes </em>mosquito", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The much-feared tiger mosquito is responsible for the transmission of several diseases throughout the world. It is the main vector of the chikungunya virus and the second of dengue fever.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(687,'biology',100,556,1113,'Which of the following hormone is related by placenta?','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{FSH}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{HCG}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Relaxin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{LH}$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'hCG(human chorionic gonadotrophin) is related to placenta.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(688,'biology',105,1280,3097,'What type of human population is represented by the following age pyramid?','[{"text": "Vanishing population", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Stable population", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Declining population", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Expanding population", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'As the base of the pyramid is denoted by pre reproductive individuals the number of pre reproductive individuals is decreasing it is a declining pyramid.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/105_688_question_1.png'),
(690,'biology',105,1280,3097,'Rapid increase in the population is indicated by','[{"text": "Large number of children", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Large number of young individuals", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Large number of old individuals", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Less number of young individuals", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Rapid increase in the population is indicated by large number of young individuals',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(691,'biology',106,1352,3254,'The common man would find it hard to believe that there are more than ____species of ants, ____ species of beetles,____ species of fishes.','[{"text": "$3,00,000,20,000,28,000$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$28,000,20,000,3,00,000$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$3,00,000,20,000,28,000$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$20,000,3,00,000,28,000$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The common man would find it hard to believe that there are more than 20,000 species of ants, 3,00,000 species of beetles, 28,000 species of fishes.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(692,'biology',100,556,1113,'Human chorionic gonadotropin hormone is secreted by<br>','[{"text": "Posterior pituitary", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Anterior pituitary", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Placenta<br>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Chorion", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'hCG is produced by the placenta at implantation, when the embryo starts to implant or attach itself into the uterine lining.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(693,'biology',103,965,2247,'Name the diseases that are controlled by vaccines?','[{"text": "polio, diphtheria", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "diphtheria, pneumonia", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "pneumonia and tetanus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of them", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Polio Vaccine protects against poliomyelitis causing polio virus. Polio or poliomyelitis, is a crippling and potentially deadly infectious disease. Virus spreads from person to person and can invade an infected person\'s brain and spinal cord, causing paralysisVaccines are available that can help prevent diphtheria, an infection caused by Corynebacterium diphtheriae bacteria. Four kinds of vaccines used today protect against diphtheria, all of which also protect against other diseases:<br>• Diphtheria and tetanus (DT) vaccines<br>• Diphtheria, tetanus, and pertussis (DTaP) vaccines<br>• Tetanus and diphtheria (Td) vaccines<br>• Tetanus, diphtheria, and pertussis (Tdap) vaccines<br>The pneumococcal vaccine protects against serious and potentially fatal pneumococcal infections. It\'s also known as the pneumonia vaccine.<br>Pneumococcal infections are caused by the bacterium Streptococcus pneumoniae and can lead to pneumonia, blood poisoning (sepsis) and meningitis.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(694,'biology',100,556,1113,'How many of the following hormones noticed in the blood of a pregnant woman?<br>Progesterone, estrogen, hCG, hPL, Relaxin cortisol','[{"text": "2", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "3", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "4", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "6", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Progesterone, estrogen, hCG, hPL, Relaxin, cortisol are noticed in blood of a pregnant woman.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(695,'biology',106,1352,3254,'It is hard to believe that there are nearly____ species of orchids.','[{"text": "1000", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1,00,000", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "2,00,000", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "20,000", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'There are nearly 20,000 species of orchids.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(696,'biology',105,1280,3097,'When there is a large number of post-reproductive or older individuals and lesser number of pre-reproductive individuals then that population is','[{"text": "Growing", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Declining", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Stable", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of these", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'When there is a large number of post-reproductive or older individuals and lesser number of pre-reproductive individuals then that population is declining',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(697,'biology',103,965,2247,'The use of vaccines and immunisation programmes have enabled us to completely eradicate a deadly disease like','[{"text": "Polio", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Tetanus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Diptheria", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Small pox", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The use of vaccines and immunisation programmes have enabled us to completely eradicate a deadly disease like smallpox. The smallpox vaccine is the first vaccine to be developed againsta contagious disease. In 1796, the British doctor Edward Jenner demonstrated that an infection with the relatively mild cowpox virus conferred immunity against the deadly smallpox virus. From 1958 to 1977, the World Health Organization (WHO) conducted a global vaccination campaign that eradicated smallpox, making it the only human disease to be eradicated.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(698,'biology',105,1280,3097,'The age pyramid with broad base indicates','[{"text": "High percentage of pre reproductive people", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Low perentage of reproductive people", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "High percentage of old individuals", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of the above", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The age pyramid with broad base indicates (High percentage of pre reproductive people)',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(699,'biology',100,556,1113,'Placenta also acts as a/an ____ tissue.','[{"text": "Exocrine", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Endocrine", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Paracrine", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Merocrine", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Placenta also act as an Endocrine tissue and produces hormones.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(700,'biology',106,1352,3254,'Match the columns I and II.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Species of ants<br>B. Species of orchids<br>C. Species of beetles<br>D. Species of fishes</div><div class="column-right">P. 20,000<br>Q. 3,00,000<br>R. 28,000<br>S. 2,00,000</div></div>','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{S}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{S}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{Q}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{R}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{S}$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'A-P, B-P,C-Q, D-R.',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(701,'biology',103,965,2247,'Recombinant DNA technology is used for the production of 3rd generation vaccine','[{"text": "Hepatitis B", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Typhoid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Tuberculosis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of the above", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'In 1987, the recombinant vaccine for Hepatitis B became the first synthetic vaccine for public use. It was first marketed by trade names Recombivax and Engerix-B. Hepatitis $B$ vaccine is safe to use, very effective and produce no allergic reactions.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(703,'biology',105,1280,3097,'The size, in nature, could be as low as $ &lt; 10$ (A at Bharatpur wetlands in any year) or go into millions (B in a pond).','[{"text": "A-Siberian cranes, B- <em>Chlamydomonas</em>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A-Siberian cranes, B- Fish", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-Nigeran cranes, B- <em>Chlamydomonas</em>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-Nigeran cranes, B- <em>Paramecium</em>", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'A-Siberian cranes, B- <em>Chlamydomonas</em>',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(704,'biology',106,1352,3254,'Who popularised the term biodiversity to describe combined diversity at all levels of biological organisation?','[{"text": "Edward Wilson", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "David Tilman", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Robert Constanza", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Alexander Von Humboldt", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Biodiversity is the term popularised by the sociobiologist Edward Wilson.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(705,'biology',103,965,2247,'Select the most appropriate statement<br>A.&nbsp;<em>Aedes</em>&nbsp;mosquitoes- mosquito is the causative agent for diseases like dengue and Filaria in many parts of India<br>B. Smallpox is a completely eradicated disease.','[{"text": "Only A is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only B is correct", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None are correct", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'A. Causative agent of dengue is Arbovirus and it is transmitted by bite of female <em>Aedes aegypti</em>. Causative agent filaria is wound worms of genus <em>Wuchereria</em> and is transmitted by female Culex mosquito<br>B. the World Health Organization (WHO) conducted a global vaccination campaign that eradicated smallpox, making it the only human disease to be eradicated.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(706,'biology',100,556,1113,'Which is not correct about placenta?','[{"text": "It acts as a foetal lung", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It acts as a foetal liver", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It acts as an endocrine gland", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It prevents passage of maternal IgG to foetus", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Placenta allows the passage of maternal IgG to foetus thereby providing it immunity.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(707,'biology',105,1280,3097,'Population size technically is called','[{"text": "Growth curve", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Demography", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Population density", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Age pyramid", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Population size technically is called population density',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(708,'biology',106,1352,3254,'Biodiversity of a geographical region represents','[{"text": "The diversity of organisms living in the region", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Endangered species found in India", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Endemic species found in India", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Genetic diversity present in the dominant species of the region", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Biodiversity of a geographical region represents the diversity of organisms living in the region',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(709,'biology',103,965,2247,'Which one of the following diseases is spred by housefly and mosquito respectively?','[{"text": "Typhoid, Amoebiasis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Amoebiasis, Encephalitis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Amoebiasis, Filariasis", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Amoebiasis, pneumonia", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Houseflies act as mechanical carriers and serve to transmit the parasite causing amoebiasis from faeces of infected person to food and food products, thereby contaminating them.<br>Filaria a threadlike parasitic nematode worm that is transmitted by biting mosquitoes, causing filariasis and related diseases.<br>Filaria spreads from person to person by mosquito bites. When a mosquito bites a person who has lymphatic filariasis, microscopic worms circulating in the person\'s blood enter and infect the mosquito. When the infected mosquito bites another person, the microscopic worms pass from the mosquito through the skin and travel to the lymph vessels of Humans.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(710,'biology',100,556,1113,'The human placenta is formed from','[{"text": "Yolk sac", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Amnion", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Allantois and chorion", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "None of these", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Placental mammals, such as humans, have a chorioallantoic placenta that forms from the chorion and allantois.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(711,'biology',106,1352,3254,'Hierarchical levels of biodiversity are','[{"text": "Genetic diversity, species diversity, community and ecosystem diversity", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Species diversity, community and ecosystem diversity", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Genetic diversity, species diversity", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Genetic diversity, community diversity, species diversity, ecosystem diversity", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Hierarchical levels of Biodiversity are genetic diversity, species diversity, community and ecosystem diversity.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(712,'biology',105,1280,3097,'In some cases, population density is measured in terms of biomass rather than in terms of number because','[{"text": "A single huge banyan tree with a large canopy is not less in comparison to 200 <i>Parthenium</i>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "It is a better method when population is huge and counting is impossible", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It is relative measure", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both (1) and (2)", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'In some cases, population density is measured in terms of biomass rather than in terms of number because<br>(1) Single huge banyan tree with a large canopy is not less in comparison to 200 <i>Parthenium</i>',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(713,'biology',103,965,2247,'Match the columns I and II<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Amoebiasis<br>B. Diphtheria<br>C. Malaria<br>D. Dengue</div><div class="column-right">P. <em>Gambusia</em><br>Q. Use only sterilized food and water<br>R. DPT vaccine<br>S. <em>Aedes</em></div></div>','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{S}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{S}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{Q}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{S}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{R}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{S}$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'A. Drinking water and food contaminated by the faecal matter are the main source of infection.<br>$\\mathrm{B}$. The DPT vaccine or DTP vaccine is a class of combination vaccines against three infectious diseases in humans: diphtheria, pertussis (whooping cough), and tetanus.<br>C. Mosquitofish (Gambusia affinis) are small fish in the guppy family that are natural predators of mosquito larvae and pupae, making them an environmentally friendly alternative to mosquito control without the use of chemical insecticides.<br>D. Dengue is transmitted by the bite od female Aedes mosquito.',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(715,'biology',106,1352,3254,'The medicinal plant, Rauwolfia vomitoria, growing in Himalayan ranges shows variation. It is an example of','[{"text": "Species diversity", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ecological diversity", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Genetic diversity", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "None of these", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The genetic variation shown by the medicinal plant Rauwolfia vomitoria growing in different Himalayan ranges might be in terms of the potency and concentration of the active chemical (reserpine) that the plant produces.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(716,'biology',105,1280,3097,'Which of the following is an example of using relative density to measure population density in a certain area?','[{"text": "Counting leaves of the banyan tree", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Counting the number of fishes caught in a trap to find population density of fishes in a lake", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Measuring biomass of bacterial culture in a petri dish to find out population density of bacteria", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both (1) and (3)", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Counting the number of fishes caught in a trap to find population density of fishes in a lake is an example of using relative density to measure population density in a certain area.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(717,'biology',100,556,1113,'Which one is not a character of hemochorial placenta?<br>','[{"text": "It protects the foetus from mechanical shock<br>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$ and excretory products pass from foetus to mother\'s body<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{O}_{2}$ and nutrients from mother\'s body enter the foetus<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Chorion villi are covered by blood sinuses of mother", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Hemochorial placenta is characteristic of humans. The chorionic villi of the foetus are covered by maternal blood sinuses. Amnion protects the foetus from external shock.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(718,'biology',103,966,2248,'The ability of the host to fight the disease causing organisms, is called ____','[{"text": "Allergy", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Immunity", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "DNA technology", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Antibody", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The body is able to defend itself from most of these foreign agents. This overall ability of the host to fight the disease-causing organisms, conferred by the immune system is called immunity.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(719,'biology',106,1352,3254,'Resperine is obtained from','[{"text": "Roots of <i>Rauwolfia serpentina</i>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Stem of <i>Rauwolfia serpentina</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Leaves of <i>Rauwolfia serpentina</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Fruits of <i>Rauwolfia serpentina</i>", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Reserpine is a drug derived from the roots of Rauwolfia serpentina. The powdered whole root of the Indian shrub Rauwolfia serpentina historically had been used to treat snakebites, insomnia, hypertension (high blood pressure), and insanity.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(720,'biology',105,1280,3097,'Select the correct answer<br>I. A population has certain attributes whereas, an individual organism does not.<br>II. An individual is either a male or a female but a population has a sex ratio','[{"text": "Only I is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only II is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both are correct", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "None are correct", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Correct statement<br>I. A population has certain attributes whereas, an individual organism does not.<br>II. An individual is either a male or a female but a population has a sex ratio',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
