(737,'biology',100,556,1114,'After one month of pregnancy which vital organ is formed in the foetus?','[{"text": "Brain", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Heart", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Lungs", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Liver", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'In human beings, after one month of pregnancy, the embryo\'s heart is formed.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(738,'biology',103,966,2248,'An antigen is','[{"text": "Residue of antibody", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Stimulus for antibody formation", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Results of antibody", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Opposite to an antibody", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'An antigen is any substance that causes your immune system to produce antibodies against it. This means your immune system does not recognize the substance, and is trying to fight it off. An antigen may be a substance from the environment, such as chemicals, bacteria, viruses, or pollen.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(739,'biology',105,1281,3098,'The rate at which a population grows or declines depends upon the rate of','[{"text": "Births and emigration", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Immigration", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Deaths", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The rate at which a population grows or declines depends upon the rate of<br>(1) Births and Emigration<br>(2) Immigration<br>(3) Deaths',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(740,'biology',106,1352,3254,'India has more than ____ genetically different strains of rice and 1000 variety of','[{"text": "5000, mango", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "50,000 , wheat", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "50,000 , oats", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "50,000, mango", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'India has more than 50,000 genetically different strains of rice, and 1,000 varieties of mango.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(741,'biology',100,556,1114,'Foetal limbs and digits are formed in the ____  month of embryonic development','[{"text": "${{\\\\rm{4}}^{{\\\\rm{th}}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${{\\\\rm{2}}^{{\\\\rm{nd}}}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${{\\\\rm{3}}^{{\\\\rm{rd}}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${{\\\\rm{7}}^{{\\\\rm{th}}}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'By the end of the second month of pregnancy, the foetus develops limbs and digits.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(742,'biology',103,966,2248,'Which out of the following can enter our body by various means multiply and cause morphological and functional damage','[{"text": "Toxin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Antigen", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pathogen", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "1 and 3 both", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Pathogen is an organism or a biological agent that can cause a disease in another organism. Pathogens are known to cause diseases upon infecting other organisms. Therefore, diseases caused by pathogens are known as infectious diseases. \'Pathogen\' is a broad term which comprises various diseasecausing organisms such as bacteria, viruses, fungi, protozoans and worms.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(743,'biology',106,1352,3254,'Which one of the following shows maximum genetic diversity in India','[{"text": "Mango", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Groundnut", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Rice", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Maize", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'India has more than 50,000 genetically different strains of rice.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(744,'biology',105,1281,3098,'If a new habitat is just being colonised, ____ X____may contribute more significantly to population growth than____Y____','[{"text": "X - Immigration, Y - Birth rates", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "X - Emmigration, Y - Birth rates", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "X - Immigration, Y - Death rates", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "X - Emmigration, Y - Death rates", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'X - Immigration, Y - Birth rates',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(745,'biology',100,556,1114,'The second trimester of human pregnancy is characterised by<br>','[{"text": "Appearance of heart and aorta<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Appearance of external genital organs<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Appearance of fine hair, eye-lashes on the eye-lids<br>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Appearance of limbs and digits", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'By the end of about 24 weeks (end of second trimester), the body is covered with fine hair, eye-lids separate, and eyelashes are formed.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(746,'biology',103,966,2248,'Non-specific host defence that is present prior to the exposure to an antigen is called','[{"text": "Innate immunity", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Passive immunity", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Artificial immunity", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Active immunity", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Innate immunity is the body\'s first line of defence against pathogens. It is general and non-specific, which means it does not differentiate between types of pathogens.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(747,'biology',105,1281,3098,'Which of the following would necessarily increase the density of a population in a given habitat?','[{"text": "Mortality and emigration", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Natality and immigration", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Natality and mortality", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Immigration and emigration", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Natality and Immigration would necessarily Increase the density of a population in a given habitat.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(748,'biology',106,1352,3254,'Presence of more than 1000 genetically different varieties of mango in India is due to','[{"text": "Genetic diversity", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Species diversity", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both 1 and 2", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ecological diversity", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'1,000 varieties of mango, this is due to genetic diversity.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(749,'biology',100,556,1114,'By which month of gestation, hair appear on head and foetal movements can be felt','[{"text": "Fourth", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Third", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Six", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Fifth", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'By the fifth month of gestation the foetal movements can be felt and there is also appearance of hair on the head.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(750,'biology',103,966,2248,'Innate immunity consist of four types of barriers','[{"text": "Physiological, Physical", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cellular", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cytokine", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of them", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Innate immunity consist of four types of barriers. These are - (i) Physical barriers : Skin on our body is the main barrier which prevents entry of the micro-organisms. Mucus coating of the epithelium lining the respiratory, gastrointestinal and urogenital tracts also help in trapping microbes entering our body. (ii) Physiological barriers : Acid in the stomach, saliva in the mouth, tears from eyes-all prevent microbial growth. (iii) Cellular barriers : Certain types of leukocytes (WBC) of our body like polymorpho-nuclear leukocytes (PMNL-neutrophils) monocytes and natural killer (type of lymphocytes) in the blood as well as macrophages in tissues can phagocytose and destroy microbes. (iv) Cytokine barriers : Virus-infected cells secrete proteins called interferons which protect noninfected cells from further viral.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(751,'biology',106,1352,3254,'The Western Ghats have a greater amphibians diversity than the Eastern Ghats. It is an example of','[{"text": "Species diversity", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Genetic diversity", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ecological diversity", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of these", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The Western Ghats have a greater amphibian species diversity than the Eastern Ghats. Thus, it is an example of species diversity which is defined as the diversity at the species level and is indicated by the variety and richness of the species of a region.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(752,'biology',105,1281,3098,'Identify the correct equation for population density at time t+1','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{N}_{\\\\mathrm{t}+1}=\\\\mathrm{N}_{\\\\mathrm{t}}+[(\\\\mathrm{D}+\\\\mathrm{I})-(\\\\mathrm{B}+\\\\mathrm{E})]$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{N}_{\\\\mathrm{t}+1}=\\\\mathrm{N}_{\\\\mathrm{t}}+[(\\\\mathrm{B}+\\\\mathrm{I})-(\\\\mathrm{D}+\\\\mathrm{E})]$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{N}_{\\\\mathrm{t}+1}=\\\\mathrm{N}_{\\\\mathrm{t}}+[(\\\\mathrm{B}+\\\\mathrm{D})-(\\\\mathrm{I}+\\\\mathrm{E})]$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{N}_{\\\\mathrm{t}+1}=\\\\mathrm{N}_{\\\\mathrm{t}}+[(\\\\mathrm{B}+\\\\mathrm{I})+(\\\\mathrm{D}+\\\\mathrm{E})]$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Population density at time ${\\rm{t + 1}}\\,<br>{{\\rm{N}}_{\\rm{t}}}{\\rm{ + 1 = }}{{\\rm{N}}_{\\rm{t}}}{\\rm{ +  [(B + I) - (D + E)]}}$',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(753,'biology',100,556,1114,'Most of the organs/system in foetus are formed by the end of','[{"text": "${{\\\\rm{1}}^{{\\\\rm{st}}}}$ trimester", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${{\\\\rm{2}}^{nd}}$ trimester", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${3^{rd}}$ trimester", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "First month<br>", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Organogenesis takes place during first 12 weeks of gestation.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(754,'biology',103,966,2248,'Increased temperature- Fever, is a part of ____ innate immunity','[{"text": "Physical", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cellular", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Physiological", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Cytokine", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Fever\'s ability to manipulate the character and extent of physiological temperature gradients correlates with the unusual influence different physiological temperatures have upon model immune responses in vitro.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(755,'biology',105,1281,3098,'What does following letters indicate?','[{"text": "E - Elongation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "D - Dismissal", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "B - Natality", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I - Initiation", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'B - Natality',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/105_755_question_1.png'),
(756,'biology',106,1353,3255,'According to Robert May the global species diversity is about','[{"text": "1.7 million", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "3 million", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "7 million", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "1.8 million", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Some extreme estimates range from 20 to 50 million, but a more conservative and scientifically sound estimate made by Robert May places the global species diversity at about 7 million.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(757,'biology',100,556,1114,'Identify A, B, C, D.<br>','[{"text": "A - Foetus,<br>\\nB - Amnion<br>\\nC - Placenta,<br>\\nD - Allontois<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - Foetus,<br>B - Amnion,<br>C - Umbilical cord,<br>D - Chorionic villi", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A - Zygote,<br>B - Amnion,<br>C - Umbilical cord,<br>D - Amniotic cavity", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - Zygote,<br>B - Amnion,<br>C - Umbilical cord<br>D - Chorionic villi", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'NCERT figure 3.12',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/100_757_question_1.png'),
(758,'biology',103,966,2248,'The physical barriers that form part of the immune system are:','[{"text": "The bones and the mucosal membranes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The skin, body temperature and the mucosal membranes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The skin and the mucosal membranes", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "All the above", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Skin forms the first line of defence of the body against pathogens. It\'s a tough outer layer formed of dead, horny cells. It prevents the entry of bacteria and viruses Mucous membrane lining the respiratory tract, throat, digestive tract and urinogenital system is also treated as part of external defence like skin.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(759,'biology',106,1353,3255,'There is estimated to be 100 million species on the earth, how many have been identified?','[{"text": "1.7 million", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "30 million", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "100 million", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1.8 million", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Around 1.7 million species have been identified in estimated 100 million species on earth.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
