(780,'biology',106,1353,3255,'Identify a, b,c ,d','[{"text": "a- Fungi, b- angiosperms, c- lichens, d-algae", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "a- Fungi, b- angiosperms, c- lichens, d-mosses", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "a- Angiosperms, b- fungi, c- algae, d-lichens", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "a- Mosses, b- fungi, c- algae, d- lichens", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'a- Angiosperms, b-fungi, c- algae, d- lichens',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/106_780_question_1.png'),
(781,'biology',100,556,1114,'In amniocentesis, the fluid for test is taken from','[{"text": "Foetal blood", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mother\'s blood", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Amniotic fluid", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Mother\'s body fluid", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'In amniocentesis, the fluid surrounding the foetus also known as amniotic fluid is taken for testing and analysis. This helps in ruling out the possibilities of any chromosomal defects.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(782,'biology',106,1353,3255,'India has only _____ percent of the world\'s land area.','[{"text": "2.8", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "2.4", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "2.1", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "8.1", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Although India has only 2.4 percent of the world\'s land area, its share of the global species diversity is an impressive 8.1 percent.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(783,'biology',105,1281,3098,'A population can grow exponentially','[{"text": "When food and space are unlimited", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "When first invading a suitable and previously unoccupied habitat", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only if there is no predation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only in the laboratory", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'A population can grow exponentially when food and space are unlimited.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(784,'biology',103,966,2248,'The only blood cells that are not considered to be part of the immune system are:','[{"text": "Glial cells", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Lymphocytes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "RBC", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Leucocytes", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The immune system consists of a range of components, including: white blood cells (leukocytes), the spleen, the bone marrow, the lymphatic system, the thymus, the tonsils, adenoids, and appendix. Red blood cell (RBC) is not a component of immune system.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(785,'biology',100,557,1115,'If endometrium is for menstruation, then myometrium is for','[{"text": "Capacitation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Micturition", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Insemination", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Parturition", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Menstrual cycle begins with menstruation which in the sloughing off of endometrium. Myometrium is the muscle layer of uterus whose centracton causes parturition or child birth.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(786,'biology',103,966,2248,'Lymphocytes acquire their antigen specificity','[{"text": "As they enter the tissues from the circulation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Before they encounter antigen", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Depending on which antigens are present", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "From contact with self antigen", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The antigen receptors of B and Tlymphocytes have several features that are important for their functions in adaptive immunity. Although these receptors have many similarities in terms of structure and mechanisms of signalling, there are fundamental differences related to the types of antigenic structures that $\\mathrm{B}$ cells and $\\mathrm{T}$ cells recognize. Antigens have determinants called epitopes. Epitopes are molecular shapes recognised by antibodies, which recognise 1 epitope rather than the whole antigen.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(787,'biology',106,1353,3255,'India\'s share in the global species diversity is about','[{"text": "$2 \\\\%$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$4 \\\\%$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$6 \\\\%$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$8 \\\\%$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'India\'s share in the global species diversity is about $8 \\%$.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(788,'biology',105,1281,3098,'Exponential growth occurs when','[{"text": "There is no competition", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "There is only asexual reproduction", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "There is a fixed carrying capacity", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "There is limited resource", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Exponential growth occurs when there is no competition.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(789,'biology',106,1353,3255,'Number of animal species yet to be discovered in India according to May\'s estimations is','[{"text": "More than $1,00,000$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "More than 3,00,000", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "90,000", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "45000", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Applying May\'s proportion to India\'s diversity figures, we estimate that there are probably more than $1,00,000$ plant species and more than 3,00, 000 animal species yet to be discovered and described.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(790,'biology',103,966,2248,'Macrophages are','[{"text": "Cytokine barriers", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cellular barrier", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Physical barriers", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Physiological barrier", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Certain types of leukocytes (WBC) of our body like polymorpho-nuclear leukocytes (PMNL-neutrophils) and monocytes and natural killer (type of lymphocytes) in the blood as well as macrophages in tissues can phagocytose and destroy.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(791,'biology',105,1281,3098,'Exponential growth in human population is represented in','[{"text": "Lag phase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Log phase", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Plateau phase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "First phase", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'In nature population do not have unlimited resources, hence populations grows logistically. When the resources are abundant at the initial state, organisms utilise resources and grows exponentially.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(792,'biology',100,557,1115,'Delivery of developed foetus is','[{"text": "Abortion", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Oviposition", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Parturition", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Conception", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'When the signals along with the placenta for a possible delivery and hence childbirth takes place also known as parturition.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(793,'biology',103,966,2248,'Which of the following cells are not included in cellular barrier of innate immunity?','[{"text": "Neutrophilis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "NK cells", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Helper T cells", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Macrophages", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Helper $T$ cells are one of the two major types of T lymphocytes in the acquired immune system and play a key role in the coordination of the immune response. They are central to adaptive immunity and are involved in almost all adaptive immune responses, as they secrete cytokines for the proliferation and stimulation of other immune cells.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(794,'biology',106,1353,3255,'Match the columns I and II about India.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. India’s share of world’s land area<br>B. India’s share global species diversity<br>C. Species of plants in India</div><div class="column-right">P. 8.1 per cent<br>Q. 2.4 per cent<br>R. 45,000</div></div>','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{Q}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{P}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{Q}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{R}$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'A-Q, B-P, C-R',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(795,'biology',105,1281,3098,'In the following reaction,<br>$\\mathrm{dN} / \\mathrm{dt}=(\\mathrm{b}-\\mathrm{d}) \\mathrm{x} \\mathrm{N}$<br>Substituting r in place of b-d then<br>$\\mathrm{dN} / \\mathrm{dt}=\\mathrm{rN}$<br>Here \' r \' is known as','[{"text": "Intrinsic rate of natural increase", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Intrinsic rate of natural decrease", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Extrinsic rate of natural decrease", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Extrinsic rate of natural increase", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'${\\rm{d N / d t = (b - d) x N}}$ Substituting r in place of b-d then ${\\rm{d N / d t = r N}}$ Here \' r \' is known as Intrinsic rate of natural increase.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(796,'biology',100,557,1115,'Foetal ejection reflex in human female is induced by<br>','[{"text": "Differentiation of mammary glands<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pressure exerted by amniotic fluid<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Release of oxytocin from pituitary<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Fully developed foetus and placenta", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The signals for parturition originate from the fully developed foetus and the placenta which induce mild uterine contractions called foetal ejection reflex.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(797,'biology',106,1354,3256,'Biodiversity is affected by','[{"text": "Latitudinal gradients and species-area relationship", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Species-area relationship and longitudinal gradients", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both 1 and 2", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "latitudinal and longitudinal gradients", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Biodiversity is affected by latitudinal gradients and species-area relationship',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(798,'biology',103,966,2248,'Globulins contained in human blood plasma are primarily involved in','[{"text": "Defense mechanism of the body", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Osmotic balance of the body fluids", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Oxygen transport in the blood", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Clotting of the blood", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Globulins are soluble in salt solutions of strong acids and bases. These are coagulated by heat and insoluble in pure water and moderately concentrated salt solutions. Globulins contained in human blood plasma are primarily involved in defence mechanisms of the body. Some examples are i.e., Rabies immun globulin, $\\mathrm{RhO}(\\mathrm{D})$ Immuno globulins, specific immunoglobulin, tetanus immuno globulin, etc.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(799,'biology',105,1281,3098,'The population of an insect species shows an explosive increase in number during rainy season followed by its disappearance at the end of the season. What does this show?','[{"text": "The population of its predator increases enormously", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "S-shaped or sigmoid growth of this insect", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The food plants mature and die at the end of the rainy season", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Its population growth curve is of J-type", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The population of an insect species shows an explosive increase in number during rainy season followed by its disappearance at the end of the season. Its population growth curve is of J-type.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(800,'biology',100,557,1115,'Following the delivery of the foetus which of the following structure is also expelled out?','[{"text": "Cervix", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Corpus luteum", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Placenta", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Ovary", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Soon after the infant is delivered, the placenta is also expelled out of the uterus.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(801,'biology',106,1354,3256,'From equator towards the poles biodiversity','[{"text": "Decreases", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Increases", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Remains same", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "First decreases then increases", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'From equator towards the poles biodiversity decreases',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(802,'biology',103,966,2248,'Interferon which protect non-infected cells from viral infection are a part of','[{"text": "Physical barriers", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cytokine barriers", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Cellular barriers", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Physiological barriers", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Cytokine barriers : Virus-infected cells secrete proteins called interferons which protect non-infected cells from further viral infection.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(803,'biology',105,1281,3098,'$\\mathrm{dN} / \\mathrm{dt}$ is','[{"text": "Rate of births", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Rate of death", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Change in population size", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Carrying capacity", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'${\\rm{dN/dt = rN}}$ (exponential growth curve) ${\\rm{dN/}}$ ${\\rm{dt = rN(K - N/K)}}$-logistic growth curve',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(804,'biology',100,558,1116,'The milk produced during the initial days of lactation is called','[{"text": "Serum", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Colostrum", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Plasma", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of these", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The milk produced during the initial few days of lactation is called colostrum which contains several antibodies absolutely essential to develop resistance for the new-born babies.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(805,'biology',106,1354,3256,'Tropics $\\left(23.5^{\\circ} \\mathrm{N}\\right.$ to $\\left.23.5^{\\circ} \\mathrm{S}\\right)$ have ____ species as compared to temperate or polar regions.','[{"text": "Less", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Equal", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "More", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "None of these", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Tropics (latitudinal range of $23.5^{\\circ} \\mathrm{N}$ to $23.5^{\\circ} \\mathrm{S}$ ) harbour more species than temperate or polar areas.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(806,'biology',103,966,2248,'The two types of lymphocytes are','[{"text": "Platelets and erythrocytes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Platelets and the T-cells", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "T-cells and erythrocytes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "B-cells and T-cells", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'There are two main types of lymphocytes:<br>• T lymphocytes ( $\\mathrm{T}$ cells): $\\mathrm{T}$ cells control your body\'s immune system response and directly attack and kill infected cells and tumor cells.<br> • B lymphocytes (B cells): B cells make antibodies. Antibodies are proteins that target viruses, bacteria and other foreign invaders.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(807,'biology',100,558,1116,'Milk production stimulated in mammals is associated with','[{"text": "Progesterone", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Oxytocin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Gonadotropin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Prolactin", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'After parturition there is secretion of a hormone from the posterior pituitary i.e., prolactin which stimulated mammary glands for milk secretion. Thereafter, another hormone oxytocin is released which signals for ejection of milk and thus, the milk is released from the mammary glands.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(808,'biology',105,1281,3098,'The r value for Norway rat, flour beetle and human population (in 1981) is ____','[{"text": "$0.15,01.2,0.0205$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$0.015,0.12,0.0205$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$0.0015,0.0205,0.12$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$1.5,0.012,0.0502$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The r value for Norway rat, flour beetle and human population (in 1981) is 0.015,0.12, 0.0205 .',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(809,'biology',106,1354,3256,'Which one of the following has the greatest biodiversity on earth?','[{"text": "Tropical Amazonian rain forest", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Eastern ghats", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Western ghats", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of the above", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Tropical Amazonian rain forests in South America have greatest biodiversity. It may be due to following reasons:<br>• Tropical latitudes have remained undistributed for millions of years thus had a long evolutionary time for species diversification.<br>• Tropical environment are less seasonal, relatively more constant and predictable which promotes niche specialization and lead to greater species diversity.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(810,'biology',103,966,2248,'Full form of PMNL is','[{"text": "Poly Morpho-Nuclear Leucocytes", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Poly Meta-Nuclear Lymphocytes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Poly Mega-Nuclear Leucocytes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Poly Morpho-Neutrophilo Lymphocytes", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Granulocytes are a category of white blood cells characterized by the presence of granules in their cytoplasm. They are also called polymorphonuclear leukocytes or polymorphonuclear neutrophils (PMN, PML, or PMNL) because of the varying shapes of the nucleus, which is usually lobed into three segments.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(811,'biology',100,557,1115,'Oxytocin is helpful in','[{"text": "Diuresis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Parturition", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Sperm formation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Molecular development", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Soon after the signal from the foetus and placenta the levels of oxytocin increase and start the process of parturition.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(812,'biology',105,1281,3098,'The integral form of the exponential growth equation is as follows','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{N}_{\\\\mathrm{t}}=\\\\mathrm{N}_{0} \\\\mathrm{e}^{\\\\mathrm{RT}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{N}_{\\\\mathrm{t}}=\\\\mathrm{N}_{0} \\\\mathrm{e}^{\\\\mathrm{rt}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{N}_{\\\\mathrm{t}}=\\\\mathrm{N}_{0}$ ert", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{N}_{\\\\mathrm{t}}=\\\\mathrm{N}_{0} \\\\mathrm{e}_{\\\\mathrm{rt}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The integral form of the exponential growth $\\mathrm{N}_{\\mathrm{t}}=\\mathrm{N}_{0} \\mathrm{e}^{\\mathrm{rt}}$',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(813,'biology',106,1354,3256,'Biodiversity','[{"text": "Increases towards the equator", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Decreases towards the equator", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Remains same throughout the planet", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Has no effect on change in latitude", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Biodiversity increases towards the equator',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL);
INSERT INTO `qb_questions` (`id`, `subject_id`, `chapter_id`, `topic_id`, `subtopic_id`, `question_html`, `options`, `correct_index`, `explanation`, `explanation_image_url`, `difficulty`, `qtype`, `year`, `tag`, `created_at`, `question_image_url`) VALUES
(814,'biology',103,966,2248,'The interferons can be used as','[{"text": "Antibacterial drugs", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Antiviral drugs", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Antibiotic drugs", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Antifungal drugs", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Natural interferons are produced by lymphocytes as part of an immunological response to viral antigens. Synthetic interferons, made by recombinant DNA technology, are used as antiviral agents to treat infections such as hepatitis and herpes zoster virus. Interferons induce the production of enzymes in the ribosomes of the host cells and inhibit the translation of viral mRNA into viral proteins, therefore stop viral reproduction.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(815,'biology',100,558,1116,'Which one of the following causes the mammary glands to enlarge at puberty?','[{"text": "Testosterone", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Progesterone", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Estrogen", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Oxytocin", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Oestrogen causes the mammary glands to enlarge at puberty.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(816,'biology',105,1281,3098,'Which population will increase fastest among all of the given population?<br>A. Population of elephants-has the intrinsic rate of natural increase is 0.1<br>B. Population of tigers -has the intrinsic rate of natural increase is 0.3<br>C. Population of birds -has the intrinsic rate of natural increase is 0.6<br>D. Population of rats -has the intrinsic rate of natural increase is 0.9','[{"text": "D", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "C", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "B", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Population of Rats -has the intrinsic rate of natural increase is 0.9 Will increase fastest.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(817,'biology',106,1354,3256,'Approximate number of species of mammals in Amazon forest','[{"text": "900", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "600", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "427", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "300", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Approximate number of species of mammals in Amazon forest is 427',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(818,'biology',103,966,2248,'A person has developed interferons in his body. He seems to carry an infection of','[{"text": "Cholera", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Malaria", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Tuberculosis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Dengue", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Dengue fever is caused by one of four dengue viruses. When a mosquito infected with the dengue virus bites you, the virus can enter your blood and make copies of itself. Natural interferons are produced by lymphocytes as part of an immunological response to viral antigens. Interferons induce the production of enzymes in the ribosomes of the host cells and inhibit the translation of viral mRNA into viral proteins, therefore stop viral reproduction.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(819,'biology',100,558,1116,'The production of milk in mammary gland occurs<br>','[{"text": "During parturition<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "After parturition<br>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Before embryogenesis<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "From the start of pregnancy", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The production of milk in mammary gland occurs after parturition.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(820,'biology',105,1281,3098,'Which of the following is true regarding exponential growth?','[{"text": "No population can grow exponentially for long", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Exponential growth is seen in tissue culture experiments when the supply of nutrients is unlimited", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Bacterial colonies have been observed to maintain exponential growth in culture plates with sufficient nutrients", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of them", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'True regarding exponential growth:<br>(1) No population can grow exponentially for long<br>(2) Exponential growth is seen in tissue culture experiments when the supply of nutrients is unlimited.<br>(3) Bacterial colonies have been observed to maintain exponential growth in culture plates with sufficient nutrients.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(821,'biology',106,1354,3256,'Tropical Amazon Rain forest in south America has greatest biodiversity on earth which harbours the amphibian species nearly.','[{"text": "427", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "1300", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "378", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "3000", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The tropical Amazonian rainforests in South America possess the greatest biodiversity on earth with 427 of amphibians',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(822,'biology',103,966,2248,'Which out of the following are involved in body defense?','[{"text": "Neutrophils", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Macrophages", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Lymphocytes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All the above", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Certain types of leukocytes (WBC) of our body like polymorpho-nuclear leukocytes (PMNL-neutrophils) and monocytes and natural killer (type of lymphocytes) in the blood as well as macrophages in tissues can phagocytose and destroy microbes.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(823,'biology',105,1281,3098,'Exponential growth occurs when there is','[{"text": "No environmental resistance", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A fixed carrying capacity", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A great environmental resistance", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "resources are limited", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Exponential growth occurs when there is<br>(1) No environmental resistance',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(824,'biology',100,558,1116,'Colostrum is rich in  ____ .','[{"text": "$\\\\operatorname{IgG}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\operatorname{IgA}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "IgM", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\operatorname{IgE}$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Colostrum is rich in IgA.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(825,'biology',106,1354,3256,'Amazon rainforest belongs to which country','[{"text": "South Africa", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Brazil", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "India", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "England", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The tropical Amazonian rainforests in South America possess the greatest biodiversity on earth. Brazil belongs to south America',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(826,'biology',103,966,2248,'Which out of the following cells is present in tissues that can phagocytose and destroy microbes?','[{"text": "Monocyte", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Macrophages", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Neutrophils", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Lymphocyte", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Macrophages are large immune cells are present in nearly all tissues and actively remove dead and damaged cells, bacteria, cancerous cells, and cellular debris from the body. The process by which macrophages engulf and digest cells and pathogens is called phagocytosis.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(827,'biology',105,1281,3098,'The graph shows two types of population growth curves, \\(\\mathrm{A}\\) is exponential and \\(\\mathrm{B}\\) is logisitic, which one of the following growth model is considered as more realistic one?<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "Exponential growth curve", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Logistic growth curve", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Z-shaped growth curve", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All the above", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Exponential growth takes place whenever there is unlimited resources, but in nature the resources are limiting and there exists competition between individuals and the dominating species survives which is true in logisitic growth.',NULL,'Easy','Graph/Figure',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/105_827_question_1.png'),
(828,'biology',100,558,1116,'Match the columns<br><div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Parturition<br>B. Foetal ejection reflex<br>C. Oxytocin<br>D. Lactation<br>E. Colostrum</div><div class="column-right">P. Release from meternal pitutary gland<br>Q. Delivery of foetus<br>R. Contraction of uterus<br>S. Contains antibodies<br>T. Release of milk from mammary gland</div></div>','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{T}, \\\\mathrm{E}-\\\\mathrm{S}$<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{T}, \\\\mathrm{E}-\\\\mathrm{S}$<br>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{S}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{T}, \\\\mathrm{E}-\\\\mathrm{Q}$<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{T}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{E}-\\\\mathrm{S}$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'A-Q, B-R, C-P, D-T, E-S',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(829,'biology',106,1354,3256,'Approximately, $50 \\%$ of total world species are present on in','[{"text": "Tropical rain forest", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Temperate rain forest", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Temperate deciduous forest", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Coral reef", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Since tropical rainforests are thought to be the oldest biome on Earth, it is not surprising that they contain most species. Tropics are enormous, spreading across the waistline of the globe. Increasing size provides ample opportunity for geographic separation of groups within a species',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(830,'biology',103,966,2248,'Interferons are synthesised in response to','[{"text": "Mycoplasma", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Bacteria", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Viruses", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Fungi", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Cells infected by virus produce interferon which is antiviral. It cautions neighbouring cells and makes them resistant to virus infections by inhibiting viral growth.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(831,'biology',100,553,1107,'Which of the following is not correct?<br>','[{"text": "Golgi complex of spermatid gives rise to acrosome<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mitochondria are absent in spermatozoa.<br>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Two centrioles are present in spermatozoa.<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Spermatozoa consists of head, body and tail.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The middle part of sperm possesses numerous mitochondria which produce energy for the movement of tail that facilitates sperm motility.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(832,'biology',105,1281,3098,'Logistic growth occurs when there is','[{"text": "No competition", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Unlimited food and space", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Fixed carrying capacity", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "All species are in absolute harmony with each other", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Logistic growth occurs when there is fixed carrying capacity .',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(833,'biology',106,1354,3256,'Which place has nearly 1,400 species of birds','[{"text": "New York", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Greenland", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "India", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Colombia located near the equator", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Colombia located near the equator has nearly 1,400 species of birds.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(834,'biology',103,966,2248,'Cytokines are:','[{"text": "Proteins", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Viruses", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Carcinogens", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Bacteria", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Cytokines are a broad and loose category of small proteins $( \\sim 5 - 25\\,{\\rm{kDa}})$ important in cell signalling. Cytokines are peptides and cannot cross the lipid bilayer of cells to enter the cytoplasm.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(835,'biology',105,1281,3098,'In the logistic growth equation $\\frac{{{\\rm{dN}}}}{{{\\rm{dt}}}}{\\rm{ = rN}}\\left( {\\frac{{{\\rm{K - N}}}}{{\\rm{K}}}} \\right)$<br>$\\mathrm{K}$ represents','[{"text": "Environmental resistance", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Intrinsic rate of natural increase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Carrying capacity", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Biotic potential", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'$\\mathrm{K}$ represents the carrying capacity. In nature, a given habitat has enough resources to support a maximum possible number, beyond which no further growth is possible. This limit is called carrying capacity $(\\mathrm{K})$ for that species in that habitat',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(836,'biology',100,553,1107,'Seminal plasma, the secretion of seminal vesicles, prostate and bulbourethral glands is','[{"text": "Rich in fructose, calcium and certain enzymes<br>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Rich in fructose, poor in calcium and has few enzymes<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Poor in fructose rich in calcium and has few enzymes<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Poor in fructose, calcium and enzymes", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The components of semen come from two sources: sperm, and "seminal plasma". Seminal plasma of humans contains a complex range of organic and inorganic constituents from various exocrine glands in male reproductive system and sperms.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(837,'biology',106,1354,3256,'New York at $41^{\\circ} \\mathrm{N}$ has ____ Greenland at $71^{\\circ} \\mathrm{N}$ only ____ species and','[{"text": "56,105", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "105,56", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "1400,56", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1200,56", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'New York at $41^{\\circ} \\mathrm{N}$ has 105 species and Greenland at $71^{\\circ} \\mathrm{N}$ only 56 species.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(838,'biology',100,551,1105,'What is the function of bulbourethral gland secretion?','[{"text": "Nourishing sperms", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Role in activating sperms", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Serves as a lubricant during sexual intercourse", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Enhancing the motility of sperms", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The secretions of bulbourethral gland helps in the lubrication of the penis during sexual intercourse.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(839,'biology',103,966,2248,'Interferon is secreted when','[{"text": "Antibody reacts with antigen in our body", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Serotonin become active", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Lymphocytes become active", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Our body cells are infected by virus", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Interferons are produced by any microbeinfected cells. They are quick in action but give a temporary protection against microbes.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
