(877,'biology',100,553,1107,'Choose the wrong statement<br>I. Number of autosomes in $1^\\circ $ and $2^\\circ $ spermatocytes are equal.<br>II. Number of allosomes in spermatogonium and $1^\\circ $ spermatocytes is equal<br>III. Number of autosomes in spermatid & sperm is not equal.<br>IV. Number of autosomes in $2^\\circ $ spermatocyte and sperm is equal<br>V. Number of pairs of autosomes in $2^\\circ $ spermatogonia is equal to that in $1^\\circ $ spermatocyte','[{"text": "I, II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III, V", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Number of autosomes in $1^{\\circ}$ and $2^{\\circ}$ are not equal. Number of autosomes in spermatids and sperms are equal.Number of pairs of autosomes in $2^{\\circ}$ Spermatogonia is not equal to that in $1^{\\circ}$ Spermatocytes.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(878,'biology',106,1354,3257,'Alexander von Humboldt observed that, within a region species richness____ with increasing explored area.','[{"text": "Remains same", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Decreased", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Increased", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Decreased up to a limit", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Alexander bon Humbodlt was a German naturalist and geographer who described species-area relationship for the first time. $\\mathrm{He}$ did extensive explorations in the wilderness of South American forests and observed that within a region, species richness with increasing explored area, but up to a certain limit.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(879,'biology',103,966,2249,'Number of polypeptide chain present in a molecule of antibody','[{"text": "2", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "4", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "6", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "8", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Each antibody molecule has two light chains and two heavy chains. The heavy chains (H-chains) are structurally and antigenically distinct and form different antibodies, represented by $\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{~L}_{2}$',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
