(882,'biology',106,1354,3257,'The relation between species richness and area is described on a logarithmic scale by the equation ____ Where $\\mathrm{S}=$ Species richness, $\\mathrm{A}=$ area, $\\mathrm{Z}=$ Slope of the line (regression co-efficient), $\\mathrm{C}=\\mathrm{Y}$ - intercept','[{"text": "$\\\\log \\\\mathrm{S}=\\\\log \\\\mathrm{C}+\\\\mathrm{z} \\\\log \\\\mathrm{A}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\log \\\\mathrm{S}=\\\\mathrm{z} \\\\log \\\\mathrm{A}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\log \\\\mathrm{C}=\\\\log \\\\mathrm{S}+\\\\mathrm{z} \\\\log \\\\mathrm{A}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\log \\\\mathrm{S}=\\\\log \\\\mathrm{C}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The relation between species richness and area is described on a logarithmic scale by the equation is $\\log \\mathrm{S}=\\log \\mathrm{C}+\\mathrm{z} \\log \\mathrm{A}$ (Where $\\mathrm{S}=$ Species richness, $\\mathrm{A}=$ area, $\\mathrm{z}=$ Slope of the line (regression co-efficient), $\\mathrm{C}=\\mathrm{Y}$ - intercept).',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
