(885,'biology',100,554,1109,'Find out which of the following statements are true $(\\mathrm{T})$ / false $(\\mathrm{F})$ and choose the correct option.<br>\ni. The menstrual phase is followed by the follicular phase.<br>\nii. The change in the ovary and uterus during menstrual cycle are induced by the changes in the levels of ovarian hormones only.<br>\niii. Lack of menstruation may be indicative of pregnancy<br>\niv. Menstrual flow occurs if the released ovum gets fertilized.','[{"text": "i - T, ii - T, iii - F, iv - F", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "i - T, ii - F, iii - T, iv - F", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "i - T, ii - T, iii - T, iv - F", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "i - F, ii - T, iii - T, iv - T", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'i-True, ii-False, iii-True, iv-False',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
