(897,'biology',100,553,1108,'The difference between primary follicle and secondary follicle in the human ovary is<br>','[{"text": "The primary follicle contains the primary oocyte whereas the secondary follicle contains the secondary oocyte<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The primary follicle contains an oocyte and the 1st polar body whereas the secondary follicle contains an oocyte and the 2 nd polar body<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The oocyte in the primary follicle is diploid whereas the oocyte in the secondary follicle is haploid<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "In the primary follicle the oocyte is surrounded by a single layer of cells whereas in the secondary follicle the oocyte is surrounded by several layers of granulosa cells", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'In a primary follicle, each primary oocyte gets surrounded by alayer of granulosa cells. The primary follicle gets surrounded by more layers of granulosa to form a secondary follicle.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
