(900,'biology',103,966,2249,'Binding of antigen to antibody is through','[{"text": "Disulphide bridges", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Amide formation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Covalent bonds", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Electrostatic interactions", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Antibodies attach to antigens through poor chemical interactions, and bonding is basically non-covalent. Noncovalent interactions such as electrostatic interactions, hydrogen bonds, Van der Waals forces, and hydrophobic interactions are interactions through which antigens are bound to antibodies.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(901,'biology',100,553,1108,'In spermatogenesis, a primary spermatocyte produce four similar sperms while in oogenesis a primary oocyte forms<br>','[{"text": "Four similar ova<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Three large ova and one polar body<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Two large ova and two polar bodies<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "One large ovum and 2-3 polar bodies", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'In oogenesis a primary oocyte forms one large ovum and 2-3 polar bodies. <img src=\'/img/data/biology/100_901_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(902,'biology',106,1354,3257,'The value of \' $Z$ \' lies in the range of ____ regardless of the taxonomic group or the region.','[{"text": "0.5 to 0.7", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "0.3 to 0.7", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "0.2 to 0.3", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "0.1 to 0.2", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Ecologists have discovered that the value of $\\mathrm{Z}$ lies in the range of 0.1 to 0.2 , regardless of the taxonomic group or the region whether it is the plants in Britain, birds in California or molluscs in New York state, the slopes of the regression line are amazingly similar.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(903,'biology',103,966,2249,'Mark the correct statement','[{"text": "The anamnestic (secondary) response against a pathogen is highly intensified.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "The T-Lymphocytes produce antibodies", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The B-Lymphocytes procues cell mediated responses.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "An antibody is represented by $\\\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\\\mathrm{~L}_{4}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Whenever our body encounter pathogen first time, it produces a low intensified primary response, subsequent encounter with the same pathogen elicits a highly intensified secondary (or) anamnestic response as body already posses the memory during first pathogen encounter.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
