(997,'biology',103,966,2250,'Match the columns I and II.<br><div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. CMI<br>B. PMNL<br>C. Active immunity<br>D. Passive immunity</div><div class="column-right">P. Antibodies are produced outside the body<br>Q. Antibodies are produced inside the body<br>R. Cell Mediated Immunity<br>S. Leucocytes</div></div>','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{S}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{P}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{S}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{Q}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{S}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{S}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'A. CMI - cell mediated immunity<br>B. PMNL - leucocytes<br>C. Active immunity - antibodies are produced inside the body<br>D. passive immunity - antibodies are produced outside the body',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(998,'biology',106,1356,3259,'Loss of biodiversity in a region may lead to<br>(a) Decline in plant production<br>(b) Increased resistance to environmental perturbations such as drought<br>(c) Increased variability in certain ecosystem processes such as plant productivity, water use, and pest and disease cycles<br>(d) Lowered resistance to environmental perturbations such as drought<br>(e) Decreased variability in certain ecosystem processes such as plant productivity, water use, and pest and disease cycles','[{"text": "a, b, c", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "a, c, d", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "a, c, e", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "a, b, e", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'a,c,d are correct.<br>(b) increased resistance to environmental perturbations such as drought<br>(d) lowered resistance to environmental perturbations such as drought<br>Both are incorrect.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(999,'biology',103,966,2251,'Immunological memory exists in','[{"text": "Active immunity", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Passive immunity", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Innate immunity", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both active & passive immunity", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Immunological memory is the ability of the immune system to respond more rapidly and effectively to pathogens that have been encountered previously, and reflects the preexistence of a clonally expanded population of antigen-specific lymphocytes. Memory responses, which are called secondary, tertiary, and so on, depending on the number of exposures to antigen, also differ qualitatively from primary responses. It exist in both active and passive immunity.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1000,'biology',100,554,1109,'The graph below gives the level of ovarian and gonadotrophic hormones in the blood sample of a normal healthy female of 35 years.<br>\nAccording to you, what was the duration of menstrual cycle at the time of test? <br>','[{"text": "Day 6 to 12", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Day 1 to 5", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Day 15 to 24", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Day 13 to 14", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Day ${\\rm{1}}{{\\rm{3}}^{{\\rm{th}}}}$ to Day ${\\rm{1}}{{\\rm{4}}^{{\\rm{th}}}}$ is the time of menstrual cycle.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/100_1000_question_1.png'),
(1001,'biology',105,1283,3100,'In the American Pacific Coast, removal of the starfish&nbsp;<em>Pisaster</em>, invertebrates become extinct due to','[{"text": "Intraspecific competition", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Interspecific competition", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Interpopulation competition", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Interregion competition", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'In the American Pacific Coast, removal of the starfish <em>Pisaster</em>, invertebrates become extinct due to Interspecific competition.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1002,'biology',106,1356,3259,'What percentage of all living species will go extinct within next 20 to 50 years from human activities, if steps are not taken to conserve species?','[{"text": "$1-2 \\\\%$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$5-10 \\\\%$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$10-25 \\\\%$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$50-75 \\\\%$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Around $10-20 \\%$ of all living species will go extinct within the next 20 to 50 years from human activities, if steps are not taken to conserve species.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1003,'biology',105,1283,3100,'Which of the following is the best example maintenance of species diversity by predation','[{"text": "Spreading of Prickly pear cactus in rangeland of Australia", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Removal of&nbsp;<em>Pisaster</em>&nbsp;fishes in field experiment lead to extinction of more than 10 invertebrate species within a year", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "The Monarch butterfly is highly distasteful to its predator (bird) because of a special chemical present in its body.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Maintenance of species diversity by predation Removal of <em>Pisaster </em>fishes in field experiment lead to extinction of more than 10 invertebrate species within a year',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1004,'biology',100,554,1109,'Study the following statements and answer the question. During \' $\\mathrm{P}$ \' phase of the menstrual cycle, if pregnancy doesn\'t happen, the \'Q\' withers and dies. Usually around day 22 in a 28 day cycle. The drop in \' $R$ \' levels causes the lining of the uterus to fall away. This is known as \' $\\mathrm{S}$ \'. Identify $\\mathrm{P}, \\mathrm{Q}, \\mathrm{R}$ and $\\mathrm{S}$.<br>','[{"text": "P-Menstrual; Q-Graafian follicle; R-Estrogen;<br>S-Menarche<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "P-ovulatory; Q-endometrium; R-Follicle stimulating hormone;<br>S-Menopause<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "P-Luteal; Q-Corpus luteum; R-progesterone;<br>S-Menstruation<br>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "P-Follicular; Q-secondary oocyte; RLuteinizing hormone; S-Menstruation", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'P- Luteal, Q- Corpus luteum, R-progesterone, S- menstruation',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1005,'biology',103,966,2251,'Passive immunity is obtained through injecting','[{"text": "Antibiotics", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Vaccines", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Antibodies", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Antigen", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'When ready-made antibodies are directly given to protect the body against foreign agents, it is called passive immunity.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1006,'biology',106,1356,3259,'What is major cause of diminishing wildlife numbers?','[{"text": "Cannibalism", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Felling trees", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Paucity of drinking water", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Habitat destruction", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Habitat loss and fragmentation: This is the most important cause driving animals and plants to extinction. The most dramatic examples of habitat loss come from tropical rain forests.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1007,'biology',100,554,1109,'Which is incorrect about menstruation?','[{"text": "At menopause, there is abrupt increase in gonadotropic hormones", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Beginning of cycle of menstruation is called menarche", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "During normal menstruation about 40 $\\\\mathrm{mL}$ of blood is lost", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Menstrual fluid can easily clot", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Menstrual flow does not clot because it lacks the clotting protein.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1008,'biology',105,1283,3100,'Which of the following statements is false ragarding predators?','[{"text": "Predators keep prey population under control", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Predators help in maintaining species diversity in a community", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "If a predator is not efficient, then the prey population would become extinct", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Herbivores (predators) have a greater advantage since the plants cannot run away to avoid predation", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'If a predator is not efficient, then the prey population would become extinct is a false statement.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1009,'biology',103,966,2251,'Which of the following immunoglobulins (Ig) is present in colostrum?','[{"text": "$\\\\operatorname{IgM}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\operatorname{IgG}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\operatorname{Ig} \\\\mathrm{A}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\operatorname{IgE}$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The yellowish fluid colostrum secreted by mother during the initial days of lactation has abundant antibodies (IgA) to protect the infant.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL);
