(1010,'biology',106,1356,3259,'Deforestation does not lead to','[{"text": "Quick nutrient cycling", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Soil erosion", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Alteration of local weather conditions", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Destruction of natural habitat of wild animals", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Deforestation cause soil erosion, flood, landslides, avalanches, extinction of wild animals, Change in pattern of rainfall, and shortage of fuel and other forest products.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1011,'biology',100,554,1109,'The correct order of the changes in hormones level at first day to ${\\rm{2}}{{\\rm{8}}^{{\\rm{th}}}}$ day of menstrual cycle.<br>','[{"text": "Estrogen and progesterone level is lower- estrogen rising- progesterone rising.<br>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Estrogen and progesterone level is higherestrogen lower- progesterone rising.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Estrogen and progesterone level is lower- estrogen rising- progesterone lower.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Estrogen and progesterone level is higherestrogen rising- progesterone rising.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Oestrogen and progesterone level is lower -oestrogen rising - progesterone rising.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1012,'biology',105,1283,3100,'Which of the following is correct in a predator-prey cycle?','[{"text": "A decline in the numbers of prey causes a increase in the number of predators", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A decrease in the numbers of prey causes a decrease in the number of predators", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "An increase in the number of predators triggers an increase in the numbers of prey", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A decrease in the numbers of predators causes a decrease in the number of prey", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'A decrease in the numbers of prey causes a decrease in the number of predators is a correct statement.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1013,'biology',103,966,2251,'Preformed antibodies are given to a person suffering from.','[{"text": "Chicken fox", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Tetanus", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Cold", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "TB", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Tetanus immunoglobulin contains antibodies that kill Clostridium tetani. It is injected into a vein and provides immediate short-term protection against tetanus.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1014,'biology',106,1356,3259,'Susceptible to extinction is due to -','[{"text": "High trophic level", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Large body size", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Small population", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of the above", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'When there are no more individuals of a species (plant or animal) alive anywhere in the world, the species is said to be extinct. Extinction is also known as the process of dying out. The process is a completely natural part of evolution. But sometimes extinctions happen at a higher and a faster rate than usual. Factors such as large body size, small population and position at a higher trophic level favour extinction.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1015,'biology',100,552,1106,'Which of the following is/are true?<br>i. Myometrium has the same type of muscle as that of urinary bladder<br>ii. Myometrium has the receptor site for oxytocin.<br>iii. Myometrium is the site of implantation','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{i}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{i}, \\\\mathrm{ii}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "iii only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ii only", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The correct statements are - Myometrium has the same type of muscle as that of urinary bladder and Myometrium has the receptor site for Oxytocin',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1016,'biology',105,1283,3100,'Who is considered as "Prudent" in nature?','[{"text": "Parasites", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Prey", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Host", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Predator", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Predator is considered as "Prudent" in nature.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1017,'biology',103,966,2251,'The covid -19 vaccination drive all over the country, is aimed for the production of','[{"text": "Weakened germs", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Dead germs", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Antibodies specific to covid virus", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Wide spectrum antibodies", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The covid -19 vaccination drive all over the country, is aimed for the production of Antibodies specific to covid virus',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1018,'biology',106,1356,3259,'The most important reason for decrease in biodiversity is','[{"text": "Habitat pollution", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Introduction of exotic species", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Over- exploitation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Habitat destruction", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Habitat loss and fragmentation: This is the most important cause driving animals and plants to extinction. The most dramatic examples of habitat loss come from tropical rain forests.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1019,'biology',100,554,1109,'Which of the following is correct?<br>','[{"text": "Average duration of menstrual cycle is 38 days<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Follicle is matured after 21 days<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A woman produces about 250 ova in her entire reproductive life span.<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Generally only one ovum is liberated in each menstrual cycle by alternative or any ovaries.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Though there are two ovaries, in one menstrual cycle, only one egg is produced by either of the ovaries.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1020,'biology',105,1283,3100,'No predator can be present in large quantity because:','[{"text": "Predators are not as intelligent as their prey", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Prey populations evolve anti predatory traits", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Predators are too slow in reproduction", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Prey populations multiply rapidly", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'No predator can be present in large quantity because: Prey populations evolve anti predatory traits.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1021,'biology',103,966,2251,'Triple antigen vaccine is not used for','[{"text": "Typhoid", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Tetanus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Diptheria", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pertussis", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Triple antigen vaccine is DPT vaccine which is effective against Diphtheria, pertussis (whooping cough) and tetanus. It is not effective against typhoid.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1022,'biology',106,1356,3259,'The term \'The Evil Quartet\' is related with','[{"text": "Four major causes of deforestation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Four major causes of population growth", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Four major causes of genetic mutation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Four major causes of biodiversity losses", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'There are four major causes ("The Evil Quartet \' is the sobriquet used to describe them) tell us about the 4 major causes of biodiversity losses.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1023,'biology',105,1283,3100,'Predators are prudent in nature because','[{"text": "It overxploit its prey", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It is too efficient in predation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "They do not over exploit their prey", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Predators are prudent in nature because They do not over exploit their prey.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1024,'biology',100,554,1109,'Generally, in a tubectomized premenopausal healthy woman','[{"text": "Ovulation occurs but not menstruation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Menstruation occurs but not ovulation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ovulation and menstruation do not occur", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ovulation and menstruation occur", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'If fallopian tubes are blocked, neither ovarian cycle nor the uterine cycle is affected (gonadotropins and ovarian hormones are normally secreted). Only transport of ova is blocked. Anterior pituitary hormones are responsible for ovulation whereas ovarian hormones are responsible for uterine cycle.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1025,'biology',103,966,2251,'Artificial active immunity can be aquired from','[{"text": "Acute infection", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Vaccination", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Repeated exposure to the some microbes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Treatment with antibiotics", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Artificial active immunity is acquired from vaccination.In vaccination, a preparation of antigenic proteins of pathogen or inactivated/ weakened pathogen (vaccine) are introduced into the body. The antibodies produced in the body against these antigens would neutralise the pathogenic agents during actual infection. The vaccines also generate memory $-\\mathrm{B}$ and T-cells that recognise the pathogen quickly on subsequent exposure and overwhelm the invaders with a massive production of antibodies.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1026,'biology',106,1356,3259,'Which of the following is responsible for biodiversity loss?','[{"text": "Habitat loss and fragmentation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Alien species invasions", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Over exploitation and co-extinctions", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of the above", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The following are responsible for biodiversity loss - Habitat loss and fragmentation, Alien species invasions, Over exploitation and co-extinctions',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1027,'biology',100,555,1110,'Study the following statements and answer the question. In a process called \' $\\mathrm{A}$ \', \'B\' division starts as the zygote moves through the \' $C$ \' of the \' $\\mathrm{D}$ \' towards the \' $\\mathrm{E}$ \'. Identify A, B, C, D and $\\mathrm{E}$.<br>','[{"text": "A-blastulation, B-meiotic, C-ampulla, D-fallopian tube, E-uterus<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-parturition, B- meiotic, C-infundibulum, D-uterus,<br>E-vagina<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-implanatation, B-Mitotic, C-fimbriae, D-ovary, E-cervix<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-cleavage, B-Mitotic, C-isthmus, D-oviduct, E-Uterus.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'NCERT figure 3.11',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1028,'biology',103,966,2251,'The vaccines generate ____ that recognise the pathogen quickly on subsequent exposure.','[{"text": "Memory - B cells", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Memory T-cells", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both of them", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "None of them", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The vaccines also generate memory - B and T-cells that recognise the pathogen quickly on subsequent exposure and overwhelm the invaders with a massive production of antibodies.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1029,'biology',105,1283,3100,'Animal prey defense includes all of the following except:','[{"text": "Camouflage", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Production of distasteful chemicals", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mimicry", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of these", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Animal prey defense includes all of the following <br>(1) Camouflage.<br>(2) Production of distasteful chemicals<br>(3) Mimicry',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1030,'biology',106,1356,3259,'Which forest harbouring probably millions of species is being cut and cleared for cultivating ____or for conversion to grasslands for raising beef cattle.','[{"text": "The Equador, faba beans", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The Equador, soya beans", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The Amazon, faba beans", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The Amazon, soya beans", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The Amazon rain forest (it is so huge that it is called the \'lungs of the planet\') harbouring probably millions of species is being cut and cleared for cultivating soya beans or for conversion to grasslands for raising beef cattle.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1031,'biology',100,555,1110,'What is true about cleavage in fertilized egg of humans?','[{"text": "Meroblastic", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Starts when egg reaches uterus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Starts in fallopian tube", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "It is identical to normal mitosis", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Cleavage starts in Fallopian tube',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1032,'biology',105,1283,3100,'Some species of insects and frogs are cryptically-coloured to avoid being detected easily by the predator. What is this process called?','[{"text": "Mimicry", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Camouflage", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Parasitism", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Predation", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Some species of insects and frogs are cryptically-coloured to avoid being detected easily by the predator this process is called camouflage.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1033,'biology',103,966,2251,'In case of snakebites, the injection which is given to the patients, contains ____','[{"text": "Preformed antibodies against the snake venom.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Preformed antibiotics against the snake venom.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Antibiotics against the snake Bacteria", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Painkiller", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Even in cases of snakebites, the injection which is given to the patients, contain preformed antibodies against the snake venom. This type of immunisation is called passive immunisation.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1034,'biology',106,1356,3259,'What is the reason many species like Steller\'s sea cow and passenger pigeon are becoming extinct?','[{"text": "Overexploitation by humans", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Pollution", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Habitat loss", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Competition from introduced species", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Many species like Steller\'s sea cow and passenger pigeon have been driven to the brink of extinction. This is due to overexploitation of a species by humans, which reduces the size of its population and it becomes vulnerable to extinction.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1035,'biology',100,555,1110,'What happens during fertilization when many sperms reach close to ovum<br>','[{"text": "Cells of corona radiata trap all the sperm except one<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only two sperms nearest to ovum penetrate zona pellucida<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Secretion of acrosome helps one sperm enter cytoplasm of ovum through zona pellucida<br>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "All sperms except the one nearest to ovum lose their tails", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The secretions of the acrosome help the sperm enter into the cytoplasm of the ovum through the zona pellucida and the plasma membrane.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1036,'biology',103,966,2251,'Match the columns I and II.<br><div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Active natural immunity<br>B. First line of defence<br>C. Passive natural immunity<br>D. Hepatitis B vaccine</div><div class="column-right">P. Antibodies transffered through the placenta<br>Q. Yeast<br>R. Direct contact with the pathogens that have entered inside the body<br>S. Innate immunity</div></div>','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{S}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{P}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{S}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{Q}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{S}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{Q}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{S}$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'A. Active natural immunity - direct contact with the pathogen that have entered inside the body<br>B. First line of defence - innate immunity<br>C. Passive natural immunity - antibodies transferred through placenta<br>D. Hepatitis B vaccine - yeast',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
