(1048,'biology',100,554,1109,'Identify the correct statement from the following<br>','[{"text": "High levels of estrogen triggers the ovulatory surge", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Functional ova in regular cycles from puberty onwards<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sperms released from seminiferous tubules are highly motile<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Progesterone level is high during the post ovulatory phase of menstrual cycle", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The process of formation of a mature female gamete is called oogenesis. After the ovulation, the empty graafian follices transforms in to yellow body or corpusluteum. It secretes progesterone.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1049,'biology',103,966,2252,'The exaggereted response of the immune system to certain antigens is called','[{"text": "Primary immune response", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Secondary immune response", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Amnestic immune response", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Allergy", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The exaggerated response of the immune system to certain antigens present in the environment is called allergy. The substances to which such an immune response is produced are called allergens.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
