(1051,'biology',100,558,1116,'Choose the incorrect statement from the following<br>','[{"text": "In birds and mammals internal fertilisation takes place<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Colostrum contains antibodies and nutrients<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Polyspermy in mammals is prevented by the chemical changes in the egg surface<br>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "In the human female implantation occurs almost seven days after fertilisation", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Polyspermy describes on egg fertilised by more than one sperm. During fertilisation, binding of the sperm to the egg induces depolarisation of the egg plasma membrane that block the entry of additional sperms, Thus polyspermy is prevented.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1052,'biology',105,1283,3100,'How many insects are known to be phytophagus','[{"text": "$25 \\\\%$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$50 \\\\%$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$100 \\\\%$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$18 \\\\%$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Phytophagus are the insects which feed on plant sap and other parts of the plants. Nearly $25 \\%$ of the insects belong to this group and it is estimated to be approximately 5,00,000 insect.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1053,'biology',103,966,2252,'A substance that causes an allergic reaction is called','[{"text": "Allergen", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Mutagen", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Foreign substance", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Oncogen", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The substances to which such an immune response is produced are called allergens.<br>Allergens are harmless substances but are foreign to the body and results in an allergic reaction.<br>Some common allergens include pollen grains, dust mites, animal dander, mold, medications, insect venoms and various foods.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
