(1061,'biology',103,966,2252,'An allergic response appears at the site of infection causes sneezing, watery eyes, running nose, pain and heat due to the certain chemicals (allergens), they are','[{"text": "Histamine and serotonin", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Histamine and cerumen", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cerumen and serotonin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mucus and cerumen", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Symptoms of allergic reactions include sneezing, watery eyes, running nose and difficulty in breathing. Allergy is due to the release of chemicals like histamine and serotonin from the mast cells.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
