(1076,'biology',100,551,1105,'Which one of the following is not a male acessory gland<br>','[{"text": "Seminal vesicle<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ampulla<br>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Prostate<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Bulbourethral gland", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Ampulla is one of the four region of Fallopian tubes, which is a part of femal reproductive system and the others are the accessory glands of male reproductive system.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1077,'biology',103,966,2252,'Hypersensitivity of an allergen is associated with','[{"text": "Aberrant functioning of the immune mechanism", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Increase in ambient temperature", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Age of the individual", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Food habits", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Allerg is hypersensitivity orinappropriate over reaction or aberrant functioning of the immune system',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1078,'biology',106,1357,3260,'Broad utilitarian use consists of','[{"text": "Provision of oxygen", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pollination", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Aesthetic pleasure", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of them", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Broad utilitarian concept includes provision of oxygen, pollination, and aesthetic pleasure.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1079,'biology',105,1283,3101,'Darwin was convinced that ____ competition is a potent force in organic evolution.','[{"text": "Inter specific", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Intra specific", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both (1) & (2)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of these", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Darwin was convinced that inter specific competition is a potent force in organic evolution.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1080,'biology',100,553,1107,'The spermatogonia undergo division to produce sperms by the process of spermatogenesis.<br>Choose the correct one with reference of above<br>','[{"text": "Spermatogonia have 46 chromosomes and always undergo meiotic cell division<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Primary spermatocytes divide by mitotic cell division<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Secondary spermatocytes have 23 chromosomes and undergo second meiotic division<br>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Spermatozoa are formed due to mitotic division", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'In testis, the immature male germ cells called Spermatogonia is diploid and contains 46 chromosomes (2n). Some of the spermatogonia transform into primary spermatocyte after growth phase and undergo (Meiosis -I) leading the formation of two equal haploid secondary spermatocytes having 23 chromosomes. Secondary spermatocytes undergo second meiotic. (Meiosis -II) division and form four haploid spermatids.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1081,'biology',103,966,2252,'An insect bite may result in inflammation of that spot. It is triggered by alarm chemicals such as','[{"text": "Histamine and dopamines", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Histamines and serotonin", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Interferon and opsonin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Interferon and histamines", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The alarm chemicals involved in inflammation after an insect bite are histamine and kinins. They mediate hypersensitive reactions. Histamine is stored in the granules of mast cells, basophils and platelets. It is released when allergens enter the body and it mediates hypersensitive reactions. Kinins are mediators of inflammation. They cause vasodilation and also activate the immune system. Example: Bradykinin.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1082,'biology',106,1357,3260,'Which one of the following is not included under in situ conservation?','[{"text": "National park", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Botanical garden", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Sanctuary", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Biosphere reserve", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Insitu conservation includes biosphere reserves, national parks and sanctuaries.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1083,'biology',105,1283,3101,'Select the correct answer<br>I. When Darwin spoke of the struggle for existence and survival of the fittest in nature, he was convinced that intraspecific competition is a potent force in organic evolution.<br>II. Competition occurs when closely related species compete for the same resources that are limiting, but this is not entirely true.','[{"text": "Only I is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only II is correct", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None are correct", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'II. Competition occurs when closely related species compete for the same resources that are limiting, but this is not entirely true.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1084,'biology',100,553,1108,'Which among the following has 23 (haploid) chromosomes?','[{"text": "Spermatogonia", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Zygote", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Secondary occyte", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Oogonia", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Seconadry oocyte formed as a result of meiotic division of primary oocyte has 23 chromosomes.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1085,'biology',103,966,2252,'Which of the following diseases is due to an allergic reaction?','[{"text": "Skin cancer", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Eczema", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Enteric fever", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Goitre", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'An allergic reaction can take a number of forms. Some people experience difficulty breathing, coughing, burning eyes, and a runny nose when they\'re having an allergic reaction. Other allergic reactions cause changes in the skin. Allergic eczema is an itchy skin rash that develops when you come into contact with an allergen. The condition often occurs hours after you\'ve been exposed to the substance that triggered the allergic reaction.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1086,'biology',106,1357,3260,'When plant diversity is maintained in natural habitat, the conservation is known as :','[{"text": "Ex situ", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "In vivo", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "In situ", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "In vitro", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'In-situ conservation aims to enable biodiversity and maintain itself within the context of the ecosystem in which it is found.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1087,'biology',105,1283,3101,'\'Competition occurs when closely related species compete for the same resources that are limiting\'<br>Which of the following suggest that the above statement is not entirely true?','[{"text": "Visiting flamingoes and resident fishes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Resources need not be limiting", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both 1 and 2", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "None of them", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'(1) Visiting flamingos and resident fishes<br>(2) Resources need not be limiting<br>These statements are not entirely true.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(3634,'biology',11,286,551,'The percentage of oxygen in human body is','[{"text": "$65\\\\% $", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$46.6\\\\% $", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$18.5\\\\% $", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$3.3\\\\% $", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The percentage of oxygen in human body is 65%',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1088,'biology',100,555,1112,'Match the following and choose the correct options.<br><div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Troploblast<br>B. Cleavage<br>C. Inner cell mass<br>D. Implantation</div><div class="column-right">1. Embeding of blastocyst in the endometrium<br>2. Group of cells that would differentiate as embryo<br>3. Outer layer of blastocyst attached to the endometrium<br>4. Mitotic division of zygote</div></div>','[{"text": "A-2, B-1, C-3, D-4", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-3, B-4, C-2, D-1", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A-3, B-1, C-2, D-4", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-2, B-4, C-3, D-1", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'A-3, B-4, C-2, D-1',NULL,'Medium','Match the following',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1089,'biology',103,966,2252,'Anti-histamine, adrenaline and steroids are administered to reduce the symptoms of','[{"text": "Bacterial disease", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Viral diseases", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Allergy", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Helminthic diseases", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The use of drugs like anti-histamine, adrenalin and steroids quickly reduce the symptoms of allergy.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1090,'biology',106,1357,3260,'Best method to conserve genetic material of wildlife is:','[{"text": "Cold storage", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Tissue culture", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Seed storage", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Growing in natural habitats", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The genetic material from wild varieties can be preserved either in gene banks or in-situ preservation. Gene bank saves the genes and other regenerative material from a wide range of plants. In-situ, is the preservation of wild variety of plants in the fields and forests where they grow.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1091,'biology',105,1283,3101,'In some shallow South American lakes, which of the following compete for the same food of lake?','[{"text": "Visiting flamingoes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Resident fishes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both (1) and (2)", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "None of these", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'In some shallow South American lakes,<br>(1) Visiting flamingos<br>(2) Resident fishes compete for the same food of lake',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1092,'biology',100,551,1105,'The vas deferens receives duct from the seminal vesicle and opens into urethra as','[{"text": "Epididymis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ejaculatory duct", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Efferent ductule", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ureter", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Vas deferens is a continuation of cauda epididymis. It enters in to the abdominal cavity through inguinal canal. Here, it passes over urinary bladder, curves round the ureter and joins with duct of seminal vesicle and opens inro urethara as ejaculatory duct.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1093,'biology',103,966,2252,'A person may die due to allergic reaction or an anaphylactic shock which is characterised by','[{"text": "Constriction of peripheral blood vessel", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Blood capillaries become highly permeable causing loss of fluid from the blood", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Drastic increase in the blood pressure", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of the above", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'When people with severe allergies, exposed to something they\'re allergic to, they\'ll experience a potentially life-threatening reaction called anaphylaxis. It\'s caused by an overreaction of your system to an allergen. As a result, their system releases chemicals that flood the body. This will cause anaphylactic shock. Histamine is released in anaphylaxis reaction, which dilates blood vessels and makes them more permeable so that they lose fluid causing swelling within the tissues. When the body goes into anaphylactic shock, blood pressure suddenly drops, and your airways narrow, possibly blocking normal breathing.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1094,'biology',106,1357,3260,'The main function of biosphere reservation is:','[{"text": "Conservation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Development", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Scientific research, monitoring and education", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Biosphere Reserve are multipurpose protected areas, which are meant for preserving genetic diversity. It has 3 zones-<br>1) Core or natural zone<br>2) Buffer zone<br>3) Transition zone or manipulation zone<br>Function - a) Restoration<br>b) Conservation<br>c) Development<br>d) Monitoring<br>e) Education and research',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1095,'biology',105,1283,3101,'Intraspecific competition is competition among:','[{"text": "Individuals of a certain region", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Individuals of a community", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Individuals of a particular species", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Species.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Intraspecific competition is competition among individuals of a particular species.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1096,'biology',100,556,1113,'Which of the following hormones is not secreted by human placenta','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{hCG}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Estrogen", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Progesterone", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{LH}$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Luteinizing Hormone is secreted by pituitary gland, placenta secretes human chorionic gonadotropin (hcG), Estrogens, Progesteone, Human Placental Lactogen (hPL), etc.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1097,'biology',103,966,2252,'The function of histamine is','[{"text": "Vasoconstriction of blood vessels", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Vasodilation of blood vessels", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Phagocytosis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "No effect on blood vessel", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Histamine is a chemical compound produced by basophil and mast cells and is biologically active in humans as well as many other organisms. It plays a major role in the natural allergic response of the body. Histamine acts by dilating blood vessels and making them more permeable to white blood cells and some proteins, thereby allowing them to tackle the pathogens/substances that cause allergies. This natural response thus manifests as what we call \'allergic reactions\'. Antihistamines used in treatment of allergies act by blocking the release of histamine from the cells that produce it so that the reaction is suppressed.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1098,'biology',106,1357,3260,'____ is considered as one<br>of the most important biogeographic zones of India, as it is one of the richest centres of endemic species.','[{"text": "The Western Ghats", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Causcasus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sundland", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Wallacea", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The Western Ghats is considered as one of the most important biogeographic zones of India, as it is one of the richest centres of endemic species.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(3635,'biology',74,249,497,'Which of the following is a parasitic fungi on mustard?','[{"text": "<i>Rhizopus</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Albugo</i>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "<i>Agaricus</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Neurospora</i>", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Albugo (the parasitic fungi on mustard).',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1099,'biology',105,1283,3101,'An indirect competition for shared resources, such as a particular nutrient, is known as ____ competition.','[{"text": "Restrictive", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Exploitation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Interference", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Advantageous", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'An indirect competition for shared resources, such as a particular nutrient, is known as interference competition.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1100,'biology',103,966,2252,'Select how many statements are true<br>I. Somehow, modern-day life style has resulted in increasing of immunity and more sensitivity to allergens<br>II. More and more children in metro cities of India suffer from allergies and asthma due to sensitivity to the environment.<br>III. This could be because of the protected environment provided early in life.','[{"text": "Only I is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only II is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only II, III is correct", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "All are correct", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Incorrect statement (I) : Somehow, modernday life style has resulted in lowering of immunity and more sensitivity to allergens',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1101,'biology',100,551,1105,'Urethral meatus refers to the<br>','[{"text": "Urinogential duct<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Opening of vas deferens into urethra<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "External opening of the urinogential duct<br>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Muscles surrounding the urinogential duct", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Urethra is the common urinogenital canal, which originates from the urinary bladder and extends as prostatic urethra, membranous urethra and penile urethra. Penile urethra passes through Penis \\& opens to out side as urethral meatus.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1102,'biology',105,1283,3101,'Select the correct answer.<br>I. <i>Calotropis</i> produces highly poisonous cardiac glycosidase<br>II. Visiting flamingoes and resident fishes compete for their common food, the zooplankton<br>Select the correct answer','[{"text": "Only I is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only II is correct", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None are correct", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'II. Visiting flamingoes and resident fishes compete for their common food, the zooplankton.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1103,'biology',106,1357,3260,'Which one of the following pairs of geographical areas show maximum biodiversity in our country:','[{"text": "Sunderbans and Rann of Kutch", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Eastern ghats and west Bengal", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Eastern Himalaya and Western Ghats", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Kerala and Punjab", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Three of these hotspots - Western Ghats and Sri Lanka, Indo-Burma and<br>Himalaya - cover our country\'s exceptionally high biodiversity regions.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1104,'biology',100,555,1112,'Morula is a development stage<br>','[{"text": "Between zygote and blastocyst<br>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Between the blastocyst and gastrula", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "After the implantation<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Between implantation and parturition", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The diploid zygote soon after fertilization, undergoes cleavage and results in solid ball of cells, called Morula, having 16 cells (occasionally 32 cells)',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1105,'biology',103,966,2253,'Memory-based acquired immunity is evolved in ____','[{"text": "Lower vertebrates", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Higher vertebrates", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Higher chordates", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Lower chordates", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Memory-based acquired immunity evolved in higher vertebrates based on the ability to differentiate foreign organisms (e.g., pathogens) from self-cells.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1106,'biology',105,1283,3101,'Competition is best defined as a process in which the fitness of one species is significantly ____ in the presence of another species.','[{"text": "Lower", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Greater", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Equal", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of them", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Competition is best defined as a process in which the fitness of one species is significantly lower in the presence of another species.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1107,'biology',106,1357,3260,'Hotspots are regions of high','[{"text": "Rarity", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Endemism", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "In intra specific competition", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Critically endangered population", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'A biodiversity hotspot is a biogeographic regions, that is both a significant reservoir of biodiversity and is threatened with destruction. The term biodiversity hotspot specifically refers to 25 biologically rich areas around the world that have lost at least 70 percent of their original habitat.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1108,'biology',100,552,1106,'Identity the odd one from the following','[{"text": "Labia minora", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Fimbriae", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Infundibulum", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Isthmus", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The female accessory ducts constitute oviducts (Fallopian tubes), uterus and vagina. Fallopian tube consists of fimbriae, infundibulum and isthmus. The odd one is Labia minora, which is part of vulva (or) femal external genitalia.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1109,'biology',103,966,2253,'Two corollaries of autoimmunity are','[{"text": "Higher vertebrates can distinguish foreign molecules as well as foreign organisms", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Due to genetic and other unknown reasons, the body attacks self-cells.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both 1 and 2", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "All of them", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Two corollaries of autoimmunity:-One, higher vertebrates can distinguish foreign molecules as well as foreign organisms. Most of the experimental immunology deals with this aspect. Two, sometimes, due to genetic and other unknown reasons, the body attacks self-cells.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1110,'biology',106,1357,3260,'___are traditional protected areas','[{"text": "Sacred forest", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Sunderbans", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "National parks", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All the above", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'In many cultures, tracts of forest were set aside, and all the trees and wildlife within were venerated and given total protection known as sacred groves.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1111,'biology',105,1283,3101,'Interaction between two species as both attempt to use the same environmental resource is','[{"text": "Predation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Parasitism", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Competition", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Symbiosis", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Interaction between two species as both attempt to use the same environmental resource is competition.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1112,'biology',100,553,1108,'The membranous cover of the ovum at ovulation is','[{"text": "Corona radiata", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Zona pellucida", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Zona glomerulosa", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Chorion<br>", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The ovum at the time of ovulation is covered by thin transparent, non-celluar coat zona pellucida and outer thick coat corona radiata.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1113,'biology',103,966,2253,'All are autoimmune diseases except','[{"text": "Rheumatoid arthritis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Hashimoto\'s thyroiditis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Amoebiasis", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Myasthenia gravis", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Amoebiasis is defined as the condition of harbouring the protozoan parasite Entamoeba histolytica. It is a common infection of the human gastro-intestinal tract. It is wide spread in India due to poor sanitary conditions and polluted drinking water.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1114,'biology',105,1283,3101,'Who propose competitive exclusion principle?','[{"text": "Darwin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Robert May", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Gause", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Conells", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Gause propose competitive exclusion principle.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1115,'biology',106,1357,3260,'What is the total number of biodiversity hotspots in the world','[{"text": "3", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "9", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "25", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "34", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Initially 25 biodiversity hotspots were identified but subsequently nine more have been added to the list, bringing the total number of biodiversity hotspots in the world to 34 .',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1116,'biology',100,552,1106,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Presence or absence of hymen is not a reliable indicator of virgniity or sexual drive.<br></div><div class="column-right">It can be broken down by a sudden fall or jolt, insertion of a vaginal tompon or active participation in sports like horse riding.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Both statements are correct.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1117,'biology',103,967,2254,'Primary lymphoid organ is','[{"text": "Tonsils", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Thymus", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Lymph nodes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Peyer\'s patches", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The primary lymphoid organs are bone marrow and thymus where immature lymphocytes differentiate into antigensensitive lymphocytes.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1118,'biology',106,1357,3260,'What is the approximate percentage of the earth covered by hotspots?','[{"text": "$1.5 \\\\%$ (less than $2 \\\\%$ )", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$2.5 \\\\%$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$3.5 \\\\%$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$4.5 \\\\%$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Although all the biodiversity hotspots put together cover less than 2 percent of the earth\'s land area.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
