(1120,'biology',100,555,1112,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Holoblastic cleavage with almost equal sized blastomeres is characteristic of placental mammal.<br></div><div class="column-right">The mitotic division starts as the zygote moves through the infundibulum of the oviduct</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Cleavage in which the segmentation lines pass through the entire eg.Dividing it completely. It occurs in alecithal, microlecithal and Mesolecithal egs.eg:- Frog, Human egg.<br>The mitotic division starts as the zygote moves through the isthmus of the oviduct.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1121,'biology',103,966,2253,'Which of the following is an autoimmune disease?','[{"text": "Asthma", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cirrhosis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "AIDS", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Rheumatoid arthritis", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Rheumatoid arthritis which affects many people in our society is an auto-immune disease. Rheumatoid arthritis, or RA, is an autoimmune and inflammatory disease, which means that your immune system attacks healthy cells in your body by mistake, causing inflammation (painful swelling) in the affected parts of the body.<br>RA mainly attacks the joints, usually many joints at once. RA commonly affects joints in the hands, wrists, and knees.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1122,'biology',106,1357,3260,'In situ strategies include.<br>I. National parks<br>II. Wildlife sanctuaries<br>III. Biosphere reserves<br>IV. Sacred groves<br>V. Seed bank<br>VI. Zoological parks<br>Choose the correct option.','[{"text": "I, II, III and VI", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III and V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II , IV, V and VI", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III and IV", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'In situ strategy is the conservation and the protection of living resources in their natural habitat, where they occur. It includes, national parks, biosphere reserves, wildlife sacturies and sacred groves, etc.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1123,'biology',105,1283,3101,'Abingdon tortoise in Galapagos Islands became extinct within a decade after____ were introduced on the island, because of the greater browsing efficiency of introduced animal.','[{"text": "Goat", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Giraffe", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cow", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<em>Pisaster</em>", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Goat were introduced on the island, because of the greater browsing efficiency of introduced animal.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1136,'biology',100,556,1113,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Mammalian ova produce hyaluronidase.<br></div><div class="column-right">After implantation, finger-like projections appear on the trophoblast called chorionic villi</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Both statements are correct.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1124,'biology',100,555,1112,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">In morula stage the cells divide with increase in size.<br></div><div class="column-right">Zona pellucida remains intact till cleavage is completed..</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Morula having 8-16 cells, there is reduction in size of the cell.<br>Zona pellucida still forms the outer cover. Morula undergo compaction. The outer cells are smaller/flat with tight junctions while inner cell mass has gap junctions with rounded cells.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1125,'biology',103,967,2254,'The immune system plays an important role in','[{"text": "Allergic reactions", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Auto-immune diseases and organ transplantation.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Recognises, respond and remember foreign antigens", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of them", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Immune system is unique in the sense that it recognises foreign antigens, responds to these and remembers them. The immune system also plays an important role in allergic reactions, auto-immune diseases and organ transplantation.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
