(1140,'biology',100,554,1109,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">In a woman after hysterectomy (removal of uterus), the ovarian cycle is stopped.<br></div><div class="column-right">Stoppage of FSH secretion.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'After hysterectomy i.e., removal of uterus the ovarian cycle stops. Since there is no endometrial lining there will be no menstrual flow. However, hormones like estrogen will be still produced normally.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1141,'biology',103,967,2254,'Which of the following include the primary lymphoid organs?','[{"text": "Thymus, lymph nodes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Bone marrow and thymus", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Bone marrow, Peyer\'s patches", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Thymus, and tonsils", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The primary lymphoid organs, also referred to as central lymphoid/lymphatic organs, are the tissues responsible for the production of lymphoid cells from progenitor cells, incuding the bone marrow and the thymus.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1142,'biology',106,1357,3260,'Animals and plants are best protected in -','[{"text": "Sanctuaries", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Zoos", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Botanical gardens", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "National Parks", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Animals and plants are best protected in National Parks',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1143,'biology',105,1283,3101,'Two species in the same habitat can coexist when they:','[{"text": "Differ in their use of resources", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Share the same resource in different ways and at different times", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Find the resource somewhere else", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both 1 and 2", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Two species in the same habitat can coexist when they:<br>(1) Differ in their use of resources<br>(2) Share the same resource in different ways and at different times',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1144,'biology',100,555,1110,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Up to ovulation, oocyte has released one polar body. <br></div><div class="column-right">Released oocyte in the fallopian tube is in secondary metaphase stage.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The primary oocyte within the tertiary follicle grows in size and completes its first meiotic division. It is an unequal division resulting in the formation of a large haploid secondary oocyte and a tiny first polar body. The tertiary follicle further matures into a Graafian follicle. The Graafian follicle swells up and finally ruptures to release the secondary oocyte (ovum) from the ovary by the process called ovulation.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1145,'biology',103,967,2254,'Identify the correct number of secondary lymphoid organs?<br>Spleen, lymph nodes, thymus, heart, tonsils, Peyer\'s patches of small intestine, liver, bone marrow, appendix.','[{"text": "4", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "5", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "3", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "6", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'After maturation the lymphocytes migrate to secondary lymphoid organs like spleen, lymph nodes, tonsils, Peyer\'s patches of small intestine and appendix.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1146,'biology',106,1357,3260,'In situ conservation of national genetic resources can be achieved by establishing','[{"text": "National park", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Wild life sanctuaries", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Biosphere reserves", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of the above", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Institution conservation includes National parks, Sanctuaries, Biosphere reserve and Sacred forests and lakes.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1147,'biology',105,1283,3101,'Who showed that five closely related species of warblers living on the same tree were able to avoid competition and co-exist due to behavioural differences in their forging activities?','[{"text": "Connell", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mc Arthur", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Gause", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Darwin", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Mc Arthur showed that five closely related species of warblers living on the same tree were able to avoid competition and co-exist due to behavioural differences in their forging activities',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1148,'biology',100,553,1108,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Corpus luteum is produced by Graafian follicle in fallopian tube after ovulation.<br></div><div class="column-right">It secretes estrogen which is necessary to maintain pregnancy.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Just after the release of the ovum, the ruptured follicle continues to grow under the influence of LH. The follicular cells become lutein cells due to the deposition of yellow lipid particles and is now known as Corpus luteum. in ovary .It secretes large amount of progesterone. This is essential to maintain the endometrium for a possible pregnancy.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1149,'biology',103,967,2254,'The secondary lymphoid organs provide the sites for,','[{"text": "Interaction of lymphocytes with the antigen", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Proliferation to become effector cells.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "To become mature B and T cells", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both 1 and 2", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The secondary lymphoid organs provide the sites for interaction of lymphocytes with the antigen, which then proliferate to become effector cells.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1150,'biology',106,1357,3260,'One of the ex situ conservation methods for endangered species is:','[{"text": "Wildlife Sanctuaries", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Biosphere reserves", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cryopreservation", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "National parks", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Gametes of threatened species can be preserved in viable and fertile condition for long periods using cryopreservation techniques, eggs can be fertilised in vitro, and plants can be propagated using tissue culture methods.It is an eg. ex -situ conservation.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1151,'biology',105,1283,3101,'Gause\'s competitive exclusion principle states that','[{"text": "Two closely unrelated species competing for the same resources cannot co-exist indefinitely and competitively inferior one will eliminated eventually", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Two closely related species competing for the same resources cannot co-exist indefinitely and competitively inferior one will eliminated eventually", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Two related species competing for the same resources can co-exist definitely and can grow together", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Two closely related species competing for the same resources can co-exist indefinitely and can grow together", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Gause\'s competitive exclusion principle states that Two closely related species competing for the same resources cannot co-exist indefinitely and competitively inferior one will eliminated eventually.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1152,'biology',100,556,1113,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Human placenta is haemochorial.<br></div><div class="column-right">Foetal blood and maternal blood in human placenta are separated by only blood capillaries.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Hemochorial type of placenta is in which all maternal layers are lost so that foetal tissue chorion is in direct contact with the maternal blood, as occurs in insectivores, rodents, rabbits and most primates like, Man.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1153,'biology',103,967,2254,'Correct about bone marrow is:<br>(a) Primary lymphoid organ<br>(b) main lymphoid organ where all blood cells are produced<br>(c) Provide micro environment for the development of T-cells<br>(d) Produces B-cells','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{a}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{b}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "a, b and c", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All statements are correct", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The bone marrow is one of two primary lymphoid organs, along with the thymus. Bone marrow is where B-cells are produced, selected, developed and matured in a process called hematopoiesis. Both bone-marrow and thymus provide micro-environments for the development and maturation of T-lymphocytes. The job of the bone marrow is - creating the cells that will become the blood cells.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1154,'biology',106,1357,3260,'____ make the easiest way to store germplasm of wild and cultivated plants at low temperature.','[{"text": "Zoological park", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Seed gene bank", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Field gene bank", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Botanical garden", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'A seed bank stores seeds to preserve genetic diversity; hence it is a type of gene bank. One reason is to have on-hand the genes that plant breeders need to increase yield, disease resistance, drought tolerance, nutritional quality etc. of plants used in agriculture.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1155,'biology',100,557,1115,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Parturition is induced by neural signal in maternal pituitary.<br></div><div class="column-right">At the end of gestation period, the maternal pituitary releases prolactin which causes uterine contractions.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Process of Child birth is parturition. It is induced by a complex neuroendocrine mechanism. At full term the foetus along with the placenta induce mild contractions called foetal ejection reflex. These contractions trigger the posterior lobe of the pituitary gland to release oxytocin into the maternal blood stream which then act on the uterine muscles and causes stronger uterine contractions.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1156,'biology',105,1283,3102,'Parasitism is an interaction between two species in which:','[{"text": "Both are benefited", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both are harmed", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "One is benefitted and the other is neither benefited nor harmed", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "One is benefited and the other is harmed", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Parasitism is an interaction between two species in which One is benefited and the other is harmed.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1157,'biology',103,967,2254,'Thymus is a lobed organ located near the ____A____ and beneath the ____B____ The most appropriate combination for A and B is','[{"text": "A - heart;B - breast bone", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A - liver;B - ribs", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - heart;B - ribs", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - intestine;B - ribs", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The thymus is a lobed organ located near the heart and beneath the breastbone.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(1158,'biology',106,1357,3260,'Preservation of germplasm in frozen state is :','[{"text": "Vernalisation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "In situ preservation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cryopreservation", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "In vivo preservation", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Cryopreservation is a type of in-vitro conservation. It is done in liquid nitrogen at a temperature of $-196^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$. This is particularly useful for conserving vegetatively propagated crops, e.g, potato. In cryopreservation, the material can be stored for a considerable long period of time in compact low maintenance refrigeration units.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
