(1165,'biology',103,967,2254,'Which is not involved in elicitation of immune response?','[{"text": "Thymus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Spleen", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Brain", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Lymph nodes", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Lymph nodes are oval-shaped lymphoid organ and stores $\\mathrm{B}, \\mathrm{T}$ and other immune cells. Lymph nodes are important for the proper functioning of the immune system, acting as filters for foreign particles and cancer cells. The spleen is a lymphoid organ acts as a blood filter. The spleen serves a valuable role in immune function because it purifies the blood and helps the immune system with recognizing and attack foreign bodies. The thymus is a specialized organ of the immune system, Within the thymus, T-cells mature and these T-cells are critical to the adaptive immune system.<br>The brain is not involved in the elicitation of the immune response.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
